(function(){if(!window.__hermes_register_book)return;window.__hermes_register_book("lucretius-nature",[{"sp":"HDR","t":"Book I"},{"sp":"SEC","t":"PROEM"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mother of Rome, delight of Gods and men,","st":"1.1"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dear Venus that beneath the gliding stars"},{"sp":"N","t":"Makest to teem the many-voyaged main"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fruitful lands—for all of living things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through thee alone are evermore conceived,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through thee are risen to visit the great sun-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before thee, Goddess, and thy coming on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flee stormy wind and massy cloud away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For thee the daedal Earth bears scented flowers,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For thee waters of the unvexed deep"},{"sp":"N","t":"Smile, and the hollows of the serene sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"Glow with diffused radiance for thee!"},{"sp":"N","t":"For soon as comes the springtime face of day,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And procreant gales blow from the West unbarred,"},{"sp":"N","t":"First fowls of air, smit to the heart by thee,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Foretoken thy approach, O thou Divine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And leap the wild herds round the happy fields"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or swim the bounding torrents. Thus amain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seized with the spell, all creatures follow thee"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whithersoever thou walkest forth to lead,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thence through seas and mountains and swift streams,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through leafy homes of birds and greening plains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Kindling the lure of love in every breast,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou bringest the eternal generations forth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Kind after kind. And since 'tis thou alone"},{"sp":"N","t":"Guidest the Cosmos, and without thee naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is risen to reach the shining shores of light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor aught of joyful or of lovely born,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thee do I crave co-partner in that verse"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which I presume on Nature to compose"},{"sp":"N","t":"For Memmius mine, whom thou hast willed to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Peerless in every grace at every hour-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore indeed, Divine one, give my words"},{"sp":"N","t":"Immortal charm. Lull to a timely rest"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'er sea and land the savage works of war,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For thou alone hast power with public peace"},{"sp":"N","t":"To aid mortality; since he who rules"},{"sp":"N","t":"The savage works of battle, puissant Mars,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How often to thy bosom flings his strength"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'ermastered by the eternal wound of love-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And there, with eyes and full throat backward thrown,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gazing, my Goddess, open-mouthed at thee,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pastures on love his greedy sight, his breath"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hanging upon thy lips. Him thus reclined"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fill with thy holy body, round, above!"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pour from those lips soft syllables to win"},{"sp":"N","t":"Peace for the Romans, glorious Lady, peace!"},{"sp":"N","t":"For in a season troublous to the state"},{"sp":"N","t":"Neither may I attend this task of mine"},{"sp":"N","t":"With thought untroubled, nor mid such events"},{"sp":"N","t":"The illustrious scion of the Memmian house"},{"sp":"N","t":"Neglect the civic cause."},{"sp":"N","t":"And for the rest, summon to judgments true,","st":"1.50"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unbusied ears and singleness of mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Withdrawn from cares; lest these my gifts, arranged"},{"sp":"N","t":"For thee with eager service, thou disdain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before thou comprehendest: since for thee"},{"sp":"N","t":"I prove the supreme law of Gods and sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the primordial germs of things unfold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence Nature all creates, and multiplies"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fosters all, and whither she resolves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each in the end when each is overthrown."},{"sp":"N","t":"This ultimate stock we have devised to name"},{"sp":"N","t":"Procreant atoms, matter, seeds of things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or primal bodies, as primal to the world."},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst human kind","st":"1.62"},{"sp":"N","t":"Throughout the lands lay miserably crushed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before all eyes beneath Religion—who"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would show her head along the region skies,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Glowering on mortals with her hideous face-"},{"sp":"N","t":"A Greek it was who first opposing dared"},{"sp":"N","t":"Raise mortal eyes that terror to withstand,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whom nor the fame of Gods nor lightning's stroke"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor threatening thunder of the ominous sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"Abashed; but rather chafed to angry zest"},{"sp":"N","t":"His dauntless heart to be the first to rend"},{"sp":"N","t":"The crossbars at the gates of Nature old."},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus his will and hardy wisdom won;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And forward thus he fared afar, beyond"},{"sp":"N","t":"The flaming ramparts of the world, until"},{"sp":"N","t":"He wandered the unmeasurable All."},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence he to us, a conqueror, reports"},{"sp":"N","t":"What things can rise to being, what cannot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by what law to each its scope prescribed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its boundary stone that clings so deep in Time."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore Religion now is under foot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And us his victory now exalts to heaven."},{"sp":"N","t":"I fear perhaps thou deemest that we fare","st":"1.80"},{"sp":"N","t":"An impious road to realms of thought profane;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But 'tis that same religion oftener far"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath bred the foul impieties of men:"},{"sp":"N","t":"As once at Aulis, the elected chiefs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Foremost of heroes, Danaan counsellors,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Defiled Diana's altar, virgin queen,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With Agamemnon's daughter, foully slain."},{"sp":"N","t":"She felt the chaplet round her maiden locks"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fillets, fluttering down on either cheek,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And at the altar marked her grieving sire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The priests beside him who concealed the knife,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all the folk in tears at sight of her."},{"sp":"N","t":"With a dumb terror and a sinking knee"},{"sp":"N","t":"She dropped; nor might avail her now that first"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twas she who gave the king a father's name."},{"sp":"N","t":"They raised her up, they bore the trembling girl"},{"sp":"N","t":"On to the altar—hither led not now"},{"sp":"N","t":"With solemn rites and hymeneal choir,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But sinless woman, sinfully foredone,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A parent felled her on her bridal day,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Making his child a sacrificial beast"},{"sp":"N","t":"To give the ships auspicious winds for Troy:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such are the crimes to which Religion leads."},{"sp":"N","t":"And there shall come the time when even thou,","st":"1.102"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forced by the soothsayer's terror-tales, shalt seek"},{"sp":"N","t":"To break from us. Ah, many a dream even now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can they concoct to rout thy plans of life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And trouble all thy fortunes with base fears."},{"sp":"N","t":"I own with reason: for, if men but knew"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some fixed end to ills, they would be strong"},{"sp":"N","t":"By some device unconquered to withstand"},{"sp":"N","t":"Religions and the menacings of seers."},{"sp":"N","t":"But now nor skill nor instrument is theirs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since men must dread eternal pains in death."},{"sp":"N","t":"For what the soul may be they do not know,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whether 'tis born, or enter in at birth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And whether, snatched by death, it die with us,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or visit the shadows and the vasty caves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of Orcus, or by some divine decree"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enter the brute herds, as our Ennius sang,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who first from lovely Helicon brought down"},{"sp":"N","t":"A laurel wreath of bright perennial leaves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Renowned forever among the Italian clans."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet Ennius too in everlasting verse"},{"sp":"N","t":"Proclaims those vaults of Acheron to be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though thence, he said, nor souls nor bodies fare,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But only phantom figures, strangely wan,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And tells how once from out those regions rose"},{"sp":"N","t":"Old Homer's ghost to him and shed salt tears"},{"sp":"N","t":"And with his words unfolded Nature's source."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then be it ours with steady mind to clasp"},{"sp":"N","t":"The purport of the skies—the law behind"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wandering courses of the sun and moon;"},{"sp":"N","t":"To scan the powers that speed all life below;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But most to see with reasonable eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of what the mind, of what the soul is made,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what it is so terrible that breaks"},{"sp":"N","t":"On us asleep, or waking in disease,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Until we seem to mark and hear at hand"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dead men whose bones earth bosomed long ago."},{"sp":"N","t":"I know how hard it is in Latian verse","st":"1.136"},{"sp":"N","t":"To tell the dark discoveries of the Greeks,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Chiefly because our pauper-speech must find"},{"sp":"N","t":"Strange terms to fit the strangeness of the thing;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet worth of thine and the expected joy"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of thy sweet friendship do persuade me on"},{"sp":"N","t":"To bear all toil and wake the clear nights through,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seeking with what of words and what of song"},{"sp":"N","t":"I may at last most gloriously uncloud"},{"sp":"N","t":"For thee the light beyond, wherewith to view"},{"sp":"N","t":"The core of being at the centre hid."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"SUBSTANCE IS ETERNAL"},{"sp":"N","t":"This terror, then, this darkness of the mind,","st":"1.146"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not sunrise with its flaring spokes of light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor glittering arrows of morning can disperse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But only Nature's aspect and her law,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, teaching us, hath this exordium:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nothing from nothing ever yet was born."},{"sp":"N","t":"Fear holds dominion over mortality"},{"sp":"N","t":"Only because, seeing in land and sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"So much the cause whereof no wise they know,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Men think Divinities are working there."},{"sp":"N","t":"Meantime, when once we know from nothing still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nothing can be create, we shall divine"},{"sp":"N","t":"More clearly what we seek: those elements"},{"sp":"N","t":"From which alone all things created are,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And how accomplished by no tool of Gods."},{"sp":"N","t":"Suppose all sprang from all things: any kind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Might take its origin from any thing,"},{"sp":"N","t":"No fixed seed required. Men from the sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"Might rise, and from the land the scaly breed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, fowl full fledged come bursting from the sky;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The horned cattle, the herds and all the wild"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would haunt with varying offspring tilth and waste;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor would the same fruits keep their olden trees,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But each might grow from any stock or limb"},{"sp":"N","t":"By chance and change. Indeed, and were there not"},{"sp":"N","t":"For each its procreant atoms, could things have"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each its unalterable mother old?"},{"sp":"N","t":"But, since produced from fixed seeds are all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each birth goes forth upon the shores of light"},{"sp":"N","t":"From its own stuff, from its own primal bodies."},{"sp":"N","t":"And all from all cannot become, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"In each resides a secret power its own."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, why see we lavished o'er the lands"},{"sp":"N","t":"At spring the rose, at summer heat the corn,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vines that mellow when the autumn lures,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If not because the fixed seeds of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"At their own season must together stream,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And new creations only be revealed"},{"sp":"N","t":"When the due times arrive and pregnant earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Safely may give unto the shores of light"},{"sp":"N","t":"Her tender progenies? But if from naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were their becoming, they would spring abroad"},{"sp":"N","t":"Suddenly, unforeseen, in alien months,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With no primordial germs, to be preserved"},{"sp":"N","t":"From procreant unions at an adverse hour."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor on the mingling of the living seeds","st":"1.185"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would space be needed for the growth of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were life an increment of nothing: then"},{"sp":"N","t":"The tiny babe forthwith would walk a man,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And from the turf would leap a branching tree-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wonders unheard of; for, by Nature, each"},{"sp":"N","t":"Slowly increases from its lawful seed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And through that increase shall conserve its kind."},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence take the proof that things enlarge and feed"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out their proper matter. Thus it comes"},{"sp":"N","t":"That earth, without her seasons of fixed rains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could bear no produce such as makes us glad,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And whatsoever lives, if shut from food,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Prolongs its kind and guards its life no more."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus easier 'tis to hold that many things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have primal bodies in common (as we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"The single letters common to many words)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than aught exists without its origins."},{"sp":"N","t":"Moreover, why should Nature not prepare"},{"sp":"N","t":"Men of a bulk to ford the seas afoot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or rend the mighty mountains with their hands,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or conquer Time with length of days, if not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because for all begotten things abides"},{"sp":"N","t":"The changeless stuff, and what from that may spring"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is fixed forevermore? Lastly we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"How far the tilled surpass the fields untilled"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to the labour of our hands return"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their more abounding crops; there are indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the earth primordial germs of things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, as the ploughshare turns the fruitful clods"},{"sp":"N","t":"And kneads the mould, we quicken into birth."},{"sp":"N","t":"Else would ye mark, without all toil of ours,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Spontaneous generations, fairer forms."},{"sp":"N","t":"Confess then, naught from nothing can become,","st":"1.205"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since all must have their seeds, wherefrom to grow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefrom to reach the gentle fields of air."},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence too it comes that Nature all dissolves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into their primal bodies again, and naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perishes ever to annihilation."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, were aught mortal in its every part,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before our eyes it might be snatched away"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto destruction; since no force were needed"},{"sp":"N","t":"To sunder its members and undo its bands."},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereas, of truth, because all things exist,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With seed imperishable, Nature allows"},{"sp":"N","t":"Destruction nor collapse of aught, until"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some outward force may shatter by a blow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or inward craft, entering its hollow cells,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dissolve it down. And more than this, if Time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That wastes with eld the works along the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Destroy entire, consuming matter all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence then may Venus back to light of life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Restore the generations kind by kind?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or how, when thus restored, may daedal Earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Foster and plenish with her ancient food,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, kind by kind, she offers unto each?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence may the water-springs, beneath the sea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or inland rivers, far and wide away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Keep the unfathomable ocean full?"},{"sp":"N","t":"And out of what does Ether feed the stars?"},{"sp":"N","t":"For lapsed years and infinite age must else"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have eat all shapes of mortal stock away:"},{"sp":"N","t":"But be it the Long Ago contained those germs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By which this sum of things recruited lives,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those same infallibly can never die,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor nothing to nothing evermore return."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, too, the selfsame power might end alike","st":"1.238"},{"sp":"N","t":"All things, were they not still together held"},{"sp":"N","t":"By matter eternal, shackled through its parts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now more, now less. A touch might be enough"},{"sp":"N","t":"To cause destruction. For the slightest force"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would loose the weft of things wherein no part"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were of imperishable stock. But now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because the fastenings of primordial parts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are put together diversely and stuff"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is everlasting, things abide the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unhurt and sure, until some power comes on"},{"sp":"N","t":"Strong to destroy the warp and woof of each:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nothing returns to naught; but all return"},{"sp":"N","t":"At their collapse to primal forms of stuff."},{"sp":"N","t":"Lo, the rains perish which Ether-father throws"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down to the bosom of Earth-mother; but then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upsprings the shining grain, and boughs are green"},{"sp":"N","t":"Amid the trees, and trees themselves wax big"},{"sp":"N","t":"And lade themselves with fruits; and hence in turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"The race of man and all the wild are fed;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence joyful cities thrive with boys and girls;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And leafy woodlands echo with new birds;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence cattle, fat and drowsy, lay their bulk"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the joyous pastures whilst the drops"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of white ooze trickle from distended bags;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence the young scamper on their weakling joints"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the tender herbs, fresh hearts afrisk"},{"sp":"N","t":"With warm new milk. Thus naught of what so seems"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perishes utterly, since Nature ever"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upbuilds one thing from other, suffering naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"To come to birth but through some other's death."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"And now, since I have taught that things cannot"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be born from nothing, nor the same, when born,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To nothing be recalled, doubt not my words,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because our eyes no primal germs perceive;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For mark those bodies which, though known to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"In this our world, are yet invisible:"},{"sp":"N","t":"The winds infuriate lash our face and frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unseen, and swamp huge ships and rend the clouds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or, eddying wildly down, bestrew the plains"},{"sp":"N","t":"With mighty trees, or scour the mountain tops"},{"sp":"N","t":"With forest-crackling blasts. Thus on they rave"},{"sp":"N","t":"With uproar shrill and ominous moan. The winds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis clear, are sightless bodies sweeping through"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sea, the lands, the clouds along the sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Vexing and whirling and seizing all amain;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And forth they flow and pile destruction round,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as the water's soft and supple bulk"},{"sp":"N","t":"Becoming a river of abounding floods,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which a wide downpour from the lofty hills"},{"sp":"N","t":"Swells with big showers, dashes headlong down"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fragments of woodland and whole branching trees;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor can the solid bridges bide the shock"},{"sp":"N","t":"As on the waters whelm: the turbulent stream,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Strong with a hundred rains, beats round the piers,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Crashes with havoc, and rolls beneath its waves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down-toppled masonry and ponderous stone,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hurling away whatever would oppose."},{"sp":"N","t":"Even so must move the blasts of all the winds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, when they spread, like to a mighty flood,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hither or thither, drive things on before"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hurl to ground with still renewed assault,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or sometimes in their circling vortex seize"},{"sp":"N","t":"And bear in cones of whirlwind down the world:"},{"sp":"N","t":"The winds are sightless bodies and naught else-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since both in works and ways they rival well"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mighty rivers, the visible in form."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then too we know the varied smells of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet never to our nostrils see them come;"},{"sp":"N","t":"With eyes we view not burning heats, nor cold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor are we wont men's voices to behold."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet these must be corporeal at the base,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since thus they smite the senses: naught there is"},{"sp":"N","t":"Save body, having property of touch."},{"sp":"N","t":"And raiment, hung by surf-beat shore, grows moist,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same, spread out before the sun, will dry;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet no one saw how sank the moisture in,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor how by heat off-driven. Thus we know,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That moisture is dispersed about in bits"},{"sp":"N","t":"Too small for eyes to see. Another case:"},{"sp":"N","t":"A ring upon the finger thins away"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the under side, with years and suns;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The drippings from the eaves will scoop the stone;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The hooked ploughshare, though of iron, wastes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Amid the fields insidiously. We view"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rock-paved highways worn by many feet;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And at the gates the brazen statues show"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their right hands leaner from the frequent touch"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of wayfarers innumerable who greet."},{"sp":"N","t":"We see how wearing-down hath minished these,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But just what motes depart at any time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The envious nature of vision bars our sight."},{"sp":"N","t":"Lastly whatever days and nature add"},{"sp":"N","t":"Little by little, constraining things to grow"},{"sp":"N","t":"In due proportion, no gaze however keen"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of these our eyes hath watched and known. No more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can we observe what's lost at any time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When things wax old with eld and foul decay,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or when salt seas eat under beetling crags."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus Nature ever by unseen bodies works."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"THE VOID"},{"sp":"N","t":"But yet creation's neither crammed nor blocked","st":"1.329"},{"sp":"N","t":"About by body: there's in things a void-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which to have known will serve thee many a turn,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor will not leave thee wandering in doubt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forever searching in the sum of all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And losing faith in these pronouncements mine."},{"sp":"N","t":"There's place intangible, a void and room."},{"sp":"N","t":"For were it not, things could in nowise move;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since body's property to block and check"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would work on all and at an times the same."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus naught could evermore push forth and go,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since naught elsewhere would yield a starting place."},{"sp":"N","t":"But now through oceans, lands, and heights of heaven,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By divers causes and in divers modes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before our eyes we mark how much may move,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, finding not a void, would fail deprived"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of stir and motion; nay, would then have been"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nowise begot at all, since matter, then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had staid at rest, its parts together crammed."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then too, however solid objects seem,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They yet are formed of matter mixed with void:"},{"sp":"N","t":"In rocks and caves the watery moisture seeps,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And beady drops stand out like plenteous tears;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And food finds way through every frame that lives;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The trees increase and yield the season's fruit"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because their food throughout the whole is poured,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even from the deepest roots, through trunks and boughs;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And voices pass the solid walls and fly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Reverberant through shut doorways of a house;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And stiffening frost seeps inward to our bones."},{"sp":"N","t":"Which but for voids for bodies to go through"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis clear could happen in nowise at all."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, why see we among objects some"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of heavier weight, but of no bulkier size?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Indeed, if in a ball of wool there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"As much of body as in lump of lead,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The two should weigh alike, since body tends"},{"sp":"N","t":"To load things downward, while the void abides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By contrary nature, the imponderable."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore, an object just as large but lighter"},{"sp":"N","t":"Declares infallibly its more of void;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as the heavier more of matter shows,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And how much less of vacant room inside."},{"sp":"N","t":"That which we're seeking with sagacious quest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exists, infallibly, commixed with things-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The void, the invisible inane."},{"sp":"N","t":"Right here","st":"1.370"},{"sp":"N","t":"I am compelled a question to expound,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forestalling something certain folk suppose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest it avail to lead thee off from truth:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Waters (they say) before the shining breed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the swift scaly creatures somehow give,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And straightway open sudden liquid paths,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because the fishes leave behind them room"},{"sp":"N","t":"To which at once the yielding billows stream."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus things among themselves can yet be moved,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And change their place, however full the Sum-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Received opinion, wholly false forsooth."},{"sp":"N","t":"For where can scaly creatures forward dart,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Save where the waters give them room? Again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where can the billows yield a way, so long"},{"sp":"N","t":"As ever the fish are powerless to go?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus either all bodies of motion are deprived,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or things contain admixture of a void"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where each thing gets its start in moving on."},{"sp":"N","t":"Lastly, where after impact two broad bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Suddenly spring apart, the air must crowd"},{"sp":"N","t":"The whole new void between those bodies formed;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But air, however it stream with hastening gusts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can yet not fill the gap at once—for first"},{"sp":"N","t":"It makes for one place, ere diffused through all."},{"sp":"N","t":"And then, if haply any think this comes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When bodies spring apart, because the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Somehow condenses, wander they from truth:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For then a void is formed, where none before;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, too, a void is filled which was before."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor can air be condensed in such a wise;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor, granting it could, without a void, I hold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It still could not contract upon itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"And draw its parts together into one."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, despite demur and counter-speech,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Confess thou must there is a void in things."},{"sp":"N","t":"And still I might by many an argument"},{"sp":"N","t":"Here scrape together credence for my words."},{"sp":"N","t":"But for the keen eye these mere footprints serve,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereby thou mayest know the rest thyself."},{"sp":"N","t":"As dogs full oft with noses on the ground,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Find out the silent lairs, though hid in brush,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of beasts, the mountain-rangers, when but once"},{"sp":"N","t":"They scent the certain footsteps of the way,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus thou thyself in themes like these alone"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can hunt from thought to thought, and keenly wind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along even onward to the secret places"},{"sp":"N","t":"And drag out truth. But, if thou loiter loth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or veer, however little, from the point,"},{"sp":"N","t":"This I can promise, Memmius, for a fact:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such copious drafts my singing tongue shall pour"},{"sp":"N","t":"From the large well-springs of my plenished breast"},{"sp":"N","t":"That much I dread slow age will steal and coil"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along our members, and unloose the gates"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of life within us, ere for thee my verse"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath put within thine ears the stores of proofs"},{"sp":"N","t":"At hand for one soever question broached."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"Nothing exists per se EXCEPT ATOMS AND THE VOID"},{"sp":"N","t":"But, now again to weave the tale begun,","st":"1.418"},{"sp":"N","t":"All nature, then, as self-sustained, consists"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of twain of things: of bodies and of void"},{"sp":"N","t":"In which they're set, and where they're moved around."},{"sp":"N","t":"For common instinct of our race declares"},{"sp":"N","t":"That body of itself exists: unless"},{"sp":"N","t":"This primal faith, deep-founded, fail us not,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Naught will there be whereunto to appeal"},{"sp":"N","t":"On things occult when seeking aught to prove"},{"sp":"N","t":"By reasonings of mind. Again, without"},{"sp":"N","t":"That place and room, which we do call the inane,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nowhere could bodies then be set, nor go"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hither or thither at all—as shown before."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, there's naught of which thou canst declare"},{"sp":"N","t":"It lives disjoined from body, shut from void-"},{"sp":"N","t":"A kind of third in nature. For whatever"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exists must be a somewhat; and the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If tangible, however fight and slight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will yet increase the count of body's sum,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With its own augmentation big or small;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But, if intangible and powerless ever"},{"sp":"N","t":"To keep a thing from passing through itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"On any side, 'twill be naught else but that"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which we do call the empty, the inane."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, whate'er exists, as of itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must either act or suffer action on it,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else be that wherein things move and be:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Naught, saving body, acts, is acted on;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Naught but the inane can furnish room. And thus,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beside the inane and bodies, is no third"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nature amid the number of all things-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Remainder none to fall at any time"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under our senses, nor be seized and seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"By any man through reasonings of mind."},{"sp":"N","t":"Name o'er creation with what names thou wilt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou'lt find but properties of those first twain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or see but accidents those twain produce."},{"sp":"N","t":"A property is that which not at all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can be disjoined and severed from a thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without a fatal dissolution: such,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Weight to the rocks, heat to the fire, and flow"},{"sp":"N","t":"To the wide waters, touch to corporal things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Intangibility to the viewless void."},{"sp":"N","t":"But state of slavery, pauperhood, and wealth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Freedom, and war, and concord, and all else"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which come and go whilst nature stands the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"We're wont, and rightly, to call accidents."},{"sp":"N","t":"Even time exists not of itself; but sense"},{"sp":"N","t":"Reads out of things what happened long ago,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What presses now, and what shall follow after:"},{"sp":"N","t":"No man, we must admit, feels time itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Disjoined from motion and repose of things."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, when they say there \"is\" the ravishment"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of Princess Helen, \"is\" the siege and sack"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of Trojan Town, look out, they force us not"},{"sp":"N","t":"To admit these acts existent by themselves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Merely because those races of mankind"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Of whom these acts were accidents) long since"},{"sp":"N","t":"Irrevocable age has borne away:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For all past actions may be said to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"But accidents, in one way, of mankind,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"In other, of some region of the world."},{"sp":"N","t":"Add, too, had been no matter, and no room"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherein all things go on, the fire of love"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upblown by that fair form, the glowing coal"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the Phrygian Alexander's breast,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had ne'er enkindled that renowned strife"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of savage war, nor had the wooden horse"},{"sp":"N","t":"Involved in flames old Pergama, by a birth"},{"sp":"N","t":"At midnight of a brood of the Hellenes."},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus thou canst remark that every act"},{"sp":"N","t":"At bottom exists not of itself, nor is"},{"sp":"N","t":"As body is, nor has like name with void;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But rather of sort more fitly to be called"},{"sp":"N","t":"An accident of body, and of place"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherein all things go on."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"CHARACTER OF THE ATOMS"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bodies, again,","st":"1.483"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are partly primal germs of things, and partly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unions deriving from the primal germs."},{"sp":"N","t":"And those which are the primal germs of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"No power can quench; for in the end they conquer"},{"sp":"N","t":"By their own solidness; though hard it be"},{"sp":"N","t":"To think that aught in things has solid frame;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For lightnings pass, no less than voice and shout,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through hedging walls of houses, and the iron"},{"sp":"N","t":"White-dazzles in the fire, and rocks will burn"},{"sp":"N","t":"With exhalations fierce and burst asunder."},{"sp":"N","t":"Totters the rigid gold dissolved in heat;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ice of bronze melts conquered in the flame;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Warmth and the piercing cold through silver seep,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since, with the cups held rightly in the hand,"},{"sp":"N","t":"We oft feel both, as from above is poured"},{"sp":"N","t":"The dew of waters between their shining sides:"},{"sp":"N","t":"So true it is no solid form is found."},{"sp":"N","t":"But yet because true reason and nature of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Constrain us, come, whilst in few verses now"},{"sp":"N","t":"I disentangle how there still exist"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bodies of solid, everlasting frame-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds of things, the primal germs we teach,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence all creation around us came to be."},{"sp":"N","t":"First since we know a twofold nature exists,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of things, both twain and utterly unlike-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Body, and place in which an things go on-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then each must be both for and through itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all unmixed: where'er be empty space,"},{"sp":"N","t":"There body's not; and so where body bides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"There not at all exists the void inane."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus primal bodies are solid, without a void."},{"sp":"N","t":"But since there's void in all begotten things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All solid matter must be round the same;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor, by true reason canst thou prove aught hides"},{"sp":"N","t":"And holds a void within its body, unless"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou grant what holds it be a solid. Know,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That which can hold a void of things within"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can be naught else than matter in union knit."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus matter, consisting of a solid frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath power to be eternal, though all else,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though all creation, be dissolved away."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, were naught of empty and inane,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The world were then a solid; as, without"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some certain bodies to fill the places held,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The world that is were but a vacant void."},{"sp":"N","t":"And so, infallibly, alternate-wise"},{"sp":"N","t":"Body and void are still distinguished,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since nature knows no wholly full nor void."},{"sp":"N","t":"There are, then, certain bodies, possessed of power"},{"sp":"N","t":"To vary forever the empty and the full;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And these can nor be sundered from without"},{"sp":"N","t":"By beats and blows, nor from within be torn"},{"sp":"N","t":"By penetration, nor be overthrown"},{"sp":"N","t":"By any assault soever through the world-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For without void, naught can be crushed, it seems,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor broken, nor severed by a cut in twain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor can it take the damp, or seeping cold"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or piercing fire, those old destroyers three;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But the more void within a thing, the more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Entirely it totters at their sure assault."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus if first bodies be, as I have taught,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Solid, without a void, they must be then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Eternal; and, if matter ne'er had been"},{"sp":"N","t":"Eternal, long ere now had all things gone"},{"sp":"N","t":"Back into nothing utterly, and all"},{"sp":"N","t":"We see around from nothing had been born-"},{"sp":"N","t":"But since I taught above that naught can be"},{"sp":"N","t":"From naught created, nor the once begotten"},{"sp":"N","t":"To naught be summoned back, these primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must have an immortality of frame."},{"sp":"N","t":"And into these must each thing be resolved,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When comes its supreme hour, that thus there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"At hand the stuff for plenishing the world."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"So primal germs have solid singleness"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor otherwise could they have been conserved"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through aeons and infinity of time"},{"sp":"N","t":"For the replenishment of wasted worlds."},{"sp":"N","t":"Once more, if nature had given a scope for things"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be forever broken more and more,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By now the bodies of matter would have been"},{"sp":"N","t":"So far reduced by breakings in old days"},{"sp":"N","t":"That from them nothing could, at season fixed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be born, and arrive its prime and top of life."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, lo, each thing is quicker marred than made;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so whate'er the long infinitude"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of days and all fore-passed time would now"},{"sp":"N","t":"By this have broken and ruined and dissolved,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That same could ne'er in all remaining time"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be builded up for plenishing the world."},{"sp":"N","t":"But mark: infallibly a fixed bound"},{"sp":"N","t":"Remaineth stablished 'gainst their breaking down;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since we behold each thing soever renewed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And unto all, their seasons, after their kind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherein they arrive the flower of their age."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, if bounds have not been set against","st":"1.551"},{"sp":"N","t":"The breaking down of this corporeal world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet must all bodies of whatever things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have still endured from everlasting time"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto this present, as not yet assailed"},{"sp":"N","t":"By shocks of peril. But because the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are, to thy thinking, of a nature frail,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It ill accords that thus they could remain"},{"sp":"N","t":"(As thus they do) through everlasting time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Vexed through the ages (as indeed they are)"},{"sp":"N","t":"By the innumerable blows of chance."},{"sp":"N","t":"So in our programme of creation, mark"},{"sp":"N","t":"How 'tis that, though the bodies of all stuff"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are solid to the core, we yet explain"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ways whereby some things are fashioned soft-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Air, water, earth, and fiery exhalations-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by what force they function and go on:"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fact is founded in the void of things."},{"sp":"N","t":"But if the primal germs themselves be soft,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Reason cannot be brought to bear to show"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ways whereby may be created these"},{"sp":"N","t":"Great crags of basalt and the during iron;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For their whole nature will profoundly lack"},{"sp":"N","t":"The first foundations of a solid frame."},{"sp":"N","t":"But powerful in old simplicity,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Abide the solid, the primeval germs;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by their combinations more condensed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All objects can be tightly knit and bound"},{"sp":"N","t":"And made to show unconquerable strength."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, since all things kind by kind obtain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fixed bounds of growing and conserving life;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since Nature hath inviolably decreed"},{"sp":"N","t":"What each can do, what each can never do;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since naught is changed, but all things so abide"},{"sp":"N","t":"That ever the variegated birds reveal"},{"sp":"N","t":"The spots or stripes peculiar to their kind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Spring after spring: thus surely all that is"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must be composed of matter immutable."},{"sp":"N","t":"For if the primal germs in any wise"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were open to conquest and to change, 'twould be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Uncertain also what could come to birth"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what could not, and by what law to each"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its scope prescribed, its boundary stone that clings"},{"sp":"N","t":"So deep in Time. Nor could the generations"},{"sp":"N","t":"Kind after kind so often reproduce"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature, habits, motions, ways of life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of their progenitors."},{"sp":"N","t":"And then again,","st":"1.599"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since there is ever an extreme bounding point"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Of that first body which our senses now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cannot perceive: That bounding point indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exists without all parts, a minimum"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of nature, nor was e'er a thing apart,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As of itself,—nor shall hereafter be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since 'tis itself still parcel of another,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A first and single part, whence other parts"},{"sp":"N","t":"And others similar in order lie"},{"sp":"N","t":"In a packed phalanx, filling to the full"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of first body: being thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not self-existent, they must cleave to that"},{"sp":"N","t":"From which in nowise they can sundered be."},{"sp":"N","t":"So primal germs have solid singleness,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which tightly packed and closely joined cohere"},{"sp":"N","t":"By virtue of their minim particles-"},{"sp":"N","t":"No compound by mere union of the same;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But strong in their eternal singleness,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nature, reserving them as seeds for things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Permitteth naught of rupture or decrease."},{"sp":"N","t":"Moreover, were there not a minimum,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The smallest bodies would have infinites,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since then a half-of-half could still be halved,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With limitless division less and less."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then what the difference 'twixt the sum and least?"},{"sp":"N","t":"None: for however infinite the sum,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet even the smallest would consist the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of infinite parts. But since true reason here"},{"sp":"N","t":"Protests, denying that the mind can think it,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Convinced thou must confess such things there are"},{"sp":"N","t":"As have no parts, the minimums of nature."},{"sp":"N","t":"And since these are, likewise confess thou must"},{"sp":"N","t":"That primal bodies are solid and eterne."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, if Nature, creatress of all things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were wont to force all things to be resolved"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto least parts, then would she not avail"},{"sp":"N","t":"To reproduce from out them anything;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because whate'er is not endowed with parts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cannot possess those properties required"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of generative stuff—divers connections,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Weights, blows, encounters, motions, whereby things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forevermore have being and go on."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"CONFUTATION OF OTHER PHILOSOPHERS"},{"sp":"N","t":"And on such grounds it is that those who held","st":"1.635"},{"sp":"N","t":"The stuff of things is fire, and out of fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alone the cosmic sum is formed, are seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mightily from true reason to have lapsed."},{"sp":"N","t":"Of whom, chief leader to do battle, comes"},{"sp":"N","t":"That Heraclitus, famous for dark speech"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the silly, not the serious Greeks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who search for truth. For dolts are ever prone"},{"sp":"N","t":"That to bewonder and adore which hides"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beneath distorted words, holding that true"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which sweetly tickles in their stupid ears,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or which is rouged in finely finished phrase."},{"sp":"N","t":"For how, I ask, can things so varied be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If formed of fire, single and pure? No whit"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twould help for fire to be condensed or thinned,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If all the parts of fire did still preserve"},{"sp":"N","t":"But fire's own nature, seen before in gross."},{"sp":"N","t":"The heat were keener with the parts compressed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Milder, again, when severed or dispersed-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And more than this thou canst conceive of naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"That from such causes could become; much less"},{"sp":"N","t":"Might earth's variety of things be born"},{"sp":"N","t":"From any fires soever, dense or rare."},{"sp":"N","t":"This too: if they suppose a void in things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then fires can be condensed and still left rare;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But since they see such opposites of thought"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rising against them, and are loath to leave"},{"sp":"N","t":"An unmixed void in things, they fear the steep"},{"sp":"N","t":"And lose the road of truth. Nor do they see,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That, if from things we take away the void,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All things are then condensed, and out of all"},{"sp":"N","t":"One body made, which has no power to dart"},{"sp":"N","t":"Swiftly from out itself not anything-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As throws the fire its light and warmth around,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Giving thee proof its parts are not compact."},{"sp":"N","t":"But if perhaps they think, in other wise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fires through their combinations can be quenched"},{"sp":"N","t":"And change their substance, very well: behold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If fire shall spare to do so in no part,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then heat will perish utterly and all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And out of nothing would the world be formed."},{"sp":"N","t":"For change in anything from out its bounds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Means instant death of that which was before;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus a somewhat must persist unharmed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Amid the world, lest all return to naught,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, born from naught, abundance thrive anew."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now since indeed there are those surest bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which keep their nature evermore the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon whose going out and coming in"},{"sp":"N","t":"And changed order things their nature change,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all corporeal substances transformed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis thine to know those primal bodies, then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are not of fire. For 'twere of no avail"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should some depart and go away, and some"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be added new, and some be changed in order,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If still all kept their nature of old heat:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For whatsoever they created then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would still in any case be only fire."},{"sp":"N","t":"The truth, I fancy, this: bodies there are"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whose clashings, motions, order, posture, shapes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Produce the fire and which, by order changed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do change the nature of the thing produced,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And are thereafter nothing like to fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor whatso else has power to send its bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"With impact touching on the senses' touch."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, to say that all things are but fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"And no true thing in number of all things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exists but fire, as this same fellow says,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seems crazed folly. For the man himself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against the senses by the senses fights,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hews at that through which is all belief,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through which indeed unto himself is known"},{"sp":"N","t":"The thing he calls the fire. For, though he thinks"},{"sp":"N","t":"The senses truly can perceive the fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"He thinks they cannot as regards all else,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which still are palpably as clear to sense-"},{"sp":"N","t":"To me a thought inept and crazy too."},{"sp":"N","t":"For whither shall we make appeal? for what"},{"sp":"N","t":"More certain than our senses can there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereby to mark asunder error and truth?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, why rather do away with all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And wish to allow heat only, then deny"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fire and still allow all else to be?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alike the madness either way it seems."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus whosoe'er have held the stuff of things","st":"1.705"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be but fire, and out of fire the sum,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And whosoever have constituted air"},{"sp":"N","t":"As first beginning of begotten things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all whoever have held that of itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Water alone contrives things, or that earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Createth all and changes things anew"},{"sp":"N","t":"To divers natures, mightily they seem"},{"sp":"N","t":"A long way to have wandered from the truth."},{"sp":"N","t":"Add, too, whoever make the primal stuff"},{"sp":"N","t":"Twofold, by joining air to fire, and earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"To water; add who deem that things can grow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out of the four—fire, earth, and breath, and rain;"},{"sp":"N","t":"As first Empedocles of Acragas,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whom that three-cornered isle of all the lands"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bore on her coasts, around which flows and flows"},{"sp":"N","t":"In mighty bend and bay the Ionic seas,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Splashing the brine from off their gray-green waves."},{"sp":"N","t":"Here, billowing onward through the narrow straits,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Swift ocean cuts her boundaries from the shores"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the Italic mainland. Here the waste"},{"sp":"N","t":"Charybdis; and here Aetna rumbles threats"},{"sp":"N","t":"To gather anew such furies of its flames"},{"sp":"N","t":"As with its force anew to vomit fires,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Belched from its throat, and skyward bear anew"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its lightnings' flash. And though for much she seem"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mighty and the wondrous isle to men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Most rich in all good things, and fortified"},{"sp":"N","t":"With generous strength of heroes, she hath ne'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"Possessed within her aught of more renown,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor aught more holy, wonderful, and dear"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than this true man. Nay, ever so far and pure"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lofty music of his breast divine"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lifts up its voice and tells of glories found,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That scarce he seems of human stock create."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet he and those forementioned (known to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"So far beneath him, less than he in all),"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though, as discoverers of much goodly truth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They gave, as 'twere from out of the heart's own shrine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Responses holier and soundlier based"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than ever the Pythia pronounced for men"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out the triped and the Delphian laurel,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have still in matter of first-elements"},{"sp":"N","t":"Made ruin of themselves, and, great men, great"},{"sp":"N","t":"Indeed and heavy there for them the fall:"},{"sp":"N","t":"First, because, banishing the void from things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They yet assign them motion, and allow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Things soft and loosely textured to exist,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As air, dew, fire, earth, animals, and grains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without admixture of void amid their frame."},{"sp":"N","t":"Next, because, thinking there can be no end"},{"sp":"N","t":"In cutting bodies down to less and less"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor pause established to their breaking up,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They hold there is no minimum in things;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Albeit we see the boundary point of aught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is that which to our senses seems its least,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereby thou mayst conjecture, that, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"The things thou canst not mark have boundary points,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They surely have their minimums. Then, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since these philosophers ascribe to things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Soft primal germs, which we behold to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of birth and body mortal, thus, throughout,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sum of things must be returned to naught,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, born from naught, abundance thrive anew-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou seest how far each doctrine stands from truth."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, next, these bodies are among themselves"},{"sp":"N","t":"In many ways poisons and foes to each,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore their congress will destroy them quite"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or drive asunder as we see in storms"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rains, winds, and lightnings all asunder fly."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus too, if all things are create of four,","st":"1.763"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all again dissolved into the four,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How can the four be called the primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of things, more than all things themselves be thought,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By retroversion, primal germs of them?"},{"sp":"N","t":"For ever alternately are both begot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With interchange of nature and aspect"},{"sp":"N","t":"From immemorial time. But if percase"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou think'st the frame of fire and earth, the air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The dew of water can in such wise meet"},{"sp":"N","t":"As not by mingling to resign their nature,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From them for thee no world can be create-"},{"sp":"N","t":"No thing of breath, no stock or stalk of tree:"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the wild congress of this varied heap"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each thing its proper nature will display,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And air will palpably be seen mixed up"},{"sp":"N","t":"With earth together, unquenched heat with water."},{"sp":"N","t":"But primal germs in bringing things to birth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must have a latent, unseen quality,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest some outstanding alien element"},{"sp":"N","t":"Confuse and minish in the thing create"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its proper being."},{"sp":"N","t":"But these men begin"},{"sp":"N","t":"From heaven, and from its fires; and first they feign"},{"sp":"N","t":"That fire will turn into the winds of air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Next, that from air the rain begotten is,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And earth created out of rain, and then"},{"sp":"N","t":"That all, reversely, are returned from earth-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The moisture first, then air thereafter heat-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that these same ne'er cease in interchange,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To go their ways from heaven to earth, from earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the stars of the aethereal world-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which in no wise at all the germs can do."},{"sp":"N","t":"Since an immutable somewhat still must be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest all things utterly be sped to naught;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For change in anything from out its bounds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Means instant death of that which was before."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, since those things, mentioned heretofore,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Suffer a changed state, they must derive"},{"sp":"N","t":"From others ever unconvertible,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest an things utterly return to naught."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then why not rather presuppose there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bodies with such a nature furnished forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"That, if perchance they have created fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can still (by virtue of a few withdrawn,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or added few, and motion and order changed)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fashion the winds of air, and thus all things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forevermore be interchanged with all?"},{"sp":"N","t":"\"But facts in proof are manifest,\" thou sayest,"},{"sp":"N","t":"\"That all things grow into the winds of air"},{"sp":"N","t":"And forth from earth are nourished, and unless"},{"sp":"N","t":"The season favour at propitious hour"},{"sp":"N","t":"With rains enough to set the trees a-reel"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the soak of bulking thunderheads,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sun, for its share, foster and give heat,"},{"sp":"N","t":"No grains, nor trees, nor breathing things can grow.\""},{"sp":"N","t":"True—and unless hard food and moisture soft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Recruited man, his frame would waste away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And life dissolve from out his thews and bones;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For out of doubt recruited and fed are we"},{"sp":"N","t":"By certain things, as other things by others."},{"sp":"N","t":"Because in many ways the many germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Common to many things are mixed in things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"No wonder 'tis that therefore divers things"},{"sp":"N","t":"By divers things are nourished. And, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Often it matters vastly with what others,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In what positions the primordial germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are bound together, and what motions, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They give and get among themselves; for these"},{"sp":"N","t":"Same germs do put together sky, sea, lands,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rivers, and sun, grains, trees, and breathing things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But yet commixed they are in divers modes"},{"sp":"N","t":"With divers things, forever as they move."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nay, thou beholdest in our verses here"},{"sp":"N","t":"Elements many, common to many worlds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Albeit thou must confess each verse, each word"},{"sp":"N","t":"From one another differs both in sense"},{"sp":"N","t":"And ring of sound—so much the elements"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can bring about by change of order alone."},{"sp":"N","t":"But those which are the primal germs of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have power to work more combinations still,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence divers things can be produced in turn."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now let us also take for scrutiny","st":"1.830"},{"sp":"N","t":"The homeomeria of Anaxagoras,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So called by Greeks, for which our pauper-speech"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yieldeth no name in the Italian tongue,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Although the thing itself is not o'erhard"},{"sp":"N","t":"For explanation. First, then, when he speaks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of this homeomeria of things, he thinks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bones to be sprung from littlest bones minute,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And from minute and littlest flesh all flesh,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And blood created out of drops of blood,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Conceiving gold compact of grains of gold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And earth concreted out of bits of earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fire made of fires, and water out of waters,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Feigning the like with all the rest of stuff."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet he concedes not any void in things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor any limit to cutting bodies down."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore to me he seems on both accounts"},{"sp":"N","t":"To err no less than those we named before."},{"sp":"N","t":"Add too: these germs he feigns are far too frail-","st":"1.847"},{"sp":"N","t":"If they be germs primordial furnished forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"With but same nature as the things themselves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And travail and perish equally with those,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And no rein curbs them from annihilation."},{"sp":"N","t":"For which will last against the grip and crush"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the teeth of death? the fire? the moist?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else the air? which then? the blood? the bones?"},{"sp":"N","t":"No one, methinks, when every thing will be"},{"sp":"N","t":"At bottom as mortal as whate'er we mark"},{"sp":"N","t":"To perish by force before our gazing eyes."},{"sp":"N","t":"But my appeal is to the proofs above"},{"sp":"N","t":"That things cannot fall back to naught, nor yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"From naught increase. And now again, since food"},{"sp":"N","t":"Augments and nourishes the human frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis thine to know our veins and blood and bones"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thews are formed of particles unlike"},{"sp":"N","t":"To them in kind; or if they say all foods"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are of mixed substance having in themselves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Small bodies of thews, and bones, and also veins"},{"sp":"N","t":"And particles of blood, then every food,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Solid or liquid, must itself be thought"},{"sp":"N","t":"As made and mixed of things unlike in kind-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of bones, of thews, of ichor and of blood."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, if all the bodies which upgrow"},{"sp":"N","t":"From earth, are first within the earth, then earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must be compound of alien substances."},{"sp":"N","t":"Which spring and bloom abroad from out the earth."},{"sp":"N","t":"Transfer the argument, and thou may'st use"},{"sp":"N","t":"The selfsame words: if flame and smoke and ash"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still lurk unseen within the wood, the wood"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must be compound of alien substances"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which spring from out the wood."},{"sp":"N","t":"Right here remains","st":"1.875"},{"sp":"N","t":"A certain slender means to skulk from truth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which Anaxagoras takes unto himself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who holds that all things lurk commixed with all"},{"sp":"N","t":"While that one only comes to view, of which"},{"sp":"N","t":"The bodies exceed in number all the rest,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And lie more close to hand and at the fore-"},{"sp":"N","t":"A notion banished from true reason far."},{"sp":"N","t":"For then 'twere meet that kernels of the grains"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should oft, when crunched between the might of stones,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Give forth a sign of blood, or of aught else"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which in our human frame is fed; and that"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rock rubbed on rock should yield a gory ooze."},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise the herbs ought oft to give forth drops"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of sweet milk, flavoured like the uddered sheep's;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Indeed we ought to find, when crumbling up"},{"sp":"N","t":"The earthy clods, there herbs, and grains, and leaves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All sorts dispersed minutely in the soil;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lastly we ought to find in cloven wood"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ashes and smoke and bits of fire there hid."},{"sp":"N","t":"But since fact teaches this is not the case,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis thine to know things are not mixed with things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thuswise; but seeds, common to many things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Commixed in many ways, must lurk in things."},{"sp":"N","t":"\"But often it happens on skiey hills\" thou sayest,"},{"sp":"N","t":"\"That neighbouring tops of lofty trees are rubbed"},{"sp":"N","t":"One against other, smote by the blustering south,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Till all ablaze with bursting flower of flame.\""},{"sp":"N","t":"Good sooth—yet fire is not ingraft in wood,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But many are the seeds of heat, and when"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rubbing together they together flow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They start the conflagrations in the forests."},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereas if flame, already fashioned, lay"},{"sp":"N","t":"Stored up within the forests, then the fires"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could not for any time be kept unseen,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But would be laying all the wildwood waste"},{"sp":"N","t":"And burning all the boscage. Now dost see"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Even as we said a little space above)"},{"sp":"N","t":"How mightily it matters with what others,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In what positions these same primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are bound together? And what motions, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They give and get among themselves? how, hence,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same, if altered 'mongst themselves, can body"},{"sp":"N","t":"Both igneous and ligneous objects forth-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Precisely as these words themselves are made"},{"sp":"N","t":"By somewhat altering their elements,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Although we mark with name indeed distinct"},{"sp":"N","t":"The igneous from the ligneous. Once again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If thou suppose whatever thou beholdest,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among all visible objects, cannot be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unless thou feign bodies of matter endowed"},{"sp":"N","t":"With a like nature,—by thy vain device"},{"sp":"N","t":"For thee will perish all the germs of things:"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twill come to pass they'll laugh aloud, like men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shaken asunder by a spasm of mirth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or moisten with salty tear-drops cheeks and chins."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"THE INFINITY OF THE UNIVERSE"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now learn of what remains! More keenly hear!","st":"1.921"},{"sp":"N","t":"And for myself, my mind is not deceived"},{"sp":"N","t":"How dark it is: But the large hope of praise"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath strook with pointed thyrsus through my heart;"},{"sp":"N","t":"On the same hour hath strook into my breast"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sweet love of the Muses, wherewith now instinct,"},{"sp":"N","t":"I wander afield, thriving in sturdy thought,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through unpathed haunts of the Pierides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Trodden by step of none before. I joy"},{"sp":"N","t":"To come on undefiled fountains there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To drain them deep; I joy to pluck new flowers,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To seek for this my head a signal crown"},{"sp":"N","t":"From regions where the Muses never yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have garlanded the temples of a man:"},{"sp":"N","t":"First, since I teach concerning mighty things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And go right on to loose from round the mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"The tightened coils of dread religion;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Next, since, concerning themes so dark, I frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Songs so pellucid, touching all throughout"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even with the Muses' charm—which, as 'twould seem,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is not without a reasonable ground:"},{"sp":"N","t":"But as physicians, when they seek to give"},{"sp":"N","t":"Young boys the nauseous wormwood, first do touch"},{"sp":"N","t":"The brim around the cup with the sweet juice"},{"sp":"N","t":"And yellow of the honey, in order that"},{"sp":"N","t":"The thoughtless age of boyhood be cajoled"},{"sp":"N","t":"As far as the lips, and meanwhile swallow down"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wormwood's bitter draught, and, though befooled,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be yet not merely duped, but rather thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grow strong again with recreated health:"},{"sp":"N","t":"So now I too (since this my doctrine seems"},{"sp":"N","t":"In general somewhat woeful unto those"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who've had it not in hand, and since the crowd"},{"sp":"N","t":"Starts back from it in horror) have desired"},{"sp":"N","t":"To expound our doctrine unto thee in song"},{"sp":"N","t":"Soft-speaking and Pierian, and, as 'twere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To touch it with sweet honey of the Muse-"},{"sp":"N","t":"If by such method haply I might hold"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mind of thee upon these lines of ours,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Till thou see through the nature of all things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And how exists the interwoven frame."},{"sp":"N","t":"But since I've taught that bodies of matter, made","st":"1.951"},{"sp":"N","t":"Completely solid, hither and thither fly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forevermore unconquered through all time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now come, and whether to the sum of them"},{"sp":"N","t":"There be a limit or be none, for thee"},{"sp":"N","t":"Let us unfold; likewise what has been found"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be the wide inane, or room, or space"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherein all things soever do go on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Let us examine if it finite be"},{"sp":"N","t":"All and entire, or reach unmeasured round"},{"sp":"N","t":"And downward an illimitable profound."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, then, the All that is is limited"},{"sp":"N","t":"In no one region of its onward paths,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For then 'tmust have forever its beyond."},{"sp":"N","t":"And a beyond 'tis seen can never be"},{"sp":"N","t":"For aught, unless still further on there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"A somewhat somewhere that may bound the same-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that the thing be seen still on to where"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of sensation of that thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can follow it no longer. Now because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Confess we must there's naught beside the sum,"},{"sp":"N","t":"There's no beyond, and so it lacks all end."},{"sp":"N","t":"It matters nothing where thou post thyself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In whatsoever regions of the same;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even any place a man has set him down"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still leaves about him the unbounded all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outward in all directions; or, supposing"},{"sp":"N","t":"A moment the all of space finite to be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If some one farthest traveller runs forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the extreme coasts and throws ahead"},{"sp":"N","t":"A flying spear, is't then thy wish to think"},{"sp":"N","t":"It goes, hurled off amain, to where 'twas sent"},{"sp":"N","t":"And shoots afar, or that some object there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can thwart and stop it? For the one or other"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou must admit and take. Either of which"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shuts off escape for thee, and does compel"},{"sp":"N","t":"That thou concede the all spreads everywhere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Owning no confines. Since whether there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aught that may block and check it so it comes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not where 'twas sent, nor lodges in its goal,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or whether borne along, in either view"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Thas started not from any end. And so"},{"sp":"N","t":"I'll follow on, and whereso'er thou set"},{"sp":"N","t":"The extreme coasts, I'll query, \"what becomes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thereafter of thy spear?\" 'Twill come to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"That nowhere can a world's-end be, and that"},{"sp":"N","t":"The chance for further flight prolongs forever"},{"sp":"N","t":"The flight itself. Besides, were all the space"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the totality and sum shut in"},{"sp":"N","t":"With fixed coasts, and bounded everywhere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then would the abundance of world's matter flow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Together by solid weight from everywhere"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still downward to the bottom of the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor aught could happen under cope of sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor could there be a sky at all or sun-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Indeed, where matter all one heap would lie,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By having settled during infinite time."},{"sp":"N","t":"But in reality, repose is given"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto no bodies 'mongst the elements,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because there is no bottom whereunto"},{"sp":"N","t":"They might, as 'twere, together flow, and where"},{"sp":"N","t":"They might take up their undisturbed abodes."},{"sp":"N","t":"In endless motion everything goes on"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forevermore; out of all regions, even"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out of the pit below, from forth the vast,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are hurtled bodies evermore supplied."},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of room, the space of the abyss","st":"1.1002"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is such that even the flashing thunderbolts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can neither speed upon their courses through,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gliding across eternal tracts of time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor, further, bring to pass, as on they run,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That they may bate their journeying one whit:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such huge abundance spreads for things around-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Room off to every quarter, without end."},{"sp":"N","t":"Lastly, before our very eyes is seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thing to bound thing: air hedges hill from hill,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mountain walls hedge air; land ends the sea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sea in turn all lands; but for the All"},{"sp":"N","t":"Truly is nothing which outside may bound."},{"sp":"N","t":"That, too, the sum of things itself may not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have power to fix a measure of its own,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Great nature guards, she who compels the void"},{"sp":"N","t":"To bound all body, as body all the void,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus rendering by these alternates the whole"},{"sp":"N","t":"An infinite; or else the one or other,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Being unbounded by the other, spreads,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even by its single nature, ne'ertheless"},{"sp":"N","t":"Immeasurably forth...."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor sea, nor earth, nor shining vaults of sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor breed of mortals, nor holy limbs of gods"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could keep their place least portion of an hour:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For, driven apart from out its meetings fit,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The stock of stuff, dissolved, would be borne"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the illimitable inane afar,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or rather, in fact, would ne'er have once combined"},{"sp":"N","t":"And given a birth to aught, since, scattered wide,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It could not be united. For of truth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Neither by counsel did the primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Stablish themselves, as by keen act of mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each in its proper place; nor did they make,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forsooth, a compact how each germ should move;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But since, being many and changed in many modes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the All, they're driven abroad and vexed"},{"sp":"N","t":"By blow on blow, even from all time of old,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They thus at last, after attempting all"},{"sp":"N","t":"The kinds of motion and conjoining, come"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into those great arrangements out of which"},{"sp":"N","t":"This sum of things established is create,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By which, moreover, through the mighty years,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It is preserved, when once it has been thrown"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the proper motions, bringing to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"That ever the streams refresh the greedy main"},{"sp":"N","t":"With river-waves abounding, and that earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lapped in warm exhalations of the sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Renews her broods, and that the lusty race"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of breathing creatures bears and blooms, and that"},{"sp":"N","t":"The gliding fires of ether are alive-"},{"sp":"N","t":"What still the primal germs nowise could do,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unless from out the infinite of space"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could come supply of matter, whence in season"},{"sp":"N","t":"They're wont whatever losses to repair."},{"sp":"N","t":"For as the nature of breathing creatures wastes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Losing its body, when deprived of food:"},{"sp":"N","t":"So all things have to be dissolved as soon"},{"sp":"N","t":"As matter, diverted by what means soever"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off its course, shall fail to be on hand."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor can the blows from outward still conserve,"},{"sp":"N","t":"On every side, whatever sum of a world"},{"sp":"N","t":"Has been united in a whole. They can"},{"sp":"N","t":"Indeed, by frequent beating, check a part,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Till others arriving may fulfil the sum;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But meanwhile often are they forced to spring"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rebounding back, and, as they spring, to yield,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto those elements whence a world derives,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Room and a time for flight, permitting them"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be from off the massy union borne"},{"sp":"N","t":"Free and afar. Wherefore, again, again:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Needs must there come a many for supply;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And also, that the blows themselves shall be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unfailing ever, must there ever be"},{"sp":"N","t":"An infinite force of matter all sides round."},{"sp":"N","t":"And in these problems, shrink, my Memmius, far","st":"1.1052"},{"sp":"N","t":"From yielding faith to that notorious talk:"},{"sp":"N","t":"That all things inward to the centre press;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus the nature of the world stands firm"},{"sp":"N","t":"With never blows from outward, nor can be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nowhere disparted—since all height and depth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have always inward to the centre pressed"},{"sp":"N","t":"(If thou art ready to believe that aught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Itself can rest upon itself ); or that"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ponderous bodies which be under earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do all press upwards and do come to rest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the earth, in some way upside down,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like to those images of things we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"At present through the waters. They contend,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With like procedure, that all breathing things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Head downward roam about, and yet cannot"},{"sp":"N","t":"Tumble from earth to realms of sky below,"},{"sp":"N","t":"No more than these our bodies wing away"},{"sp":"N","t":"Spontaneously to vaults of sky above;"},{"sp":"N","t":"That, when those creatures look upon the sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"We view the constellations of the night;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that with us the seasons of the sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"They thus alternately divide, and thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do pass the night coequal to our days,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But a vain error has given these dreams to fools,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which they've embraced with reasoning perverse"},{"sp":"N","t":"For centre none can be where world is still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Boundless, nor yet, if now a centre were,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could aught take there a fixed position more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than for some other cause 'tmight be dislodged."},{"sp":"N","t":"For all of room and space we call the void"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must both through centre and non-centre yield"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alike to weights where'er their motions tend."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor is there any place, where, when they've come,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bodies can be at standstill in the void,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deprived of force of weight; nor yet may void"},{"sp":"N","t":"Furnish support to any,—nay, it must,"},{"sp":"N","t":"True to its bent of nature, still give way."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus in such manner not at all can things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be held in union, as if overcome"},{"sp":"N","t":"By craving for a centre."},{"sp":"N","t":"But besides,","st":"1.1083"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seeing they feign that not all bodies press"},{"sp":"N","t":"To centre inward, rather only those"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of earth and water (liquid of the sea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the big billows from the mountain slopes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And whatsoever are encased, as 'twere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In earthen body), contrariwise, they teach"},{"sp":"N","t":"How the thin air, and with it the hot fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is borne asunder from the centre, and how,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For this all ether quivers with bright stars,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the sun's flame along the blue is fed"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Because the heat, from out the centre flying,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All gathers there), and how, again, the boughs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the tree-tops could not sprout their leaves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unless, little by little, from out the earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"For each were nutriment..."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest, after the manner of the winged flames,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ramparts of the world should flee away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dissolved amain throughout the mighty void,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And lest all else should likewise follow after,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aye, lest the thundering vaults of heaven should burst"},{"sp":"N","t":"And splinter upward, and the earth forthwith"},{"sp":"N","t":"Withdraw from under our feet, and all its bulk,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among its mingled wrecks and those of heaven,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With slipping asunder of the primal seeds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should pass, along the immeasurable inane,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Away forever, and, that instant, naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of wrack and remnant would be left, beside"},{"sp":"N","t":"The desolate space, and germs invisible."},{"sp":"N","t":"For on whatever side thou deemest first"},{"sp":"N","t":"The primal bodies lacking, lo, that side"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will be for things the very door of death:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherethrough the throng of matter all will dash,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out and abroad."},{"sp":"N","t":"These points, if thou wilt ponder,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, with but paltry trouble led along..."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"For one thing after other will grow clear,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor shall the blind night rob thee of the road,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To hinder thy gaze on nature's Farthest-forth."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus things for things shall kindle torches new."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Book II"},{"sp":"SEC","t":"PROEM"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis sweet, when, down the mighty main, the winds","st":"2.1"},{"sp":"N","t":"Roll up its waste of waters, from the land"},{"sp":"N","t":"To watch another's labouring anguish far,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not that we joyously delight that man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should thus be smitten, but because 'tis sweet"},{"sp":"N","t":"To mark what evils we ourselves be spared;"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis sweet, again, to view the mighty strife"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of armies embattled yonder o'er the plains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ourselves no sharers in the peril; but naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"There is more goodly than to hold the high"},{"sp":"N","t":"Serene plateaus, well fortressed by the wise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence thou may'st look below on other men"},{"sp":"N","t":"And see them ev'rywhere wand'ring, all dispersed"},{"sp":"N","t":"In their lone seeking for the road of life;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rivals in genius, or emulous in rank,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pressing through days and nights with hugest toil"},{"sp":"N","t":"For summits of power and mastery of the world."},{"sp":"N","t":"O wretched minds of men! O blinded hearts!"},{"sp":"N","t":"In how great perils, in what darks of life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are spent the human years, however brief!-"},{"sp":"N","t":"O not to see that nature for herself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Barks after nothing, save that pain keep off,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Disjoined from the body, and that mind enjoy"},{"sp":"N","t":"Delightsome feeling, far from care and fear!"},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore we see that our corporeal life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Needs little, altogether, and only such"},{"sp":"N","t":"As takes the pain away, and can besides"},{"sp":"N","t":"Strew underneath some number of delights."},{"sp":"N","t":"More grateful 'tis at times (for nature craves"},{"sp":"N","t":"No artifice nor luxury), if forsooth"},{"sp":"N","t":"There be no golden images of boys"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the halls, with right hands holding out"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lamps ablaze, the lights for evening feasts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And if the house doth glitter not with gold"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor gleam with silver, and to the lyre resound"},{"sp":"N","t":"No fretted and gilded ceilings overhead,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet still to lounge with friends in the soft grass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beside a river of water, underneath"},{"sp":"N","t":"A big tree's boughs, and merrily to refresh"},{"sp":"N","t":"Our frames, with no vast outlay—most of all"},{"sp":"N","t":"If the weather is laughing and the times of the year"},{"sp":"N","t":"Besprinkle the green of the grass around with flowers."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor yet the quicker will hot fevers go,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If on a pictured tapestry thou toss,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or purple robe, than if 'tis thine to lie"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the poor man's bedding. Wherefore, since"},{"sp":"N","t":"Treasure, nor rank, nor glory of a reign"},{"sp":"N","t":"Avail us naught for this our body, thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Reckon them likewise nothing for the mind:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Save then perchance, when thou beholdest forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thy legions swarming round the Field of Mars,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rousing a mimic warfare—either side"},{"sp":"N","t":"Strengthened with large auxiliaries and horse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alike equipped with arms, alike inspired;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or save when also thou beholdest forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thy fleets to swarm, deploying down the sea:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For then, by such bright circumstance abashed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Religion pales and flees thy mind; O then"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fears of death leave heart so free of care."},{"sp":"N","t":"But if we note how all this pomp at last"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is but a drollery and a mocking sport,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And of a truth man's dread, with cares at heels,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dreads not these sounds of arms, these savage swords"},{"sp":"N","t":"But among kings and lords of all the world"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mingles undaunted, nor is overawed"},{"sp":"N","t":"By gleam of gold nor by the splendour bright"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of purple robe, canst thou then doubt that this"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is aught, but power of thinking?- when, besides"},{"sp":"N","t":"The whole of life but labours in the dark."},{"sp":"N","t":"For just as children tremble and fear all"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the viewless dark, so even we at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dread in the light so many things that be"},{"sp":"N","t":"No whit more fearsome than what children feign,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shuddering, will be upon them in the dark."},{"sp":"N","t":"This terror then, this darkness of the mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not sunrise with its flaring spokes of light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor glittering arrows of morning can disperse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But only nature's aspect and her law."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"ATOMIC MOTIONS"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now come: I will untangle for thy steps","st":"2.62"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now by what motions the begetting bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the world-stuff beget the varied world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then forever resolve it when begot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by what force they are constrained to this,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what the speed appointed unto them"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherewith to travel down the vast inane:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do thou remember to yield thee to my words."},{"sp":"N","t":"For truly matter coheres not, crowds not tight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since we behold each thing to wane away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And we observe how all flows on and off,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As 'twere, with age-old time, and from our eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"How eld withdraws each object at the end,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Albeit the sum is seen to bide the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unharmed, because these motes that leave each thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Diminish what they part from, but endow"},{"sp":"N","t":"With increase those to which in turn they come,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Constraining these to wither in old age,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And those to flower at the prime (and yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"Biding not long among them). Thus the sum"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forever is replenished, and we live"},{"sp":"N","t":"As mortals by eternal give and take."},{"sp":"N","t":"The nations wax, the nations wane away;"},{"sp":"N","t":"In a brief space the generations pass,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And like to runners hand the lamp of life"},{"sp":"N","t":"One unto other."},{"sp":"N","t":"But if thou believe","st":"2.80"},{"sp":"N","t":"That the primordial germs of things can stop,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in their stopping give new motions birth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Afar thou wanderest from the road of truth."},{"sp":"N","t":"For since they wander through the void inane,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All the primordial germs of things must needs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be borne along, either by weight their own,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or haply by another's blow without."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, when, in their incessancy so oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"They meet and clash, it comes to pass amain"},{"sp":"N","t":"They leap asunder, face to face: not strange-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Being most hard, and solid in their weights,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And naught opposing motion, from behind."},{"sp":"N","t":"And that more clearly thou perceive how all"},{"sp":"N","t":"These mites of matter are darted round about,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Recall to mind how nowhere in the sum"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of All exists a bottom,—nowhere is"},{"sp":"N","t":"A realm of rest for primal bodies; since"},{"sp":"N","t":"(As amply shown and proved by reason sure)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Space has no bound nor measure, and extends"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unmetered forth in all directions round."},{"sp":"N","t":"Since this stands certain, thus 'tis out of doubt"},{"sp":"N","t":"No rest is rendered to the primal bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the unfathomable inane; but rather,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Inveterately plied by motions mixed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some, at their jamming, bound aback and leave"},{"sp":"N","t":"Huge gaps between, and some from off the blow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are hurried about with spaces small between."},{"sp":"N","t":"And all which, brought together with slight gaps,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In more condensed union bound aback,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Linked by their own all inter-tangled shapes,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"These form the irrefragable roots of rocks"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the brute bulks of iron, and what else"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is of their kind..."},{"sp":"N","t":"The rest leap far asunder, far recoil,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Leaving huge gaps between: and these supply"},{"sp":"N","t":"For us thin air and splendour-lights of the sun."},{"sp":"N","t":"And many besides wander the mighty void-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cast back from unions of existing things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nowhere accepted in the universe,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And nowise linked in motions to the rest."},{"sp":"N","t":"And of this fact (as I record it here)"},{"sp":"N","t":"An image, a type goes on before our eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Present each moment; for behold whenever"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sun's light and the rays, let in, pour down"},{"sp":"N","t":"Across dark halls of houses: thou wilt see"},{"sp":"N","t":"The many mites in many a manner mixed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Amid a void in the very light of the rays,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And battling on, as in eternal strife,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in battalions contending without halt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In meetings, partings, harried up and down."},{"sp":"N","t":"From this thou mayest conjecture of what sort"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ceaseless tossing of primordial seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Amid the mightier void—at least so far"},{"sp":"N","t":"As small affair can for a vaster serve,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by example put thee on the spoor"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of knowledge. For this reason too 'tis fit"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou turn thy mind the more unto these bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which here are witnessed tumbling in the light:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Namely, because such tumblings are a sign"},{"sp":"N","t":"That motions also of the primal stuff"},{"sp":"N","t":"Secret and viewless lurk beneath, behind."},{"sp":"N","t":"For thou wilt mark here many a speck, impelled"},{"sp":"N","t":"By viewless blows, to change its little course,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And beaten backwards to return again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hither and thither in all directions round."},{"sp":"N","t":"Lo, all their shifting movement is of old,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From the primeval atoms; for the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"Primordial seeds of things first move of self,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then those bodies built of unions small"},{"sp":"N","t":"And nearest, as it were, unto the powers"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the primeval atoms, are stirred up"},{"sp":"N","t":"By impulse of those atoms' unseen blows,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And these thereafter goad the next in size:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus motion ascends from the primevals on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And stage by stage emerges to our sense,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Until those objects also move which we"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can mark in sunbeams, though it not appears"},{"sp":"N","t":"What blows do urge them."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now what the speed to matter's atoms given","st":"2.142"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou mayest in few, my Memmius, learn from this:"},{"sp":"N","t":"When first the dawn is sprinkling with new light"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lands, and all the breed of birds abroad"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flit round the trackless forests, with liquid notes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Filling the regions along the mellow air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"We see 'tis forthwith manifest to man"},{"sp":"N","t":"How suddenly the risen sun is wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"At such an hour to overspread and clothe"},{"sp":"N","t":"The whole with its own splendour; but the sun's"},{"sp":"N","t":"Warm exhalations and this serene light"},{"sp":"N","t":"Travel not down an empty void; and thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"They are compelled more slowly to advance,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst, as it were, they cleave the waves of air;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor one by one travel these particles"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the warm exhalations, but are all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Entangled and enmassed, whereby at once"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each is restrained by each, and from without"},{"sp":"N","t":"Checked, till compelled more slowly to advance."},{"sp":"N","t":"But the primordial atoms with their old"},{"sp":"N","t":"Simple solidity, when forth they travel"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the empty void, all undelayed"},{"sp":"N","t":"By aught outside them there, and they, each one"},{"sp":"N","t":"Being one unit from nature of its parts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are borne to that one place on which they strive"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still to lay hold, must then, beyond a doubt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outstrip in speed, and be more swiftly borne"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than light of sun, and over regions rush,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of space much vaster, in the self-same time"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sun's effulgence widens round the sky."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor to pursue the atoms one by one,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To see the law whereby each thing goes on."},{"sp":"N","t":"But some men, ignorant of matter, think,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Opposing this, that not without the gods,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In such adjustment to our human ways,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can nature change the seasons of the years,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And bring to birth the grains and all of else"},{"sp":"N","t":"To which divine Delight, the guide of life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Persuades mortality and leads it on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That, through her artful blandishments of love,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It propagate the generations still,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest humankind should perish. When they feign"},{"sp":"N","t":"That gods have stablished all things but for man,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They seem in all ways mightily to lapse"},{"sp":"N","t":"From reason's truth: for ev'n if ne'er I knew"},{"sp":"N","t":"What seeds primordial are, yet would I dare"},{"sp":"N","t":"This to affirm, ev'n from deep judgment based"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the ways and conduct of the skies-"},{"sp":"N","t":"This to maintain by many a fact besides-"},{"sp":"N","t":"That in no wise the nature of the world"},{"sp":"N","t":"For us was builded by a power divine-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So great the faults it stands encumbered with:"},{"sp":"N","t":"The which, my Memmius, later on, for thee"},{"sp":"N","t":"We will clear up. Now as to what remains"},{"sp":"N","t":"Concerning motions we'll unfold our thought."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now is the place, meseems, in these affairs","st":"2.184"},{"sp":"N","t":"To prove for thee this too: nothing corporeal"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of its own force can e'er be upward borne,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or upward go—nor let the bodies of flames"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deceive thee here: for they engendered are"},{"sp":"N","t":"With urge to upwards, taking thus increase,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereby grow upwards shining grains and trees,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though all the weight within them downward bears."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor, when the fires will leap from under round"},{"sp":"N","t":"The roofs of houses, and swift flame laps up"},{"sp":"N","t":"Timber and beam, 'tis then to be supposed"},{"sp":"N","t":"They act of own accord, no force beneath"},{"sp":"N","t":"To urge them up. 'Tis thus that blood, discharged"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out our bodies, spurts its jets aloft"},{"sp":"N","t":"And spatters gore. And hast thou never marked"},{"sp":"N","t":"With what a force the water will disgorge"},{"sp":"N","t":"Timber and beam? The deeper, straight and down,"},{"sp":"N","t":"We push them in, and, many though we be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The more we press with main and toil, the more"},{"sp":"N","t":"The water vomits up and flings them back,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That, more than half their length, they there emerge,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rebounding. Yet we never doubt, meseems,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That all the weight within them downward bears"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through empty void. Well, in like manner, flames"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ought also to be able, when pressed out,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through winds of air to rise aloft, even though"},{"sp":"N","t":"The weight within them strive to draw them down."},{"sp":"N","t":"Hast thou not seen, sweeping so far and high,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The meteors, midnight flambeaus of the sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How after them they draw long trails of flame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherever Nature gives a thoroughfare?"},{"sp":"N","t":"How stars and constellations drop to earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seest not? Nay, too, the sun from peak of heaven"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sheds round to every quarter its large heat,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sows the new-ploughed intervales with light:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus also sun's heat downward tends to earth."},{"sp":"N","t":"Athwart the rain thou seest the lightning fly;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now here, now there, bursting from out the clouds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fires dash zig-zag—and that flaming power"},{"sp":"N","t":"Falls likewise down to earth."},{"sp":"N","t":"In these affairs","st":"2.216"},{"sp":"N","t":"We wish thee also well aware of this:"},{"sp":"N","t":"The atoms, as their own weight bears them down"},{"sp":"N","t":"Plumb through the void, at scarce determined times,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In scarce determined places, from their course"},{"sp":"N","t":"Decline a little—call it, so to speak,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mere changed trend. For were it not their wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thuswise to swerve, down would they fall, each one,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like drops of rain, through the unbottomed void;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then collisions ne'er could be nor blows"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the primal elements; and thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nature would never have created aught."},{"sp":"N","t":"But, if perchance be any that believe"},{"sp":"N","t":"The heavier bodies, as more swiftly borne"},{"sp":"N","t":"Plumb down the void, are able from above"},{"sp":"N","t":"To strike the lighter, thus engendering blows"},{"sp":"N","t":"Able to cause those procreant motions, far"},{"sp":"N","t":"From highways of true reason they retire."},{"sp":"N","t":"For whatsoever through the waters fall,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or through thin air, must quicken their descent,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each after its weight—on this account, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Both bulk of water and the subtle air"},{"sp":"N","t":"By no means can retard each thing alike,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But give more quick before the heavier weight;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But contrariwise the empty void cannot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"On any side, at any time, to aught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Oppose resistance, but will ever yield,"},{"sp":"N","t":"True to its bent of nature. Wherefore all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With equal speed, though equal not in weight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must rush, borne downward through the still inane."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus ne'er at all have heavier from above"},{"sp":"N","t":"Been swift to strike the lighter, gendering strokes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which cause those divers motions, by whose means"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nature transacts her work. And so I say,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The atoms must a little swerve at times-"},{"sp":"N","t":"But only the least, lest we should seem to feign"},{"sp":"N","t":"Motions oblique, and fact refute us there."},{"sp":"N","t":"For this we see forthwith is manifest:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whatever the weight, it can't obliquely go,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down on its headlong journey from above,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At least so far as thou canst mark; but who"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is there can mark by sense that naught can swerve"},{"sp":"N","t":"At all aside from off its road's straight line?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, if ev'r all motions are co-linked,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And from the old ever arise the new"},{"sp":"N","t":"In fixed order, and primordial seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Produce not by their swerving some new start"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of motion to sunder the covenants of fate,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That cause succeed not cause from everlasting,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence this free will for creatures o'er the lands,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence is it wrested from the fates,—this will"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereby we step right forward where desire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Leads each man on, whereby the same we swerve"},{"sp":"N","t":"In motions, not as at some fixed time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor at some fixed line of space, but where"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mind itself has urged? For out of doubt"},{"sp":"N","t":"In these affairs 'tis each man's will itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"That gives the start, and hence throughout our limbs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Incipient motions are diffused. Again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dost thou not see, when, at a point of time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The bars are opened, how the eager strength"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of horses cannot forward break as soon"},{"sp":"N","t":"As pants their mind to do? For it behooves"},{"sp":"N","t":"That all the stock of matter, through the frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be roused, in order that, through every joint,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aroused, it press and follow mind's desire;"},{"sp":"N","t":"So thus thou seest initial motion's gendered"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out the heart, aye, verily, proceeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"First from the spirit's will, whence at the last"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis given forth through joints and body entire."},{"sp":"N","t":"Quite otherwise it is, when forth we move,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Impelled by a blow of another's mighty powers"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mighty urge; for then 'tis clear enough"},{"sp":"N","t":"All matter of our total body goes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hurried along, against our own desire-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Until the will has pulled upon the reins"},{"sp":"N","t":"And checked it back, throughout our members all;"},{"sp":"N","t":"At whose arbitrament indeed sometimes"},{"sp":"N","t":"The stock of matter's forced to change its path,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Throughout our members and throughout our joints,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, after being forward cast, to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Reined up, whereat it settles back again."},{"sp":"N","t":"So seest thou not, how, though external force"},{"sp":"N","t":"Drive men before, and often make them move,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Onward against desire, and headlong snatched,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet is there something in these breasts of ours"},{"sp":"N","t":"Strong to combat, strong to withstand the same?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore no less within the primal seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou must admit, besides all blows and weight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some other cause of motion, whence derives"},{"sp":"N","t":"This power in us inborn, of some free act.-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since naught from nothing can become, we see."},{"sp":"N","t":"For weight prevents all things should come to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through blows, as 'twere, by some external force;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But that man's mind itself in all it does"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath not a fixed necessity within,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor is not, like a conquered thing, compelled"},{"sp":"N","t":"To bear and suffer,—this state comes to man"},{"sp":"N","t":"From that slight swervement of the elements"},{"sp":"N","t":"In no fixed line of space, in no fixed time."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor ever was the stock of stuff more crammed,","st":"2.294"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor ever, again, sundered by bigger gaps:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For naught gives increase and naught takes away;"},{"sp":"N","t":"On which account, just as they move to-day,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The elemental bodies moved of old"},{"sp":"N","t":"And shall the same hereafter evermore."},{"sp":"N","t":"And what was wont to be begot of old"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shall be begotten under selfsame terms"},{"sp":"N","t":"And grow and thrive in power, so far as given"},{"sp":"N","t":"To each by Nature's changeless, old decrees."},{"sp":"N","t":"The sum of things there is no power can change,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For naught exists outside, to which can flee"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out of the world matter of any kind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor forth from which a fresh supply can spring,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Break in upon the founded world, and change"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whole nature of things, and turn their motions about."},{"sp":"N","t":"Herein wonder not","st":"2.308"},{"sp":"N","t":"How 'tis that, while the seeds of things are all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Moving forever, the sum yet seems to stand"},{"sp":"N","t":"Supremely still, except in cases where"},{"sp":"N","t":"A thing shows motion of its frame as whole."},{"sp":"N","t":"For far beneath the ken of senses lies"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of those ultimates of the world;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so, since those themselves thou canst not see,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their motion also must they veil from men-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For mark, indeed, how things we can see, oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet hide their motions, when afar from us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the distant landscape. Often thus,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon a hillside will the woolly flocks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be cropping their goodly food and creeping about"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whither the summons of the grass, begemmed"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the fresh dew, is calling, and the lambs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Well filled, are frisking, locking horns in sport:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet all for us seem blurred and blent afar-"},{"sp":"N","t":"A glint of white at rest on a green hill."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, when mighty legions, marching round,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fill all the quarters of the plains below,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rousing a mimic warfare, there the sheen"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shoots up the sky, and all the fields about"},{"sp":"N","t":"Glitter with brass, and from beneath, a sound"},{"sp":"N","t":"Goes forth from feet of stalwart soldiery,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mountain walls, smote by the shouting, send"},{"sp":"N","t":"The voices onward to the stars of heaven,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hither and thither darts the cavalry,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And of a sudden down the midmost fields"},{"sp":"N","t":"Charges with onset stout enough to rock"},{"sp":"N","t":"The solid earth: and yet some post there is"},{"sp":"N","t":"Up the high mountains, viewed from which they seem"},{"sp":"N","t":"To stand—a gleam at rest along the plains."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"ATOMIC FORMS AND THEIR COMBINATIONS"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now come, and next hereafter apprehend","st":"2.333"},{"sp":"N","t":"What sorts, how vastly different in form,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How varied in multitudinous shapes they are-"},{"sp":"N","t":"These old beginnings of the universe;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not in the sense that only few are furnished"},{"sp":"N","t":"With one like form, but rather not at all"},{"sp":"N","t":"In general have they likeness each with each,"},{"sp":"N","t":"No marvel: since the stock of them's so great"},{"sp":"N","t":"That there's no end (as I have taught) nor sum,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They must indeed not one and all be marked"},{"sp":"N","t":"By equal outline and by shape the same."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Moreover, humankind, and the mute flocks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of scaly creatures swimming in the streams,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And joyous herds around, and all the wild,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all the breeds of birds—both those that teem"},{"sp":"N","t":"In gladsome regions of the water-haunts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"About the river-banks and springs and pools,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And those that throng, flitting from tree to tree,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through trackless woods- Go, take which one thou wilt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In any kind: thou wilt discover still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each from the other still unlike in shape."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor in no other wise could offspring know"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mother, nor mother offspring—which we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"They yet can do, distinguished one from other,"},{"sp":"N","t":"No less than human beings, by clear signs."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus oft before fair temples of the gods,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beside the incense-burning altars slain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Drops down the yearling calf, from out its breast"},{"sp":"N","t":"Breathing warm streams of blood; the orphaned mother,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ranging meanwhile green woodland pastures round,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Knows well the footprints, pressed by cloven hoofs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With eyes regarding every spot about,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For sight somewhere of youngling gone from her;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, stopping short, filleth the leafy lanes"},{"sp":"N","t":"With her complaints; and oft she seeks again"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the stall, pierced by her yearning still."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor tender willows, nor dew-quickened grass,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor the loved streams that glide along low banks,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can lure her mind and turn the sudden pain;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor other shapes of calves that graze thereby"},{"sp":"N","t":"Distract her mind or lighten pain the least-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So keen her search for something known and hers."},{"sp":"N","t":"Moreover, tender kids with bleating throats"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do know their horned dams, and butting lambs"},{"sp":"N","t":"The flocks of sheep, and thus they patter on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unfailingly each to its proper teat,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As nature intends. Lastly, with any grain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou'lt see that no one kernel in one kind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is so far like another, that there still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is not in shapes some difference running through."},{"sp":"N","t":"By a like law we see how earth is pied"},{"sp":"N","t":"With shells and conchs, where, with soft waves, the sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beats on the thirsty sands of curving shores."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore again, again, since seeds of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exist by nature, nor were wrought with hands"},{"sp":"N","t":"After a fixed pattern of one other,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They needs must flitter to and fro with shapes"},{"sp":"N","t":"In types dissimilar to one another."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . .","st":"2.381"},{"sp":"N","t":"Easy enough by thought of mind to solve"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why fires of lightning more can penetrate"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than these of ours from pitch-pine born on earth."},{"sp":"N","t":"For thou canst say lightning's celestial fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So subtle, is formed of figures finer far,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And passes thus through holes which this our fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Born from the wood, created from the pine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cannot. Again, light passes through the horn"},{"sp":"N","t":"On the lantern's side, while rain is dashed away."},{"sp":"N","t":"And why?- unless those bodies of light should be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Finer than those of water's genial showers."},{"sp":"N","t":"We see how quickly through a colander"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wines will flow; how, on the other hand,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sluggish olive-oil delays: no doubt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because 'tis wrought of elements more large,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else more crook'd and intertangled. Thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"It comes that the primordials cannot be"},{"sp":"N","t":"So suddenly sundered one from other, and seep,"},{"sp":"N","t":"One through each several hole of anything."},{"sp":"N","t":"And note, besides, that liquor of honey or milk","st":"2.398"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yields in the mouth agreeable taste to tongue,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst nauseous wormwood, pungent centaury,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With their foul flavour set the lips awry;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus simple 'tis to see that whatsoever"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can touch the senses pleasingly are made"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of smooth and rounded elements, whilst those"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which seem the bitter and the sharp, are held"},{"sp":"N","t":"Entwined by elements more crook'd, and so"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are wont to tear their ways into our senses,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And rend our body as they enter in."},{"sp":"N","t":"In short all good to sense, all bad to touch,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Being up-built of figures so unlike,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are mutually at strife—lest thou suppose"},{"sp":"N","t":"That the shrill rasping of a squeaking saw"},{"sp":"N","t":"Consists of elements as smooth as song"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, waked by nimble fingers, on the strings"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sweet musicians fashion; or suppose"},{"sp":"N","t":"That same-shaped atoms through men's nostrils pierce"},{"sp":"N","t":"When foul cadavers burn, as when the stage"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is with Cilician saffron sprinkled fresh,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the altar near exhales Panchaean scent;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or hold as of like seed the goodly hues"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of things which feast our eyes, as those which sting"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against the smarting pupil and draw tears,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or show, with gruesome aspect, grim and vile."},{"sp":"N","t":"For never a shape which charms our sense was made"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without some elemental smoothness; whilst"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whate'er is harsh and irksome has been framed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still with some roughness in its elements."},{"sp":"N","t":"Some, too, there are which justly are supposed"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be nor smooth nor altogether hooked,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With bended barbs, but slightly angled-out,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To tickle rather than to wound the sense-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And of which sort is the salt tartar of wine"},{"sp":"N","t":"And flavours of the gummed elecampane."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, that glowing fire and icy rime"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are fanged with teeth unlike whereby to sting"},{"sp":"N","t":"Our body's sense, the touch of each gives proof."},{"sp":"N","t":"For touch—by sacred majesties of Gods!-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Touch is indeed the body's only sense-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be't that something in-from-outward works,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be't that something in the body born"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wounds, or delighteth as it passes out"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the procreant paths of Aphrodite;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or be't the seeds by some collision whirl"},{"sp":"N","t":"Disordered in the body and confound"},{"sp":"N","t":"By tumult and confusion all the sense-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As thou mayst find, if haply with the hand"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thyself thou strike thy body's any part."},{"sp":"N","t":"On which account, the elemental forms"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must differ widely, as enabled thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"To cause diverse sensations."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What seems to us the hardened and condensed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must be of atoms among themselves more hooked,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be held compacted deep within, as 'twere"},{"sp":"N","t":"By branch-like atoms—of which sort the chief"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are diamond stones, despisers of all blows,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And stalwart flint and strength of solid iron,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And brazen bars, which, budging hard in locks,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do grate and scream. But what are liquid, formed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of fluid body, they indeed must be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of elements more smooth and round—because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their globules severally will not cohere:"},{"sp":"N","t":"To suck the poppy-seeds from palm of hand"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is quite as easy as drinking water down,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And they, once struck, roll like unto the same."},{"sp":"N","t":"But that thou seest among the things that flow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some bitter, as the brine of ocean is,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is not the least a marvel..."},{"sp":"N","t":"For since 'tis fluid, smooth its atoms are"},{"sp":"N","t":"And round, with painful rough ones mixed therein;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet need not these be held together hooked:"},{"sp":"N","t":"In fact, though rough, they're globular besides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Able at once to roll, and rasp the sense."},{"sp":"N","t":"And that the more thou mayst believe me here,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That with smooth elements are mixed the rough"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Whence Neptune's salt astringent body comes),"},{"sp":"N","t":"There is a means to separate the twain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thereupon dividedly to see"},{"sp":"N","t":"How the sweet water, after filtering through"},{"sp":"N","t":"So often underground, flows freshened forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into some hollow; for it leaves above"},{"sp":"N","t":"The primal germs of nauseating brine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since cling the rough more readily in earth."},{"sp":"N","t":"Lastly, whatso thou markest to disperse"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the instant—smoke, and cloud, and flame-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must not (even though not all of smooth and round)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be yet co-linked with atoms intertwined,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That thus they can, without together cleaving,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So pierce our body and so bore the rocks."},{"sp":"N","t":"Whatever we see..."},{"sp":"N","t":"Given to senses, that thou must perceive"},{"sp":"N","t":"They're not from linked but pointed elements."},{"sp":"N","t":"The which now having taught, I will go on","st":"2.478"},{"sp":"N","t":"To bind thereto a fact to this allied"},{"sp":"N","t":"And drawing from this its proof: these primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Vary, yet only with finite tale of shapes."},{"sp":"N","t":"For were these shapes quite infinite, some seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would have a body of infinite increase."},{"sp":"N","t":"For in one seed, in one small frame of any,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The shapes can't vary from one another much."},{"sp":"N","t":"Assume, we'll say, that of three minim parts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Consist the primal bodies, or add a few:"},{"sp":"N","t":"When, now, by placing all these parts of one"},{"sp":"N","t":"At top and bottom, changing lefts and rights,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou hast with every kind of shift found out"},{"sp":"N","t":"What the aspect of shape of its whole body"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each new arrangement gives, for what remains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If thou percase wouldst vary its old shapes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"New parts must then be added; follows next,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If thou percase wouldst vary still its shapes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That by like logic each arrangement still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Requires its increment of other parts."},{"sp":"N","t":"Ergo, an augmentation of its frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Follows upon each novelty of forms."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, it cannot be thou'lt undertake"},{"sp":"N","t":"That seeds have infinite differences in form,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest thus thou forcest some indeed to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of an immeasurable immensity-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which I have taught above cannot be proved."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"And now for thee barbaric robes, and gleam"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of Meliboean purple, touched with dye"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the Thessalian shell..."},{"sp":"N","t":"The peacock's golden generations, stained"},{"sp":"N","t":"With spotted gaieties, would lie o'erthrown"},{"sp":"N","t":"By some new colour of new things more bright;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The odour of myrrh and savours of honey despised;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The swan's old lyric, and Apollo's hymns,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Once modulated on the many chords,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would likewise sink o'ermastered and be mute:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For, lo, a somewhat, finer than the rest,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would be arising evermore. So, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into some baser part might all retire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as we said to better might they come:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For, lo, a somewhat, loathlier than the rest"},{"sp":"N","t":"To nostrils, ears, and eyes, and taste of tongue,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would then, by reasoning reversed, be there."},{"sp":"N","t":"Since 'tis not so, but unto things are given"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their fixed limitations which do bound"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their sum on either side, 'tmust be confessed"},{"sp":"N","t":"That matter, too, by finite tale of shapes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Does differ. Again, from earth's midsummer heats"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the icy hoar-frosts of the year"},{"sp":"N","t":"The forward path is fixed, and by like law"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'ertravelled backwards at the dawn of spring."},{"sp":"N","t":"For each degree of hot, and each of cold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the half-warm, all filling up the sum"},{"sp":"N","t":"In due progression, lie, my Memmius, there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Betwixt the two extremes: the things create"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must differ, therefore, by a finite change,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since at each end marked off they ever are"},{"sp":"N","t":"By fixed point—on one side plagued by flames"},{"sp":"N","t":"And on the other by congealing frosts."},{"sp":"N","t":"The which now having taught, I will go on","st":"2.522"},{"sp":"N","t":"To bind thereto a fact to this allied"},{"sp":"N","t":"And drawing from this its proof: those primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which have been fashioned all of one like shape"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are infinite in tale; for, since the forms"},{"sp":"N","t":"Themselves are finite in divergences,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then those which are alike will have to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Infinite, else the sum of stuff remains"},{"sp":"N","t":"A finite—what I've proved is not the fact,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Showing in verse how corpuscles of stuff,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From everlasting and to-day the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Uphold the sum of things, all sides around"},{"sp":"N","t":"By old succession of unending blows."},{"sp":"N","t":"For though thou view'st some beasts to be more rare,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mark'st in them a less prolific stock,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet in another region, in lands remote,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That kind abounding may make up the count;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as we mark among the four-foot kind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Snake-handed elephants, whose thousands wall"},{"sp":"N","t":"With ivory ramparts India about,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That her interiors cannot entered be-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So big her count of brutes of which we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such few examples. Or suppose, besides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"We feign some thing, one of its kind and sole"},{"sp":"N","t":"With body born, to which is nothing like"},{"sp":"N","t":"In all the lands: yet now unless shall be"},{"sp":"N","t":"An infinite count of matter out of which"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus to conceive and bring it forth to life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It cannot be created and—what's more-"},{"sp":"N","t":"It cannot take its food and get increase."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yea, if through all the world in finite tale"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be tossed the procreant bodies of one thing,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence, then, and where in what mode, by what power,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shall they to meeting come together there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In such vast ocean of matter and tumult strange?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"No means they have of joining into one."},{"sp":"N","t":"But, just as, after mighty ship-wrecks piled,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mighty main is wont to scatter wide"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rowers' banks, the ribs, the yards, the prow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The masts and swimming oars, so that afar"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along all shores of lands are seen afloat"},{"sp":"N","t":"The carven fragments of the rended poop,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Giving a lesson to mortality"},{"sp":"N","t":"To shun the ambush of the faithless main,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The violence and the guile, and trust it not"},{"sp":"N","t":"At any hour, however much may smile"},{"sp":"N","t":"The crafty enticements of the placid deep:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exactly thus, if once thou holdest true"},{"sp":"N","t":"That certain seeds are finite in their tale,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The various tides of matter, then, must needs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Scatter them flung throughout the ages all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that not ever can they join, as driven"},{"sp":"N","t":"Together into union, nor remain"},{"sp":"N","t":"In union, nor with increment can grow-"},{"sp":"N","t":"But facts in proof are manifest for each:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Things can be both begotten and increase."},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis therefore manifest that primal germs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are infinite in any class thou wilt-"},{"sp":"N","t":"From whence is furnished matter for all things."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor can those motions that bring death prevail"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forever, nor eternally entomb"},{"sp":"N","t":"The welfare of the world; nor, further, can"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those motions that give birth to things and growth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Keep them forever when created there."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus the long war, from everlasting waged,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With equal strife among the elements"},{"sp":"N","t":"Goes on and on. Now here, now there, prevail"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vital forces of the world—or fall."},{"sp":"N","t":"Mixed with the funeral is the wildered wail"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of infants coming to the shores of light:"},{"sp":"N","t":"No night a day, no dawn a night hath followed"},{"sp":"N","t":"That heard not, mingling with the small birth-cries,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wild laments, companions old of death"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the black rites."},{"sp":"N","t":"This, too, in these affairs","st":"2.581"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis fit thou hold well sealed, and keep consigned"},{"sp":"N","t":"With no forgetting brain: nothing there is"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whose nature is apparent out of hand"},{"sp":"N","t":"That of one kind of elements consists-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nothing there is that's not of mixed seed."},{"sp":"N","t":"And whatsoe'er possesses in itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"More largely many powers and properties"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shows thus that here within itself there are"},{"sp":"N","t":"The largest number of kinds and differing shapes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of elements. And, chief of all, the earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath in herself first bodies whence the springs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rolling chill waters, renew forevermore"},{"sp":"N","t":"The unmeasured main; hath whence the fires arise-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For burns in many a spot her flamed crust,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst the impetuous Aetna raves indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"From more profounder fires—and she, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath in herself the seed whence she can raise"},{"sp":"N","t":"The shining grains and gladsome trees for men;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence, also, rivers, fronds, and gladsome pastures"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can she supply for mountain-roaming beasts."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore great mother of gods, and mother of beasts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And parent of man hath she alone been named."},{"sp":"N","t":"Her hymned the old and learned bards of Greece"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Seated in chariot o'er the realms of air"},{"sp":"N","t":"To drive her team of lions, teaching thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"That the great earth hangs poised and cannot lie"},{"sp":"N","t":"Resting on other earth. Unto her car"},{"sp":"N","t":"They've yoked the wild beasts, since a progeny,"},{"sp":"N","t":"However savage, must be tamed and chid"},{"sp":"N","t":"By care of parents. They have girt about"},{"sp":"N","t":"With turret-crown the summit of her head,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since, fortressed in her goodly strongholds high,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis she sustains the cities; now, adorned"},{"sp":"N","t":"With that same token, to-day is carried forth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With solemn awe through many a mighty land,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The image of that mother, the divine."},{"sp":"N","t":"Her the wide nations, after antique rite,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do name Idaean Mother, giving her"},{"sp":"N","t":"Escort of Phrygian bands, since first, they say,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out those regions 'twas that grain began"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through all the world. To her do they assign"},{"sp":"N","t":"The Galli, the emasculate, since thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"They wish to show that men who violate"},{"sp":"N","t":"The majesty of the mother and have proved"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ingrate to parents are to be adjudged"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unfit to give unto the shores of light"},{"sp":"N","t":"A living progeny. The Galli come:"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hollow cymbals, tight-skinned tambourines"},{"sp":"N","t":"Resound around to bangings of their hands;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fierce horns threaten with a raucous bray;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The tubed pipe excites their maddened minds"},{"sp":"N","t":"In Phrygian measures; they bear before them knives,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wild emblems of their frenzy, which have power"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rabble's ingrate heads and impious hearts"},{"sp":"N","t":"To panic with terror of the goddess' might."},{"sp":"N","t":"And so, when through the mighty cities borne,"},{"sp":"N","t":"She blesses man with salutations mute,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They strew the highway of her journeyings"},{"sp":"N","t":"With coin of brass and silver, gifting her"},{"sp":"N","t":"With alms and largesse, and shower her and shade"},{"sp":"N","t":"With flowers of roses falling like the snow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the Mother and her companion-bands."},{"sp":"N","t":"Here is an armed troop, the which by Greeks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are called the Phrygian Curetes. Since"},{"sp":"N","t":"Haply among themselves they use to play"},{"sp":"N","t":"In games of arms and leap in measure round"},{"sp":"N","t":"With bloody mirth and by their nodding shake"},{"sp":"N","t":"The terrorizing crests upon their heads,"},{"sp":"N","t":"This is the armed troop that represents"},{"sp":"N","t":"The arm'd Dictaean Curetes, who, in Crete,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As runs the story, whilom did out-drown"},{"sp":"N","t":"That infant cry of Zeus, what time their band,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Young boys, in a swift dance around the boy,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To measured step beat with the brass on brass,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That Saturn might not get him for his jaws,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And give its mother an eternal wound"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along her heart. And 'tis on this account"},{"sp":"N","t":"That armed they escort the mighty Mother,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else because they signify by this"},{"sp":"N","t":"That she, the goddess, teaches men to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Eager with armed valour to defend"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their motherland, and ready to stand forth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The guard and glory of their parents' years."},{"sp":"N","t":"A tale, however beautifully wrought,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That's wide of reason by a long remove:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For all the gods must of themselves enjoy"},{"sp":"N","t":"Immortal aeons and supreme repose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Withdrawn from our affairs, detached, afar:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Immune from peril and immune from pain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Themselves abounding in riches of their own,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Needing not us, they are not touched by wrath"},{"sp":"N","t":"They are not taken by service or by gift."},{"sp":"N","t":"Truly is earth insensate for all time;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But, by obtaining germs of many things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In many a way she brings the many forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the light of sun. And here, whoso"},{"sp":"N","t":"Decides to call the ocean Neptune, or"},{"sp":"N","t":"The grain-crop Ceres, and prefers to abuse"},{"sp":"N","t":"The name of Bacchus rather than pronounce"},{"sp":"N","t":"The liquor's proper designation, him"},{"sp":"N","t":"Let us permit to go on calling earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mother of Gods, if only he will spare"},{"sp":"N","t":"To taint his soul with foul religion."},{"sp":"N","t":"So, too, the wooly flocks, and horned kine,","st":"2.660"},{"sp":"N","t":"And brood of battle-eager horses, grazing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Often together along one grassy plain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the cope of one blue sky, and slaking"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out one stream of water each its thirst,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All live their lives with face and form unlike,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Keeping the parents' nature, parents' habits,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, kind by kind, through ages they repeat."},{"sp":"N","t":"So great in any sort of herb thou wilt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So great again in any river of earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are the distinct diversities of matter."},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence, further, every creature—any one"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out them all—compounded is the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of bones, blood, veins, heat, moisture, flesh, and thews-"},{"sp":"N","t":"All differing vastly in their forms, and built"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of elements dissimilar in shape."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, all things by fire consumed ablaze,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within their frame lay up, if naught besides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At least those atoms whence derives their power"},{"sp":"N","t":"To throw forth fire and send out light from under,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To shoot the sparks and scatter embers wide."},{"sp":"N","t":"If, with like reasoning of mind, all else"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou traverse through, thou wilt discover thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"That in their frame the seeds of many things"},{"sp":"N","t":"They hide, and divers shapes of seeds contain."},{"sp":"N","t":"Further, thou markest much, to which are given"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along together colour and flavour and smell,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among which, chief, are most burnt offerings."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus must they be of divers shapes composed."},{"sp":"N","t":"A smell of scorching enters in our frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where the bright colour from the dye goes not;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And colour in one way, flavour in quite another"},{"sp":"N","t":"Works inward to our senses—so mayst see"},{"sp":"N","t":"They differ too in elemental shapes."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus unlike forms into one mass combine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And things exist by intermixed seed."},{"sp":"N","t":"But still 'tmust not be thought that in all ways"},{"sp":"N","t":"All things can be conjoined; for then wouldst view"},{"sp":"N","t":"Portents begot about thee every side:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hulks of mankind half brute astarting up,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At times big branches sprouting from man's trunk,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Limbs of a sea-beast to a land-beast knit,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And nature along the all-producing earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Feeding those dire Chimaeras breathing flame"},{"sp":"N","t":"From hideous jaws- Of which 'tis simple fact"},{"sp":"N","t":"That none have been begot; because we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"All are from fixed seed and fixed dam"},{"sp":"N","t":"Engendered and so function as to keep"},{"sp":"N","t":"Throughout their growth their own ancestral type."},{"sp":"N","t":"This happens surely by a fixed law:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For from all food-stuff, when once eaten down,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Go sundered atoms, suited to each creature,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Throughout their bodies, and, conjoining there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Produce the proper motions; but we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"How, contrariwise, nature upon the ground"},{"sp":"N","t":"Throws off those foreign to their frame; and many"},{"sp":"N","t":"With viewless bodies from their bodies fly,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By blows impelled—those impotent to join"},{"sp":"N","t":"To any part, or, when inside, to accord"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to take on the vital motions there."},{"sp":"N","t":"But think not, haply, living forms alone"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are bound by these laws: they distinguished all."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"For just as all things of creation are,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In their whole nature, each to each unlike,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So must their atoms be in shape unlike-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not since few only are fashioned of like form,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But since they all, as general rule, are not"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same as all. Nay, here in these our verses,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Elements many, common to many words,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou seest, though yet 'tis needful to confess"},{"sp":"N","t":"The words and verses differ, each from each,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Compounded out of different elements-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not since few only, as common letters, run"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through all the words, or no two words are made,"},{"sp":"N","t":"One and the other, from all like elements,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But since they all, as general rule, are not"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same as all. Thus, too, in other things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst many germs common to many things"},{"sp":"N","t":"There are, yet they, combined among themselves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can form new wholes to others quite unlike."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus fairly one may say that humankind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The grains, the gladsome trees, are all made up"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of different atoms. Further, since the seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are different, difference must there also be"},{"sp":"N","t":"In intervening spaces, thoroughfares,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Connections, weights, blows, clashings, motions, all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which not alone distinguish living forms,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But sunder earth's whole ocean from the lands,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hold all heaven from the lands away."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"ABSENCE OF SECONDARY QUALITIES"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now come, this wisdom by my sweet toil sought","st":"2.730"},{"sp":"N","t":"Look thou perceive, lest haply thou shouldst guess"},{"sp":"N","t":"That the white objects shining to thine eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are gendered of white atoms, or the black"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of a black seed; or yet believe that aught"},{"sp":"N","t":"That's steeped in any hue should take its dye"},{"sp":"N","t":"From bits of matter tinct with hue the same."},{"sp":"N","t":"For matter's bodies own no hue the least-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or like to objects or, again, unlike."},{"sp":"N","t":"But, if percase it seem to thee that mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Itself can dart no influence of its own"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into these bodies, wide thou wand'rest off."},{"sp":"N","t":"For since the blind-born, who have ne'er surveyed"},{"sp":"N","t":"The light of sun, yet recognise by touch"},{"sp":"N","t":"Things that from birth had ne'er a hue for them,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis thine to know that bodies can be brought"},{"sp":"N","t":"No less unto the ken of our minds too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though yet those bodies with no dye be smeared."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, ourselves whatever in the dark"},{"sp":"N","t":"We touch, the same we do not find to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Tinctured with any colour."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now that here"},{"sp":"N","t":"I win the argument, I next will teach"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, every colour changes, none except,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And every..."},{"sp":"N","t":"Which the primordials ought nowise to do."},{"sp":"N","t":"Since an immutable somewhat must remain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest all things utterly be brought to naught."},{"sp":"N","t":"For change of anything from out its bounds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Means instant death of that which was before."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore be mindful not to stain with colour"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds of things, lest things return for thee"},{"sp":"N","t":"All utterly to naught."},{"sp":"N","t":"But now, if seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Receive no property of colour, and yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be still endowed with variable forms"},{"sp":"N","t":"From which all kinds of colours they beget"},{"sp":"N","t":"And vary (by reason that ever it matters much"},{"sp":"N","t":"With what seeds, and in what positions joined,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what the motions that they give and get),"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forthwith most easily thou mayst devise"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why what was black of hue an hour ago"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can of a sudden like the marble gleam,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As ocean, when the high winds have upheaved"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its level plains, is changed to hoary waves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of marble whiteness: for, thou mayst declare,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That, when the thing we often see as black"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is in its matter then commixed anew,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some atoms rearranged, and some withdrawn,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And added some, 'tis seen forthwith to turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"Glowing and white. But if of azure seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Consist the level waters of the deep,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They could in nowise whiten: for however"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou shakest azure seeds, the same can never"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pass into marble hue. But, if the seeds-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which thus produce the ocean's one pure sheen-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be now with one hue, now another dyed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As oft from alien forms and divers shapes"},{"sp":"N","t":"A cube's produced all uniform in shape,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twould be but natural, even as in the cube"},{"sp":"N","t":"We see the forms to be dissimilar,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That thus we'd see in brightness of the deep"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Or in whatever one pure sheen thou wilt)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Colours diverse and all dissimilar."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, the unlike shapes don't thwart the least"},{"sp":"N","t":"The whole in being externally a cube;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But differing hues of things do block and keep"},{"sp":"N","t":"The whole from being of one resultant hue."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, too, the reason which entices us"},{"sp":"N","t":"At times to attribute colours to the seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Falls quite to pieces, since white things are not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Create from white things, nor are black from black,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But evermore they are create from things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of divers colours. Verily, the white"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will rise more readily, is sooner born"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out of no colour, than of black or aught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which stands in hostile opposition thus."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, since colours cannot be, sans light,","st":"2.795"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the primordials come not forth to light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis thine to know they are not clothed with colour-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Truly, what kind of colour could there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the viewless dark? Nay, in the light itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"A colour changes, gleaming variedly,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When smote by vertical or slanting ray."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus in the sunlight shows the down of doves"},{"sp":"N","t":"That circles, garlanding, the nape and throat:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now it is ruddy with a bright gold-bronze,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, by a strange sensation it becomes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Green-emerald blended with the coral-red."},{"sp":"N","t":"The peacock's tail, filled with the copious light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Changes its colours likewise, when it turns."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, since by some blow of light begot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without such blow these colours can't become."},{"sp":"N","t":"And since the pupil of the eye receives"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within itself one kind of blow, when said"},{"sp":"N","t":"To feel a white hue, then another kind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When feeling a black or any other hue,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And since it matters nothing with what hue"},{"sp":"N","t":"The things thou touchest be perchance endowed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But rather with what sort of shape equipped,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis thine to know the atoms need not colour,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But render forth sensations, as of touch,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That vary with their varied forms."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides,","st":"2.817"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since special shapes have not a special colour,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all formations of the primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can be of any sheen thou wilt, why, then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are not those objects which are of them made"},{"sp":"N","t":"Suffused, each kind with colours of every kind?"},{"sp":"N","t":"For then 'twere meet that ravens, as they fly,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should dartle from white pinions a white sheen,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or swans turn black from seed of black, or be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of any single varied dye thou wilt."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, the more an object's rent to bits,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The more thou see its colour fade away"},{"sp":"N","t":"Little by little till 'tis quite extinct;"},{"sp":"N","t":"As happens when the gaudy linen's picked"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shred after shred away: the purple there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Phoenician red, most brilliant of all dyes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is lost asunder, ravelled thread by thread;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence canst perceive the fragments die away"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out their colour, long ere they depart"},{"sp":"N","t":"Back to the old primordials of things."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, last, since thou concedest not all bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Send out a voice or smell, it happens thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"That not to all thou givest sounds and smells."},{"sp":"N","t":"So, too, since we behold not all with eyes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis thine to know some things there are as much"},{"sp":"N","t":"Orphaned of colour, as others without smell,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And reft of sound; and those the mind alert"},{"sp":"N","t":"No less can apprehend than it can mark"},{"sp":"N","t":"The things that lack some other qualities."},{"sp":"N","t":"But think not haply that the primal bodies","st":"2.842"},{"sp":"N","t":"Remain despoiled alone of colour: so,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are they from warmth dissevered and from cold"},{"sp":"N","t":"And from hot exhalations; and they move,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Both sterile of sound and dry of juice; and throw"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not any odour from their proper bodies."},{"sp":"N","t":"Just as, when undertaking to prepare"},{"sp":"N","t":"A liquid balm of myrrh and marjoram,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And flower of nard, which to our nostrils breathes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Odour of nectar, first of all behooves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou seek, as far as find thou may and can,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The inodorous olive-oil (which never sends"},{"sp":"N","t":"One whiff of scent to nostrils), that it may"},{"sp":"N","t":"The least debauch and ruin with sharp tang"},{"sp":"N","t":"The odorous essence with its body mixed"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in it seethed. And on the same account"},{"sp":"N","t":"The primal germs of things must not be thought"},{"sp":"N","t":"To furnish colour in begetting things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor sound, since pow'rless they to send forth aught"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out themselves, nor any flavour, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor cold, nor exhalation hot or warm."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"The rest; yet since these things are mortal all-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The pliant mortal, with a body soft;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The brittle mortal, with a crumbling frame;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The hollow with a porous-all must be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Disjoined from the primal elements,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If still we wish under the world to lay"},{"sp":"N","t":"Immortal ground-works, whereupon may rest"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sum of weal and safety, lest for thee"},{"sp":"N","t":"All things return to nothing utterly."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, too: whate'er we see possessing sense"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must yet confessedly be stablished all"},{"sp":"N","t":"From elements insensate. And those signs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So clear to all and witnessed out of hand,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do not refute this dictum nor oppose;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But rather themselves do lead us by the hand,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Compelling belief that living things are born"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of elements insensate, as I say."},{"sp":"N","t":"Sooth, we may see from out the stinking dung"},{"sp":"N","t":"Live worms spring up, when, after soaking rains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The drenched earth rots; and all things change the same:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lo, change the rivers, the fronds, the gladsome pastures"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the cattle, the cattle their nature change"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into our bodies, and from our body, oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grow strong the powers and bodies of wild beasts"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mighty-winged birds. Thus nature changes"},{"sp":"N","t":"All foods to living frames, and procreates"},{"sp":"N","t":"From them the senses of live creatures all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In manner about as she uncoils in flames"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dry logs of wood and turns them all to fire."},{"sp":"N","t":"And seest not, therefore, how it matters much"},{"sp":"N","t":"After what order are set the primal germs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And with what other germs they all are mixed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what the motions that they give and get?"},{"sp":"N","t":"But now, what is't that strikes thy sceptic mind,","st":"2.886"},{"sp":"N","t":"Constraining thee to sundry arguments"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against belief that from insensate germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sensible is gendered?- Verily,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis this: that liquids, earth, and wood, though mixed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are yet unable to gender vital sense."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, therefore, 'twill be well in these affairs"},{"sp":"N","t":"This to remember: that I have not said"},{"sp":"N","t":"Senses are born, under conditions all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From all things absolutely which create"},{"sp":"N","t":"Objects that feel; but much it matters here"},{"sp":"N","t":"Firstly, how small the seeds which thus compose"},{"sp":"N","t":"The feeling thing, then, with what shapes endowed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And lastly what they in positions be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In motions, in arrangements. Of which facts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Naught we perceive in logs of wood and clods;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And yet even these, when sodden by the rains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Give birth to wormy grubs, because the bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of matter, from their old arrangements stirred"},{"sp":"N","t":"By the new factor, then combine anew"},{"sp":"N","t":"In such a way as genders living things."},{"sp":"N","t":"Next, they who deem that feeling objects can"},{"sp":"N","t":"From feeling objects be create, and these,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In turn, from others that are wont to feel"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"When soft they make them; for all sense is linked"},{"sp":"N","t":"With flesh, and thews, and veins—and such, we see,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are fashioned soft and of a mortal frame."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet be't that these can last forever on:"},{"sp":"N","t":"They'll have the sense that's proper to a part,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else be judged to have a sense the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"As that within live creatures as a whole."},{"sp":"N","t":"But of themselves those parts can never feel,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For all the sense in every member back"},{"sp":"N","t":"To something else refers—a severed hand,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or any other member of our frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Itself alone cannot support sensation."},{"sp":"N","t":"It thus remains they must resemble, then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Live creatures as a whole, to have the power"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of feeling sensation concordant in each part"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the vital sense; and so they're bound to feel"},{"sp":"N","t":"The things we feel exactly as do we."},{"sp":"N","t":"If such the case, how, then, can they be named"},{"sp":"N","t":"The primal germs of things, and how avoid"},{"sp":"N","t":"The highways of destruction?- since they be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mere living things and living things be all"},{"sp":"N","t":"One and the same with mortal. Grant they could,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet by their meetings and their unions all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Naught would result, indeed, besides a throng"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hurly-burly all of living things-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Precisely as men, and cattle, and wild beasts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By mere conglomeration each with each"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can still beget not anything of new."},{"sp":"N","t":"But if by chance they lose, inside a body,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their own sense and another sense take on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What, then, avails it to assign them that"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which is withdrawn thereafter? And besides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To touch on proof that we pronounced before,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Just as we see the eggs of feathered fowls"},{"sp":"N","t":"To change to living chicks, and swarming worms"},{"sp":"N","t":"To bubble forth when from the soaking rains"},{"sp":"N","t":"The earth is sodden, sure, sensations all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can out of non-sensations be begot."},{"sp":"N","t":"But if one say that sense can so far rise","st":"2.931"},{"sp":"N","t":"From non-sense by mutation, or because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Brought forth as by a certain sort of birth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twill serve to render plain to him and prove"},{"sp":"N","t":"There is no birth, unless there be before"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some formed union of the elements,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor any change, unless they be unite."},{"sp":"N","t":"In first place, senses can't in body be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before its living nature's been begot,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since all its stuff, in faith, is held dispersed"},{"sp":"N","t":"About through rivers, air, and earth, and all"},{"sp":"N","t":"That is from earth created, nor has met"},{"sp":"N","t":"In combination, and, in proper mode,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Conjoined into those vital motions which"},{"sp":"N","t":"Kindle the all-perceiving senses—they"},{"sp":"N","t":"That keep and guard each living thing soever."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, a blow beyond its nature's strength"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shatters forthwith each living thing soe'er,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And on it goes confounding all the sense"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of body and mind. For of the primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are loosed their old arrangements, and, throughout,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vital motions blocked,—until the stuff,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shaken profoundly through the frame entire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Undoes the vital knots of soul from body"},{"sp":"N","t":"And throws that soul, to outward wide-dispersed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through all the pores. For what may we surmise"},{"sp":"N","t":"A blow inflicted can achieve besides"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shaking asunder and loosening all apart?"},{"sp":"N","t":"It happens also, when less sharp the blow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vital motions which are left are wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"Oft to win out—win out, and stop and still"},{"sp":"N","t":"The uncouth tumults gendered by the blow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And call each part to its own courses back,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And shake away the motion of death which now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Begins its own dominion in the body,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And kindle anew the senses almost gone."},{"sp":"N","t":"For by what other means could they the more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Collect their powers of thought and turn again"},{"sp":"N","t":"From very doorways of destruction"},{"sp":"N","t":"Back unto life, rather than pass whereto"},{"sp":"N","t":"They be already well-nigh sped and so"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pass quite away?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, since pain is there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where bodies of matter, by some force stirred up,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through vitals and through joints, within their seats"},{"sp":"N","t":"Quiver and quake inside, but soft delight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When they remove unto their place again:"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis thine to know the primal germs can be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Assaulted by no pain, nor from themselves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take no delight; because indeed they are"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not made of any bodies of first things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under whose strange new motions they might ache"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or pluck the fruit of any dear new sweet."},{"sp":"N","t":"And so they must be furnished with no sense."},{"sp":"N","t":"Once more, if thus, that every living thing","st":"2.973"},{"sp":"N","t":"May have sensation, needful 'tis to assign"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sense also to its elements, what then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of those fixed elements from which mankind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath been, by their peculiar virtue, formed?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of verity, they'll laugh aloud, like men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shaken asunder by a spasm of mirth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or sprinkle with dewy tear-drops cheeks and chins,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And have the cunning hardihood to say"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much on the composition of the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in their turn inquire what elements"},{"sp":"N","t":"They have themselves,—since, thus the same in kind"},{"sp":"N","t":"As a whole mortal creature, even they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must also be from other elements,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then those others from others evermore-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that thou darest nowhere make a stop."},{"sp":"N","t":"Oho, I'll follow thee until thou grant"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seed (which here thou say'st speaks, laughs, and thinks)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is yet derived out of other seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which in their turn are doing just the same."},{"sp":"N","t":"But if we see what raving nonsense this,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that a man may laugh, though not, forsooth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Compounded out of laughing elements,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And think and utter reason with learn'd speech,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though not himself compounded, for a fact,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of sapient seeds and eloquent, why, then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cannot those things which we perceive to have"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their own sensation be composed as well"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of intermixed seeds quite void of sense?"},{"sp":"SEC","t":"INFINITE WORLDS"},{"sp":"N","t":"Once more, we all from seed celestial spring,","st":"2.991"},{"sp":"N","t":"To all is that same father, from whom earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fostering mother, as she takes the drops"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of liquid moisture, pregnant bears her broods-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The shining grains, and gladsome shrubs and trees,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And bears the human race and of the wild"},{"sp":"N","t":"The generations all, the while she yields"},{"sp":"N","t":"The foods wherewith all feed their frames and lead"},{"sp":"N","t":"The genial life and propagate their kind;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore she owneth that maternal name,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By old desert. What was before from earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same in earth sinks back, and what was sent"},{"sp":"N","t":"From shores of ether, that, returning home,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vaults of sky receive. Nor thus doth death"},{"sp":"N","t":"So far annihilate things that she destroys"},{"sp":"N","t":"The bodies of matter; but she dissipates"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their combinations, and conjoins anew"},{"sp":"N","t":"One element with others; and contrives"},{"sp":"N","t":"That all things vary forms and change their colours"},{"sp":"N","t":"And get sensations and straight give them o'er."},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus may'st know it matters with what others"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in what structure the primordial germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are held together, and what motions they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among themselves do give and get; nor think"},{"sp":"N","t":"That aught we see hither and thither afloat"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the crest of things, and now a birth"},{"sp":"N","t":"And straightway now a ruin, inheres at rest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deep in the eternal atoms of the world."},{"sp":"N","t":"Why, even in these our very verses here"},{"sp":"N","t":"It matters much with what and in what order"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each element is set: the same denote"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sky, and the ocean, lands, and streams, and sun;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same, the grains, and trees, and living things."},{"sp":"N","t":"And if not all alike, at least the most-"},{"sp":"N","t":"But what distinctions by positions wrought!"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus no less in things themselves, when once"},{"sp":"N","t":"Around are changed the intervals between,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The paths of matter, its connections, weights,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Blows, clashings, motions, order, structure, shapes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The things themselves must likewise changed be."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now to true reason give thy mind for us."},{"sp":"N","t":"Since here strange truth is putting forth its might"},{"sp":"N","t":"To hit thee in thine ears, a new aspect"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of things to show its front. Yet naught there is"},{"sp":"N","t":"So easy that it standeth not at first"},{"sp":"N","t":"More hard to credit than it after is;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And naught soe'er that's great to such degree,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor wonderful so far, but all mankind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Little by little abandon their surprise."},{"sp":"N","t":"Look upward yonder at the bright clear sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what it holds—the stars that wander o'er,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The moon, the radiance of the splendour-sun:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet all, if now they first for mortals were,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If unforeseen now first asudden shown,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What might there be more wonderful to tell,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What that the nations would before have dared"},{"sp":"N","t":"Less to believe might be?- I fancy, naught-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So strange had been the marvel of that sight."},{"sp":"N","t":"The which o'erwearied to behold, to-day"},{"sp":"N","t":"None deigns look upward to those lucent realms."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, spew not reason from thy mind away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beside thyself because the matter's new,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But rather with keen judgment nicely weigh;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And if to thee it then appeareth true,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Render thy hands, or, if 'tis false at last,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gird thee to combat. For my mind-of-man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now seeks the nature of the vast Beyond"},{"sp":"N","t":"There on the other side, that boundless sum"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which lies without the ramparts of the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Toward which the spirit longs to peer afar,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Toward which indeed the swift elan of thought"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flies unencumbered forth."},{"sp":"N","t":"Firstly, we find,","st":"2.1048"},{"sp":"N","t":"Off to all regions round, on either side,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Above, beneath, throughout the universe"},{"sp":"N","t":"End is there none—as I have taught, as too"},{"sp":"N","t":"The very thing of itself declares aloud,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And as from nature of the unbottomed deep"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shines clearly forth. Nor can we once suppose"},{"sp":"N","t":"In any way 'tis likely, (seeing that space"},{"sp":"N","t":"To all sides stretches infinite and free,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And seeds, innumerable in number, in sum"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bottomless, there in many a manner fly,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bestirred in everlasting motion there),"},{"sp":"N","t":"That only this one earth and sky of ours"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath been create and that those bodies of stuff,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So many, perform no work outside the same;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seeing, moreover, this world too hath been"},{"sp":"N","t":"By nature fashioned, even as seeds of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"By innate motion chanced to clash and cling-"},{"sp":"N","t":"After they'd been in many a manner driven"},{"sp":"N","t":"Together at random, without design, in vain-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And as at last those seeds together dwelt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, when together of a sudden thrown,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should alway furnish the commencements fit"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of mighty things—the earth, the sea, the sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And race of living creatures. Thus, I say,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, again, 'tmust be confessed there are"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such congregations of matter otherwhere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like this our world which vasty ether holds"},{"sp":"N","t":"In huge embrace."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, when matter abundant"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is ready there, when space on hand, nor object"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor any cause retards, no marvel 'tis"},{"sp":"N","t":"That things are carried on and made complete,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perforce. And now, if store of seeds there is"},{"sp":"N","t":"So great that not whole life-times of the living"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can count the tale..."},{"sp":"N","t":"And if their force and nature abide the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Able to throw the seeds of things together"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into their places, even as here are thrown"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds together in this world of ours,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tmust be confessed in other realms there are"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still other worlds, still other breeds of men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And other generations of the wild."},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence too it happens in the sum there is"},{"sp":"N","t":"No one thing single of its kind in birth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And single and sole in growth, but rather it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"One member of some generated race,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among full many others of like kind."},{"sp":"N","t":"First, cast thy mind abroad upon the living:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou'lt find the race of mountain-ranging wild"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even thus to be, and thus the scions of men"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be begot, and lastly the mute flocks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of scaled fish, and winged frames of birds."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore confess we must on grounds the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"That earth, sun, moon, and ocean, and all else,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exist not sole and single—rather in number"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exceeding number. Since that deeply set"},{"sp":"N","t":"Old boundary stone of life remains for them"},{"sp":"N","t":"No less, and theirs a body of mortal birth"},{"sp":"N","t":"No less, than every kind which here on earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is so abundant in its members found."},{"sp":"N","t":"Which well perceived if thou hold in mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then Nature, delivered from every haughty lord,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And forthwith free, is seen to do all things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Herself and through herself of own accord,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rid of all gods. For—by their holy hearts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which pass in long tranquillity of peace"},{"sp":"N","t":"Untroubled ages and a serene life!-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who hath the power (I ask), who hath the power"},{"sp":"N","t":"To rule the sum of the immeasurable,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To hold with steady hand the giant reins"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the unfathomed deep? Who hath the power"},{"sp":"N","t":"At once to roll a multitude of skies,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At once to heat with fires ethereal all"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fruitful lands of multitudes of worlds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be at all times in all places near,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To stablish darkness by his clouds, to shake"},{"sp":"N","t":"The serene spaces of the sky with sound,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hurl his lightnings,—ha, and whelm how oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"In ruins his own temples, and to rave,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Retiring to the wildernesses, there"},{"sp":"N","t":"At practice with that thunderbolt of his,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which yet how often shoots the guilty by,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And slays the honourable blameless ones!"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ere since the birth-time of the world, ere since","st":"2.1105"},{"sp":"N","t":"The risen first-born day of sea, earth, sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have many germs been added from outside,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have many seeds been added round about,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which the great All, the while it flung them on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Brought hither, that from them the sea and lands"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could grow more big, and that the house of heaven"},{"sp":"N","t":"Might get more room and raise its lofty roofs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Far over earth, and air arise around."},{"sp":"N","t":"For bodies all, from out all regions, are"},{"sp":"N","t":"Divided by blows, each to its proper thing,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all retire to their own proper kinds:"},{"sp":"N","t":"The moist to moist retires; earth gets increase"},{"sp":"N","t":"From earthy body; and fires, as on a forge,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beat out new fire; and ether forges ether;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Till nature, author and ender of the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath led all things to extreme bound of growth:"},{"sp":"N","t":"As haps when that which hath been poured inside"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vital veins of life is now no more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than that which ebbs within them and runs off."},{"sp":"N","t":"This is the point where life for each thing ends;"},{"sp":"N","t":"This is the point where nature with her powers"},{"sp":"N","t":"Curbs all increase. For whatsoe'er thou seest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grow big with glad increase, and step by step"},{"sp":"N","t":"Climb upward to ripe age, these to themselves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take in more bodies than they send from selves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst still the food is easily infused"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through all the veins, and whilst the things are not"},{"sp":"N","t":"So far expanded that they cast away"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such numerous atoms as to cause a waste"},{"sp":"N","t":"Greater than nutriment whereby they wax."},{"sp":"N","t":"For 'tmust be granted, truly, that from things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Many a body ebbeth and runs off;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But yet still more must come, until the things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have touched development's top pinnacle;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then old age breaks their powers and ripe strength"},{"sp":"N","t":"And falls away into a worser part."},{"sp":"N","t":"For ever the ampler and more wide a thing,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As soon as ever its augmentation ends,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It scatters abroad forthwith to all sides round"},{"sp":"N","t":"More bodies, sending them from out itself."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor easily now is food disseminate"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through all its veins; nor is that food enough"},{"sp":"N","t":"To equal with a new supply on hand"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those plenteous exhalations it gives off."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, fairly, all things perish, when with ebbing"},{"sp":"N","t":"They're made less dense and when from blows without"},{"sp":"N","t":"They are laid low; since food at last will fail"},{"sp":"N","t":"Extremest eld, and bodies from outside"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cease not with thumping to undo a thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"And overmaster by infesting blows."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, too, the ramparts of the mighty world","st":"2.1144"},{"sp":"N","t":"On all sides round shall taken be by storm,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And tumble to wrack and shivered fragments down."},{"sp":"N","t":"For food it is must keep things whole, renewing;"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis food must prop and give support to all,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"But to no purpose, since nor veins suffice"},{"sp":"N","t":"To hold enough, nor nature ministers"},{"sp":"N","t":"As much as needful. And even now 'tis thus:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its age is broken and the earth, outworn"},{"sp":"N","t":"With many parturitions, scarce creates"},{"sp":"N","t":"The little lives—she who created erst"},{"sp":"N","t":"All generations and gave forth at birth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enormous bodies of wild beasts of old."},{"sp":"N","t":"For never, I fancy, did a golden cord"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off the firmament above let down"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mortal generations to the fields;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor sea, nor breakers pounding on the rocks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Created them; but earth it was who bore-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same to-day who feeds them from herself."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, herself of own accord, she first"},{"sp":"N","t":"The shining grains and vineyards of all joy"},{"sp":"N","t":"Created for mortality; herself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gave the sweet fruitage and the pastures glad,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which now to-day yet scarcely wax in size,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even when aided by our toiling arms."},{"sp":"N","t":"We break the ox, and wear away the strength"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of sturdy farm-hands; iron tools to-day"},{"sp":"N","t":"Barely avail for tilling of the fields,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So niggardly they grudge our harvestings,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So much increase our labour. Now to-day"},{"sp":"N","t":"The aged ploughman, shaking of his head,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sighs o'er and o'er that labours of his hands"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have fallen out in vain, and, as he thinks"},{"sp":"N","t":"How present times are not as times of old,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Often he praises the fortunes of his sire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And crackles, prating, how the ancient race,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fulfilled with piety, supported life"},{"sp":"N","t":"With simple comfort in a narrow plot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since, man for man, the measure of each field"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was smaller far i' the old days. And, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The gloomy planter of the withered vine"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rails at the season's change and wearies heaven,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor grasps that all of things by sure degrees"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are wasting away and going to the tomb,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outworn by venerable length of life."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Book III"},{"sp":"SEC","t":"PROEM"},{"sp":"N","t":"O thou who first uplifted in such dark","st":"3.1"},{"sp":"N","t":"So clear a torch aloft, who first shed light"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the profitable ends of man,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O thee I follow, glory of the Greeks,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And set my footsteps squarely planted now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even in the impress and the marks of thine-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Less like one eager to dispute the palm,"},{"sp":"N","t":"More as one craving out of very love"},{"sp":"N","t":"That I may copy thee!- for how should swallow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Contend with swans or what compare could be"},{"sp":"N","t":"In a race between young kids with tumbling legs"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the strong might of the horse? Our father thou,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And finder-out of truth, and thou to us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Suppliest a father's precepts; and from out"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those scriven leaves of thine, renowned soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Like bees that sip of all in flowery wolds),"},{"sp":"N","t":"We feed upon thy golden sayings all-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Golden, and ever worthiest endless life."},{"sp":"N","t":"For soon as ever thy planning thought that sprang"},{"sp":"N","t":"From god-like mind begins its loud proclaim"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of nature's courses, terrors of the brain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Asunder flee, the ramparts of the world"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dispart away, and through the void entire"},{"sp":"N","t":"I see the movements of the universe."},{"sp":"N","t":"Rises to vision the majesty of gods,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And their abodes of everlasting calm"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which neither wind may shake nor rain-cloud splash,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor snow, congealed by sharp frosts, may harm"},{"sp":"N","t":"With its white downfall: ever, unclouded sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'er roofs, and laughs with far-diffused light."},{"sp":"N","t":"And nature gives to them their all, nor aught"},{"sp":"N","t":"May ever pluck their peace of mind away."},{"sp":"N","t":"But nowhere to my vision rise no more"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vaults of Acheron, though the broad earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bars me no more from gazing down o'er all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which under our feet is going on below"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the void. O, here in these affairs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some new divine delight and trembling awe"},{"sp":"N","t":"Takes hold through me, that thus by power of thine"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nature, so plain and manifest at last,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath been on every side laid bare to man!"},{"sp":"N","t":"And since I've taught already of what sort"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds of all things are, and how, distinct"},{"sp":"N","t":"In divers forms, they flit of own accord,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Stirred with a motion everlasting on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in what mode things be from them create,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, after such matters, should my verse, meseems,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Make clear the nature of the mind and soul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And drive that dread of Acheron without,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Headlong, which so confounds our human life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto its deeps, pouring o'er all that is"},{"sp":"N","t":"The black of death, nor leaves not anything"},{"sp":"N","t":"To prosper—a liquid and unsullied joy."},{"sp":"N","t":"For as to what men sometimes will affirm:","st":"3.41"},{"sp":"N","t":"That more than Tartarus (the realm of death)"},{"sp":"N","t":"They fear diseases and a life of shame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And know the substance of the soul is blood,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or rather wind (if haply thus their whim),"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so need naught of this our science, then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou well may'st note from what's to follow now"},{"sp":"N","t":"That more for glory do they braggart forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than for belief. For mark these very same:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exiles from country, fugitives afar"},{"sp":"N","t":"From sight of men, with charges foul attaint,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Abased with every wretchedness, they yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"Live, and where'er the wretches come, they yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"Make the ancestral sacrifices there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Butcher the black sheep, and to gods below"},{"sp":"N","t":"Offer the honours, and in bitter case"},{"sp":"N","t":"Turn much more keenly to religion."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, it's surer testing of a man"},{"sp":"N","t":"In doubtful perils—mark him as he is"},{"sp":"N","t":"Amid adversities; for then alone"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are the true voices conjured from his breast,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mask off-stripped, reality behind."},{"sp":"N","t":"And greed, again, and the blind lust of honours"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which force poor wretches past the bounds of law,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, oft allies and ministers of crime,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To push through nights and days with hugest toil"},{"sp":"N","t":"To rise untrammelled to the peaks of power-"},{"sp":"N","t":"These wounds of life in no mean part are kept"},{"sp":"N","t":"Festering and open by this fright of death."},{"sp":"N","t":"For ever we see fierce Want and foul Disgrace"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dislodged afar from secure life and sweet,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like huddling Shapes before the doors of death."},{"sp":"N","t":"And whilst, from these, men wish to scape afar,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Driven by false terror, and afar remove,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With civic blood a fortune they amass,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They double their riches, greedy, heapers-up"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of corpse on corpse they have a cruel laugh"},{"sp":"N","t":"For the sad burial of a brother-born,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hatred and fear of tables of their kin."},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise, through this same terror, envy oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Makes them to peak because before their eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"That man is lordly, that man gazed upon"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who walks begirt with honour glorious,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst they in filth and darkness roll around;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some perish away for statues and a name,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And oft to that degree, from fright of death,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will hate of living and beholding light"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take hold on humankind that they inflict"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their own destruction with a gloomy heart-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forgetful that this fear is font of cares,"},{"sp":"N","t":"This fear the plague upon their sense of shame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And this that breaks the ties of comradry"},{"sp":"N","t":"And oversets all reverence and faith,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mid direst slaughter. For long ere to-day"},{"sp":"N","t":"Often were traitors to country and dear parents"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through quest to shun the realms of Acheron."},{"sp":"N","t":"For just as children tremble and fear all"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the viewless dark, so even we at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dread in the light so many things that be"},{"sp":"N","t":"No whit more fearsome than what children feign,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shuddering, will be upon them in the dark."},{"sp":"N","t":"This terror, then, this darkness of the mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not sunrise with its flaring spokes of light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor glittering arrows of morning sun disperse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But only nature's aspect and her law."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"NATURE AND COMPOSITION OF THE MIND"},{"sp":"N","t":"First, then, I say, the mind which oft we call","st":"3.94"},{"sp":"N","t":"The intellect, wherein is seated life's"},{"sp":"N","t":"Counsel and regimen, is part no less"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of man than hand and foot and eyes are parts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of one whole breathing creature. [But some hold]"},{"sp":"N","t":"That sense of mind is in no fixed part seated,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But is of body some one vital state,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Named \"harmony\" by Greeks, because thereby"},{"sp":"N","t":"We live with sense, though intellect be not"},{"sp":"N","t":"In any part: as oft the body is said"},{"sp":"N","t":"To have good health (when health, however, 's not"},{"sp":"N","t":"One part of him who has it), so they place"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sense of mind in no fixed part of man."},{"sp":"N","t":"Mightily, diversly, meseems they err."},{"sp":"N","t":"Often the body palpable and seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sickens, while yet in some invisible part"},{"sp":"N","t":"We feel a pleasure; oft the other way,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A miserable in mind feels pleasure still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Throughout his body—quite the same as when"},{"sp":"N","t":"A foot may pain without a pain in head."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, when these our limbs are given o'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"To gentle sleep and lies the burdened frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"At random void of sense, a something else"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is yet within us, which upon that time"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bestirs itself in many a wise, receiving"},{"sp":"N","t":"All motions of joy and phantom cares of heart."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, for to see that in man's members dwells"},{"sp":"N","t":"Also the soul, and body ne'er is wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"To feel sensation by a \"harmony\""},{"sp":"N","t":"Take this in chief: the fact that life remains"},{"sp":"N","t":"Oft in our limbs, when much of body's gone;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet that same life, when particles of heat,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though few, have scattered been, and through the mouth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Air has been given forth abroad, forthwith"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forever deserts the veins, and leaves the bones."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus mayst thou know that not all particles"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perform like parts, nor in like manner all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are props of weal and safety: rather those-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds of wind and exhalations warm-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take care that in our members life remains."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore a vital heat and wind there is"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the very body, which at death"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deserts our frames. And so, since nature of mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"And even of soul is found to be, as 'twere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A part of man, give over \"harmony\"-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Name to musicians brought from Helicon,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unless themselves they filched it otherwise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To serve for what was lacking name till then."},{"sp":"N","t":"Whate'er it be, they're welcome to it—thou,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hearken my other maxims."},{"sp":"N","t":"Mind and soul,","st":"3.136"},{"sp":"N","t":"I say, are held conjoined one with other,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And form one single nature of themselves;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But chief and regnant through the frame entire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is still that counsel which we call the mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that cleaves seated in the midmost breast."},{"sp":"N","t":"Here leap dismay and terror; round these haunts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be blandishments of joys; and therefore here"},{"sp":"N","t":"The intellect, the mind. The rest of soul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Throughout the body scattered, but obeys-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Moved by the nod and motion of the mind."},{"sp":"N","t":"This, for itself, sole through itself, hath thought;"},{"sp":"N","t":"This for itself hath mirth, even when the thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"That moves it, moves nor soul nor body at all."},{"sp":"N","t":"And as, when head or eye in us is smit"},{"sp":"N","t":"By assailing pain, we are not tortured then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through all the body, so the mind alone"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is sometimes smitten, or livens with a joy,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst yet the soul's remainder through the limbs"},{"sp":"N","t":"And through the frame is stirred by nothing new."},{"sp":"N","t":"But when the mind is moved by shock more fierce,"},{"sp":"N","t":"We mark the whole soul suffering all at once"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along man's members: sweats and pallors spread"},{"sp":"N","t":"Over the body, and the tongue is broken,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fails the voice away, and ring the ears,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mists blind the eyeballs, and the joints collapse,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aye, men drop dead from terror of the mind."},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence, whoso will can readily remark"},{"sp":"N","t":"That soul conjoined is with mind, and, when"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis strook by influence of the mind, forthwith"},{"sp":"N","t":"In turn it hits and drives the body too."},{"sp":"N","t":"And this same argument establisheth"},{"sp":"N","t":"That nature of mind and soul corporeal is:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For when 'tis seen to drive the members on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To snatch from sleep the body, and to change"},{"sp":"N","t":"The countenance, and the whole state of man"},{"sp":"N","t":"To rule and turn,—what yet could never be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sans contact, and sans body contact fails-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must we not grant that mind and soul consist"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of a corporeal nature?- And besides"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou markst that likewise with this body of ours"},{"sp":"N","t":"Suffers the mind and with our body feels."},{"sp":"N","t":"If the dire speed of spear that cleaves the bones"},{"sp":"N","t":"And bares the inner thews hits not the life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet follows a fainting and a foul collapse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, on the ground, dazed tumult in the mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And whiles a wavering will to rise afoot."},{"sp":"N","t":"So nature of mind must be corporeal, since"},{"sp":"N","t":"From stroke and spear corporeal 'tis in throes."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, of what body, what components formed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is this same mind I will go on to tell."},{"sp":"N","t":"First, I aver, 'tis superfine, composed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of tiniest particles—that such the fact"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou canst perceive, if thou attend, from this:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nothing is seen to happen with such speed","st":"3.182"},{"sp":"N","t":"As what the mind proposes and begins;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore the same bestirs itself more swiftly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than aught whose nature's palpable to eyes."},{"sp":"N","t":"But what's so agile must of seeds consist"},{"sp":"N","t":"Most round, most tiny, that they may be moved,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When hit by impulse slight. So water moves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In waves along, at impulse just the least-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Being create of little shapes that roll;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But, contrariwise, the quality of honey"},{"sp":"N","t":"More stable is, its liquids more inert,"},{"sp":"N","t":"More tardy its flow; for all its stock of matter"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cleaves more together, since, indeed, 'tis made"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of atoms not so smooth, so fine, and round."},{"sp":"N","t":"For the light breeze that hovers yet can blow"},{"sp":"N","t":"High heaps of poppy-seed away for thee"},{"sp":"N","t":"Downward from off the top; but, contrariwise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A pile of stones or spiny ears of wheat"},{"sp":"N","t":"It can't at all. Thus, in so far as bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are small and smooth, is their mobility;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But, contrariwise, the heavier and more rough,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The more immovable they prove. Now, then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since nature of mind is movable so much,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Consist it must of seeds exceeding small"},{"sp":"N","t":"And smooth and round. Which fact once known to thee,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Good friend, will serve thee opportune in else."},{"sp":"N","t":"This also shows the nature of the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How nice its texture, in how small a space"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twould go, if once compacted as a pellet:"},{"sp":"N","t":"When death's unvexed repose gets hold on man"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mind and soul retire, thou markest there"},{"sp":"N","t":"From the whole body nothing ta'en in form,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nothing in weight. Death grants ye everything,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But vital sense and exhalation hot."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus soul entire must be of smallmost seeds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Twined through the veins, the vitals, and the thews,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seeing that, when 'tis from whole body gone,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The outward figuration of the limbs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is unimpaired and weight fails not a whit."},{"sp":"N","t":"Just so, when vanished the bouquet of wine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or when an unguent's perfume delicate"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the winds away departs, or when"},{"sp":"N","t":"From any body savour's gone, yet still"},{"sp":"N","t":"The thing itself seems minished naught to eyes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thereby, nor aught abstracted from its weight-"},{"sp":"N","t":"No marvel, because seeds many and minute"},{"sp":"N","t":"Produce the savours and the redolence"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the whole body of the things."},{"sp":"N","t":"And so,","st":"3.228"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, again, nature of mind and soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis thine to know created is of seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"The tiniest ever, since at flying-forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"It beareth nothing of the weight away."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet fancy not its nature simple so."},{"sp":"N","t":"For an impalpable aura, mixed with heat,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deserts the dying, and heat draws off the air;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And heat there's none, unless commixed with air:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For, since the nature of all heat is rare,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Athrough it many seeds of air must move."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus nature of mind is triple; yet those all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Suffice not for creating sense—since mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Accepteth not that aught of these can cause"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sense-bearing motions, and much less the thoughts"},{"sp":"N","t":"A man revolves in mind. So unto these"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must added be a somewhat, and a fourth;"},{"sp":"N","t":"That somewhat's altogether void of name;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than which existeth naught more mobile, naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"More an impalpable, of elements"},{"sp":"N","t":"More small and smooth and round. That first transmits"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sense-bearing motions through the frame, for that"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is roused the first, composed of little shapes;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thence heat and viewless force of wind take up"},{"sp":"N","t":"The motions, and thence air, and thence all things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are put in motion; the blood is strook, and then"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vitals all begin to feel, and last"},{"sp":"N","t":"To bones and marrow the sensation comes-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pleasure or torment. Nor will pain for naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enter so far, nor a sharp ill seep through,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But all things be perturbed to that degree"},{"sp":"N","t":"That room for life will fail, and parts of soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will scatter through the body's every pore."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet as a rule, almost upon the skin"},{"sp":"N","t":"These motion aIl are stopped, and this is why"},{"sp":"N","t":"We have the power to retain our life."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now in my eagerness to tell thee how"},{"sp":"N","t":"They are commixed, through what unions fit"},{"sp":"N","t":"They function so, my country's pauper-speech"},{"sp":"N","t":"Constrains me sadly. As I can, however,"},{"sp":"N","t":"I'll touch some points and pass."},{"sp":"N","t":"In such a wise","st":"3.262"},{"sp":"N","t":"Course these primordials 'mongst one another"},{"sp":"N","t":"With inter-motions that no one can be"},{"sp":"N","t":"From other sundered, nor its agency"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perform, if once divided by a space;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like many powers in one body they work."},{"sp":"N","t":"As in the flesh of any creature still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is odour and savour and a certain warmth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And yet from all of these one bulk of body"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is made complete, so, viewless force of wind"},{"sp":"N","t":"And warmth and air, commingled, do create"},{"sp":"N","t":"One nature, by that mobile energy"},{"sp":"N","t":"Assisted which from out itself to them"},{"sp":"N","t":"Imparts initial motion, whereby first"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sense-bearing motion along the vitals springs."},{"sp":"N","t":"For lurks this essence far and deep and under,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor in our body is aught more shut from view,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And 'tis the very soul of all the soul."},{"sp":"N","t":"And as within our members and whole frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"The energy of mind and power of soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is mixed and latent, since create it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of bodies small and few, so lurks this fourth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"This essence void of name, composed of small,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And seems the very soul of all the soul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And holds dominion o'er the body all."},{"sp":"N","t":"And by like reason wind and air and heat"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must function so, commingled through the frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And now the one subside and now another"},{"sp":"N","t":"In interchange of dominance, that thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"From all of them one nature be produced,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest heat and wind apart, and air apart,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Make sense to perish, by disseverment."},{"sp":"N","t":"There is indeed in mind that heat it gets","st":"3.288"},{"sp":"N","t":"When seething in rage, and flashes from the eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"More swiftly fire; there is, again, that wind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much, and so cold, companion of all dread,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which rouses the shudder in the shaken frame;"},{"sp":"N","t":"There is no less that state of air composed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Making the tranquil breast, the serene face."},{"sp":"N","t":"But more of hot have they whose restive hearts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whose minds of passion quickly seethe in rage-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of which kind chief are fierce abounding lions,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who often with roaring burst the breast o'erwrought,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unable to hold the surging wrath within;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But the cold mind of stags has more of wind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And speedier through their inwards rouses up"},{"sp":"N","t":"The icy currents which make their members quake."},{"sp":"N","t":"But more the oxen live by tranquil air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor e'er doth smoky torch of wrath applied,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'erspreading with shadows of a darkling murk,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rouse them too far; nor will they stiffen stark,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pierced through by icy javelins of fear;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But have their place half-way between the two-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Stags and fierce lions. Thus the race of men:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though training make them equally refined,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It leaves those pristine vestiges behind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of each mind's nature. Nor may we suppose"},{"sp":"N","t":"Evil can e'er be rooted up so far"},{"sp":"N","t":"That one man's not more given to fits of wrath,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Another's not more quickly touched by fear,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A third not more long-suffering than he should."},{"sp":"N","t":"And needs must differ in many things besides"},{"sp":"N","t":"The varied natures and resulting habits"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of humankind—of which not now can I"},{"sp":"N","t":"Expound the hidden causes, nor find names"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enough for all the divers shapes of those"},{"sp":"N","t":"Primordials whence this variation springs."},{"sp":"N","t":"But this meseems I'm able to declare:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those vestiges of natures left behind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which reason cannot quite expel from us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are still so slight that naught prevents a man"},{"sp":"N","t":"From living a life even worthy of the gods."},{"sp":"N","t":"So then this soul is kept by all the body,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Itself the body's guard, and source of weal:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For they with common roots cleave each to each,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor can be torn asunder without death."},{"sp":"N","t":"Not easy 'tis from lumps of frankincense"},{"sp":"N","t":"To tear their fragrance forth, without its nature"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perishing likewise: so, not easy 'tis"},{"sp":"N","t":"From all the body nature of mind and soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"To draw away, without the whole dissolved."},{"sp":"N","t":"With seeds so intertwined even from birth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They're dowered conjointly with a partner-life;"},{"sp":"N","t":"No energy of body or mind, apart,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each of itself without the other's power,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can have sensation; but our sense, enkindled"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the vitals, to flame is blown by both"},{"sp":"N","t":"With mutual motions. Besides the body alone"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is nor begot nor grows, nor after death"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seen to endure. For not as water at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gives off the alien heat, nor is thereby"},{"sp":"N","t":"Itself destroyed, but unimpaired remains-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not thus, I say, can the deserted frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bear the dissevering of its joined soul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But, rent and ruined, moulders all away."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus the joint contact of the body and soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Learns from their earliest age the vital motions,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even when still buried in the mother's womb;"},{"sp":"N","t":"So no dissevering can hap to them,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without their bane and ill. And thence mayst see"},{"sp":"N","t":"That, as conjoined is their source of weal,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Conjoined also must their nature be."},{"sp":"N","t":"If one, moreover, denies that body feel,","st":"3.350"},{"sp":"N","t":"And holds that soul, through all the body mixed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Takes on this motion which we title \"sense,\""},{"sp":"N","t":"He battles in vain indubitable facts:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For who'll explain what body's feeling is,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Except by what the public fact itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Has given and taught us? \"But when soul is parted,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Body's without all sense.\" True!- loses what"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was even in its life-time not its own;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And much beside it loses, when soul's driven"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forth from that life-time. Or, to say that eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Themselves can see no thing, but through the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mind looks forth, as out of opened doors,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is—a hard saying; since the feel in eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Says the reverse. For this itself draws on"},{"sp":"N","t":"And forces into the pupils of our eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Our consciousness. And note the case when often"},{"sp":"N","t":"We lack the power to see refulgent things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because our eyes are hampered by their light-"},{"sp":"N","t":"With a mere doorway this would happen not;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For, since it is our very selves that see,"},{"sp":"N","t":"No open portals undertake the toil."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, if eyes of ours but act as doors,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Methinks that, were our sight removed, the mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ought then still better to behold a thing-"},{"sp":"N","t":"When even the door-posts have been cleared away."},{"sp":"N","t":"Herein in these affairs nowise take up"},{"sp":"N","t":"What honoured sage, Democritus, lays down-"},{"sp":"N","t":"That proposition, that primordials"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of body and mind, each super-posed on each,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Vary alternately and interweave"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fabric of our members. For not only"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are the soul-elements smaller far than those"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which this our body and inward parts compose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But also are they in their number less,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And scattered sparsely through our frame. And thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"This canst thou guarantee: soul's primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Maintain between them intervals as large"},{"sp":"N","t":"At least as are the smallest bodies, which,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When thrown against us, in our body rouse"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sense-bearing motions."},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence it comes that we","st":"3.381"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sometimes don't feel alighting on our frames"},{"sp":"N","t":"The clinging dust, or chalk that settles soft;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor mists of night, nor spider's gossamer"},{"sp":"N","t":"We feel against us, when, upon our road,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its net entangles us, nor on our head"},{"sp":"N","t":"The dropping of its withered garmentings;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor bird-feathers, nor vegetable down,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flying about, so light they barely fall;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor feel the steps of every crawling thing,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor each of all those footprints on our skin"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of midges and the like. To that degree"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must many primal germs be stirred in us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ere once the seeds of soul that through our frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are intermingled 'gin to feel that those"},{"sp":"N","t":"Primordials of the body have been strook,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And ere, in pounding with such gaps between,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They clash, combine and leap apart in turn."},{"sp":"N","t":"But mind is more the keeper of the gates,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath more dominion over life than soul."},{"sp":"N","t":"For without intellect and mind there's not"},{"sp":"N","t":"One part of soul can rest within our frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Least part of time; companioning, it goes"},{"sp":"N","t":"With mind into the winds away, and leaves"},{"sp":"N","t":"The icy members in the cold of death."},{"sp":"N","t":"But he whose mind and intellect abide"},{"sp":"N","t":"Himself abides in life. However much"},{"sp":"N","t":"The trunk be mangled, with the limbs lopped off,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The soul withdrawn and taken from the limbs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still lives the trunk and draws the vital air."},{"sp":"N","t":"Even when deprived of all but all the soul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet will it linger on and cleave to life,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Just as the power of vision still is strong,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If but the pupil shall abide unharmed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even when the eye around it's sorely rent-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Provided only thou destroyest not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wholly the ball, but, cutting round the pupil,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Leavest that pupil by itself behind-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For more would ruin sight. But if that centre,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That tiny part of eye, be eaten through,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forthwith the vision fails and darkness comes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though in all else the unblemished ball be clear."},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis by like compact that the soul and mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are each to other bound forevermore."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"THE SOUL IS MORTAL"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now come: that thou mayst able be to know","st":"3.417"},{"sp":"N","t":"That minds and the light souls of all that live"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have mortal birth and death, I will go on"},{"sp":"N","t":"Verses to build meet for thy rule of life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sought after long, discovered with sweet toil."},{"sp":"N","t":"But under one name I'd have thee yoke them both;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And when, for instance, I shall speak of soul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Teaching the same to be but mortal, think"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thereby I'm speaking also of the mind-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since both are one, a substance inter-joined."},{"sp":"N","t":"First, then, since I have taught how soul exists"},{"sp":"N","t":"A subtle fabric, of particles minute,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Made up from atoms smaller much than those"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of water's liquid damp, or fog, or smoke,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So in mobility it far excels,"},{"sp":"N","t":"More prone to move, though strook by lighter cause"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even moved by images of smoke or fog-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As where we view, when in our sleeps we're lulled,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The altars exhaling steam and smoke aloft-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For, beyond doubt, these apparitions come"},{"sp":"N","t":"To us from outward. Now, then, since thou seest,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their liquids depart, their waters flow away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When jars are shivered, and since fog and smoke"},{"sp":"N","t":"Depart into the winds away, believe"},{"sp":"N","t":"The soul no less is shed abroad and dies"},{"sp":"N","t":"More quickly far, more quickly is dissolved"},{"sp":"N","t":"Back to its primal bodies, when withdrawn"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out man's members it has gone away."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, sure, if body (container of the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like as a jar), when shivered from some cause,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And rarefied by loss of blood from veins,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cannot for longer hold the soul, how then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thinkst thou it can be held by any air-"},{"sp":"N","t":"A stuff much rarer than our bodies be?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides we feel that mind to being comes","st":"3.445"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along with body, with body grows and ages."},{"sp":"N","t":"For just as children totter round about"},{"sp":"N","t":"With frames infirm and tender, so there follows"},{"sp":"N","t":"A weakling wisdom in their minds; and then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where years have ripened into robust powers,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Counsel is also greater, more increased"},{"sp":"N","t":"The power of mind; thereafter, where already"},{"sp":"N","t":"The body's shattered by master-powers of eld,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fallen the frame with its enfeebled powers,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thought hobbles, tongue wanders, and the mind gives way;"},{"sp":"N","t":"All fails, all's lacking at the selfsame time."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore it suits that even the soul's dissolved,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like smoke, into the lofty winds of air;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since we behold the same to being come"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along with body and grow, and, as I've taught,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Crumble and crack, therewith outworn by eld."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, too, we see, that, just as body takes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Monstrous diseases and the dreadful pain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So mind its bitter cares, the grief, the fear;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore it tallies that the mind no less"},{"sp":"N","t":"Partaker is of death; for pain and disease"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are both artificers of death,—as well"},{"sp":"N","t":"We've learned by the passing of many a man ere now."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nay, too, in diseases of body, often the mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wanders afield; for 'tis beside itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And crazed it speaks, or many a time it sinks,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With eyelids closing and a drooping nod,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In heavy drowse, on to eternal sleep;"},{"sp":"N","t":"From whence nor hears it any voices more,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor able is to know the faces here"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of those about him standing with wet cheeks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who vainly call him back to light and life."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore mind too, confess we must, dissolves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seeing, indeed, contagions of disease"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enter into the same. Again, O why,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When the strong wine has entered into man,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And its diffused fire gone round the veins,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why follows then a heaviness of limbs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A tangle of the legs as round he reels,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A stuttering tongue, an intellect besoaked,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Eyes all aswim, and hiccups, shouts, and brawls,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And whatso else is of that ilk?- Why this?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"If not that violent and impetuous wine"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is wont to confound the soul within the body?"},{"sp":"N","t":"But whatso can confounded be and balked,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gives proof, that if a hardier cause got in,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twould hap that it would perish then, bereaved"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of any life thereafter."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, moreover,","st":"3.487"},{"sp":"N","t":"Often will some one in a sudden fit,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As if by stroke of lightning, tumble down"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before our eyes, and sputter foam, and grunt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Blither, and twist about with sinews taut,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gasp up in starts, and weary out his limbs"},{"sp":"N","t":"With tossing round. No marvel, since distract"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through frame by violence of disease."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Confounds, he foams, as if to vomit soul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As on the salt sea boil the billows round"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the master might of winds. And now"},{"sp":"N","t":"A groan's forced out, because his limbs are griped,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But, in the main, because the seeds of voice"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are driven forth and carried in a mass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outwards by mouth, where they are wont to go,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And have a builded highway. He becomes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mere fool, since energy of mind and soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Confounded is, and, as I've shown, to-riven,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Asunder thrown, and torn to pieces all"},{"sp":"N","t":"By the same venom. But, again, where cause"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of that disease has faced about, and back"},{"sp":"N","t":"Retreats sharp poison of corrupted frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into its shadowy lairs, the man at first"},{"sp":"N","t":"Arises reeling, and gradually comes back"},{"sp":"N","t":"To all his senses and recovers soul."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, since within the body itself of man"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mind and soul are by such great diseases"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shaken, so miserably in labour distraught,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why, then, believe that in the open air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without a body, they can pass their life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Immortal, battling with the master winds?"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, since we mark the mind itself is cured,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like the sick body, and restored can be"},{"sp":"N","t":"By medicine, this is forewarning too"},{"sp":"N","t":"That mortal lives the mind. For proper it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"That whosoe'er begins and undertakes"},{"sp":"N","t":"To alter the mind, or meditates to change"},{"sp":"N","t":"Any another nature soever, should add"},{"sp":"N","t":"New parts, or readjust the order given,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or from the sum remove at least a bit."},{"sp":"N","t":"But what's immortal willeth for itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its parts be nor increased, nor rearranged,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor any bit soever flow away:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For change of anything from out its bounds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Means instant death of that which was before."},{"sp":"N","t":"Ergo, the mind, whether in sickness fallen,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or by the medicine restored, gives signs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As I have taught, of its mortality."},{"sp":"N","t":"So surely will a fact of truth make head"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Gainst errors' theories all, and so shut off"},{"sp":"N","t":"All refuge from the adversary, and rout"},{"sp":"N","t":"Error by two-edged confutation."},{"sp":"N","t":"And since the mind is of a man one part,","st":"3.548"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which in one fixed place remains, like ears,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And eyes, and every sense which pilots life;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And just as hand, or eye, or nose, apart,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Severed from us, can neither feel nor be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But in the least of time is left to rot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus mind alone can never be, without"},{"sp":"N","t":"The body and the man himself, which seems,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As 'twere the vessel of the same—or aught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whate'er thou'lt feign as yet more closely joined:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since body cleaves to mind by surest bonds."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, the body's and the mind's live powers"},{"sp":"N","t":"Only in union prosper and enjoy;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For neither can nature of mind, alone of self"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sans body, give the vital motions forth;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor, then, can body, wanting soul, endure"},{"sp":"N","t":"And use the senses. Verily, as the eye,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alone, up-rended from its roots, apart"},{"sp":"N","t":"From all the body, can peer about at naught,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So soul and mind it seems are nothing able,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When by themselves. No marvel, because, commixed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through veins and inwards, and through bones and thews,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their elements primordial are confined"},{"sp":"N","t":"By all the body, and own no power free"},{"sp":"N","t":"To bound around through interspaces big,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, shut within these confines, they take on"},{"sp":"N","t":"Motions of sense, which, after death, thrown out"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beyond the body to the winds of air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take on they cannot—and on this account,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because no more in such a way confined."},{"sp":"N","t":"For air will be a body, be alive,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If in that air the soul can keep itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in that air enclose those motions all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which in the thews and in the body itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"A while ago 'twas making. So for this,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, again, I say confess we must,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That, when the body's wrappings are unwound,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And when the vital breath is forced without,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The soul, the senses of the mind dissolve,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since for the twain the cause and ground of life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is in the fact of their conjoined estate."},{"sp":"N","t":"Once more, since body's unable to sustain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Division from the soul, without decay"},{"sp":"N","t":"And obscene stench, how canst thou doubt but that"},{"sp":"N","t":"The soul, uprisen from the body's deeps,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Has filtered away, wide-drifted like a smoke,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or that the changed body crumbling fell"},{"sp":"N","t":"With ruin so entire, because, indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its deep foundations have been moved from place,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The soul out-filtering even through the frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And through the body's every winding way"},{"sp":"N","t":"And orifice? And so by many means"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou'rt free to learn that nature of the soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath passed in fragments out along the frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that 'twas shivered in the very body"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ere ever it slipped abroad and swam away"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the winds of air."},{"sp":"N","t":"For never a man","st":"3.592"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dying appears to feel the soul go forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"As one sure whole from all his body at once,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor first come up the throat and into mouth;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But feels it failing in a certain spot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as he knows the senses too dissolve"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each in its own location in the frame."},{"sp":"N","t":"But were this mind of ours immortal mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dying 'twould scarce bewail a dissolution,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But rather the going, the leaving of its coat,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like to a snake. Wherefore, when once the body"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath passed away, admit we must that soul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shivered in all that body, perished too."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nay, even when moving in the bounds of life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Often the soul, now tottering from some cause,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Craves to go out, and from the frame entire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Loosened to be; the countenance becomes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flaccid, as if the supreme hour were there;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And flabbily collapse the members all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against the bloodless trunk—the kind of case"},{"sp":"N","t":"We see when we remark in common phrase,"},{"sp":"N","t":"\"That man's quite gone,\" or \"fainted dead away\";"},{"sp":"N","t":"And where there's now a bustle of alarm,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all are eager to get some hold upon"},{"sp":"N","t":"The man's last link of life. For then the mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all the power of soul are shook so sore,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And these so totter along with all the frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That any cause a little stronger might"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dissolve them altogether.- Why, then, doubt"},{"sp":"N","t":"That soul, when once without the body thrust,"},{"sp":"N","t":"There in the open, an enfeebled thing,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its wrappings stripped away, cannot endure"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not only through no everlasting age,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But even, indeed, through not the least of time?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, too, why never is the intellect,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The counselling mind, begotten in the head,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The feet, the hands, instead of cleaving still"},{"sp":"N","t":"To one sole seat, to one fixed haunt, the breast,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If not that fixed places be assigned"},{"sp":"N","t":"For each thing's birth, where each, when 'tis create,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is able to endure, and that our frames"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have such complex adjustments that no shift"},{"sp":"N","t":"In order of our members may appear?"},{"sp":"N","t":"To that degree effect succeeds to cause,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor is the flame once wont to be create"},{"sp":"N","t":"In flowing streams, nor cold begot in fire."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, if nature of soul immortal be,","st":"3.624"},{"sp":"N","t":"And able to feel, when from our frame disjoined,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same, I fancy, must be thought to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Endowed with senses five,—nor is there way"},{"sp":"N","t":"But this whereby to image to ourselves"},{"sp":"N","t":"How under-souls may roam in Acheron."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus painters and the elder race of bards"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have pictured souls with senses so endowed."},{"sp":"N","t":"But neither eyes, nor nose, nor hand, alone"},{"sp":"N","t":"Apart from body can exist for soul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor tongue nor ears apart. And hence indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alone by self they can nor feel nor be."},{"sp":"N","t":"And since we mark the vital sense to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the whole body, all one living thing,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If of a sudden a force with rapid stroke"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should slice it down the middle and cleave in twain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beyond a doubt likewise the soul itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Divided, dissevered, asunder will be flung"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along with body. But what severed is"},{"sp":"N","t":"And into sundry parts divides, indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Admits it owns no everlasting nature."},{"sp":"N","t":"We hear how chariots of war, areek"},{"sp":"N","t":"With hurly slaughter, lop with flashing scythes"},{"sp":"N","t":"The limbs away so suddenly that there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fallen from the trunk, they quiver on the earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The while the mind and powers of the man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can feel no pain, for swiftness of his hurt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sheer abandon in the zest of battle:"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the remainder of his frame he seeks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Anew the battle and the slaughter, nor marks"},{"sp":"N","t":"How the swift wheels and scythes of ravin have dragged"},{"sp":"N","t":"Off with the horses his left arm and shield;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor other how his right has dropped away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mounting again and on. A third attempts"},{"sp":"N","t":"With leg dismembered to arise and stand,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst, on the ground hard by, the dying foot"},{"sp":"N","t":"Twitches its spreading toes. And even the head,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When from the warm and living trunk lopped off,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Keeps on the ground the vital countenance"},{"sp":"N","t":"And open eyes, until 't has rendered up"},{"sp":"N","t":"All remnants of the soul. Nay, once again:"},{"sp":"N","t":"If, when a serpent's darting forth its tongue,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And lashing its tail, thou gettest chance to hew"},{"sp":"N","t":"With axe its length of trunk to many parts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou'lt see each severed fragment writhing round"},{"sp":"N","t":"With its fresh wound, and spattering up the sod,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And there the fore-part seeking with the jaws"},{"sp":"N","t":"After the hinder, with bite to stop the pain."},{"sp":"N","t":"So shall we say that these be souls entire"},{"sp":"N","t":"In all those fractions?- but from that 'twould follow"},{"sp":"N","t":"One creature'd have in body many souls."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore, the soul, which was indeed but one,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Has been divided with the body too:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each is but mortal, since alike is each"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hewn into many parts. Again, how often"},{"sp":"N","t":"We view our fellow going by degrees,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And losing limb by limb the vital sense;"},{"sp":"N","t":"First nails and fingers of the feet turn blue,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Next die the feet and legs, then o'er the rest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Slow crawl the certain footsteps of cold death."},{"sp":"N","t":"And since this nature of the soul is torn,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor mounts away, as at one time, entire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"We needs must hold it mortal. But perchance"},{"sp":"N","t":"If thou supposest that the soul itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can inward draw along the frame, and bring"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its parts together to one place, and so"},{"sp":"N","t":"From all the members draw the sense away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why, then, that place in which such stock of soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Collected is, should greater seem in sense."},{"sp":"N","t":"But since such place is nowhere, for a fact,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As said before, 'tis rent and scattered forth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so goes under. Or again, if now"},{"sp":"N","t":"I please to grant the false, and say that soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can thus be lumped within the frames of those"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who leave the sunshine, dying bit by bit,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still must the soul as mortal be confessed;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor aught it matters whether to wrack it go,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dispersed in the winds, or, gathered in a mass"},{"sp":"N","t":"From all its parts, sink down to brutish death,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since more and more in every region sense"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fails the whole man, and less and less of life"},{"sp":"N","t":"In every region lingers."},{"sp":"N","t":"And besides,","st":"3.670"},{"sp":"N","t":"If soul immortal is, and winds its way"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the body at the birth of man,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why can we not remember something, then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of life-time spent before? why keep we not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some footprints of the things we did of, old?"},{"sp":"N","t":"But if so changed hath been the power of mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That every recollection of things done"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is fallen away, at no o'erlong remove"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is that, I trow, from what we mean by death."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore 'tis sure that what hath been before"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath died, and what now is is now create."},{"sp":"N","t":"Moreover, if after the body hath been built"},{"sp":"N","t":"Our mind's live powers are wont to be put in,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Just at the moment that we come to birth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And cross the sills of life, 'twould scarcely fit"},{"sp":"N","t":"For them to live as if they seemed to grow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along with limbs and frame, even in the blood,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But rather as in a cavern all alone."},{"sp":"N","t":"(Yet all the body duly throngs with sense.)"},{"sp":"N","t":"But public fact declares against all this:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For soul is so entwined through the veins,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The flesh, the thews, the bones, that even the teeth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Share in sensation, as proven by dull ache,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By twinge from icy water, or grating crunch"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon a stone that got in mouth with bread."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, again, again, souls must be thought"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor void of birth, nor free from law of death;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor, if, from outward, in they wound their way,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could they be thought as able so to cleave"},{"sp":"N","t":"To these our frames, nor, since so interwove,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Appears it that they're able to go forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unhurt and whole and loose themselves unscathed"},{"sp":"N","t":"From all the thews, articulations, bones."},{"sp":"N","t":"But, if perchance thou thinkest that the soul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From outward winding in its way, is wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"To seep and soak along these members ours,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then all the more 'twill perish, being thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"With body fused—for what will seep and soak"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will be dissolved and will therefore die."},{"sp":"N","t":"For just as food, dispersed through all the pores"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of body, and passed through limbs and all the frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perishes, supplying from itself the stuff"},{"sp":"N","t":"For other nature, thus the soul and mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though whole and new into a body going,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are yet, by seeping in, dissolved away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst, as through pores, to all the frame there pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those particles from which created is"},{"sp":"N","t":"This nature of mind, now ruler of our body,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Born from that soul which perished, when divided"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the frame."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore it seems that soul","st":"3.711"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath both a natal and funeral hour."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides are seeds of soul there left behind"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the breathless body, or not? If there they are,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It cannot justly be immortal deemed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since, shorn of some parts lost, 'thas gone away:"},{"sp":"N","t":"But if, borne off with members uncorrupt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Thas fled so absolutely all away"},{"sp":"N","t":"It leaves not one remainder of itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Behind in body, whence do cadavers, then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out their putrid flesh exhale the worms,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And whence does such a mass of living things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Boneless and bloodless, o'er the bloated frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bubble and swarm? But if perchance thou thinkest"},{"sp":"N","t":"That souls from outward into worms can wind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And each into a separate body come,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And reckonest not why many thousand souls"},{"sp":"N","t":"Collect where only one has gone away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Here is a point, in sooth, that seems to need"},{"sp":"N","t":"Inquiry and a putting to the test:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whether the souls go on a hunt for seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of worms wherewith to build their dwelling places,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or enter bodies ready-made, as 'twere."},{"sp":"N","t":"But why themselves they thus should do and toil"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis hard to say, since, being free of body,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They flit around, harassed by no disease,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor cold nor famine; for the body labours"},{"sp":"N","t":"By more of kinship to these flaws of life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mind by contact with that body suffers"},{"sp":"N","t":"So many ills. But grant it be for them"},{"sp":"N","t":"However useful to construct a body"},{"sp":"N","t":"To which to enter in, 'tis plain they can't."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, souls for self no frames nor bodies make,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor is there how they once might enter in"},{"sp":"N","t":"To bodies ready-made—for they cannot"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be nicely interwoven with the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And there'll be formed no interplay of sense"},{"sp":"N","t":"Common to each."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, why is't there goes","st":"3.741"},{"sp":"N","t":"Impetuous rage with lion's breed morose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And cunning with foxes, and to deer why given"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ancestral fear and tendency to flee,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And why in short do all the rest of traits"},{"sp":"N","t":"Engender from the very start of life"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the members and mentality, if not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because one certain power of mind that came"},{"sp":"N","t":"From its own seed and breed waxes the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along with all the body? But were mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Immortal, were it wont to change its bodies,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How topsy-turvy would earth's creatures act!"},{"sp":"N","t":"The Hyrcan hound would flee the onset oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of antlered stag, the scurrying hawk would quake"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the winds of air at the coming dove,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And men would dote, and savage beasts be wise;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For false the reasoning of those that say"},{"sp":"N","t":"Immortal mind is changed by change of body-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For what is changed dissolves, and therefore dies."},{"sp":"N","t":"For parts are re-disposed and leave their order;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore they must be also capable"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of dissolution through the frame at last,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That they along with body perish all."},{"sp":"N","t":"But should some say that always souls of men"},{"sp":"N","t":"Go into human bodies, I will ask:"},{"sp":"N","t":"How can a wise become a dullard soul?"},{"sp":"N","t":"And why is never a child's a prudent soul?"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the mare's filly why not trained so well"},{"sp":"N","t":"As sturdy strength of steed? We may be sure"},{"sp":"N","t":"They'll take their refuge in the thought that mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Becomes a weakling in a weakling frame."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet be this so, 'tis needful to confess"},{"sp":"N","t":"The soul but mortal, since, so altered now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Throughout the frame, it loses the life and sense"},{"sp":"N","t":"It had before. Or how can mind wax strong"},{"sp":"N","t":"Coequally with body and attain"},{"sp":"N","t":"The craved flower of life, unless it be"},{"sp":"N","t":"The body's colleague in its origins?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or what's the purport of its going forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"From aged limbs?- fears it, perhaps, to stay,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pent in a crumbled body? Or lest its house,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outworn by venerable length of days,"},{"sp":"N","t":"May topple down upon it? But indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"For an immortal perils are there none."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, at parturitions of the wild","st":"3.776"},{"sp":"N","t":"And at the rites of Love, that souls should stand"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ready hard by seems ludicrous enough-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Immortals waiting for their mortal limbs"},{"sp":"N","t":"In numbers innumerable, contending madly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which shall be first and chief to enter in!-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unless perchance among the souls there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such treaties stablished that the first to come"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flying along, shall enter in the first,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that they make no rivalries of strength!"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, in ether can't exist a tree,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor clouds in ocean deeps, nor in the fields"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can fishes live, nor blood in timber be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor sap in boulders: fixed and arranged"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where everything may grow and have its place."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus nature of mind cannot arise alone"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without the body, nor exist afar"},{"sp":"N","t":"From thews and blood. But if 'twere possible,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much rather might this very power of mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be in the head, the shoulders or the heels,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, born in any part soever, yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the same man, in the same vessel abide."},{"sp":"N","t":"But since within this body even of ours"},{"sp":"N","t":"Stands fixed and appears arranged sure"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where soul and mind can each exist and grow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deny we must the more that they can have"},{"sp":"N","t":"Duration and birth, wholly outside the frame."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, verily, the mortal to conjoin"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the eternal, and to feign they feel"},{"sp":"N","t":"Together, and can function each with each,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is but to dote: for what can be conceived"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of more unlike, discrepant, ill-assorted,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than something mortal in a union joined"},{"sp":"N","t":"With an immortal and a secular"},{"sp":"N","t":"To bear the outrageous tempests?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whatever abides eternal must indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Either repel all strokes, because 'tis made"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of solid body, and permit no entrance"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of aught with power to sunder from within"},{"sp":"N","t":"The parts compact—as are those seeds of stuff"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whose nature we've exhibited before;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else be able to endure through time"},{"sp":"N","t":"For this: because they are from blows exempt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As is the void, the which abides untouched,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unsmit by any stroke; or else because"},{"sp":"N","t":"There is no room around, whereto things can,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As 'twere, depart in dissolution all,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as the sum of sums eternal is,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without or place beyond whereto things may"},{"sp":"N","t":"Asunder fly, or bodies which can smite,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus dissolve them by the blows of might."},{"sp":"N","t":"But if perchance the soul's to be adjudged","st":"3.819"},{"sp":"N","t":"Immortal, mainly on ground 'tis kept secure"},{"sp":"N","t":"In vital forces—either because there come"},{"sp":"N","t":"Never at all things hostile to its weal,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else because what come somehow retire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Repelled or ere we feel the harm they work,"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, lo, besides that, when the frame's diseased,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Soul sickens too, there cometh, many a time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That which torments it with the things to be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Keeps it in dread, and wearies it with cares;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And even when evil acts are of the past,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still gnaw the old transgressions bitterly."},{"sp":"N","t":"Add, too, that frenzy, peculiar to the mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that oblivion of the things that were;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Add its submergence in the murky waves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of drowse and torpor."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"FOLLY OF THE FEAR OF DEATH"},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore death to us","st":"3.830"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is nothing, nor concerns us in the least,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since nature of mind is mortal evermore."},{"sp":"N","t":"And just as in the ages gone before"},{"sp":"N","t":"We felt no touch of ill, when all sides round"},{"sp":"N","t":"To battle came the Carthaginian host,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the times, shaken by tumultuous war,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the aery coasts of arching heaven"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shuddered and trembled, and all humankind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Doubted to which the empery should fall"},{"sp":"N","t":"By land and sea, thus when we are no more,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When comes that sundering of our body and soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through which we're fashioned to a single state,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Verily naught to us, us then no more,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can come to pass, naught move our senses then-"},{"sp":"N","t":"No, not if earth confounded were with sea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sea with heaven. But if indeed do feel"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of mind and energy of soul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"After their severance from this body of ours,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet nothing 'tis to us who in the bonds"},{"sp":"N","t":"And wedlock of the soul and body live,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through which we're fashioned to a single state."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, even if time collected after death"},{"sp":"N","t":"The matter of our frames and set it all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again in place as now, and if again"},{"sp":"N","t":"To us the light of life were given, O yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"That process too would not concern us aught,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When once the self-succession of our sense"},{"sp":"N","t":"Has been asunder broken. And now and here,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Little enough we're busied with the selves"},{"sp":"N","t":"We were aforetime, nor, concerning them,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Suffer a sore distress. For shouldst thou gaze"},{"sp":"N","t":"Backwards across all yesterdays of time"},{"sp":"N","t":"The immeasurable, thinking how manifold"},{"sp":"N","t":"The motions of matter are, then couldst thou well"},{"sp":"N","t":"Credit this too: often these very seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"(From which we are to-day) of old were set"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the same order as they are to-day-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet this we can't to consciousness recall"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through the remembering mind. For there hath been"},{"sp":"N","t":"An interposed pause of life, and wide"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have all the motions wandered everywhere"},{"sp":"N","t":"From these our senses. For if woe and ail"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perchance are toward, then the man to whom"},{"sp":"N","t":"The bane can happen must himself be there"},{"sp":"N","t":"At that same time. But death precludeth this,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forbidding life to him on whom might crowd"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such irk and care; and granted 'tis to know:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nothing for us there is to dread in death,"},{"sp":"N","t":"No wretchedness for him who is no more,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same estate as if ne'er born before,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When death immortal hath ta'en the mortal life."},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence, where thou seest a man to grieve because","st":"3.870"},{"sp":"N","t":"When dead he rots with body laid away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or perishes in flames or jaws of beasts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Know well: he rings not true, and that beneath"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still works an unseen sting upon his heart,"},{"sp":"N","t":"However he deny that he believes."},{"sp":"N","t":"His shall be aught of feeling after death."},{"sp":"N","t":"For he, I fancy, grants not what he says,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor what that presupposes, and he fails"},{"sp":"N","t":"To pluck himself with all his roots from life"},{"sp":"N","t":"And cast that self away, quite unawares"},{"sp":"N","t":"Feigning that some remainder's left behind."},{"sp":"N","t":"For when in life one pictures to oneself"},{"sp":"N","t":"His body dead by beasts and vultures torn,"},{"sp":"N","t":"He pities his state, dividing not himself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefrom, removing not the self enough"},{"sp":"N","t":"From the body flung away, imagining"},{"sp":"N","t":"Himself that body, and projecting there"},{"sp":"N","t":"His own sense, as he stands beside it: hence"},{"sp":"N","t":"He grieves that he is mortal born, nor marks"},{"sp":"N","t":"That in true death there is no second self"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alive and able to sorrow for self destroyed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or stand lamenting that the self lies there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mangled or burning. For if it an evil is"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dead to be jerked about by jaw and fang"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the wild brutes, I see not why 'twere not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bitter to lie on fires and roast in flames,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or suffocate in honey, and, reclined"},{"sp":"N","t":"On the smooth oblong of an icy slab,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grow stiff in cold, or sink with load of earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down-crushing from above."},{"sp":"N","t":"\"Thee now no more","st":"3.894"},{"sp":"N","t":"The joyful house and best of wives shall welcome,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor little sons run up to snatch their kisses"},{"sp":"N","t":"And touch with silent happiness thy heart."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou shalt not speed in undertakings more,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor be the warder of thine own no more."},{"sp":"N","t":"Poor wretch,\" they say, \"one hostile hour hath ta'en"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wretchedly from thee all life's many guerdons,\""},{"sp":"N","t":"But add not, \"yet no longer unto thee"},{"sp":"N","t":"Remains a remnant of desire for them\""},{"sp":"N","t":"If this they only well perceived with mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"And followed up with maxims, they would free"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their state of man from anguish and from fear."},{"sp":"N","t":"\"O even as here thou art, aslumber in death,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So shalt thou slumber down the rest of time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Released from every harrying pang. But we,"},{"sp":"N","t":"We have bewept thee with insatiate woe,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Standing beside whilst on the awful pyre"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou wert made ashes; and no day shall take"},{"sp":"N","t":"For us the eternal sorrow from the breast.\""},{"sp":"N","t":"But ask the mourner what's the bitterness"},{"sp":"N","t":"That man should waste in an eternal grief,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If, after all, the thing's but sleep and rest?"},{"sp":"N","t":"For when the soul and frame together are sunk"},{"sp":"N","t":"In slumber, no one then demands his self"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or being. Well, this sleep may be forever,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without desire of any selfhood more,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For all it matters unto us asleep."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet not at all do those primordial germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Roam round our members, at that time, afar"},{"sp":"N","t":"From their own motions that produce our senses-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since, when he's startled from his sleep, a man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Collects his senses. Death is, then, to us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much less—if there can be a less than that"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which is itself a nothing: for there comes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hard upon death a scattering more great"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the throng of matter, and no man wakes up"},{"sp":"N","t":"On whom once falls the icy pause of life."},{"sp":"N","t":"This too, O often from the soul men say,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along their couches holding of the cups,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With faces shaded by fresh wreaths awry:"},{"sp":"N","t":"\"Brief is this fruit of joy to paltry man,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Soon, soon departed, and thereafter, no,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It may not be recalled.\"- As if, forsooth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It were their prime of evils in great death"},{"sp":"N","t":"To parch, poor tongues, with thirst and arid drought,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or chafe for any lack."},{"sp":"N","t":"Once more, if Nature","st":"3.931"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should of a sudden send a voice abroad,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And her own self inveigh against us so:"},{"sp":"N","t":"\"Mortal, what hast thou of such grave concern"},{"sp":"N","t":"That thou indulgest in too sickly plaints?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why this bemoaning and beweeping death?"},{"sp":"N","t":"For if thy life aforetime and behind"},{"sp":"N","t":"To thee was grateful, and not all thy good"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was heaped as in sieve to flow away"},{"sp":"N","t":"And perish unavailingly, why not,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even like a banqueter, depart the halls,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Laden with life? why not with mind content"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take now, thou fool, thy unafflicted rest?"},{"sp":"N","t":"But if whatever thou enjoyed hath been"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lavished and lost, and life is now offence,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why seekest more to add—which in its turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will perish foully and fall out in vain?"},{"sp":"N","t":"O why not rather make an end of life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of labour? For all I may devise or find"},{"sp":"N","t":"To pleasure thee is nothing: all things are"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same forever. Though not yet thy body"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wrinkles with years, nor yet the frame exhausts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outworn, still things abide the same, even if"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou goest on to conquer all of time"},{"sp":"N","t":"With length of days, yea, if thou never diest\"-"},{"sp":"N","t":"What were our answer, but that Nature here"},{"sp":"N","t":"Urges just suit and in her words lays down"},{"sp":"N","t":"True cause of action? Yet should one complain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Riper in years and elder, and lament,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Poor devil, his death more sorely than is fit,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then would she not, with greater right, on him"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cry out, inveighing with a voice more shrill:"},{"sp":"N","t":"\"Off with thy tears, and choke thy whines, buffoon!"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou wrinklest—after thou hast had the sum"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the guerdons of life; yet, since thou cravest ever"},{"sp":"N","t":"What's not at hand, contemning present good,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That life has slipped away, unperfected"},{"sp":"N","t":"And unavailing unto thee. And now,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or ere thou guessed it, death beside thy head"},{"sp":"N","t":"Stands—and before thou canst be going home"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sated and laden with the goodly feast."},{"sp":"N","t":"But now yield all that's alien to thine age,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Up, with good grace! make room for sons: thou must.\""},{"sp":"N","t":"Justly, I fancy, would she reason thus,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Justly inveigh and gird: since ever the old"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outcrowded by the new gives way, and ever"},{"sp":"N","t":"The one thing from the others is repaired."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor no man is consigned to the abyss"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of Tartarus, the black. For stuff must be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That thus the after-generations grow,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though these, their life completed, follow thee;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus like thee are generations all-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Already fallen, or some time to fall."},{"sp":"N","t":"So one thing from another rises ever;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in fee-simple life is given to none,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But unto all mere usufruct."},{"sp":"N","t":"Look back:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nothing to us was all fore-passed eld"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of time the eternal, ere we had a birth."},{"sp":"N","t":"And Nature holds this like a mirror up"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of time-to-be when we are dead and gone."},{"sp":"N","t":"And what is there so horrible appears?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now what is there so sad about it all?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is't not serener far than any sleep?"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, verily, those tortures said to be","st":"3.978"},{"sp":"N","t":"In Acheron, the deep, they all are ours"},{"sp":"N","t":"Here in this life. No Tantalus, benumbed"},{"sp":"N","t":"With baseless terror, as the fables tell,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fears the huge boulder hanging in the air:"},{"sp":"N","t":"But, rather, in life an empty dread of Gods"},{"sp":"N","t":"Urges mortality, and each one fears"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such fall of fortune as may chance to him."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor eat the vultures into Tityus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Prostrate in Acheron, nor can they find,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forsooth, throughout eternal ages, aught"},{"sp":"N","t":"To pry around for in that mighty breast."},{"sp":"N","t":"However hugely he extend his bulk-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who hath for outspread limbs not acres nine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But the whole earth—he shall not able be"},{"sp":"N","t":"To bear eternal pain nor furnish food"},{"sp":"N","t":"From his own frame forever. But for us"},{"sp":"N","t":"A Tityus is he whom vultures rend"},{"sp":"N","t":"Prostrate in love, whom anxious anguish eats,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whom troubles of any unappeased desires"},{"sp":"N","t":"Asunder rip. We have before our eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Here in this life also a Sisyphus"},{"sp":"N","t":"In him who seeketh of the populace"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rods, the axes fell, and evermore"},{"sp":"N","t":"Retires a beaten and a gloomy man."},{"sp":"N","t":"For to seek after power—an empty name,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor given at all—and ever in the search"},{"sp":"N","t":"To endure a world of toil, O this it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"To shove with shoulder up the hill a stone"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which yet comes rolling back from off the top,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And headlong makes for levels of the plain."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then to be always feeding an ingrate mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Filling with good things, satisfying never-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As do the seasons of the year for us,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When they return and bring their progenies"},{"sp":"N","t":"And varied charms, and we are never filled"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the fruits of life- O this, I fancy, 'tis"},{"sp":"N","t":"To pour, like those young virgins in the tale,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Waters into a sieve, unfilled forever."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Cerberus and Furies, and that Lack of Light"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Tartarus, out-belching from his mouth the surge"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of horrible heat—the which are nowhere, nor"},{"sp":"N","t":"Indeed can be: but in this life is fear"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of retributions just and expiations"},{"sp":"N","t":"For evil acts: the dungeon and the leap"},{"sp":"N","t":"From that dread rock of infamy, the stripes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The executioners, the oaken rack,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The iron plates, bitumen, and the torch."},{"sp":"N","t":"And even though these are absent, yet the mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With a fore-fearing conscience, plies its goads"},{"sp":"N","t":"And burns beneath the lash, nor sees meanwhile"},{"sp":"N","t":"What terminus of ills, what end of pine"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can ever be, and feareth lest the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"But grow more heavy after death. Of truth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The life of fools is Acheron on earth."},{"sp":"N","t":"This also to thy very self sometimes","st":"3.1024"},{"sp":"N","t":"Repeat thou mayst: \"Lo, even good Ancus left"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sunshine with his eyes, in divers things"},{"sp":"N","t":"A better man than thou, O worthless hind;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And many other kings and lords of rule"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thereafter have gone under, once who swayed"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'er mighty peoples. And he also, he-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who whilom paved a highway down the sea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And gave his legionaries thoroughfare"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the deep, and taught them how to cross"},{"sp":"N","t":"The pools of brine afoot, and did contemn,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Trampling upon it with his cavalry,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The bellowings of ocean—poured his soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"From dying body, as his light was ta'en."},{"sp":"N","t":"And Scipio's son, the thunderbolt of war,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Horror of Carthage, gave his bones to earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like to the lowliest villein in the house."},{"sp":"N","t":"Add finders-out of sciences and arts;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Add comrades of the Heliconian dames,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among whom Homer, sceptered o'er them all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now lies in slumber sunken with the rest."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, too, Democritus, when ripened eld"},{"sp":"N","t":"Admonished him his memory waned away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of own accord offered his head to death."},{"sp":"N","t":"Even Epicurus went, his light of life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Run out, the man in genius who o'er-topped"},{"sp":"N","t":"The human race, extinguishing all others,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As sun, in ether arisen, all the stars."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wilt thou, then, dally, thou complain to go?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For whom already life's as good as dead,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst yet thou livest and lookest?- who in sleep"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wastest thy life—time's major part, and snorest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even when awake, and ceasest not to see"},{"sp":"N","t":"The stuff of dreams, and bearest a mind beset"},{"sp":"N","t":"By baseless terror, nor discoverest oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"What's wrong with thee, when, like a sotted wretch,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou'rt jostled along by many crowding cares,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And wanderest reeling round, with mind aswim.\""},{"sp":"N","t":"If men, in that same way as on the mind","st":"3.1053"},{"sp":"N","t":"They feel the load that wearies with its weight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could also know the causes whence it comes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And why so great the heap of ill on heart,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O not in this sort would they live their life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As now so much we see them, knowing not"},{"sp":"N","t":"What 'tis they want, and seeking ever and ever"},{"sp":"N","t":"A change of place, as if to drop the burden."},{"sp":"N","t":"The man who sickens of his home goes out,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forth from his splendid halls, and straight—returns,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Feeling i'faith no better off abroad."},{"sp":"N","t":"He races, driving his Gallic ponies along,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down to his villa, madly,—as in haste"},{"sp":"N","t":"To hurry help to a house afire.- At once"},{"sp":"N","t":"He yawns, as soon as foot has touched the threshold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or drowsily goes off in sleep and seeks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forgetfulness, or maybe bustles about"},{"sp":"N","t":"And makes for town again. In such a way"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each human flees himself—a self in sooth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As happens, he by no means can escape;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And willy-nilly he cleaves to it and loathes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sick, sick, and guessing not the cause of ail."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet should he see but that, O chiefly then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Leaving all else, he'd study to divine"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of things, since here is in debate"},{"sp":"N","t":"Eternal time and not the single hour,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mortal's estate in whatsoever remains"},{"sp":"N","t":"After great death."},{"sp":"N","t":"And too, when all is said,","st":"3.1076"},{"sp":"N","t":"What evil lust of life is this so great"},{"sp":"N","t":"Subdues us to live, so dreadfully distraught"},{"sp":"N","t":"In perils and alarms? one fixed end"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of life abideth for mortality;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Death's not to shun, and we must go to meet."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides we're busied with the same devices,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ever and ever, and we are at them ever,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And there's no new delight that may be forged"},{"sp":"N","t":"By living on. But whilst the thing we long for"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is lacking, that seems good above all else;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thereafter, when we've touched it, something else"},{"sp":"N","t":"We long for; ever one equal thirst of life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grips us agape. And doubtful 'tis what fortune"},{"sp":"N","t":"The future times may carry, or what be"},{"sp":"N","t":"That chance may bring, or what the issue next"},{"sp":"N","t":"Awaiting us. Nor by prolonging life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take we the least away from death's own time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor can we pluck one moment off, whereby"},{"sp":"N","t":"To minish the aeons of our state of death."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore, O man, by living on, fulfil"},{"sp":"N","t":"As many generations as thou may:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Eternal death shall there be waiting still;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And he who died with light of yesterday"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shall be no briefer time in death's No-more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than he who perished months or years before."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Book IV"},{"sp":"SEC","t":"PROEM"},{"sp":"N","t":"I wander afield, thriving in sturdy thought,","st":"4.1"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through unpathed haunts of the Pierides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Trodden by step of none before. I joy"},{"sp":"N","t":"To come on undefiled fountains there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To drain them deep; I joy to pluck new flowers,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To seek for this my head a signal crown"},{"sp":"N","t":"From regions where the Muses never yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have garlanded the temples of a man:"},{"sp":"N","t":"First, since I teach concerning mighty things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And go right on to loose from round the mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"The tightened coils of dread religion;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Next, since, concerning themes so dark, I frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Song so pellucid, touching all throughout"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even with the Muses' charm—which, as 'twould seem,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is not without a reasonable ground:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For as physicians, when they seek to give"},{"sp":"N","t":"Young boys the nauseous wormwood, first do touch"},{"sp":"N","t":"The brim around the cup with the sweet juice"},{"sp":"N","t":"And yellow of the honey, in order that"},{"sp":"N","t":"The thoughtless age of boyhood be cajoled"},{"sp":"N","t":"As far as the lips, and meanwhile swallow down"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wormwood's bitter draught, and, though befooled,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be yet not merely duped, but rather thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grow strong again with recreated health:"},{"sp":"N","t":"So now I too (since this my doctrine seems"},{"sp":"N","t":"In general somewhat woeful unto those"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who've had it not in hand, and since the crowd"},{"sp":"N","t":"Starts back from it in horror) have desired"},{"sp":"N","t":"To expound our doctrine unto thee in song"},{"sp":"N","t":"Soft-speaking and Pierian, and, as 'twere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To touch it with sweet honey of the Muse-"},{"sp":"N","t":"If by such method haply I might hold"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mind of thee upon these lines of ours,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Till thou dost learn the nature of all things"},{"sp":"N","t":"And understandest their utility."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"EXISTENCE AND CHARACTER OF THE IMAGES"},{"sp":"N","t":"But since I've taught already of what sort","st":"4.26"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds of all things are, and how distinct"},{"sp":"N","t":"In divers forms they flit of own accord,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Stirred with a motion everlasting on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in what mode things be from them create,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And since I've taught what the mind's nature is,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And of what things 'tis with the body knit"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thrives in strength, and by what mode uptorn"},{"sp":"N","t":"That mind returns to its primordials,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now will I undertake an argument-"},{"sp":"N","t":"One for these matters of supreme concern-"},{"sp":"N","t":"That there exist those somewhats which we call"},{"sp":"N","t":"The images of things: these, like to films"},{"sp":"N","t":"Scaled off the utmost outside of the things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flit hither and thither through the atmosphere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the same terrify our intellects,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Coming upon us waking or in sleep,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When oft we peer at wonderful strange shapes"},{"sp":"N","t":"And images of people lorn of light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which oft have horribly roused us when we lay"},{"sp":"N","t":"In slumber—that haply nevermore may we"},{"sp":"N","t":"Suppose that souls get loose from Acheron,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or shades go floating in among the living,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or aught of us is left behind at death,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When body and mind, destroyed together, each"},{"sp":"N","t":"Back to its own primordials goes away."},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus I say that effigies of things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And tenuous shapes from off the things are sent,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off the utmost outside of the things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which are like films or may be named a rind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because the image bears like look and form"},{"sp":"N","t":"With whatso body has shed it fluttering forth-"},{"sp":"N","t":"A fact thou mayst, however dull thy wits,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Well learn from this: mainly, because we see","st":"4.54"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even 'mongst visible objects many be"},{"sp":"N","t":"That send forth bodies, loosely some diffused-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like smoke from oaken logs and heat from fires-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And some more interwoven and condensed-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As when the locusts in the summertime"},{"sp":"N","t":"Put off their glossy tunics, or when calves"},{"sp":"N","t":"At birth drop membranes from their body's surface,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or when, again, the slippery serpent doffs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its vestments 'mongst the thorns—for oft we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"The breres augmented with their flying spoils:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since such takes place, 'tis likewise certain too"},{"sp":"N","t":"That tenuous images from things are sent,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off the utmost outside of the things."},{"sp":"N","t":"For why those kinds should drop and part from things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rather than others tenuous and thin,"},{"sp":"N","t":"No power has man to open mouth to tell;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Especially, since on outsides of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are bodies many and minute which could,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the same order which they had before,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And with the figure of their form preserved,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be thrown abroad, and much more swiftly too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Being less subject to impediments,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As few in number and placed along the front."},{"sp":"N","t":"For truly many things we see discharge"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their stuff at large, not only from their cores"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deep-set within, as we have said above,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But from their surfaces at times no less-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their very colours too. And commonly"},{"sp":"N","t":"The awnings, saffron, red and dusky blue,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Stretched overhead in mighty theatres,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon their poles and cross-beams fluttering,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have such an action quite; for there they dye"},{"sp":"N","t":"And make to undulate with their every hue"},{"sp":"N","t":"The circled throng below, and all the stage,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And rich attire in the patrician seats."},{"sp":"N","t":"And ever the more the theatre's dark walls"},{"sp":"N","t":"Around them shut, the more all things within"},{"sp":"N","t":"Laugh in the bright suffusion of strange glints,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The daylight being withdrawn. And therefore, since"},{"sp":"N","t":"The canvas hangings thus discharge their dye"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off their surface, things in general must"},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise their tenuous effigies discharge,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because in either case they are off-thrown"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off the surface. So there are indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such certain prints and vestiges of forms"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which flit around, of subtlest texture made,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Invisible, when separate, each and one."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, all odour, smoke, and heat, and such","st":"4.90"},{"sp":"N","t":"Streams out of things diffusedly, because,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst coming from the deeps of body forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"And rising out, along their bending path"},{"sp":"N","t":"They're torn asunder, nor have gateways straight"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherethrough to mass themselves and struggle abroad."},{"sp":"N","t":"But contrariwise, when such a tenuous film"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of outside colour is thrown off, there's naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can rend it, since 'tis placed along the front"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ready to hand. Lastly those images"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which to our eyes in mirrors do appear,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In water, or in any shining surface,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must be, since furnished with like look of things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fashioned from images of things sent out."},{"sp":"N","t":"There are, then, tenuous effigies of forms,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like unto them, which no one can divine"},{"sp":"N","t":"When taken singly, which do yet give back,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When by continued and recurrent discharge"},{"sp":"N","t":"Expelled, a picture from the mirrors' plane."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor otherwise, it seems, can they be kept"},{"sp":"N","t":"So well conserved that thus be given back"},{"sp":"N","t":"Figures so like each object."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now then, learn","st":"4.110"},{"sp":"N","t":"How tenuous is the nature of an image."},{"sp":"N","t":"And in the first place, since primordials be"},{"sp":"N","t":"So far beneath our senses, and much less"},{"sp":"N","t":"E'en than those objects which begin to grow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Too small for eyes to note, learn now in few"},{"sp":"N","t":"How nice are the beginnings of all things-"},{"sp":"N","t":"That this, too, I may yet confirm in proof:"},{"sp":"N","t":"First, living creatures are sometimes so small"},{"sp":"N","t":"That even their third part can nowise be seen;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Judge, then, the size of any inward organ-"},{"sp":"N","t":"What of their sphered heart, their eyes, their limbs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The skeleton?- How tiny thus they are!"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what besides of those first particles"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence soul and mind must fashioned be?- Seest not"},{"sp":"N","t":"How nice and how minute? Besides, whatever"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exhales from out its body a sharp smell-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nauseous absinth, or the panacea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Strong southernwood, or bitter centaury-"},{"sp":"N","t":"If never so lightly with thy [fingers] twain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perchance [thou touch] a one of them"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then why not rather know that images"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flit hither and thither, many, in many modes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bodiless and invisible?"},{"sp":"N","t":"But lest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Haply thou holdest that those images"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which come from objects are the sole that flit,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Others indeed there be of own accord"},{"sp":"N","t":"Begot, self-formed in earth's aery skies,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, moulded to innumerable shapes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are borne aloft, and, fluid as they are,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cease not to change appearance and to turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into new outlines of all sorts of forms;"},{"sp":"N","t":"As we behold the clouds grow thick on high"},{"sp":"N","t":"And smirch the serene vision of the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Stroking the air with motions. For oft are seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"The giants' faces flying far along"},{"sp":"N","t":"And trailing a spread of shadow; and at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mighty mountains and mountain-sundered rocks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Going before and crossing on the sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereafter a monstrous beast dragging amain"},{"sp":"N","t":"And leading in the other thunderheads."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now [hear] how easy and how swift they be","st":"4.143"},{"sp":"N","t":"Engendered, and perpetually flow off"},{"sp":"N","t":"From things and gliding pass away...."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"For ever every outside streams away"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off all objects, since discharge they may;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And when this outside reaches other things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As chiefly glass, it passes through; but where"},{"sp":"N","t":"It reaches the rough rocks or stuff of wood,"},{"sp":"N","t":"There 'tis so rent that it cannot give back"},{"sp":"N","t":"An image. But when gleaming objects dense,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As chiefly mirrors, have been set before it,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nothing of this sort happens. For it can't"},{"sp":"N","t":"Go, as through glass, nor yet be rent—its safety,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By virtue of that smoothness, being sure."},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis therefore that from them the images"},{"sp":"N","t":"Stream back to us; and howso suddenly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou place, at any instant, anything"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before a mirror, there an image shows;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Proving that ever from a body's surface"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flow off thin textures and thin shapes of things."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus many images in little time"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are gendered; so their origin is named"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rightly a speedy. And even as the sun"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must send below, in little time, to earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"So many beams to keep all things so full"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of light incessant; thus, on grounds the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From things there must be borne, in many modes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To every quarter round, upon the moment,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The many images of things; because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto whatever face of things we turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mirror, things of form and hue the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"Respond. Besides, though but a moment since"},{"sp":"N","t":"Serenest was the weather of the sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So fiercely sudden is it foully thick"},{"sp":"N","t":"That ye might think that round about all murk"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had parted forth from Acheron and filled"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mighty vaults of sky—so grievously,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As gathers thus the storm-clouds' gruesome night,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do faces of black horror hang on high-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of which how small a part an image is"},{"sp":"N","t":"There's none to tell or reckon out in words."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now come; with what swift motion they are borne,","st":"4.176"},{"sp":"N","t":"These images, and what the speed assigned"},{"sp":"N","t":"To them across the breezes swimming on-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that o'er lengths of space a little hour"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alone is wasted, toward whatever region"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each with its divers impulse tends- I'll tell"},{"sp":"N","t":"In verses sweeter than they many are;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as the swan's slight note is better far"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than that dispersed clamour of the cranes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the southwind's aery clouds. And first,"},{"sp":"N","t":"One oft may see that objects which are light"},{"sp":"N","t":"And made of tiny bodies are the swift;"},{"sp":"N","t":"In which class is the sun's light and his heat,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since made from small primordial elements"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, as it were, are forward knocked along"},{"sp":"N","t":"And through the interspaces of the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"To pass delay not, urged by blows behind;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For light by light is instantly supplied"},{"sp":"N","t":"And gleam by following gleam is spurred and driven."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus likewise must the images have power"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through unimaginable space to speed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within a point of time,—first, since a cause"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exceeding small there is, which at their back"},{"sp":"N","t":"Far forward drives them and propels, where, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They're carried with such winged lightness on;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, secondly, since furnished, when sent off,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With texture of such rareness that they can"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through objects whatsoever penetrate"},{"sp":"N","t":"And ooze, as 'twere, through intervening air."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, if those fine particles of things","st":"4.199"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which from so deep within are sent abroad,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As light and heat of sun, are seen to glide"},{"sp":"N","t":"And spread themselves through all the space of heaven"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon one instant of the day, and fly"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'er sea and lands and flood the heaven, what then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of those which on the outside stand prepared,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When they're hurled off with not a thing to check"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their going out? Dost thou not see indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"How swifter and how farther must they go"},{"sp":"N","t":"And speed through manifold the length of space"},{"sp":"N","t":"In time the same that from the sun the rays"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'erspread the heaven? This also seems to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Example chief and true with what swift speed"},{"sp":"N","t":"The images of things are borne about:"},{"sp":"N","t":"That soon as ever under open skies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is spread the shining water, all at once,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If stars be out in heaven, upgleam from earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Serene and radiant in the water there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The constellations of the universe-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now seest thou not in what a point of time"},{"sp":"N","t":"An image from the shores of ether falls"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the shores of earth? Wherefore, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And yet again, 'tis needful to confess"},{"sp":"N","t":"With wondrous..."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"THE SENSES AND MENTAL PICTURES"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bodies that strike the eyes, awaking sight.","st":"4.217"},{"sp":"N","t":"From certain things flow odours evermore,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As cold from rivers, heat from sun, and spray"},{"sp":"N","t":"From waves of ocean, eater-out of walls"},{"sp":"N","t":"Around the coasts. Nor ever cease to flit"},{"sp":"N","t":"The varied voices, sounds athrough the air."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then too there comes into the mouth at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wet of a salt taste, when by the sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"We roam about; and so, whene'er we watch"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wormword being mixed, its bitter stings."},{"sp":"N","t":"To such degree from all things is each thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Borne streamingly along, and sent about"},{"sp":"N","t":"To every region round; and nature grants"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor rest nor respite of the onward flow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since 'tis incessantly we feeling have,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all the time are suffered to descry"},{"sp":"N","t":"And smell all things at hand, and hear them sound."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, since shape examined by our hands","st":"4.230"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the dark is known to be the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"As that by eyes perceived within the light"},{"sp":"N","t":"And lustrous day, both touch and sight must be"},{"sp":"N","t":"By one like cause aroused. So, if we test"},{"sp":"N","t":"A square and get its stimulus on us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the dark, within the light what square"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can fall upon our sight, except a square"},{"sp":"N","t":"That images the things? Wherefore it seems"},{"sp":"N","t":"The source of seeing is in images,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor without these can anything be viewed."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now these same films I name are borne about"},{"sp":"N","t":"And tossed and scattered into regions all."},{"sp":"N","t":"But since we do perceive alone through eyes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It follows hence that whitherso we turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"Our sight, all things do strike against it there"},{"sp":"N","t":"With form and hue. And just how far from us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each thing may be away, the image yields"},{"sp":"N","t":"To us the power to see and chance to tell:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For when 'tis sent, at once it shoves ahead"},{"sp":"N","t":"And drives along the air that's in the space"},{"sp":"N","t":"Betwixt it and our eyes. And thus this air"},{"sp":"N","t":"All glides athrough our eyeballs, and, as 'twere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Brushes athrough our pupils and thuswise"},{"sp":"N","t":"Passes across. Therefore it comes we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"How far from us each thing may be away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the more air there be that's driven before,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And too the longer be the brushing breeze"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against our eyes, the farther off removed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each thing is seen to be: forsooth, this work"},{"sp":"N","t":"With mightily swift order all goes on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that upon one instant we may see"},{"sp":"N","t":"What kind the object and how far away."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor over-marvellous must this be deemed"},{"sp":"N","t":"In these affairs that, though the films which strike"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the eyes cannot be singly seen,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The things themselves may be perceived. For thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"When the wind beats upon us stroke by stroke"},{"sp":"N","t":"And when the sharp cold streams, 'tis not our wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"To feel each private particle of wind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or of that cold, but rather all at once;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so we see how blows affect our body,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As if one thing were beating on the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"And giving us the feel of its own body"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outside of us. Again, whene'er we thump"},{"sp":"N","t":"With finger-tip upon a stone, we touch"},{"sp":"N","t":"But the rock's surface and the outer hue,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor feel that hue by contact—rather feel"},{"sp":"N","t":"The very hardness deep within the rock."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now come, and why beyond a looking-glass","st":"4.269"},{"sp":"N","t":"An image may be seen, perceive. For seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"It soothly is, removed far within."},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis the same sort as objects peered upon"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outside in their true shape, whene'er a door"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yields through itself an open peering-place,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And lets us see so many things outside"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beyond the house. Also that sight is made"},{"sp":"N","t":"By a twofold twin air: for first is seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"The air inside the door-posts; next the doors,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The twain to left and right; and afterwards"},{"sp":"N","t":"A light beyond comes brushing through our eyes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then other air, then objects peered upon"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outside in their true shape. And thus, when first"},{"sp":"N","t":"The image of the glass projects itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As to our gaze it comes, it shoves ahead"},{"sp":"N","t":"And drives along the air that's in the space"},{"sp":"N","t":"Betwixt it and our eyes, and brings to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"That we perceive the air ere yet the glass."},{"sp":"N","t":"But when we've also seen the glass itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forthwith that image which from us is borne"},{"sp":"N","t":"Reaches the glass, and there thrown back again"},{"sp":"N","t":"Comes back unto our eyes, and driving rolls"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ahead of itself another air, that then"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis this we see before itself, and thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"It looks so far removed behind the glass."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore again, again, there's naught for wonder"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"In those which render from the mirror's plane"},{"sp":"N","t":"A vision back, since each thing comes to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"By means of the two airs. Now, in the glass"},{"sp":"N","t":"The right part of our members is observed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the left, because, when comes the image"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hitting against the level of the glass,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis not returned unshifted; but forced off"},{"sp":"N","t":"Backwards in line direct and not oblique,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exactly as whoso his plaster-mask"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should dash, before 'twere dry, on post or beam,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And it should straightway keep, at clinging there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its shape, reversed, facing him who threw,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so remould the features it gives back:"},{"sp":"N","t":"It comes that now the right eye is the left,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The left the right."},{"sp":"N","t":"An image too may be","st":"4.302"},{"sp":"N","t":"From mirror into mirror handed on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Until of idol-films even five or six"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have thus been gendered. For whatever things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shall hide back yonder in the house, the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"However far removed in twisting ways,"},{"sp":"N","t":"May still be all brought forth through bending paths"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by these several mirrors seen to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the house, since nature so compels"},{"sp":"N","t":"All things to be borne backward and spring off"},{"sp":"N","t":"At equal angles from all other things."},{"sp":"N","t":"To such degree the image gleams across"},{"sp":"N","t":"From mirror unto mirror; where 'twas left"},{"sp":"N","t":"It comes to be the right, and then again"},{"sp":"N","t":"Returns and changes round unto the left."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, those little sides of mirrors curved"},{"sp":"N","t":"Proportionate to the bulge of our own flank"},{"sp":"N","t":"Send back to us their idols with the right"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the right; and this is so because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Either the image is passed on along"},{"sp":"N","t":"From mirror unto mirror, and thereafter,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When twice dashed off, flies back unto ourselves;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else the image wheels itself around,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When once unto the mirror it has come,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since the curved surface teaches it to turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"To usward. Further, thou might'st well believe"},{"sp":"N","t":"That these film-idols step along with us"},{"sp":"N","t":"And set their feet in unison with ours"},{"sp":"N","t":"And imitate our carriage, since from that"},{"sp":"N","t":"Part of a mirror whence thou hast withdrawn"},{"sp":"N","t":"Straightway no images can be returned."},{"sp":"N","t":"Further, our eye-balls tend to flee the bright"},{"sp":"N","t":"And shun to gaze thereon; the sun even blinds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If thou goest on to strain them unto him,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because his strength is mighty, and the films"},{"sp":"N","t":"Heavily downward from on high are borne"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through the pure ether and the viewless winds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And strike the eyes, disordering their joints."},{"sp":"N","t":"So piecing lustre often burns the eyes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because it holdeth many seeds of fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, working into eyes, engender pain."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, whatever jaundiced people view"},{"sp":"N","t":"Becomes wan-yellow, since from out their bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flow many seeds wan-yellow forth to meet"},{"sp":"N","t":"The films of things, and many too are mixed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within their eye, which by contagion paint"},{"sp":"N","t":"All things with sallowness."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, we view","st":"4.337"},{"sp":"N","t":"From dark recesses things that stand in light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because, when first has entered and possessed"},{"sp":"N","t":"The open eyes this nearer darkling air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Swiftly the shining air and luminous"},{"sp":"N","t":"Followeth in, which purges then the eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"And scatters asunder of that other air"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sable shadows, for in large degrees"},{"sp":"N","t":"This air is nimbler, nicer, and more strong."},{"sp":"N","t":"And soon as ever 'thas filled and oped with light"},{"sp":"N","t":"The pathways of the eyeballs, which before"},{"sp":"N","t":"Black air had blocked, there follow straightaway"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those films of things out-standing in the light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Provoking vision—what we cannot do"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out the light with objects in the dark,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because that denser darkling air behind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Followeth in, and fills each aperture"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus blockades the pathways of the eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"That there no images of any things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can be thrown in and agitate the eyes."},{"sp":"N","t":"And when from far away we do behold"},{"sp":"N","t":"The squared towers of a city, oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rounded they seem,—on this account because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each distant angle is perceived obtuse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or rather it is not perceived at all;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And perishes its blow nor to our gaze"},{"sp":"N","t":"Arrives its stroke, since through such length of air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are borne along the idols that the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Makes blunt the idol of the angle's point"},{"sp":"N","t":"By numerous collidings. When thuswise"},{"sp":"N","t":"The angles of the tower each and all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have quite escaped the sense, the stones appear"},{"sp":"N","t":"As rubbed and rounded on a turner's wheel-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet not like objects near and truly round,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But with a semblance to them, shadowily."},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise, our shadow in the sun appears"},{"sp":"N","t":"To move along and follow our own steps"},{"sp":"N","t":"And imitate our carriage—if thou thinkest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Air that is thus bereft of light can walk,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Following the gait and motion of mankind."},{"sp":"N","t":"For what we use to name a shadow, sure"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is naught but air deprived of light. No marvel:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because the earth from spot to spot is reft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Progressively of light of sun, whenever"},{"sp":"N","t":"In moving round we get within its way,"},{"sp":"N","t":"While any spot of earth by us abandoned"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is filled with light again, on this account"},{"sp":"N","t":"It comes to pass that what was body's shadow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seems still the same to follow after us"},{"sp":"N","t":"In one straight course. Since, evermore pour in"},{"sp":"N","t":"New lights of rays, and perish then the old,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Just like the wool that's drawn into the flame."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore the earth is easily spoiled of light"},{"sp":"N","t":"And easily refilled and from herself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Washeth the black shadows quite away."},{"sp":"N","t":"And yet in this we don't at all concede","st":"4.379"},{"sp":"N","t":"That eyes be cheated. For their task it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"To note in whatsoever place be light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In what be shadow: whether or no the gleams"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be still the same, and whether the shadow which"},{"sp":"N","t":"Just now was here is that one passing thither,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or whether the facts be what we said above,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis after all the reasoning of mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"That must decide; nor can our eyeballs know"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of reality. And so"},{"sp":"N","t":"Attach thou not this fault of mind to eyes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor lightly think our senses everywhere"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are tottering. The ship in which we sail"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is borne along, although it seems to stand;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ship that bides in roadstead is supposed"},{"sp":"N","t":"There to be passing by. And hills and fields"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seem fleeing fast astern, past which we urge"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ship and fly under the bellying sails."},{"sp":"N","t":"The stars, each one, do seem to pause, affixed"},{"sp":"N","t":"To the ethereal caverns, though they all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forever are in motion, rising out"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thence revisiting their far descents"},{"sp":"N","t":"When they have measured with their bodies bright"},{"sp":"N","t":"The span of heaven. And likewise sun and moon"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seem biding in a roadstead,—objects which,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As plain fact proves, are really borne along."},{"sp":"N","t":"Between two mountains far away aloft"},{"sp":"N","t":"From midst the whirl of waters open lies"},{"sp":"N","t":"A gaping exit for the fleet, and yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"They seem conjoined in a single isle."},{"sp":"N","t":"When boys themselves have stopped their spinning round,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The halls still seem to whirl and posts to reel,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Until they now must almost think the roofs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Threaten to ruin down upon their heads."},{"sp":"N","t":"And now, when nature begins to lift on high"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sun's red splendour and the tremulous fires,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And raise him o'er the mountain-tops, those mountains-"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'er which he seemeth then to thee to be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"His glowing self hard by atingeing them"},{"sp":"N","t":"With his own fire—are yet away from us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Scarcely two thousand arrow-shots, indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Oft scarce five hundred courses of a dart;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Although between those mountains and the sun"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lie the huge plains of ocean spread beneath"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vasty shores of ether, and intervene"},{"sp":"N","t":"A thousand lands, possessed by many a folk"},{"sp":"N","t":"And generations of wild beasts. Again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A pool of water of but a finger's depth,","st":"4.414"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which lies between the stones along the pave,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Offers a vision downward into earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"As far, as from the earth o'erspread on high"},{"sp":"N","t":"The gulfs of heaven; that thus thou seemest to view"},{"sp":"N","t":"Clouds down below and heavenly bodies plunged"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wondrously in heaven under earth."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then too, when in the middle of the stream"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sticks fast our dashing horse, and down we gaze"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the river's rapid waves, some force"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seems then to bear the body of the horse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though standing still, reversely from his course,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And swiftly push up-stream. And wheresoe'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"We cast our eyes across, all objects seem"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus to be onward borne and flow along"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the same way as we. A portico,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Albeit it stands well propped from end to end"},{"sp":"N","t":"On equal columns, parallel and big,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Contracts by stages in a narrow cone,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When from one end the long, long whole is seen,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Until, conjoining ceiling with the floor,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the whole right side with the left, it draws"},{"sp":"N","t":"Together to a cone's nigh-viewless point."},{"sp":"N","t":"To sailors on the main the sun he seems"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out the waves to rise, and in the waves"},{"sp":"N","t":"To set and bury his light—because indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"They gaze on naught but water and the sky."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, to gazers ignorant of the sea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Vessels in port seem, as with broken poops,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To lean upon the water, quite agog;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For any portion of the oars that's raised"},{"sp":"N","t":"Above the briny spray is straight, and straight"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rudders from above. But other parts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those sunk, immersed below the water-line,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seem broken all and bended and inclined"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sloping to upwards, and turned back to float"},{"sp":"N","t":"Almost atop the water. And when the winds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Carry the scattered drifts along the sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the night-time, then seem to glide along"},{"sp":"N","t":"The radiant constellations 'gainst the clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"And there on high to take far other course"},{"sp":"N","t":"From that whereon in truth they're borne. And then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If haply our hand be set beneath one eye","st":"4.447"},{"sp":"N","t":"And press below thereon, then to our gaze"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each object which we gaze on seems to be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By some sensation twain—then twain the lights"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of lampions burgeoning in flowers of flame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And twain the furniture in all the house,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Two-fold the visages of fellow-men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And twain their bodies. And again, when sleep"},{"sp":"N","t":"Has bound our members down in slumber soft"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all the body lies in deep repose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet then we seem to self to be awake"},{"sp":"N","t":"And move our members; and in night's blind gloom"},{"sp":"N","t":"We think to mark the daylight and the sun;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, shut within a room, yet still we seem"},{"sp":"N","t":"To change our skies, our oceans, rivers, hills,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To cross the plains afoot, and hear new sounds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though still the austere silence of the night"},{"sp":"N","t":"Abides around us, and to speak replies,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though voiceless. Other cases of the sort"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wondrously many do we see, which all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seek, so to say, to injure faith in sense-"},{"sp":"N","t":"In vain, because the largest part of these"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deceives through mere opinions of the mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which we do add ourselves, feigning to see"},{"sp":"N","t":"What by the senses are not seen at all."},{"sp":"N","t":"For naught is harder than to separate"},{"sp":"N","t":"Plain facts from dubious, which the mind forthwith"},{"sp":"N","t":"Adds by itself."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, if one suppose","st":"4.469"},{"sp":"N","t":"That naught is known, he knows not whether this"},{"sp":"N","t":"Itself is able to be known, since he"},{"sp":"N","t":"Confesses naught to know. Therefore with him"},{"sp":"N","t":"I waive discussion—who has set his head"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even where his feet should be. But let me grant"},{"sp":"N","t":"That this he knows,- I question: whence he knows"},{"sp":"N","t":"What 'tis to know and not-to-know in turn,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what created concept of the truth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what device has proved the dubious"},{"sp":"N","t":"To differ from the certain?- since in things"},{"sp":"N","t":"He's heretofore seen naught of true. Thou'lt find"},{"sp":"N","t":"That from the senses first hath been create"},{"sp":"N","t":"Concept of truth, nor can the senses be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rebutted. For criterion must be found"},{"sp":"N","t":"Worthy of greater trust, which shall defeat"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through own authority the false by true;"},{"sp":"N","t":"What, then, than these our senses must there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Worthy a greater trust? Shall reason, sprung"},{"sp":"N","t":"From some false sense, prevail to contradict"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those senses, sprung as reason wholly is"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out the senses?- For lest these be true,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All reason also then is falsified."},{"sp":"N","t":"Or shall the ears have power to blame the eyes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or yet the touch the ears? Again, shall taste"},{"sp":"N","t":"Accuse this touch or shall the nose confute"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or eyes defeat it? Methinks not so it is:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For unto each has been divided off"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its function quite apart, its power to each;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus we're still constrained to perceive"},{"sp":"N","t":"The soft, the cold, the hot apart, apart"},{"sp":"N","t":"All divers hues and whatso things there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Conjoined with hues. Likewise the tasting tongue"},{"sp":"N","t":"Has its own power apart, and smells apart"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sounds apart are known. And thus it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"That no one sense can e'er convict another."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor shall one sense have power to blame itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because it always must be deemed the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Worthy of equal trust. And therefore what"},{"sp":"N","t":"At any time unto these senses showed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same is true."},{"sp":"N","t":"And if the reason be","st":"4.500"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unable to unravel us the cause"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why objects, which at hand were square, afar"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seemed rounded, yet it more availeth us,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lacking the reason, to pretend a cause"},{"sp":"N","t":"For each configuration, than to let"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out our hands escape the obvious things"},{"sp":"N","t":"And injure primal faith in sense, and wreck"},{"sp":"N","t":"All those foundations upon which do rest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Our life and safety. For not only reason"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would topple down; but even our very life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would straightaway collapse, unless we dared"},{"sp":"N","t":"To trust our senses and to keep away"},{"sp":"N","t":"From headlong heights and places to be shunned"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of a like peril, and to seek with speed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their opposites! Again, as in a building,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If the first plumb-line be askew, and if"},{"sp":"N","t":"The square deceiving swerve from lines exact,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And if the level waver but the least"},{"sp":"N","t":"In any part, the whole construction then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must turn out faulty—shelving and askew,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Leaning to back and front, incongruous,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That now some portions seem about to fall,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And falls the whole ere long—betrayed indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"By first deceiving estimates: so too"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thy calculations in affairs of life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must be askew and false, if sprung for thee"},{"sp":"N","t":"From senses false. So all that troop of words"},{"sp":"N","t":"Marshalled against the senses is quite vain."},{"sp":"N","t":"And now remains to demonstrate with ease","st":"4.522"},{"sp":"N","t":"How other senses each their things perceive."},{"sp":"N","t":"Firstly, a sound and every voice is heard,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When, getting into ears, they strike the sense"},{"sp":"N","t":"With their own body. For confess we must"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even voice and sound to be corporeal,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because they're able on the sense to strike."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides voice often scrapes against the throat,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And screams in going out do make more rough"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wind-pipe—naturally enough, methinks,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When, through the narrow exit rising up"},{"sp":"N","t":"In larger throng, these primal germs of voice"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have thus begun to issue forth. In sooth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Also the door of the mouth is scraped against"},{"sp":"N","t":"[By air blown outward] from distended [cheeks]."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus no doubt there is, that voice and words"},{"sp":"N","t":"Consist of elements corporeal,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With power to pain. Nor art thou unaware"},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise how much of body's ta'en away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How much from very thews and powers of men"},{"sp":"N","t":"May be withdrawn by steady talk, prolonged"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even from the rising splendour of the morn"},{"sp":"N","t":"To shadows of black evening,—above all"},{"sp":"N","t":"If 't be outpoured with most exceeding shouts."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore the voice must be corporeal,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since the long talker loses from his frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"A part."},{"sp":"N","t":"Moreover, roughness in the sound"},{"sp":"N","t":"Comes from the roughness in the primal germs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As a smooth sound from smooth ones is create;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor have these elements a form the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"When the trump rumbles with a hollow roar,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As when barbaric Berecynthian pipe"},{"sp":"N","t":"Buzzes with raucous boomings, or when swans"},{"sp":"N","t":"By night from icy shores of Helicon"},{"sp":"N","t":"With wailing voices raise their liquid dirge."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, when from deep within our frame we force","st":"4.549"},{"sp":"N","t":"These voices, and at mouth expel them forth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mobile tongue, artificer of words,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Makes them articulate, and too the lips"},{"sp":"N","t":"By their formations share in shaping them."},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence when the space is short from starting-point"},{"sp":"N","t":"To where that voice arrives, the very words"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must too be plainly heard, distinctly marked."},{"sp":"N","t":"For then the voice conserves its own formation,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Conserves its shape. But if the space between"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be longer than is fit, the words must be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through the much air confounded, and the voice"},{"sp":"N","t":"Disordered in its flight across the winds-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so it haps, that thou canst sound perceive,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet not determine what the words may mean;"},{"sp":"N","t":"To such degree confounded and encumbered"},{"sp":"N","t":"The voice approaches us. Again, one word,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sent from the crier's mouth, may rouse all ears"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the populace. And thus one voice"},{"sp":"N","t":"Scatters asunder into many voices,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since it divides itself for separate ears,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Imprinting form of word and a clear tone."},{"sp":"N","t":"But whatso part of voices fails to hit"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ears themselves perishes, borne beyond,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Idly diffused among the winds. A part,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beating on solid porticoes, tossed back"},{"sp":"N","t":"Returns a sound; and sometimes mocks the ear"},{"sp":"N","t":"With a mere phantom of a word."},{"sp":"N","t":"When this","st":"4.572"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou well hast noted, thou canst render count"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto thyself and others why it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the lonely places that the rocks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Give back like shapes of words in order like,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When search we after comrades wandering"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the shady mountains, and aloud"},{"sp":"N","t":"Call unto them, the scattered. I have seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"Spots that gave back even voices six or seven"},{"sp":"N","t":"For one thrown forth—for so the very hills,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dashing them back against the hills, kept on"},{"sp":"N","t":"With their reverberations. And these spots"},{"sp":"N","t":"The neighbouring country-side doth feign to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Haunts of the goat-foot satyrs and the nymphs;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And tells ye there be fauns, by whose night noise"},{"sp":"N","t":"And antic revels yonder they declare"},{"sp":"N","t":"The voiceless silences are broken oft,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And tones of strings are made and wailings sweet"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which the pipe, beat by players' finger-tips,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pours out; and far and wide the farmer-race"},{"sp":"N","t":"Begins to hear, when, shaking the garmentings"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of pine upon his half-beast head, god-Pan"},{"sp":"N","t":"With puckered lip oft runneth o'er and o'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"The open reeds,—lest flute should cease to pour"},{"sp":"N","t":"The woodland music! Other prodigies"},{"sp":"N","t":"And wonders of this ilk they love to tell,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest they be thought to dwell in lonely spots"},{"sp":"N","t":"And even by gods deserted. This is why"},{"sp":"N","t":"They boast of marvels in their story-tellings;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or by some other reason are led on-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Greedy, as all mankind hath ever been,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To prattle fables into ears."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again,","st":"4.595"},{"sp":"N","t":"One need not wonder how it comes about"},{"sp":"N","t":"That through those places (through which eyes cannot"},{"sp":"N","t":"View objects manifest) sounds yet may pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"And assail the ears. For often we observe"},{"sp":"N","t":"People conversing, though the doors be closed;"},{"sp":"N","t":"No marvel either, since all voice unharmed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can wind through bended apertures of things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"While idol-films decline to—for they're rent,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unless along straight apertures they swim,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like those in glass, through which all images"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do fly across. And yet this voice itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In passing through shut chambers of a house,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is dulled, and in a jumble enters ears,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sound we seem to hear far more than words."},{"sp":"N","t":"Moreover, a voice is into all directions"},{"sp":"N","t":"Divided up, since off from one another"},{"sp":"N","t":"New voices are engendered, when one voice"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath once leapt forth, outstarting into many-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As oft a spark of fire is wont to sprinkle"},{"sp":"N","t":"Itself into its several fires. And so,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Voices do fill those places hid behind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which all are in a hubbub round about,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Astir with sound. But idol-films do tend,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As once sent forth, in straight directions all;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore one can inside a wall see naught,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet catch the voices from beyond the same."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor tongue and palate, whereby we flavour feel,","st":"4.615"},{"sp":"N","t":"Present more problems for more work of thought."},{"sp":"N","t":"Firstly, we feel a flavour in the mouth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When forth we squeeze it, in chewing up our food,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As any one perchance begins to squeeze"},{"sp":"N","t":"With hand and dry a sponge with water soaked."},{"sp":"N","t":"Next, all which forth we squeeze is spread about"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the pores and intertwined paths"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the loose-textured tongue. And so, when smooth"},{"sp":"N","t":"The bodies of the oozy flavour, then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Delightfully they touch, delightfully"},{"sp":"N","t":"They treat all spots, around the wet and trickling"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enclosures of the tongue. And contrariwise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They sting and pain the sense with their assault,"},{"sp":"N","t":"According as with roughness they're supplied."},{"sp":"N","t":"Next, only up to palate is the pleasure"},{"sp":"N","t":"Coming from flavour; for in truth when down"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Thas plunged along the throat, no pleasure is,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst into all the frame it spreads around;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor aught it matters with what food is fed"},{"sp":"N","t":"The body, if only what thou take thou canst"},{"sp":"N","t":"Distribute well digested to the frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"And keep the stomach in a moist career."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, how it is we see some food for some,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Others for others...."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"I will unfold, or wherefore what to some"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is foul and bitter, yet the same to others"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can seem delectable to eat,—why here"},{"sp":"N","t":"So great the distance and the difference is"},{"sp":"N","t":"That what is food to one to some becomes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fierce poison, as a certain snake there is"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, touched by spittle of a man, will waste"},{"sp":"N","t":"And end itself by gnawing up its coil."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, fierce poison is the hellebore"},{"sp":"N","t":"To us, but puts the fat on goats and quails."},{"sp":"N","t":"That thou mayst know by what devices this"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is brought about, in chief thou must recall"},{"sp":"N","t":"What we have said before, that seeds are kept"},{"sp":"N","t":"Commixed in things in divers modes. Again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As all the breathing creatures which take food"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are outwardly unlike, and outer cut"},{"sp":"N","t":"And contour of their members bounds them round,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each differing kind by kind, they thus consist"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of seeds of varying shape. And furthermore,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since seeds do differ, divers too must be"},{"sp":"N","t":"The interstices and paths (which we do call"},{"sp":"N","t":"The apertures) in all the members, even"},{"sp":"N","t":"In mouth and palate too. Thus some must be"},{"sp":"N","t":"More small or yet more large, three-cornered some"},{"sp":"N","t":"And others squared, and many others round,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And certain of them many-angled too"},{"sp":"N","t":"In many modes. For, as the combination"},{"sp":"N","t":"And motion of their divers shapes demand,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The shapes of apertures must be diverse"},{"sp":"N","t":"And paths must vary according to their walls"},{"sp":"N","t":"That bound them. Hence when what is sweet to some,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Becomes to others bitter, for him to whom"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis sweet, the smoothest particles must needs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have entered caressingly the palate's pores."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, contrariwise, with those to whom that sweet"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is sour within the mouth, beyond a doubt"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rough and barbed particles have got"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the narrows of the apertures."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now easy it is from these affairs to know"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whatever..."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Indeed, where one from o'er-abundant bile"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is stricken with fever, or in other wise"},{"sp":"N","t":"Feels the roused violence of some malady,"},{"sp":"N","t":"There the whole frame is now upset, and there"},{"sp":"N","t":"All the positions of the seeds are changed,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that the bodies which before were fit"},{"sp":"N","t":"To cause the savour, now are fit no more,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And now more apt are others which be able"},{"sp":"N","t":"To get within the pores and gender sour."},{"sp":"N","t":"Both sorts, in sooth, are intermixed in honey-"},{"sp":"N","t":"What oft we've proved above to thee before."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now come, and I will indicate what wise","st":"4.673"},{"sp":"N","t":"Impact of odour on the nostrils touches."},{"sp":"N","t":"And first, 'tis needful there be many things"},{"sp":"N","t":"From whence the streaming flow of varied odours"},{"sp":"N","t":"May roll along, and we're constrained to think"},{"sp":"N","t":"They stream and dart and sprinkle themselves about"},{"sp":"N","t":"Impartially. But for some breathing creatures"},{"sp":"N","t":"One odour is more apt, to others another-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because of differing forms of seeds and pores."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus on and on along the zephyrs bees"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are led by odour of honey, vultures too"},{"sp":"N","t":"By carcasses. Again, the forward power"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of scent in dogs doth lead the hunter on"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whithersoever the splay-foot of wild beast"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath hastened its career; and the white goose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The saviour of the Roman citadel,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forescents afar the odour of mankind."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, diversly to divers ones is given"},{"sp":"N","t":"Peculiar smell that leadeth each along"},{"sp":"N","t":"To his own food or makes him start aback"},{"sp":"N","t":"From loathsome poison, and in this wise are"},{"sp":"N","t":"The generations of the wild preserved."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet is this pungence not alone in odours"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or in the class of flavours; but, likewise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The look of things and hues agree not all"},{"sp":"N","t":"So well with senses unto all, but that"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some unto some will be, to gaze upon,"},{"sp":"N","t":"More keen and painful. Lo, the raving lions,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They dare not face and gaze upon the cock"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who's wont with wings to flap away the night"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off the stage, and call the beaming morn"},{"sp":"N","t":"With clarion voice—and lions straightway thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bethink themselves of flight, because, ye see,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the body of the cocks there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some certain seeds, which, into lions' eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Injected, bore into the pupils deep"},{"sp":"N","t":"And yield such piercing pain they can't hold out"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against the cocks, however fierce they be-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst yet these seeds can't hurt our gaze the least,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Either because they do not penetrate,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or since they have free exit from the eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"As soon as penetrating, so that thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"They cannot hurt our eyes in any part"},{"sp":"N","t":"By there remaining."},{"sp":"N","t":"To speak once more of odour;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whatever assail the nostrils, some can travel"},{"sp":"N","t":"A longer way than others. None of them,"},{"sp":"N","t":"However, 's borne so far as sound or voice-"},{"sp":"N","t":"While I omit all mention of such things"},{"sp":"N","t":"As hit the eyesight and assail the vision."},{"sp":"N","t":"For slowly on a wandering course it comes"},{"sp":"N","t":"And perishes sooner, by degrees absorbed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Easily into all the winds of air;-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And first, because from deep inside the thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"It is discharged with labour (for the fact"},{"sp":"N","t":"That every object, when 'tis shivered, ground,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or crumbled by the fire, will smell the stronger"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is sign that odours flow and part away"},{"sp":"N","t":"From inner regions of the things). And next,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou mayest see that odour is create"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of larger primal germs than voice, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"It enters not through stony walls, wherethrough"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unfailingly the voice and sound are borne;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, besides, thou wilt observe 'tis not"},{"sp":"N","t":"So easy to trace out in whatso place"},{"sp":"N","t":"The smelling object is. For, dallying on"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the winds, the particles cool off,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then the scurrying messengers of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Arrive our senses, when no longer hot."},{"sp":"N","t":"So dogs oft wander astray, and hunt the scent."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now mark, and hear what objects move the mind,","st":"4.722"},{"sp":"N","t":"And learn, in few, whence unto intellect"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do come what come. And first I tell thee this:"},{"sp":"N","t":"That many images of objects rove"},{"sp":"N","t":"In many modes to every region round-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So thin that easily the one with other,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When once they meet, uniteth in mid-air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like gossamer or gold-leaf. For, indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Far thinner are they in their fabric than"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those images which take a hold on eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"And smite the vision, since through body's pores"},{"sp":"N","t":"They penetrate, and inwardly stir up"},{"sp":"N","t":"The subtle nature of mind and smite the sense."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, Centaurs and the limbs of Scyllas, thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"The Cerberus-visages of dogs we see,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And images of people gone before-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dead men whose bones earth bosomed long ago;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because the images of every kind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are everywhere about us borne—in part"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those which are gendered in the very air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of own accord, in part those others which"},{"sp":"N","t":"From divers things do part away, and those"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which are compounded, made from out their shapes."},{"sp":"N","t":"For soothly from no living Centaur is"},{"sp":"N","t":"That phantom gendered, since no breed of beast"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like him was ever; but, when images"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of horse and man by chance have come together,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They easily cohere, as aforesaid,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At once, through subtle nature and fabric thin."},{"sp":"N","t":"In the same fashion others of this ilk"},{"sp":"N","t":"Created are. And when they're quickly borne"},{"sp":"N","t":"In their exceeding lightness, easily"},{"sp":"N","t":"(As earlier I showed) one subtle image,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Compounded, moves by its one blow the mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Itself so subtle and so strangely quick."},{"sp":"N","t":"That these things come to pass as I record,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From this thou easily canst understand:"},{"sp":"N","t":"So far as one is unto other like,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seeing with mind as well as with the eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must come to pass in fashion not unlike."},{"sp":"N","t":"Well, now, since I have shown that I perceive"},{"sp":"N","t":"Haply a lion through those idol-films"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such as assail my eyes, 'tis thine to know"},{"sp":"N","t":"Also the mind is in like manner moved,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sees, nor more nor less than eyes do see"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Except that it perceives more subtle films)"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lion and aught else through idol-films."},{"sp":"N","t":"And when the sleep has overset our frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mind's intelligence is now awake,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still for no other reason, save that these-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The self-same films as when we are awake-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Assail our minds, to such degree indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"That we do seem to see for sure the man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whom, void of life, now death and earth have gained"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dominion over. And nature forces this"},{"sp":"N","t":"To come to pass because the body's senses"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are resting, thwarted through the members all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unable now to conquer false with true;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And memory lies prone and languishes"},{"sp":"N","t":"In slumber, nor protests that he, the man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whom the mind feigns to see alive, long since"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath been the gain of death and dissolution."},{"sp":"N","t":"And further, 'tis no marvel idols move"},{"sp":"N","t":"And toss their arms and other members round"},{"sp":"N","t":"In rhythmic time—and often in men's sleeps"},{"sp":"N","t":"It haps an image this is seen to do;"},{"sp":"N","t":"In sooth, when perishes the former image,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And other is gendered of another pose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That former seemeth to have changed its gestures."},{"sp":"N","t":"Of course the change must be conceived as speedy;"},{"sp":"N","t":"So great the swiftness and so great the store"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of idol-things, and (in an instant brief"},{"sp":"N","t":"As mind can mark) so great, again, the store"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of separate idol-parts to bring supplies."},{"sp":"N","t":"It happens also that there is supplied"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sometimes an image not of kind the same;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But what before was woman, now at hand"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is seen to stand there, altered into male;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or other visage, other age succeeds;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But slumber and oblivion take care"},{"sp":"N","t":"That we shall feel no wonder at the thing."},{"sp":"N","t":"And much in these affairs demands inquiry,","st":"4.777"},{"sp":"N","t":"And much, illumination—if we crave"},{"sp":"N","t":"With plainness to exhibit facts. And first,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why doth the mind of one to whom the whim"},{"sp":"N","t":"To think has come behold forthwith that thing?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or do the idols watch upon our will,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And doth an image unto us occur,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Directly we desire—if heart prefer"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sea, the land, or after all the sky?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Assemblies of the citizens, parades,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Banquets, and battles, these and all doth she,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nature, create and furnish at our word?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Maugre the fact that in same place and spot"},{"sp":"N","t":"Another's mind is meditating things"},{"sp":"N","t":"All far unlike. And what, again, of this:"},{"sp":"N","t":"When we in sleep behold the idols step,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In measure, forward, moving supple limbs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst forth they put each supple arm in turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"With speedy motion, and with eyeing heads"},{"sp":"N","t":"Repeat the movement, as the foot keeps time?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forsooth, the idols they are steeped in art,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And wander to and fro well taught indeed,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus to be able in the time of night"},{"sp":"N","t":"To make such games! Or will the truth be this:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because in one least moment that we mark-"},{"sp":"N","t":"That is, the uttering of a single sound-"},{"sp":"N","t":"There lurk yet many moments, which the reason"},{"sp":"N","t":"Discovers to exist, therefore it comes"},{"sp":"N","t":"That, in a moment how so brief ye will,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The divers idols are hard by, and ready"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each in its place diverse? So great the swiftness,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So great, again, the store of idol-things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so, when perishes the former image,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And other is gendered of another pose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The former seemeth to have changed its gestures."},{"sp":"N","t":"And since they be so tenuous, mind can mark"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sharply alone the ones it strains to see;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus the rest do perish one and all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Save those for which the mind prepares itself."},{"sp":"N","t":"Further, it doth prepare itself indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hopes to see what follows after each-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence this result. For hast thou not observed"},{"sp":"N","t":"How eyes, essaying to perceive the fine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will strain in preparation, otherwise"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unable sharply to perceive at all?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet know thou canst that, even in objects plain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If thou attendest not, 'tis just the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"As if 'twere all the time removed and far."},{"sp":"N","t":"What marvel, then, that mind doth lose the rest,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Save those to which 'thas given up itself?"},{"sp":"N","t":"So 'tis that we conjecture from small signs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Things wide and weighty, and involve ourselves"},{"sp":"N","t":"In snarls of self-deceit."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"SOME VITAL FUNCTIONS"},{"sp":"N","t":"In these affairs","st":"4.823"},{"sp":"N","t":"We crave that thou wilt passionately flee"},{"sp":"N","t":"The one offence, and anxiously wilt shun"},{"sp":"N","t":"The error of presuming the clear lights"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of eyes created were that we might see;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or thighs and knees, aprop upon the feet,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thuswise can bended be, that we might step"},{"sp":"N","t":"With goodly strides ahead; or forearms joined"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the sturdy uppers, or serving hands"},{"sp":"N","t":"On either side were given, that we might do"},{"sp":"N","t":"Life's own demands. All such interpretation"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is aft-for-fore with inverse reasoning,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since naught is born in body so that we"},{"sp":"N","t":"May use the same, but birth engenders use:"},{"sp":"N","t":"No seeing ere the lights of eyes were born,"},{"sp":"N","t":"No speaking ere the tongue created was;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But origin of tongue came long before"},{"sp":"N","t":"Discourse of words, and ears created were"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much earlier than any sound was heard;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all the members, so meseems, were there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before they got their use: and therefore, they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could not be gendered for the sake of use."},{"sp":"N","t":"But contrariwise, contending in the fight"},{"sp":"N","t":"With hand to hand, and rending of the joints,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fouling of the limbs with gore, was there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O long before the gleaming spears ere flew;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And nature prompted man to shun a wound,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before the left arm by the aid of art"},{"sp":"N","t":"Opposed the shielding targe. And, verily,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yielding the weary body to repose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Far ancienter than cushions of soft beds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And quenching thirst is earlier than cups."},{"sp":"N","t":"These objects, therefore, which for use and life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have been devised, can be conceived as found"},{"sp":"N","t":"For sake of using. But apart from such"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are all which first were born and afterwards"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gave knowledge of their own utility-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Chief in which sort we note the senses, limbs:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, again, 'tis quite beyond thy power"},{"sp":"N","t":"To hold that these could thus have been create"},{"sp":"N","t":"For office of utility."},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise,","st":"4.858"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis nothing strange that all the breathing creatures"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seek, even by nature of their frame, their food."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yes, since I've taught thee that from off the things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Stream and depart innumerable bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"In modes innumerable too; but most"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must be the bodies streaming from the living-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which bodies, vexed by motion evermore,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are through the mouth exhaled innumerable,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When weary creatures pant, or through the sweat"},{"sp":"N","t":"Squeezed forth innumerable from deep within."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus body rarefies, so undermined"},{"sp":"N","t":"In all its nature, and pain attends its state."},{"sp":"N","t":"And so the food is taken to underprop"},{"sp":"N","t":"The tottering joints, and by its interfusion"},{"sp":"N","t":"To re-create their powers, and there stop up"},{"sp":"N","t":"The longing, open-mouthed through limbs and veins,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For eating. And the moist no less departs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into all regions that demand the moist;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And many heaped-up particles of hot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which cause such burnings in these bellies of ours,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The liquid on arriving dissipates"},{"sp":"N","t":"And quenches like a fire, that parching heat"},{"sp":"N","t":"No longer now can scorch the frame. And so,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou seest how panting thirst is washed away"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off our body, how the hunger-pang"},{"sp":"N","t":"It, too, appeased."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, how it comes that we,","st":"4.877"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whene'er we wish, can step with strides ahead,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And how 'tis given to move our limbs about,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what device is wont to push ahead"},{"sp":"N","t":"This the big load of our corporeal frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"I'll say to thee—do thou attend what's said."},{"sp":"N","t":"I say that first some idol-films of walking"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into our mind do fall and smite the mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As said before. Thereafter will arises;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For no one starts to do a thing, before"},{"sp":"N","t":"The intellect previsions what it wills;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what it there pre-visioneth depends"},{"sp":"N","t":"On what that image is. When, therefore, mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Doth so bestir itself that it doth will"},{"sp":"N","t":"To go and step along, it strikes at once"},{"sp":"N","t":"That energy of soul that's sown about"},{"sp":"N","t":"In all the body through the limbs and frame-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And this is easy of performance, since"},{"sp":"N","t":"The soul is close conjoined with the mind."},{"sp":"N","t":"Next, soul in turn strikes body, and by degrees"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus the whole mass is pushed along and moved."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then too the body rarefies, and air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forsooth as ever of such nimbleness,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Comes on and penetrates aboundingly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through opened pores, and thus is sprinkled round"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto all smallest places in our frame."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus then by these twain factors, severally,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Body is borne like ship with oars and wind."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor yet in these affairs is aught for wonder"},{"sp":"N","t":"That particles so fine can whirl around"},{"sp":"N","t":"So great a body and turn this weight of ours;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For wind, so tenuous with its subtle body,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet pushes, driving on the mighty ship"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of mighty bulk; one hand directs the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whatever its momentum, and one helm"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whirls it around, whither ye please; and loads,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Many and huge, are moved and hoisted high"},{"sp":"N","t":"By enginery of pulley-blocks and wheels,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With but light strain."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, by what modes this sleep","st":"4.907"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pours through our members waters of repose"},{"sp":"N","t":"And frees the breast from cares of mind, I'll tell"},{"sp":"N","t":"In verses sweeter than they many are;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as the swan's slight note is better far"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than that dispersed clamour of the cranes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the southwind's aery clouds. Do thou"},{"sp":"N","t":"Give me sharp ears and a sagacious mind,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"That thou mayst not deny the things to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereof I'm speaking, nor depart away"},{"sp":"N","t":"With bosom scorning these the spoken truths,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thyself at fault unable to perceive."},{"sp":"N","t":"Sleep chiefly comes when energy of soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath now been scattered through the frame, and part"},{"sp":"N","t":"Expelled abroad and gone away, and part"},{"sp":"N","t":"Crammed back and settling deep within the frame-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereafter then our loosened members droop."},{"sp":"N","t":"For doubt is none that by the work of soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exist in us this sense, and when by slumber"},{"sp":"N","t":"That sense is thwarted, we are bound to think"},{"sp":"N","t":"The soul confounded and expelled abroad-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet not entirely, else the frame would lie"},{"sp":"N","t":"Drenched in the everlasting cold of death."},{"sp":"N","t":"In sooth, where no one part of soul remained"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lurking among the members, even as fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lurks buried under many ashes, whence"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could sense amain rekindled be in members,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As flame can rise anew from unseen fire?"},{"sp":"N","t":"By what devices this strange state and new","st":"4.929"},{"sp":"N","t":"May be occasioned, and by what the soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can be confounded and the frame grow faint,"},{"sp":"N","t":"I will untangle: see to it, thou, that I"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pour forth my words not unto empty winds."},{"sp":"N","t":"In first place, body on its outer parts-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since these are touched by neighbouring aery gusts-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must there be thumped and strook by blows of air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Repeatedly. And therefore almost all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are covered either with hides, or else with shells,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or with the horny callus, or with bark."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet this same air lashes their inner parts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When creatures draw a breath or blow it out."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, since body thus is flogged alike"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the inside and the out, and blows"},{"sp":"N","t":"Come in upon us through the little pores"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even inward to our body's primal parts"},{"sp":"N","t":"And primal elements, there comes to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"By slow degrees, along our members then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A kind of overthrow; for then confounded"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are those arrangements of the primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of body and of mind. It comes to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"That next a part of soul's expelled abroad,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A part retreateth in recesses hid,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A part, too, scattered all about the frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cannot become united nor engage"},{"sp":"N","t":"In interchange of motion. Nature now"},{"sp":"N","t":"So hedges off approaches and the paths;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus the sense, its motions all deranged,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Retires down deep within; and since there's naught,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As 'twere, to prop the frame, the body weakens,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all the members languish, and the arms"},{"sp":"N","t":"And eyelids fall, and, as ye lie abed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even there the houghs will sag and loose their powers."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, sleep follows after food, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"The food produces same result as air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst being scattered round through all the veins;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And much the heaviest is that slumber which,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Full or fatigued, thou takest; since 'tis then"},{"sp":"N","t":"That the most bodies disarrange themselves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bruised by labours hard. And in same wise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"This three-fold change: a forcing of the soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down deeper, more a casting-forth of it,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A moving more divided in its parts"},{"sp":"N","t":"And scattered more."},{"sp":"N","t":"And to whate'er pursuit","st":"4.962"},{"sp":"N","t":"A man most clings absorbed, or what the affairs"},{"sp":"N","t":"On which we theretofore have tarried much,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mind hath strained upon the more, we seem"},{"sp":"N","t":"In sleep not rarely to go at the same."},{"sp":"N","t":"The lawyers seem to plead and cite decrees,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Commanders they to fight and go at frays,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sailors to live in combat with the winds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And we ourselves indeed to make this book,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And still to seek the nature of the world"},{"sp":"N","t":"And set it down, when once discovered, here"},{"sp":"N","t":"In these my country's leaves. Thus all pursuits,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All arts in general seem in sleeps to mock"},{"sp":"N","t":"And master the minds of men. And whosoever"},{"sp":"N","t":"Day after day for long to games have given"},{"sp":"N","t":"Attention undivided, still they keep"},{"sp":"N","t":"(As oft we note), even when they've ceased to grasp"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those games with their own senses, open paths"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the mind wherethrough the idol-films"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of just those games can come. And thus it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"For many a day thereafter those appear"},{"sp":"N","t":"Floating before the eyes, that even awake"},{"sp":"N","t":"They think they view the dancers moving round"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their supple limbs, and catch with both the ears"},{"sp":"N","t":"The liquid song of harp and speaking chords,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And view the same assembly on the seats,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And manifold bright glories of the stage-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So great the influence of pursuit and zest,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And of the affairs wherein 'thas been the wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of men to be engaged-nor only men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But soothly all the animals. Behold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou'lt see the sturdy horses, though outstretched,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet sweating in their sleep, and panting ever,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And straining utmost strength, as if for prize,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As if, with barriers opened now..."},{"sp":"N","t":"And hounds of huntsmen oft in soft repose"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet toss asudden all their legs about,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And growl and bark, and with their nostrils sniff"},{"sp":"N","t":"The winds again, again, as though indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"They'd caught the scented foot-prints of wild beasts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, even when wakened, often they pursue"},{"sp":"N","t":"The phantom images of stags, as though"},{"sp":"N","t":"They did perceive them fleeing on before,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Until the illusion's shaken off and dogs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Come to themselves again. And fawning breed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of house-bred whelps do feel the sudden urge"},{"sp":"N","t":"To shake their bodies and start from off the ground,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As if beholding stranger-visages."},{"sp":"N","t":"And ever the fiercer be the stock, the more"},{"sp":"N","t":"In sleep the same is ever bound to rage."},{"sp":"N","t":"But flee the divers tribes of birds and vex"},{"sp":"N","t":"With sudden wings by night the groves of gods,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When in their gentle slumbers they have dreamed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of hawks in chase, aswooping on for fight."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, the minds of mortals which perform"},{"sp":"N","t":"With mighty motions mighty enterprises,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Often in sleep will do and dare the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"In manner like. Kings take the towns by storm,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Succumb to capture, battle on the field,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Raise a wild cry as if their throats were cut"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even then and there. And many wrestle on"},{"sp":"N","t":"And groan with pains, and fill all regions round"},{"sp":"N","t":"With mighty cries and wild, as if then gnawed"},{"sp":"N","t":"By fangs of panther or of lion fierce."},{"sp":"N","t":"Many amid their slumbers talk about"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their mighty enterprises, and have often"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enough become the proof of their own crimes."},{"sp":"N","t":"Many meet death; many, as if headlong"},{"sp":"N","t":"From lofty mountains tumbling down to earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"With all their frame, are frenzied in their fright;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And after sleep, as if still mad in mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They scarce come to, confounded as they are"},{"sp":"N","t":"By ferment of their frame. The thirsty man,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise, he sits beside delightful spring"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or river and gulpeth down with gaping throat"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nigh the whole stream. And oft the innocent young,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By sleep o'ermastered, think they lift their dress"},{"sp":"N","t":"By pail or public jordan and then void"},{"sp":"N","t":"The water filtered down their frame entire"},{"sp":"N","t":"And drench the Babylonian coverlets,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Magnificently bright. Again, those males"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the surging channels of whose years"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now first has passed the seed (engendered"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within their members by the ripened days)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are in their sleep confronted from without"},{"sp":"N","t":"By idol-images of some fair form-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Tidings of glorious face and lovely bloom,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which stir and goad the regions turgid now"},{"sp":"N","t":"With seed abundant; so that, as it were"},{"sp":"N","t":"With all the matter acted duly out,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They pour the billows of a potent stream"},{"sp":"N","t":"And stain their garment."},{"sp":"N","t":"And as said before,","st":"4.1037"},{"sp":"N","t":"That seed is roused in us when once ripe age"},{"sp":"N","t":"Has made our body strong..."},{"sp":"N","t":"As divers causes give to divers things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Impulse and irritation, so one force"},{"sp":"N","t":"In human kind rouses the human seed"},{"sp":"N","t":"To spurt from man. As soon as ever it issues,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forced from its first abodes, it passes down"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the whole body through the limbs and frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Meeting in certain regions of our thews,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And stirs amain the genitals of man."},{"sp":"N","t":"The goaded regions swell with seed, and then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Comes the delight to dart the same at what"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mad desire so yearns, and body seeks"},{"sp":"N","t":"That object, whence the mind by love is pierced."},{"sp":"N","t":"For well-nigh each man falleth toward his wound,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And our blood spurts even toward the spot from whence"},{"sp":"N","t":"The stroke wherewith we are strook, and if indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"The foe be close, the red jet reaches him."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, one who gets a stroke from Venus' shafts-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whether a boy with limbs effeminate"},{"sp":"N","t":"Assault him, or a woman darting love"},{"sp":"N","t":"From all her body—that one strains to get"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even to the thing whereby he's hit, and longs"},{"sp":"N","t":"To join with it and cast into its frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fluid drawn even from within its own."},{"sp":"N","t":"For the mute craving doth presage delight."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"THE PASSION OF LOVE"},{"sp":"N","t":"This craving 'tis that's Venus unto us:","st":"4.1058"},{"sp":"N","t":"From this, engender all the lures of love,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From this, O first hath into human hearts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Trickled that drop of joyance which ere long"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is by chill care succeeded. Since, indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though she thou lovest now be far away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet idol-images of her are near"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the sweet name is floating in thy ear."},{"sp":"N","t":"But it behooves to flee those images;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And scare afar whatever feeds thy love;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And turn elsewhere thy mind; and vent the sperm,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within thee gathered, into sundry bodies,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor, with thy thoughts still busied with one love,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Keep it for one delight, and so store up"},{"sp":"N","t":"Care for thyself and pain inevitable."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, lo, the ulcer just by nourishing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grows to more life with deep inveteracy,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And day by day the fury swells aflame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the woe waxes heavier day by day-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unless thou dost destroy even by new blows"},{"sp":"N","t":"The former wounds of love, and curest them"},{"sp":"N","t":"While yet they're fresh, by wandering freely round"},{"sp":"N","t":"After the freely-wandering Venus, or"},{"sp":"N","t":"Canst lead elsewhere the tumults of thy mind."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor doth that man who keeps away from love","st":"4.1073"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet lack the fruits of Venus; rather takes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those pleasures which are free of penalties."},{"sp":"N","t":"For the delights of Venus, verily,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are more unmixed for mortals sane-of-soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than for those sick-at-heart with love-pining."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yea, in the very moment of possessing,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Surges the heat of lovers to and fro,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Restive, uncertain; and they cannot fix"},{"sp":"N","t":"On what to first enjoy with eyes and hands."},{"sp":"N","t":"The parts they sought for, those they squeeze so tight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And pain the creature's body, close their teeth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Often against her lips, and smite with kiss"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mouth into mouth,—because this same delight"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is not unmixed; and underneath are stings"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which goad a man to hurt the very thing,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whate'er it be, from whence arise for him"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those germs of madness. But with gentle touch"},{"sp":"N","t":"Venus subdues the pangs in midst of love,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the admixture of a fondling joy"},{"sp":"N","t":"Doth curb the bites of passion. For they hope"},{"sp":"N","t":"That by the very body whence they caught"},{"sp":"N","t":"The heats of love their flames can be put out."},{"sp":"N","t":"But nature protests 'tis all quite otherwise;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For this same love it is the one sole thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of which, the more we have, the fiercer burns"},{"sp":"N","t":"The breast with fell desire. For food and drink"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are taken within our members; and, since they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can stop up certain parts, thus, easily"},{"sp":"N","t":"Desire of water is glutted and of bread."},{"sp":"N","t":"But, lo, from human face and lovely bloom"},{"sp":"N","t":"Naught penetrates our frame to be enjoyed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Save flimsy idol-images and vain-"},{"sp":"N","t":"A sorry hope which oft the winds disperse."},{"sp":"N","t":"As when the thirsty man in slumber seeks"},{"sp":"N","t":"To drink, and water ne'er is granted him"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherewith to quench the heat within his members,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But after idols of the liquids strives"},{"sp":"N","t":"And toils in vain, and thirsts even whilst he gulps"},{"sp":"N","t":"In middle of the torrent, thus in love"},{"sp":"N","t":"Venus deludes with idol-images"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lovers. Nor they cannot sate their lust"},{"sp":"N","t":"By merely gazing on the bodies, nor"},{"sp":"N","t":"They cannot with their palms and fingers rub"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aught from each tender limb, the while they stray"},{"sp":"N","t":"Uncertain over all the body. Then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At last, with members intertwined, when they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enjoy the flower of their age, when now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their bodies have sweet presage of keen joys,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And Venus is about to sow the fields"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of woman, greedily their frames they lock,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mingle the slaver of their mouths, and breathe"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into each other, pressing teeth on mouths-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet to no purpose, since they're powerless"},{"sp":"N","t":"To rub off aught, or penetrate and pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"With body entire into body—for oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"They seem to strive and struggle thus to do;"},{"sp":"N","t":"So eagerly they cling in Venus' bonds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst melt away their members, overcome"},{"sp":"N","t":"By violence of delight. But when at last"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lust, gathered in the thews, hath spent itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"There come a brief pause in the raging heat-"},{"sp":"N","t":"But then a madness just the same returns"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that old fury visits them again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When once again they seek and crave to reach"},{"sp":"N","t":"They know not what, all powerless to find"},{"sp":"N","t":"The artifice to subjugate the bane."},{"sp":"N","t":"In such uncertain state they waste away"},{"sp":"N","t":"With unseen wound."},{"sp":"N","t":"To which be added too,","st":"4.1121"},{"sp":"N","t":"They squander powers and with the travail wane;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be added too, they spend their futile years"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under another's beck and call; their duties"},{"sp":"N","t":"Neglected languish and their honest name"},{"sp":"N","t":"Reeleth sick, sick; and meantime their estates"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are lost in Babylonian tapestries;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And unguents and dainty Sicyonian shoes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Laugh on her feet; and (as ye may be sure)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Big emeralds of green light are set in gold;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And rich sea-purple dress by constant wear"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grows shabby and all soaked with Venus' sweat;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the well-earned ancestral property"},{"sp":"N","t":"Becometh head-bands, coifs, and many a time"},{"sp":"N","t":"The cloaks, or garments Alidensian"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or of the Cean isle. And banquets, set"},{"sp":"N","t":"With rarest cloth and viands, are prepared-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And games of chance, and many a drinking cup,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And unguents, crowns and garlands. All in vain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since from amid the well-spring of delights"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bubbles some drop of bitter to torment"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the very flowers—when haply mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gnaws into self, now stricken with remorse"},{"sp":"N","t":"For slothful years and ruin in baudels,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else because she's left him all in doubt"},{"sp":"N","t":"By launching some sly word, which still like fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lives wildly, cleaving to his eager heart;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else because he thinks she darts her eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Too much about and gazes at another,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in her face sees traces of a laugh."},{"sp":"N","t":"These ills are found in prospering love and true;","st":"4.1141"},{"sp":"N","t":"But in crossed love and helpless there be such"},{"sp":"N","t":"As through shut eyelids thou canst still take in-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Uncounted ills; so that 'tis better far"},{"sp":"N","t":"To watch beforehand, in the way I've shown,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And guard against enticements. For to shun"},{"sp":"N","t":"A fall into the hunting-snares of love"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is not so hard, as to get out again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When tangled in the very nets, and burst"},{"sp":"N","t":"The stoutly-knotted cords of Aphrodite."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet even when there enmeshed with tangled feet,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still canst thou scape the danger-lest indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou standest in the way of thine own good,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And overlookest first all blemishes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of mind and body of thy much preferred,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Desirable dame. For so men do,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Eyeless with passion, and assign to them"},{"sp":"N","t":"Graces not theirs in fact. And thus we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"Creatures in many a wise crooked and ugly"},{"sp":"N","t":"The prosperous sweethearts in a high esteem;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And lovers gird each other and advise"},{"sp":"N","t":"To placate Venus, since their friends are smit"},{"sp":"N","t":"With a base passion—miserable dupes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who seldom mark their own worst bane of all."},{"sp":"N","t":"The black-skinned girl is \"tawny like the honey\";"},{"sp":"N","t":"The filthy and the fetid's \"negligee\";"},{"sp":"N","t":"The cat-eyed she's \"a little Pallas,\" she;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sinewy and wizened's \"a gazelle\";"},{"sp":"N","t":"The pudgy and the pigmy is \"piquant,"},{"sp":"N","t":"One of the Graces sure\"; the big and bulky"},{"sp":"N","t":"O she's \"an Admiration, imposante\";"},{"sp":"N","t":"The stuttering and tongue-tied \"sweetly lisps\";"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mute girl's \"modest\"; and the garrulous,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The spiteful spit-fire, is \"a sparkling wit\";"},{"sp":"N","t":"And she who scarcely lives for scrawniness"},{"sp":"N","t":"Becomes \"a slender darling\"; \"delicate\""},{"sp":"N","t":"Is she who's nearly dead of coughing-fit;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The pursy female with protuberant breasts"},{"sp":"N","t":"She is \"like Ceres when the goddess gave"},{"sp":"N","t":"Young Bacchus suck\"; the pug-nosed lady-love"},{"sp":"N","t":"\"A Satyress, a feminine Silenus\";"},{"sp":"N","t":"The blubber-lipped is \"all one luscious kiss\"-"},{"sp":"N","t":"A weary while it were to tell the whole."},{"sp":"N","t":"But let her face possess what charm ye will,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Let Venus' glory rise from all her limbs,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forsooth there still are others; and forsooth"},{"sp":"N","t":"We lived before without her; and forsooth"},{"sp":"N","t":"She does the same things—and we know she does-"},{"sp":"N","t":"All, as the ugly creature, and she scents,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yes she, her wretched self with vile perfumes;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whom even her handmaids flee and giggle at"},{"sp":"N","t":"Behind her back. But he, the lover, in tears"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because shut out, covers her threshold o'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"Often with flowers and garlands, and anoints"},{"sp":"N","t":"Her haughty door-posts with the marjoram,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And prints, poor fellow, kisses on the doors-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Admitted at last, if haply but one whiff"},{"sp":"N","t":"Got to him on approaching, he would seek"},{"sp":"N","t":"Decent excuses to go out forthwith;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And his lament, long pondered, then would fall"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down at his heels; and there he'd damn himself"},{"sp":"N","t":"For his fatuity, observing how"},{"sp":"N","t":"He had assigned to that same lady more-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than it is proper to concede to mortals."},{"sp":"N","t":"And these our Venuses are 'ware of this."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore the more are they at pains to hide"},{"sp":"N","t":"All the-behind-the-scenes of life from those"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whom they desire to keep in bonds of love-"},{"sp":"N","t":"In vain, since ne'ertheless thou canst by thought"},{"sp":"N","t":"Drag all the matter forth into the light"},{"sp":"N","t":"And well search out the cause of all these smiles;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And if of graceful mind she be and kind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do thou, in thy turn, overlook the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus allow for poor mortality."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor sighs the woman always with feigned love,","st":"4.1192"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who links her body round man's body locked"},{"sp":"N","t":"And holds him fast, making his kisses wet"},{"sp":"N","t":"With lips sucked into lips; for oft she acts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even from desire, and, seeking mutual joys,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Incites him there to run love's race-course through."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor otherwise can cattle, birds, wild beasts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sheep and mares submit unto the males,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Except that their own nature is in heat,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And burns abounding and with gladness takes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Once more the Venus of the mounting males."},{"sp":"N","t":"And seest thou not how those whom mutual pleasure"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath bound are tortured in their common bonds?"},{"sp":"N","t":"How often in the cross-roads dogs that pant"},{"sp":"N","t":"To get apart strain eagerly asunder"},{"sp":"N","t":"With utmost might?- When all the while they're fast"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the stout links of Venus. But they'd ne'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"So pull, except they knew those mutual joys-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So powerful to cast them unto snares"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hold them bound. Wherefore again, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as I say, there is a joint delight."},{"sp":"N","t":"And when perchance, in mingling seed with his,","st":"4.1209"},{"sp":"N","t":"The female hath o'erpowered the force of male"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by a sudden fling hath seized it fast,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then are the offspring, more from mothers' seed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"More like their mothers; as, from fathers' seed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They're like to fathers. But whom seest to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Partakers of each shape, one equal blend"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of parents' features, these are generate"},{"sp":"N","t":"From fathers' body and from mothers' blood,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When mutual and harmonious heat hath dashed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Together seeds, aroused along their frames"},{"sp":"N","t":"By Venus' goads, and neither of the twain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mastereth or is mastered. Happens too"},{"sp":"N","t":"That sometimes offspring can to being come"},{"sp":"N","t":"In likeness of their grandsires, and bring back"},{"sp":"N","t":"Often the shapes of grandsires' sires, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their parents in their bodies oft retain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Concealed many primal germs, commixed"},{"sp":"N","t":"In many modes, which, starting with the stock,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sire handeth down to son, himself a sire;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence Venus by a variable chance"},{"sp":"N","t":"Engenders shapes, and diversely brings back"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ancestral features, voices too, and hair."},{"sp":"N","t":"A female generation rises forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"From seed paternal, and from mother's body"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exist created males: since sex proceeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"No more from singleness of seed than faces"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or bodies or limbs of ours: for every birth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is from a twofold seed; and what's created"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath, of that parent which it is more like,"},{"sp":"N","t":"More than its equal share; as thou canst mark,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whether the breed be male or female stock."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor do the powers divine grudge any man","st":"4.1233"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fruits of his seed-sowing, so that never"},{"sp":"N","t":"He be called \"father\" by sweet children his,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And end his days in sterile love forever."},{"sp":"N","t":"What many men suppose; and gloomily"},{"sp":"N","t":"They sprinkle the altars with abundant blood,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And make the high platforms odorous with burnt gifts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To render big by plenteous seed their wives-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And plague in vain godheads and sacred lots."},{"sp":"N","t":"For sterile are these men by seed too thick,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else by far too watery and thin."},{"sp":"N","t":"Because the thin is powerless to cleave"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fast to the proper places, straightaway"},{"sp":"N","t":"It trickles from them, and, returned again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Retires abortively. And then since seed"},{"sp":"N","t":"More gross and solid than will suit is spent"},{"sp":"N","t":"By some men, either it flies not forth amain"},{"sp":"N","t":"With spurt prolonged enough, or else it fails"},{"sp":"N","t":"To enter suitably the proper places,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or, having entered, the seed is weakly mixed"},{"sp":"N","t":"With seed of the woman: harmonies of Venus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are seen to matter vastly here; and some"},{"sp":"N","t":"Impregnate some more readily, and from some"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some women conceive more readily and become"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pregnant. And many women, sterile before"},{"sp":"N","t":"In several marriage-beds, have yet thereafter"},{"sp":"N","t":"Obtained the mates from whom they could conceive"},{"sp":"N","t":"The baby-boys, and with sweet progeny"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grow rich. And even for husbands (whose own wives,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Although of fertile wombs, have borne for them"},{"sp":"N","t":"No babies in the house) are also found"},{"sp":"N","t":"Concordant natures so that they at last"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can bulwark their old age with goodly sons."},{"sp":"N","t":"A matter of great moment 'tis in truth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That seeds may mingle readily with seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Suited for procreation, and that thick"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should mix with fluid seeds, with thick the fluid."},{"sp":"N","t":"And in this business 'tis of some import"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon what diet life is nourished:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For some foods thicken seeds within our members,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And others thin them out and waste away."},{"sp":"N","t":"And in what modes the fond delight itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is carried on—this too importeth vastly."},{"sp":"N","t":"For commonly 'tis thought that wives conceive"},{"sp":"N","t":"More readily in manner of wild-beasts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"After the custom of the four-foot breeds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because so postured, with the breasts beneath"},{"sp":"N","t":"And buttocks then upreared, the seeds can take"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their proper places. Nor is need the least"},{"sp":"N","t":"For wives to use the motions of blandishment;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For thus the woman hinders and resists"},{"sp":"N","t":"Her own conception, if too joyously"},{"sp":"N","t":"Herself she treats the Venus of the man"},{"sp":"N","t":"With haunches heaving, and with all her bosom"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now yielding like the billows of the sea-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aye, from the ploughshare's even course and track"},{"sp":"N","t":"She throws the furrow, and from proper places"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deflects the spurt of seed. And courtesans"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are thuswise wont to move for their own ends,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To keep from pregnancy and lying in,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all the while to render Venus more"},{"sp":"N","t":"A pleasure for the men—the which meseems"},{"sp":"N","t":"Our wives have never need of."},{"sp":"N","t":"Sometimes too","st":"4.1278"},{"sp":"N","t":"It happens—and through no divinity"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor arrows of Venus—that a sorry chit"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of scanty grace will be beloved by man;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For sometimes she herself by very deeds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By her complying ways, and tidy habits,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will easily accustom thee to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"With her thy life-time—and, moreover, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Long habitude can gender human love,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as an object smitten o'er and o'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"By blows, however lightly, yet at last"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is overcome and wavers. Seest thou not,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, how drops of water falling down"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against the stones at last bore through the stones?"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Book V"},{"sp":"SEC","t":"PROEM"},{"sp":"N","t":"O who can build with puissant breast a song","st":"5.1"},{"sp":"N","t":"Worthy the majesty of these great finds?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or who in words so strong that he can frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fit laudations for deserts of him"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who left us heritors of such vast prizes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By his own breast discovered and sought out?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"There shall be none, methinks, of mortal stock."},{"sp":"N","t":"For if must needs be named for him the name"},{"sp":"N","t":"Demanded by the now known majesty"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of these high matters, then a god was he,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hear me, illustrious Memmius—a god;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who first and chief found out that plan of life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which now is called philosophy, and who"},{"sp":"N","t":"By cunning craft, out of such mighty waves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out of such mighty darkness, moored life"},{"sp":"N","t":"In havens so serene, in light so clear."},{"sp":"N","t":"Compare those old discoveries divine"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of others: lo, according to the tale,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ceres established for mortality"},{"sp":"N","t":"The grain, and Bacchus juice of vine-born grape,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though life might yet without these things abide,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as report saith now some peoples live."},{"sp":"N","t":"But man's well-being was impossible"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without a breast all free. Wherefore the more"},{"sp":"N","t":"That man doth justly seem to us a god,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From whom sweet solaces of life, afar"},{"sp":"N","t":"Distributed o'er populous domains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now soothe the minds of men. But if thou thinkest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Labours of Hercules excel the same,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much farther from true reasoning thou farest."},{"sp":"N","t":"For what could hurt us now that mighty maw"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of Nemeaean Lion, or what the Boar"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who bristled in Arcadia? Or, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O what could Cretan Bull, or Hydra, pest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of Lerna, fenced with vipers venomous?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or what the triple-breasted power of her"},{"sp":"N","t":"The three-fold Geryon..."},{"sp":"N","t":"The sojourners in the Stymphalian fens"},{"sp":"N","t":"So dreadfully offend us, or the Steeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of Thracian Diomedes breathing fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out their nostrils off along the zones"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bistonian and Ismarian? And the Snake,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The dread fierce gazer, guardian of the golden"},{"sp":"N","t":"And gleaming apples of the Hesperides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Coiled round the tree-trunk with tremendous bulk,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O what, again, could he inflict on us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the Atlantic shore and wastes of sea?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where neither one of us approacheth nigh"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor no barbarian ventures. And the rest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of all those monsters slain, even if alive,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unconquered still, what injury could they do?"},{"sp":"N","t":"None, as I guess. For so the glutted earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Swarms even now with savage beasts, even now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is filled with anxious terrors through the woods"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mighty mountains and the forest deeps-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Quarters 'tis ours in general to avoid."},{"sp":"N","t":"But lest the breast be purged, what conflicts then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What perils, must bosom, in our own despite!"},{"sp":"N","t":"O then how great and keen the cares of lust"},{"sp":"N","t":"That split the man distraught! How great the fears!"},{"sp":"N","t":"And lo, the pride, grim greed, and wantonness-"},{"sp":"N","t":"How great the slaughters in their train! and lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Debaucheries and every breed of sloth!"},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore that man who subjugated these,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And from the mind expelled, by words indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not arms, O shall it not be seemly him"},{"sp":"N","t":"To dignify by ranking with the gods?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all the more since he was wont to give,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Concerning the immortal gods themselves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Many pronouncements with a tongue divine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to unfold by his pronouncements all"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of the world."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"ARGUMENT OF THE BOOK AND NEW PROEM AGAINST A TELEOLOGICAL CONCEPT"},{"sp":"N","t":"And walking now","st":"5.55"},{"sp":"N","t":"In his own footprints, I do follow through"},{"sp":"N","t":"His reasonings, and with pronouncements teach"},{"sp":"N","t":"The covenant whereby all things are framed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How under that covenant they must abide"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor ever prevail to abrogate the aeons'"},{"sp":"N","t":"Inexorable decrees,—how (as we've found),"},{"sp":"N","t":"In class of mortal objects, o'er all else,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mind exists of earth-born frame create"},{"sp":"N","t":"And impotent unscathed to abide"},{"sp":"N","t":"Across the mighty aeons, and how come"},{"sp":"N","t":"In sleep those idol-apparitions,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That so befool intelligence when we"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do seem to view a man whom life has left."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus far we've gone; the order of my plan"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath brought me now unto the point where I"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must make report how, too, the universe"},{"sp":"N","t":"Consists of mortal body, born in time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in what modes that congregated stuff"},{"sp":"N","t":"Established itself as earth and sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ocean, and stars, and sun, and ball of moon;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then what living creatures rose from out"},{"sp":"N","t":"The old telluric places, and what ones"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were never born at all; and in what mode"},{"sp":"N","t":"The human race began to name its things"},{"sp":"N","t":"And use the varied speech from man to man;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in what modes hath bosomed in their breasts"},{"sp":"N","t":"That awe of gods, which halloweth in all lands"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fanes, altars, groves, lakes, idols of the gods."},{"sp":"N","t":"Also I shall untangle by what power"},{"sp":"N","t":"The steersman nature guides the sun's courses,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the meanderings of the moon, lest we,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Percase, should fancy that of own free will"},{"sp":"N","t":"They circle their perennial courses round,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Timing their motions for increase of crops"},{"sp":"N","t":"And living creatures, or lest we should think"},{"sp":"N","t":"They roll along by any plan of gods."},{"sp":"N","t":"For even those men who have learned full well"},{"sp":"N","t":"That godheads lead a long life free of care,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If yet meanwhile they wonder by what plan"},{"sp":"N","t":"Things can go on (and chiefly yon high things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Observed o'erhead on the ethereal coasts),"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again are hurried back unto the fears"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of old religion and adopt again"},{"sp":"N","t":"Harsh masters, deemed almighty,—wretched men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unwitting what can be and what cannot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by what law to each its scope prescribed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its boundary stone that clings so deep in Time."},{"sp":"N","t":"But for the rest,—lest we delay thee here","st":"5.91"},{"sp":"N","t":"Longer by empty promises—behold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before all else, the seas, the lands, the sky:"},{"sp":"N","t":"O Memmius, their threefold nature, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their bodies three, three aspects so unlike,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Three frames so vast, a single day shall give"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto annihilation! Then shall crash"},{"sp":"N","t":"That massive form and fabric of the world"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sustained so many aeons! Nor do I"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fail to perceive how strange and marvellous"},{"sp":"N","t":"This fact must strike the intellect of man,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Annihilation of the sky and earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"That is to be,—and with what toil of words"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis mine to prove the same; as happens oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"When once ye offer to man's listening ears"},{"sp":"N","t":"Something before unheard of, but may not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Subject it to the view of eyes for him"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor put it into hand—the sight and touch,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereby the opened highways of belief"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lead most directly into human breast"},{"sp":"N","t":"And regions of intelligence. But yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"I will speak out. The fact itself, perchance,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will force belief in these my words, and thou"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mayst see, in little time, tremendously"},{"sp":"N","t":"With risen commotions of the lands all things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Quaking to pieces—which afar from us"},{"sp":"N","t":"May she, the steersman Nature, guide: and may"},{"sp":"N","t":"Reason, O rather than the fact itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Persuade us that all things can be o'erthrown"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sink with awful-sounding breakage down!"},{"sp":"N","t":"But ere on this I take a step to utter","st":"5.110"},{"sp":"N","t":"Oracles holier and soundlier based"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than ever the Pythian pronounced for men"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out the tripod and the Delphian laurel,"},{"sp":"N","t":"I will unfold for thee with learned words"},{"sp":"N","t":"Many a consolation, lest perchance,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still bridled by religion, thou suppose"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lands, sun, and sky, sea, constellations, moon,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must dure forever, as of frame divine-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so conclude that it is just that those,"},{"sp":"N","t":"(After the manner of the Giants), should all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pay the huge penalties for monstrous crime,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who by their reasonings do overshake"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ramparts of the universe and wish"},{"sp":"N","t":"There to put out the splendid sun of heaven,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Branding with mortal talk immortal things-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though these same things are even so far removed"},{"sp":"N","t":"From any touch of deity and seem"},{"sp":"N","t":"So far unworthy of numbering with the gods,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That well they may be thought to furnish rather"},{"sp":"N","t":"A goodly instance of the sort of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"That lack the living motion, living sense."},{"sp":"N","t":"For sure 'tis quite beside the mark to think"},{"sp":"N","t":"That judgment and the nature of the mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"In any kind of body can exist-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Just as in ether can't exist a tree,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor clouds in the salt sea, nor in the fields"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can fishes live, nor blood in timber be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor sap in boulders: fixed and arranged"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where everything may grow and have its place."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus nature of mind cannot arise alone"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without the body, nor have its being far"},{"sp":"N","t":"From thews and blood. Yet if 'twere possible?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much rather might this very power of mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be in the head, the shoulders, or the heels,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, born in any part soever, yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the same man, in the same vessel abide"},{"sp":"N","t":"But since within this body even of ours"},{"sp":"N","t":"Stands fixed and appears arranged sure"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where soul and mind can each exist and grow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deny we must the more that they can dure"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outside the body and the breathing form"},{"sp":"N","t":"In rotting clods of earth, in the sun's fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In water, or in ether's skiey coasts."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore these things no whit are furnished"},{"sp":"N","t":"With sense divine, since never can they be"},{"sp":"N","t":"With life-force quickened."},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise, thou canst ne'er","st":"5.146"},{"sp":"N","t":"Believe the sacred seats of gods are here"},{"sp":"N","t":"In any regions of this mundane world;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Indeed, the nature of the gods, so subtle,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So far removed from these our senses, scarce"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is seen even by intelligence of mind."},{"sp":"N","t":"And since they've ever eluded touch and thrust"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of human hands, they cannot reach to grasp"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aught tangible to us. For what may not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Itself be touched in turn can never touch."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, besides, also their seats must be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unlike these seats of ours,—even subtle too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As meet for subtle essence—as I'll prove"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hereafter unto thee with large discourse."},{"sp":"N","t":"Further, to say that for the sake of men"},{"sp":"N","t":"They willed to prepare this world's magnificence,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that 'tis therefore duty and behoof"},{"sp":"N","t":"To praise the work of gods as worthy praise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that 'tis sacrilege for men to shake"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ever by any force from out their seats"},{"sp":"N","t":"What hath been stablished by the Forethought old"},{"sp":"N","t":"To everlasting for races of mankind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that 'tis sacrilege to assault by words"},{"sp":"N","t":"And overtopple all from base to beam,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Memmius, such notions to concoct and pile,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is verily—to dote. Our gratefulness,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O what emoluments could it confer"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon Immortals and upon the Blessed"},{"sp":"N","t":"That they should take a step to manage aught"},{"sp":"N","t":"For sake of us? Or what new factor could,"},{"sp":"N","t":"After so long a time, inveigle them-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The hitherto reposeful—to desire"},{"sp":"N","t":"To change their former life? For rather he"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whom old things chafe seems likely to rejoice"},{"sp":"N","t":"At new; but one that in fore-passed time"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath chanced upon no ill, through goodly years,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O what could ever enkindle in such an one"},{"sp":"N","t":"Passion for strange experiment? Or what"},{"sp":"N","t":"The evil for us, if we had ne'er been born?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As though, forsooth, in darkling realms and woe"},{"sp":"N","t":"Our life were lying till should dawn at last"},{"sp":"N","t":"The day-spring of creation! Whosoever"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath been begotten wills perforce to stay"},{"sp":"N","t":"In life, so long as fond delight detains;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But whoso ne'er hath tasted love of life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And ne'er was in the count of living things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What hurts it him that he was never born?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence, further, first was planted in the gods"},{"sp":"N","t":"The archetype for gendering the world"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the fore-notion of what man is like,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that they knew and pre-conceived with mind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Just what they wished to make? Or how were known"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ever the energies of primal germs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what those germs, by interchange of place,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could thus produce, if nature's self had not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Given example for creating all?"},{"sp":"N","t":"For in such wise primordials of things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Many in many modes, astir by blows"},{"sp":"N","t":"From immemorial aeons, in motion too"},{"sp":"N","t":"By their own weights, have evermore been wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be so borne along and in all modes"},{"sp":"N","t":"To meet together and to try all sorts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, by combining one with other, they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are powerful to create, that thus it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"No marvel now, if they have also fallen"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into arrangements such, and if they've passed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into vibrations such, as those whereby"},{"sp":"N","t":"This sum of things is carried on to-day"},{"sp":"N","t":"By fixed renewal."},{"sp":"N","t":"But knew I never what","st":"5.195"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds primordial were, yet would I dare"},{"sp":"N","t":"This to affirm, even from deep judgments based"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the ways and conduct of the skies-"},{"sp":"N","t":"This to maintain by many a fact besides-"},{"sp":"N","t":"That in no wise the nature of all things"},{"sp":"N","t":"For us was fashioned by a power divine-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So great the faults it stands encumbered with."},{"sp":"N","t":"First, mark all regions which are overarched"},{"sp":"N","t":"By the prodigious reaches of the sky:"},{"sp":"N","t":"One yawning part thereof the mountain-chains"},{"sp":"N","t":"And forests of the beasts do have and hold;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And cliffs, and desert fens, and wastes of sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Which sunder afar the beaches of the lands)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Possess it merely; and, again, thereof"},{"sp":"N","t":"Well-nigh two-thirds intolerable heat"},{"sp":"N","t":"And a perpetual fall of frost doth rob"},{"sp":"N","t":"From mortal kind. And what is left to till,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even that the force of nature would o'errun"},{"sp":"N","t":"With brambles, did not human force oppose,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Long wont for livelihood to groan and sweat"},{"sp":"N","t":"Over the two-pronged mattock and to cleave"},{"sp":"N","t":"The soil in twain by pressing on the plough."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Unless, by the ploughshare turning the fruitful clods"},{"sp":"N","t":"And kneading the mould, we quicken into birth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"[The crops] spontaneously could not come up"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the free bright air. Even then sometimes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When things acquired by the sternest toil"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are now in leaf, are now in blossom all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Either the skiey sun with baneful heats"},{"sp":"N","t":"Parches, or sudden rains or chilling rime"},{"sp":"N","t":"Destroys, or flaws of winds with furious whirl"},{"sp":"N","t":"Torment and twist. Beside these matters, why"},{"sp":"N","t":"Doth nature feed and foster on land and sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"The dreadful breed of savage beasts, the foes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the human clan? Why do the seasons bring"},{"sp":"N","t":"Distempers with them? Wherefore stalks at large"},{"sp":"N","t":"Death, so untimely? Then, again, the babe,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like to the castaway of the raging surf,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lies naked on the ground, speechless, in want"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of every help for life, when nature first"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath poured him forth upon the shores of light"},{"sp":"N","t":"With birth-pangs from within the mother's womb,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And with a plaintive wail he fills the place,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As well befitting one for whom remains"},{"sp":"N","t":"In life a journey through so many ills."},{"sp":"N","t":"But all the flocks and herds and all wild beasts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Come forth and grow, nor need the little rattles,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor must be treated to the humouring nurse's"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dear, broken chatter; nor seek they divers clothes"},{"sp":"N","t":"To suit the changing skies; nor need, in fine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor arms, nor lofty ramparts, wherewithal"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their own to guard—because the earth herself"},{"sp":"N","t":"And nature, artificer of the world, bring forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aboundingly all things for all."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"THE WORLD IS NOT ETERNAL"},{"sp":"N","t":"And first,","st":"5.235"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since body of earth and water, air's light breath,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fiery exhalations (of which four"},{"sp":"N","t":"This sum of things is seen to be compact)"},{"sp":"N","t":"So all have birth and perishable frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus the whole nature of the world itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must be conceived as perishable too."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, verily, those things of which we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"The parts and members to have birth in time"},{"sp":"N","t":"And perishable shapes, those same we mark"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be invariably born in time"},{"sp":"N","t":"And born to die. And therefore when I see"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mightiest members and the parts of this"},{"sp":"N","t":"Our world consumed and begot again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis mine to know that also sky above"},{"sp":"N","t":"And earth beneath began of old in time"},{"sp":"N","t":"And shall in time go under to disaster."},{"sp":"N","t":"And lest in these affairs thou deemest me"},{"sp":"N","t":"To have seized upon this point by sleight to serve"},{"sp":"N","t":"My own caprice—because I have assumed"},{"sp":"N","t":"That earth and fire are mortal things indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And have not doubted water and the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Both perish too and have affirmed the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be again begotten and wax big-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mark well the argument: in first place, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some certain parts of earth, grievously parched"},{"sp":"N","t":"By unremitting suns, and trampled on"},{"sp":"N","t":"By a vast throng of feet, exhale abroad"},{"sp":"N","t":"A powdery haze and flying clouds of dust,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which the stout winds disperse in the whole air."},{"sp":"N","t":"A part, moreover, of her sod and soil"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is summoned to inundation by the rains;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And rivers graze and gouge the banks away."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, whatever takes a part its own"},{"sp":"N","t":"In fostering and increasing [aught]..."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Is rendered back; and since, beyond a doubt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Earth, the all-mother, is beheld to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise the common sepulchre of things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore thou seest her minished of her plenty,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then again augmented with new growth."},{"sp":"N","t":"And for the rest, that sea, and streams, and springs","st":"5.261"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forever with new waters overflow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that perennially the fluids well,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Needeth no words—the mighty flux itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of multitudinous waters round about"},{"sp":"N","t":"Declareth this. But whatso water first"},{"sp":"N","t":"Streams up is ever straightway carried off,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus it comes to pass that all in all"},{"sp":"N","t":"There is no overflow; in part because"},{"sp":"N","t":"The burly winds (that over-sweep amain)"},{"sp":"N","t":"And skiey sun (that with his rays dissolves)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do minish the level seas; in part because"},{"sp":"N","t":"The water is diffused underground"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through all the lands. The brine is filtered off,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then the liquid stuff seeps back again"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all regathers at the river-heads,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence in fresh-water currents on it flows"},{"sp":"N","t":"Over the lands, adown the channels which"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were cleft erstwhile and erstwhile bore along"},{"sp":"N","t":"The liquid-footed floods."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, then, of air","st":"5.273"},{"sp":"N","t":"I'll speak, which hour by hour in all its body"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is changed innumerably. For whatso'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"Streams up in dust or vapour off of things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same is all and always borne along"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the mighty ocean of the air;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And did not air in turn restore to things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bodies, and thus recruit them as they stream,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All things by this time had resolved been"},{"sp":"N","t":"And changed into air. Therefore it never"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ceases to be engendered off of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to return to things, since verily"},{"sp":"N","t":"In constant flux do all things stream."},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise,","st":"5.281"},{"sp":"N","t":"The abounding well-spring of the liquid light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ethereal sun, doth flood the heaven o'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"With constant flux of radiance ever new,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And with fresh light supplies the place of light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the instant. For whatever effulgence"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath first streamed off, no matter where it falls,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is lost unto the sun. And this 'tis thine"},{"sp":"N","t":"To know from these examples: soon as clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have first begun to under-pass the sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, as it were, to rend the rays of light"},{"sp":"N","t":"In twain, at once the lower part of them"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is lost entire, and earth is overcast"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where'er the thunderheads are rolled along-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So know thou mayst that things forever need"},{"sp":"N","t":"A fresh replenishment of gleam and glow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And each effulgence, foremost flashed forth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perisheth one by one. Nor otherwise"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can things be seen in sunlight, lest alway"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fountain-head of light supply new light."},{"sp":"N","t":"Indeed your earthly beacons of the night,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The hanging lampions and the torches, bright"},{"sp":"N","t":"With darting gleams and dense with livid soot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do hurry in like manner to supply"},{"sp":"N","t":"With ministering heat new light amain;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are all alive to quiver with their fires,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are so alive, that thus the light ne'er leaves"},{"sp":"N","t":"The spots it shines on, as if rent in twain:"},{"sp":"N","t":"So speedily is its destruction veiled"},{"sp":"N","t":"By the swift birth of flame from all the fires."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, then, we must suppose that sun and moon"},{"sp":"N","t":"And stars dart forth their light from under-births"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ever and ever new, and whatso flames"},{"sp":"N","t":"First rise do perish always one by one-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest, haply, thou shouldst think they each endure"},{"sp":"N","t":"Inviolable."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, perceivest not","st":"5.306"},{"sp":"N","t":"How stones are also conquered by Time?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not how the lofty towers ruin down,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And boulders crumble?- Not how shrines of gods"},{"sp":"N","t":"And idols crack outworn?- Nor how indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"The holy Influence hath yet no power"},{"sp":"N","t":"There to postpone the Terminals of Fate,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or headway make 'gainst Nature's fixed decrees?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, behold we not the monuments"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of heroes, now in ruins, asking us,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In their turn likewise, if we don't believe"},{"sp":"N","t":"They also age with eld? Behold we not"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rended basalt ruining amain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down from the lofty mountains, powerless"},{"sp":"N","t":"To dure and dree the mighty forces there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of finite time?- for they would never fall"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rended asudden, if from infinite Past"},{"sp":"N","t":"They had prevailed against all engin'ries"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the assaulting aeons, with no crash."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, now look at This, which round, above,","st":"5.318"},{"sp":"N","t":"Contains the whole earth in its one embrace:"},{"sp":"N","t":"If from itself it procreates all things-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As some men tell—and takes them to itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"When once destroyed, entirely must it be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of mortal birth and body; for whate'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out itself giveth to other things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Increase and food, the same perforce must be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Minished, and then recruited when it takes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Things back into itself."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides all this,","st":"5.324"},{"sp":"N","t":"If there had been no origin-in-birth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of lands and sky, and they had ever been"},{"sp":"N","t":"The everlasting, why, ere Theban war"},{"sp":"N","t":"And obsequies of Troy, have other bards"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not also chanted other high affairs?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whither have sunk so oft so many deeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of heroes? Why do those deeds live no more,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ingrafted in eternal monuments"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of glory? Verily, I guess, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"The Sum is new, and of a recent date"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of our universe, and had"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not long ago its own exordium."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, even now some arts are being still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Refined, still increased: now unto ships"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is being added many a new device;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And but the other day musician-folk"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gave birth to melic sounds of organing;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, then, this nature, this account of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath been discovered latterly, and I"},{"sp":"N","t":"Myself have been discovered only now,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As first among the first, able to turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same into ancestral Roman speech."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet if, percase, thou deemest that ere this"},{"sp":"N","t":"Existed all things even the same, but that"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perished the cycles of the human race"},{"sp":"N","t":"In fiery exhalations, or cities fell"},{"sp":"N","t":"By some tremendous quaking of the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or rivers in fury, after constant rains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had plunged forth across the lands of earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"And whelmed the towns—then, all the more must thou"},{"sp":"N","t":"Confess, defeated by the argument,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That there shall be annihilation too"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of lands and sky. For at a time when things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were being taxed by maladies so great,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so great perils, if some cause more fell"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had then assailed them, far and wide they would"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have gone to disaster and supreme collapse."},{"sp":"N","t":"And by no other reasoning are we"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seen to be mortal, save that all of us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sicken in turn with those same maladies"},{"sp":"N","t":"With which have sickened in the past those men"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whom nature hath removed from life."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again,","st":"5.351"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whatever abides eternal must indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Either repel all strokes, because 'tis made"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of solid body, and permit no entrance"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of aught with power to sunder from within"},{"sp":"N","t":"The parts compact—as are those seeds of stuff"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whose nature we've exhibited before;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else be able to endure through time"},{"sp":"N","t":"For this: because they are from blows exempt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As is the void, the which abides untouched,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unsmit by any stroke; or else because"},{"sp":"N","t":"There is no room around, whereto things can,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As 'twere, depart in dissolution all,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as the sum of sums eternal is,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without or place beyond whereto things may"},{"sp":"N","t":"Asunder fly, or bodies which can smite,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus dissolve them by the blows of might."},{"sp":"N","t":"But not of solid body, as I've shown,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exists the nature of the world, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"In things is intermingled there a void;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor is the world yet as the void, nor are,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Moreover, bodies lacking which, percase,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rising from out the infinite, can fell"},{"sp":"N","t":"With fury-whirlwinds all this sum of things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or bring upon them other cataclysm"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of peril strange; and yonder, too, abides"},{"sp":"N","t":"The infinite space and the profound abyss-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereinto, lo, the ramparts of the world"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can yet be shivered. Or some other power"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can pound upon them till they perish all."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus is the door of doom, O nowise barred"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against the sky, against the sun and earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"And deep-sea waters, but wide open stands"},{"sp":"N","t":"And gloats upon them, monstrous and agape."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, again, 'tis needful to confess"},{"sp":"N","t":"That these same things are born in time; for things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which are of mortal body could indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Never from infinite past until to-day"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have spurned the multitudinous assaults"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the immeasurable aeons old."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, since battle so fiercely one with other","st":"5.380"},{"sp":"N","t":"The four most mighty members the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aroused in an all unholy war,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seest not that there may be for them an end"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the long strife?- Or when the skiey sun"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all the heat have won dominion o'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sucked-up waters all?- And this they try"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still to accomplish, though as yet they fail,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For so aboundingly the streams supply"},{"sp":"N","t":"New store of waters that 'tis rather they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who menace the world with inundations vast"},{"sp":"N","t":"From forth the unplumbed chasms of the sea."},{"sp":"N","t":"But vain—since winds (that over-sweep amain)"},{"sp":"N","t":"And skiey sun (that with his rays dissolves)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do minish the level seas and trust their power"},{"sp":"N","t":"To dry up all, before the waters can"},{"sp":"N","t":"Arrive at the end of their endeavouring."},{"sp":"N","t":"Breathing such vasty warfare, they contend"},{"sp":"N","t":"In balanced strife the one with other still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Concerning mighty issues,—though indeed"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fire was once the more victorious,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And once—as goes the tale—the water won"},{"sp":"N","t":"A kingdom in the fields. For fire o'ermastered"},{"sp":"N","t":"And licked up many things and burnt away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What time the impetuous horses of the Sun"},{"sp":"N","t":"Snatched Phaethon headlong from his skiey road"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down the whole ether and over all the lands."},{"sp":"N","t":"But the omnipotent Father in keen wrath"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then with the sudden smite of thunderbolt"},{"sp":"N","t":"Did hurl the mighty-minded hero off"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those horses to the earth. And Sol, his sire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Meeting him as he fell, caught up in hand"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ever-blazing lampion of the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And drave together the pell-mell horses there"},{"sp":"N","t":"And yoked them all a-tremble, and amain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Steering them over along their own old road,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Restored the cosmos,—as forsooth we hear"},{"sp":"N","t":"From songs of ancient poets of the Greeks-"},{"sp":"N","t":"A tale too far away from truth, meseems."},{"sp":"N","t":"For fire can win when from the infinite"},{"sp":"N","t":"Has risen a larger throng of particles"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of fiery stuff; and then its powers succumb,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Somehow subdued again, or else at last"},{"sp":"N","t":"It shrivels in torrid atmospheres the world."},{"sp":"N","t":"And whilom water too began to win-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As goes the story—when it overwhelmed"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lives of men with billows; and thereafter,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When all that force of water-stuff which forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out the infinite had risen up"},{"sp":"N","t":"Did now retire, as somehow turned aside,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rain-storms stopped, and streams their fury checked."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"FORMATION OF THE WORLD AND ASTRONOMICAL QUESTIONS"},{"sp":"N","t":"But in what modes that conflux of first-stuff","st":"5.416"},{"sp":"N","t":"Did found the multitudinous universe"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of earth, and sky, and the unfathomed deeps"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of ocean, and courses of the sun and moon,"},{"sp":"N","t":"I'll now in order tell. For of a truth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Neither by counsel did the primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Stablish themselves, as by keen act of mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each in its proper place; nor did they make,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forsooth, a compact how each germ should move;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But, lo, because primordials of things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Many in many modes, astir by blows"},{"sp":"N","t":"From immemorial aeons, in motion too"},{"sp":"N","t":"By their own weights, have evermore been wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be so borne along and in all modes"},{"sp":"N","t":"To meet together and to try all sorts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, by combining one with other, they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are powerful to create: because of this"},{"sp":"N","t":"It comes to pass that those primordials,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Diffused far and wide through mighty aeons,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The while they unions try, and motions too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of every kind, meet at the last amain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so become oft the commencements fit"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of mighty things—earth, sea, and sky, and race"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of living creatures."},{"sp":"N","t":"In that long-ago","st":"5.432"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wheel of the sun could nowhere be discerned"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flying far up with its abounding blaze,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor constellations of the mighty world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor ocean, nor heaven, nor even earth nor air."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor aught of things like unto things of ours"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could then be seen—but only some strange storm"},{"sp":"N","t":"And a prodigious hurly-burly mass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Compounded of all kinds of primal germs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whose battling discords in disorder kept"},{"sp":"N","t":"Interstices, and paths, coherencies,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And weights, and blows, encounterings, and motions,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because, by reason of their forms unlike"},{"sp":"N","t":"And varied shapes, they could not all thuswise"},{"sp":"N","t":"Remain conjoined nor harmoniously"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have interplay of movements. But from there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Portions began to fly asunder, and like"},{"sp":"N","t":"With like to join, and to block out a world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to divide its members and dispose"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its mightier parts—that is, to set secure"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lofty heavens from the lands, and cause"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sea to spread with waters separate,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fires of ether separate and pure"},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise to congregate apart."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, lo,","st":"5.449"},{"sp":"N","t":"First came together the earthy particles"},{"sp":"N","t":"(As being heavy and intertangled) there"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the mid-region, and all began to take"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lowest abodes; and ever the more they got"},{"sp":"N","t":"One with another intertangled, the more"},{"sp":"N","t":"They pressed from out their mass those particles"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which were to form the sea, the stars, the sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And moon, and ramparts of the mighty world-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For these consist of seeds more smooth and round"},{"sp":"N","t":"And of much smaller elements than earth."},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus it was that ether, fraught with fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"First broke away from out the earthen parts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Athrough the innumerable pores of earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And raised itself aloft, and with itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bore lightly off the many starry fires;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And not far otherwise we often see"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"And the still lakes and the perennial streams"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exhale a mist, and even as earth herself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is seen at times to smoke, when first at dawn"},{"sp":"N","t":"The light of the sun, the many-rayed, begins"},{"sp":"N","t":"To redden into gold, over the grass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Begemmed with dew. When all of these are brought"},{"sp":"N","t":"Together overhead, the clouds on high"},{"sp":"N","t":"With now concreted body weave a cover"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beneath the heavens. And thuswise ether too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Light and diffusive, with concreted body"},{"sp":"N","t":"On all sides spread, on all sides bent itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into a dome, and, far and wide diffused"},{"sp":"N","t":"On unto every region on all sides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus hedged all else within its greedy clasp."},{"sp":"N","t":"Hard upon ether came the origins"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of sun and moon, whose globes revolve in air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Midway between the earth and mightiest ether,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For neither took them, since they weighed too little"},{"sp":"N","t":"To sink and settle, but too much to glide"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the upmost shores; and yet they are"},{"sp":"N","t":"In such a wise midway between the twain"},{"sp":"N","t":"As ever to whirl their living bodies round,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And ever to dure as parts of the wide Whole;"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the same fashion as certain members may"},{"sp":"N","t":"In us remain at rest, whilst others move."},{"sp":"N","t":"When, then, these substances had been withdrawn,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Amain the earth, where now extend the vast"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cerulean zones of all the level seas,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Caved in, and down along the hollows poured"},{"sp":"N","t":"The whirlpools of her brine; and day by day"},{"sp":"N","t":"The more the tides of ether and rays of sun"},{"sp":"N","t":"On every side constrained into one mass"},{"sp":"N","t":"The earth by lashing it again, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon its outer edges (so that then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Being thus beat upon, 'twas all condensed"},{"sp":"N","t":"About its proper centre), ever the more"},{"sp":"N","t":"The salty sweat, from out its body squeezed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Augmented ocean and the fields of foam"},{"sp":"N","t":"By seeping through its frame, and all the more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those many particles of heat and air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Escaping, began to fly aloft, and form,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By condensation there afar from earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The high refulgent circuits of the heavens."},{"sp":"N","t":"The plains began to sink, and windy slopes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the high mountains to increase; for rocks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could not subside, nor all the parts of ground"},{"sp":"N","t":"Settle alike to one same level there."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, then, the massy weight of earth stood firm","st":"5.495"},{"sp":"N","t":"With now concreted body, when (as 'twere)"},{"sp":"N","t":"All of the slime of the world, heavy and gross,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had run together and settled at the bottom,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like lees or bilge. Then ocean, then the air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then ether herself, the fraught-with-fire, were all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Left with their liquid bodies pure and free,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And each more lighter than the next below;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And ether, most light and liquid of the three,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Floats on above the long aerial winds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor with the brawling of the winds of air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mingles its liquid body. It doth leave"},{"sp":"N","t":"All there—those under-realms below her heights-"},{"sp":"N","t":"There to be overset in whirlwinds wild,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Doth leave all there to brawl in wayward gusts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst, gliding with a fixed impulse still,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Itself it bears its fires along. For, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That ether can flow thus steadily on, on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With one unaltered urge, the Pontus proves-"},{"sp":"N","t":"That sea which floweth forth with fixed tides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Keeping one onward tenor as it glides."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now let us sing what makes the stars to move.","st":"5.509"},{"sp":"N","t":"In first place, if the mighty sphere of heaven"},{"sp":"N","t":"Revolveth round, then needs we must aver"},{"sp":"N","t":"That on the upper and the under pole"},{"sp":"N","t":"Presses a certain air, and from without"},{"sp":"N","t":"Confines them and encloseth at each end;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that, moreover, another air above"},{"sp":"N","t":"Streams on athwart the top of the sphere and tends"},{"sp":"N","t":"In same direction as are rolled along"},{"sp":"N","t":"The glittering stars of the eternal world;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or that another still streams on below"},{"sp":"N","t":"To whirl the sphere from under up and on"},{"sp":"N","t":"In opposite direction—as we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rivers turn the wheels and water-scoops."},{"sp":"N","t":"It may be also that the heavens do all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Remain at rest, whilst yet are borne along"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lucid constellations; either because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Swift tides of ether are by sky enclosed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And whirl around, seeking a passage out,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And everywhere make roll the starry fires"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through the Summanian regions of the sky;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else because some air, streaming along"},{"sp":"N","t":"From an eternal quarter off beyond,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whileth the driven fires, or, then, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fires themselves have power to creep along,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Going wherever their food invites and calls,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And feeding their flaming bodies everywhere"},{"sp":"N","t":"Throughout the sky. Yet which of these is cause"},{"sp":"N","t":"In this our world 'tis hard to say for sure;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But what can be throughout the universe,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In divers worlds on divers plan create,"},{"sp":"N","t":"This only do I show, and follow on"},{"sp":"N","t":"To assign unto the motions of the stars"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even several causes which 'tis possible"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exist throughout the universal All;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of which yet one must be the cause even here"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which maketh motion for our constellations."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet to decide which one of them it be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is not the least the business of a man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Advancing step by cautious step, as I."},{"sp":"N","t":"And that the earth may there abide at rest","st":"5.534"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the mid-region of the world, it needs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must vanish bit by bit in weight and lessen,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And have another substance underneath,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Conjoined to it from its earliest age"},{"sp":"N","t":"In linked unison with the vasty world's"},{"sp":"N","t":"Realms of the air in which it roots and lives."},{"sp":"N","t":"On this account, the earth is not a load,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor presses down on winds of air beneath;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as unto a man his members be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without all weight—the head is not a load"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the neck; nor do we feel the whole"},{"sp":"N","t":"Weight of the body to centre in the feet."},{"sp":"N","t":"But whatso weights come on us from without,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Weights laid upon us, these harass and chafe,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though often far lighter. For to such degree"},{"sp":"N","t":"It matters always what the innate powers"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of any given thing may be. The earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was, then, no alien substance fetched amain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And from no alien firmament cast down"},{"sp":"N","t":"On alien air; but was conceived, like air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the first origin of this the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As a fixed portion of the same, as now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Our members are seen to be a part of us."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, the earth, when of a sudden shook"},{"sp":"N","t":"By the big thunder, doth with her motion shake"},{"sp":"N","t":"All that's above her—which she ne'er could do"},{"sp":"N","t":"By any means, were earth not bounden fast"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the great world's realms of air and sky:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For they cohere together with common roots,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Conjoined both, even from their earliest age,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In linked unison. Aye, seest thou not"},{"sp":"N","t":"That this most subtle energy of soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"Supports our body, though so heavy a weight,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because, indeed, 'tis with it so conjoined"},{"sp":"N","t":"In linked unison? What power, in sum,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can raise with agile leap our body aloft,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Save energy of mind which steers the limbs?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now seest thou not how powerful may be"},{"sp":"N","t":"A subtle nature, when conjoined it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"With heavy body, as air is with the earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Conjoined, and energy of mind with us?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor can the sun's wheel larger be by much","st":"5.564"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor its own blaze much less than either seems"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto our senses. For from whatso spaces"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fires have the power on us to cast their beams"},{"sp":"N","t":"And blow their scorching exhalations forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against our members, those same distances"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take nothing by those intervals away"},{"sp":"N","t":"From bulk of flames; and to the sight the fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is nothing shrunken. Therefore, since the heat"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the outpoured light of skiey sun"},{"sp":"N","t":"Arrive our senses and caress our limbs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Form too and bigness of the sun must look"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even here from earth just as they really be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that thou canst scarce nothing take or add."},{"sp":"N","t":"And whether the journeying moon illuminate"},{"sp":"N","t":"The regions round with bastard beams, or throw"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off her proper body her own light,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whichever it be, she journeys with a form"},{"sp":"N","t":"Naught larger than the form doth seem to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which we with eyes of ours perceive. For all"},{"sp":"N","t":"The far removed objects of our gaze"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seem through much air confused in their look"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ere minished in their bigness. Wherefore, moon,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since she presents bright look and clear-cut form,"},{"sp":"N","t":"May there on high by us on earth be seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"Just as she is with extreme bounds defined,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And just of the size. And lastly, whatso fires"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of ether thou from earth beholdest, these"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou mayst consider as possibly of size"},{"sp":"N","t":"The least bit less, or larger by a hair"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than they appear—since whatso fires we view"},{"sp":"N","t":"Here in the lands of earth are seen to change"},{"sp":"N","t":"From time to time their size to less or more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Only the least, when more or less away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So long as still they bicker clear, and still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their glow's perceived."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor need there be for men","st":"5.592"},{"sp":"N","t":"Astonishment that yonder sun so small"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can yet send forth so great a light as fills"},{"sp":"N","t":"Oceans and all the lands and sky aflood,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And with its fiery exhalations steeps"},{"sp":"N","t":"The world at large. For it may be, indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That one vast-flowing well-spring of the whole"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wide world from here hath opened and out-gushed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And shot its light abroad; because thuswise"},{"sp":"N","t":"The elements of fiery exhalations"},{"sp":"N","t":"From all the world around together come,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thuswise flow into a bulk so big"},{"sp":"N","t":"That from one single fountain-head may stream"},{"sp":"N","t":"This heat and light. And seest thou not, indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How widely one small water-spring may wet"},{"sp":"N","t":"The meadow-lands at times and flood the fields?"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis even possible, besides, that heat"},{"sp":"N","t":"From forth the sun's own fire, albeit that fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be not a great, may permeate the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the fierce hot—if but, perchance, the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be of condition and so tempered then"},{"sp":"N","t":"As to be kindled, even when beat upon"},{"sp":"N","t":"Only by little particles of heat-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Just as we sometimes see the standing grain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or stubble straw in conflagration all"},{"sp":"N","t":"From one lone spark. And possibly the sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Agleam on high with rosy lampion,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Possesses about him with invisible heats"},{"sp":"N","t":"A plenteous fire, by no effulgence marked,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that he maketh, he, the Fraught-with-fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Increase to such degree the force of rays."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor is there one sure cause revealed to men","st":"5.614"},{"sp":"N","t":"How the sun journeys from his summer haunts"},{"sp":"N","t":"On to the mid-most winter turning-points"},{"sp":"N","t":"In Capricorn, the thence reverting veers"},{"sp":"N","t":"Back to solstitial goals of Cancer; nor"},{"sp":"N","t":"How 'tis the moon is seen each month to cross"},{"sp":"N","t":"That very distance which in traversing"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sun consumes the measure of a year."},{"sp":"N","t":"I say, no one clear reason hath been given"},{"sp":"N","t":"For these affairs. Yet chief in likelihood"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seemeth the doctrine which the holy thought"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of great Democritus lays down: that ever"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nearer the constellations be to earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"The less can they by whirling of the sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be borne along, because those skiey powers"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of speed aloft do vanish and decrease"},{"sp":"N","t":"In under-regions, and the sun is thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Left by degrees behind amongst those signs"},{"sp":"N","t":"That follow after, since the sun he lies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Far down below the starry signs that blaze;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the moon lags even tardier than the sun:"},{"sp":"N","t":"In just so far as is her course removed"},{"sp":"N","t":"From upper heaven and nigh unto the lands,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In just so far she fails to keep the pace"},{"sp":"N","t":"With starry signs above; for just so far"},{"sp":"N","t":"As feebler is the whirl that bears her on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Being, indeed, still lower than the sun),"},{"sp":"N","t":"In just so far do all the starry signs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Circling around, o'ertake her and o'erpass."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore it happens that the moon appears"},{"sp":"N","t":"More swiftly to return to any sign"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the Zodiac, than doth the sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because those signs do visit her again"},{"sp":"N","t":"More swiftly than they visit the great sun."},{"sp":"N","t":"It can be also that two streams of air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alternately at fixed periods"},{"sp":"N","t":"Blow out from transverse regions of the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of which the one may thrust the sun away"},{"sp":"N","t":"From summer-signs to mid-most winter goals"},{"sp":"N","t":"And rigors of the cold, and the other then"},{"sp":"N","t":"May cast him back from icy shades of chill"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even to the heat-fraught regions and the signs"},{"sp":"N","t":"That blaze along the Zodiac. So, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"We must suppose the moon and all the stars,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which through the mighty and sidereal years"},{"sp":"N","t":"Roll round in mighty orbits, may be sped"},{"sp":"N","t":"By streams of air from regions alternate."},{"sp":"N","t":"Seest thou not also how the clouds be sped"},{"sp":"N","t":"By contrary winds to regions contrary,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lower clouds diversely from the upper?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, why may yonder stars in ether there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along their mighty orbits not be borne"},{"sp":"N","t":"By currents opposite the one to other?"},{"sp":"N","t":"But night o'erwhelms the lands with vasty murk","st":"5.650"},{"sp":"N","t":"Either when sun, after his diurnal course,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath walked the ultimate regions of the sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"And wearily hath panted forth his fires,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shivered by their long journeying and wasted"},{"sp":"N","t":"By traversing the multitudinous air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else because the self-same force that drave"},{"sp":"N","t":"His orb along above the lands compels"},{"sp":"N","t":"Him then to turn his course beneath the lands."},{"sp":"N","t":"Matuta also at a fixed hour"},{"sp":"N","t":"Spreadeth the roseate morning out along"},{"sp":"N","t":"The coasts of heaven and deploys the light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Either because the self-same sun, returning"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the lands, aspires to seize the sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Striving to set it blazing with his rays"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ere he himself appear, or else because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fires then will congregate and many seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of heat are wont, even at a fixed time,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To stream together—gendering evermore"},{"sp":"N","t":"New suns and light. Just so the story goes"},{"sp":"N","t":"That from the Idaean mountain-tops are seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dispersed fires upon the break of day"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which thence combine, as 'twere, into one ball"},{"sp":"N","t":"And form an orb. Nor yet in these affairs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is aught for wonder that these seeds of fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can thus together stream at time so fixed"},{"sp":"N","t":"And shape anew the splendour of the sun."},{"sp":"N","t":"For many facts we see which come to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"At fixed time in all things: burgeon shrubs"},{"sp":"N","t":"At fixed time, and at a fixed time"},{"sp":"N","t":"They cast their flowers; and Eld commands the teeth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At time as surely fixed, to drop away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And Youth commands the growing boy to bloom"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the soft down and let from both his cheeks"},{"sp":"N","t":"The soft beard fall. And lastly, thunder-bolts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Snow, rains, clouds, winds, at seasons of the year"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nowise unfixed, all do come to pass."},{"sp":"N","t":"For where, even from their old primordial start"},{"sp":"N","t":"Causes have ever worked in such a way,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And where, even from the world's first origin,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thuswise have things befallen, so even now"},{"sp":"N","t":"After a fixed order they come round"},{"sp":"N","t":"In sequence also."},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise, days may wax","st":"5.680"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst the nights wane, and daylight minished be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst nights do take their augmentations,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Either because the self-same sun, coursing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the lands and over in two arcs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A longer and a briefer, doth dispart"},{"sp":"N","t":"The coasts of ether and divides in twain"},{"sp":"N","t":"His orbit all unequally, and adds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As round he's borne, unto the one half there"},{"sp":"N","t":"As much as from the other half he's ta'en,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Until he then arrives that sign of heaven"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where the year's node renders the shades of night"},{"sp":"N","t":"Equal unto the periods of light."},{"sp":"N","t":"For when the sun is midway on his course"},{"sp":"N","t":"Between the blasts of northwind and of south,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Heaven keeps his two goals parted equally,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By virtue of the fixed position old"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the whole starry Zodiac, through which"},{"sp":"N","t":"That sun, in winding onward, takes a year,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Illumining the sky and all the lands"},{"sp":"N","t":"With oblique light—as men declare to us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Who by their diagrams have charted well"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those regions of the sky which be adorned"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the arranged signs of Zodiac."},{"sp":"N","t":"Or else, because in certain parts the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the lands is denser, the tremulous"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bright beams of fire do waver tardily,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor easily can penetrate that air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor yet emerge unto their rising-place:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For this it is that nights in winter time"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do linger long, ere comes the many-rayed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Round Badge of the day. Or else because, as said,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In alternating seasons of the year"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fires, now more quick, and now more slow, are wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"To stream together,—the fires which make the sun"},{"sp":"N","t":"To rise in some one spot—therefore it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"That those men seem to speak the truth [who hold"},{"sp":"N","t":"A new sun is with each new daybreak born]."},{"sp":"N","t":"The moon she possibly doth shine because","st":"5.705"},{"sp":"N","t":"Strook by the rays of sun, and day by day"},{"sp":"N","t":"May turn unto our gaze her light, the more"},{"sp":"N","t":"She doth recede from orb of sun, until,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Facing him opposite across the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"She hath with full effulgence gleamed abroad,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, at her rising as she soars above,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath there observed his setting; thence likewise"},{"sp":"N","t":"She needs must hide, as 'twere, her light behind"},{"sp":"N","t":"By slow degrees, the nearer now she glides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the circle of the Zodiac,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From her far place toward fires of yonder sun,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As those men hold who feign the moon to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Just like a ball and to pursue a course"},{"sp":"N","t":"Betwixt the sun and earth. There is, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some reason to suppose that moon may roll"},{"sp":"N","t":"With light her very own, and thus display"},{"sp":"N","t":"The varied shapes of her resplendence there."},{"sp":"N","t":"For near her is, percase, another body,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Invisible, because devoid of light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Borne on and gliding all along with her,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which in three modes may block and blot her disk."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, she may revolve upon herself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like to a ball's sphere—if perchance that be-"},{"sp":"N","t":"One half of her dyed o'er with glowing light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by the revolution of that sphere"},{"sp":"N","t":"She may beget for us her varying shapes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Until she turns that fiery part of her"},{"sp":"N","t":"Full to the sight and open eyes of men;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thence by slow stages round and back she whirls,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Withdrawing thus the luminiferous part"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of her sphered mass and ball, as, verily,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The Babylonian doctrine of Chaldees,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Refuting the art of Greek astrologers,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Labours, in opposition, to prove sure-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As if, forsooth, the thing for which each fights,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Might not alike be true,—or aught there were"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore thou mightest risk embracing one"},{"sp":"N","t":"More than the other notion. Then, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why a new moon might not forevermore"},{"sp":"N","t":"Created be with fixed successions there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of shapes and with configurations fixed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And why each day that bright created moon"},{"sp":"N","t":"Might not miscarry and another be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In its stead and place, engendered anew,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis hard to show by reason, or by words"},{"sp":"N","t":"To prove absurd—since, lo, so many things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can be create with fixed successions:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Spring-time and Venus come, and Venus' boy,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The winged harbinger, steps on before,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hard on Zephyr's foot-prints Mother Flora,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sprinkling the ways before them, filleth all"},{"sp":"N","t":"With colours and with odours excellent;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereafter follows arid Heat, and he"},{"sp":"N","t":"Companioned is by Ceres, dusty one,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by the Etesian Breezes of the north;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then cometh Autumn on, and with him steps"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lord Bacchus, and then other Seasons too"},{"sp":"N","t":"And other Winds do follow—the high roar"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of great Volturnus, and the Southwind strong"},{"sp":"N","t":"With thunder-bolts. At last earth's Shortest-Day"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bears on to men the snows and brings again"},{"sp":"N","t":"The numbing cold. And Winter follows her,"},{"sp":"N","t":"His teeth with chills a-chatter. Therefore, 'tis"},{"sp":"N","t":"The less a marvel, if at fixed time"},{"sp":"N","t":"A moon is thus begotten and again"},{"sp":"N","t":"At fixed time destroyed, since things so many"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can come to being thus at fixed time."},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise, the sun's eclipses and the moon's"},{"sp":"N","t":"Far occultations rightly thou mayst deem"},{"sp":"N","t":"As due to several causes. For, indeed,","st":"5.751"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why should the moon be able to shut out"},{"sp":"N","t":"Earth from the light of sun, and on the side"},{"sp":"N","t":"To earthward thrust her high head under sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Opposing dark orb to his glowing beams-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And yet, at same time, one suppose the effect"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could not result from some one other body"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which glides devoid of light forevermore?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, why could not sun, in weakened state,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At fixed time for-lose his fires, and then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When he has passed on along the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beyond the regions, hostile to his flames,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That quench and kill his fires, why could not he"},{"sp":"N","t":"Renew his light? And why should earth in turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have power to rob the moon of light, and there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Herself on high, keep the sun hid beneath,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst the moon glideth in her monthly course"},{"sp":"N","t":"Athrough the rigid shadows of the cone?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And yet, at same time, some one other body"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not have the power to under-pass the moon,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or glide along above the orb of sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Breaking his rays and outspread light asunder?"},{"sp":"N","t":"And still, if moon herself refulgent be"},{"sp":"N","t":"With her own sheen, why could she not at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"In some one quarter of the mighty world"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grow weak and weary, whilst she passeth through"},{"sp":"N","t":"Regions unfriendly to the beams her own?"},{"sp":"SEC","t":"ORIGINS OF VEGETABLE AND ANIMAL LIFE"},{"sp":"N","t":"And now to what remains!- Since I've resolved","st":"5.772"},{"sp":"N","t":"By what arrangements all things come to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through the blue regions of the mighty world,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"How we can know what energy and cause"},{"sp":"N","t":"Started the various courses of the sun"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the moon's goings, and by what far means"},{"sp":"N","t":"They can succumb, the while with thwarted light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And veil with shade the unsuspecting lands,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When, as it were, they blink, and then again"},{"sp":"N","t":"With open eye survey all regions wide,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Resplendent with white radiance- I do now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Return unto the world's primeval age"},{"sp":"N","t":"And tell what first the soft young fields of earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"With earliest parturition had decreed"},{"sp":"N","t":"To raise in air unto the shores of light"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to entrust unto the wayward winds."},{"sp":"N","t":"In the beginning, earth gave forth, around"},{"sp":"N","t":"The hills and over all the length of plains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The race of grasses and the shining green;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The flowery meadows sparkled all aglow"},{"sp":"N","t":"With greening colour, and thereafter, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the divers kinds of trees was given"},{"sp":"N","t":"An emulous impulse mightily to shoot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With a free rein, aloft into the air."},{"sp":"N","t":"As feathers and hairs and bristles are begot"},{"sp":"N","t":"The first on members of the four-foot breeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"And on the bodies of the strong-y-winged,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus then the new Earth first of all put forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grasses and shrubs, and afterward begat"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mortal generations, there upsprung-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Innumerable in modes innumerable-"},{"sp":"N","t":"After diverging fashions. For from sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"These breathing-creatures never can have dropped,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor the land-dwellers ever have come up"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out of sea-pools of salt. How true remains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How merited is that adopted name"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of earth- \"The Mother!\"- since from out the earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are all begotten. And even now arise"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out the loams how many living things-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Concreted by the rains and heat of the sun."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore 'tis less a marvel, if they sprang"},{"sp":"N","t":"In Long Ago more many, and more big,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Matured of those days in the fresh young years"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of earth and ether. First of all, the race"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the winged ones and parti-coloured birds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hatched out in spring-time, left their eggs behind;"},{"sp":"N","t":"As now-a-days in summer tree-crickets"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do leave their shiny husks of own accord,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seeking their food and living. Then it was"},{"sp":"N","t":"This earth of thine first gave unto the day"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mortal generations; for prevailed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the fields abounding hot and wet."},{"sp":"N","t":"And hence, where any fitting spot was given,"},{"sp":"N","t":"There 'gan to grow womb-cavities, by roots"},{"sp":"N","t":"Affixed to earth. And when in ripened time"},{"sp":"N","t":"The age of the young within (that sought the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fled earth's damps) had burst these wombs, O then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would Nature thither turn the pores of earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"And make her spurt from open veins a juice"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like unto milk; even as a woman now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is filled, at child-bearing, with the sweet milk,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because all that swift stream of aliment"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is thither turned unto the mother-breasts."},{"sp":"N","t":"There earth would furnish to the children food;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Warmth was their swaddling cloth, the grass their bed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Abounding in soft down. Earth's newness then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would rouse no dour spells of the bitter cold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor extreme heats nor winds of mighty powers-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For all things grow and gather strength through time"},{"sp":"N","t":"In like proportions; and then earth was young."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, again, again, how merited","st":"5.821"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is that adopted name of Earth- The Mother!-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since she herself begat the human race,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And at one well-nigh fixed time brought forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each breast that ranges raving round about"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the mighty mountains and all birds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aerial with many a varied shape."},{"sp":"N","t":"But, lo, because her bearing years must end,"},{"sp":"N","t":"She ceased, like to a woman worn by eld."},{"sp":"N","t":"For lapsing aeons change the nature of"},{"sp":"N","t":"The whole wide world, and all things needs must take"},{"sp":"N","t":"One status after other, nor aught persists"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forever like itself. All things depart;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nature she changeth all, compelleth all"},{"sp":"N","t":"To transformation. Lo, this moulders down,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A-slack with weary eld, and that, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Prospers in glory, issuing from contempt."},{"sp":"N","t":"In suchwise, then, the lapsing aeons change"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of the whole wide world, and earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Taketh one status after other. And what"},{"sp":"N","t":"She bore of old, she now can bear no longer,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what she never bore, she can to-day."},{"sp":"N","t":"In those days also the telluric world"},{"sp":"N","t":"Strove to beget the monsters that upsprung"},{"sp":"N","t":"With their astounding visages and limbs-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The Man-woman—a thing betwixt the twain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet neither, and from either sex remote-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some gruesome Boggles orphaned of the feet,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some widowed of the hands, dumb Horrors too"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without a mouth, or blind Ones of no eye,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or Bulks all shackled by their legs and arms"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cleaving unto the body fore and aft,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thuswise, that never could they do or go,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor shun disaster, nor take the good they would."},{"sp":"N","t":"And other prodigies and monsters earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was then begetting of this sort—in vain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since Nature banned with horror their increase,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And powerless were they to reach unto"},{"sp":"N","t":"The coveted flower of fair maturity,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or to find aliment, or to intertwine"},{"sp":"N","t":"In works of Venus. For we see there must"},{"sp":"N","t":"Concur in life conditions manifold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If life is ever by begetting life"},{"sp":"N","t":"To forge the generations one by one:"},{"sp":"N","t":"First, foods must be; and, next, a path whereby"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds of impregnation in the frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"May ooze, released from the members all;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Last, the possession of those instruments"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereby the male with female can unite,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The one with other in mutual ravishments."},{"sp":"N","t":"And in the ages after monsters died,","st":"5.855"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perforce there perished many a stock, unable"},{"sp":"N","t":"By propagation to forge a progeny."},{"sp":"N","t":"For whatsoever creatures thou beholdest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Breathing the breath of life, the same have been"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even from their earliest age preserved alive"},{"sp":"N","t":"By cunning, or by valour, or at least"},{"sp":"N","t":"By speed of foot or wing. And many a stock"},{"sp":"N","t":"Remaineth yet, because of use to man,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so committed to man's guardianship."},{"sp":"N","t":"Valour hath saved alive fierce lion-breeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"And many another terrorizing race,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cunning the foxes, flight the antlered stags."},{"sp":"N","t":"Light-sleeping dogs with faithful heart in breast,"},{"sp":"N","t":"However, and every kind begot from seed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of beasts of draft, as, too, the woolly flocks"},{"sp":"N","t":"And horned cattle, all, my Memmius,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have been committed to guardianship of men."},{"sp":"N","t":"For anxiously they fled the savage beasts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And peace they sought and their abundant foods,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Obtained with never labours of their own,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which we secure to them as fit rewards"},{"sp":"N","t":"For their good service. But those beasts to whom"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nature has granted naught of these same things-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beasts quite unfit by own free will to thrive"},{"sp":"N","t":"And vain for any service unto us"},{"sp":"N","t":"In thanks for which we should permit their kind"},{"sp":"N","t":"To feed and be in our protection safe-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those, of a truth, were wont to be exposed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enshackled in the gruesome bonds of doom,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As prey and booty for the rest, until"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nature reduced that stock to utter death."},{"sp":"N","t":"But Centaurs ne'er have been, nor can there be","st":"5.878"},{"sp":"N","t":"Creatures of twofold stock and double frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Compact of members alien in kind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet formed with equal function, equal force"},{"sp":"N","t":"In every bodily part—a fact thou mayst,"},{"sp":"N","t":"However dull thy wits, well learn from this:"},{"sp":"N","t":"The horse, when his three years have rolled away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flowers in his prime of vigour; but the boy"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not so, for oft even then he gropes in sleep"},{"sp":"N","t":"After the milky nipples of the breasts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"An infant still. And later, when at last"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lusty powers of horses and stout limbs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now weak through lapsing life, do fail with age,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lo, only then doth youth with flowering years"},{"sp":"N","t":"Begin for boys, and clothe their ruddy cheeks"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the soft down. So never deem, percase,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That from a man and from the seed of horse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The beast of draft, can Centaurs be composed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or e'er exist alive, nor Scyllas be-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The half-fish bodies girdled with mad dogs-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor others of this sort, in whom we mark"},{"sp":"N","t":"Members discordant each with each; for ne'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"At one same time they reach their flower of age"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or gain and lose full vigour of their frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And never burn with one same lust of love,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And never in their habits they agree,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor find the same foods equally delightsome-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sooth, as one oft may see the bearded goats"},{"sp":"N","t":"Batten upon the hemlock which to man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is violent poison. Once again, since flame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is wont to scorch and burn the tawny bulks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the great lions as much as other kinds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of flesh and blood existing in the lands,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How could it be that she, Chimaera lone,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With triple body—fore, a lion she;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And aft, a dragon; and betwixt, a goat-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Might at the mouth from out the body belch"},{"sp":"N","t":"Infuriate flame? Wherefore, the man who feigns"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such beings could have been engendered"},{"sp":"N","t":"When earth was new and the young sky was fresh"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Basing his empty argument on new)"},{"sp":"N","t":"May babble with like reason many whims"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into our ears: he'll say, perhaps, that then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rivers of gold through every landscape flowed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That trees were wont with precious stones to flower,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or that in those far aeons man was born"},{"sp":"N","t":"With such gigantic length and lift of limbs"},{"sp":"N","t":"As to be able, based upon his feet,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deep oceans to bestride or with his hands"},{"sp":"N","t":"To whirl the firmament around his head."},{"sp":"N","t":"For though in earth were many seeds of things"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the old time when this telluric world"},{"sp":"N","t":"First poured the breeds of animals abroad,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still that is nothing of a sign that then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such hybrid creatures could have been begot"},{"sp":"N","t":"And limbs of all beasts heterogeneous"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have been together knit; because, indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The divers kinds of grasses and the grains"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the delightsome trees—which even now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Spring up abounding from within the earth-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can still ne'er be begotten with their stems"},{"sp":"N","t":"Begrafted into one; but each sole thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Proceeds according to its proper wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all conserve their own distinctions based"},{"sp":"N","t":"In nature's fixed decree."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"ORIGINS AND SAVAGE PERIOD OF MANKIND"},{"sp":"N","t":"But mortal man","st":"5.925"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was then far hardier in the old champaign,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As well he should be, since a hardier earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had him begotten; builded too was he"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of bigger and more solid bones within,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And knit with stalwart sinews through the flesh,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor easily seized by either heat or cold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or alien food or any ail or irk."},{"sp":"N","t":"And whilst so many lustrums of the sun"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rolled on across the sky, men led a life"},{"sp":"N","t":"After the roving habit of wild beasts."},{"sp":"N","t":"Not then were sturdy guiders of curved ploughs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And none knew then to work the fields with iron,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or plant young shoots in holes of delved loam,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or lop with hooked knives from off high trees"},{"sp":"N","t":"The boughs of yester-year. What sun and rains"},{"sp":"N","t":"To them had given, what earth of own accord"},{"sp":"N","t":"Created then, was boon enough to glad"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their simple hearts. Mid acorn-laden oaks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would they refresh their bodies for the nonce;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the wild berries of the arbute-tree,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which now thou seest to ripen purple-red"},{"sp":"N","t":"In winter time, the old telluric soil"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would bear then more abundant and more big."},{"sp":"N","t":"And many coarse foods, too, in long ago"},{"sp":"N","t":"The blooming freshness of the rank young world"},{"sp":"N","t":"Produced, enough for those poor wretches there."},{"sp":"N","t":"And rivers and springs would summon them of old"},{"sp":"N","t":"To slake the thirst, as now from the great hills"},{"sp":"N","t":"The water's down-rush calls aloud and far"},{"sp":"N","t":"The thirsty generations of the wild."},{"sp":"N","t":"So, too, they sought the grottos of the Nymphs-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The woodland haunts discovered as they ranged-"},{"sp":"N","t":"From forth of which they knew that gliding rills"},{"sp":"N","t":"With gush and splash abounding laved the rocks,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The dripping rocks, and trickled from above"},{"sp":"N","t":"Over the verdant moss; and here and there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Welled up and burst across the open flats."},{"sp":"N","t":"As yet they knew not to enkindle fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against the cold, nor hairy pelts to use"},{"sp":"N","t":"And clothe their bodies with the spoils of beasts;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But huddled in groves, and mountain-caves, and woods,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And 'mongst the thickets hid their squalid backs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When driven to flee the lashings of the winds"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the big rains. Nor could they then regard"},{"sp":"N","t":"The general good, nor did they know to use"},{"sp":"N","t":"In common any customs, any laws:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whatever of booty fortune unto each"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had proffered, each alone would bear away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By instinct trained for self to thrive and live."},{"sp":"N","t":"And Venus in the forests then would link"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lovers' bodies; for the woman yielded"},{"sp":"N","t":"Either from mutual flame, or from the man's"},{"sp":"N","t":"Impetuous fury and insatiate lust,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or from a bribe—as acorn-nuts, choice pears,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or the wild berries of the arbute-tree."},{"sp":"N","t":"And trusting wondrous strength of hands and legs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They'd chase the forest-wanderers, the beasts;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And many they'd conquer, but some few they fled,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A-skulk into their hiding-places..."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"With the flung stones and with the ponderous heft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of gnarled branch. And by the time of night"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'ertaken, they would throw, like bristly boars,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their wildman's limbs naked upon the earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rolling themselves in leaves and fronded boughs."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor would they call with lamentations loud"},{"sp":"N","t":"Around the fields for daylight and the sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Quaking and wand'ring in shadows of the night;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But, silent and buried in a sleep, they'd wait"},{"sp":"N","t":"Until the sun with rosy flambeau brought"},{"sp":"N","t":"The glory to the sky. From childhood wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ever to see the dark and day begot"},{"sp":"N","t":"In times alternate, never might they be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wildered by wild misgiving, lest a night"},{"sp":"N","t":"Eternal should possess the lands, with light"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of sun withdrawn forever. But their care"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was rather that the clans of savage beasts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would often make their sleep-time horrible"},{"sp":"N","t":"For those poor wretches; and, from home y-driven,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They'd flee their rocky shelters at approach"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of boar, the spumy-lipped, or lion strong,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in the midnight yield with terror up"},{"sp":"N","t":"To those fierce guests their beds of out-spread leaves."},{"sp":"N","t":"And yet in those days not much more than now","st":"5.988"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would generations of mortality"},{"sp":"N","t":"Leave the sweet light of fading life behind."},{"sp":"N","t":"Indeed, in those days here and there a man,"},{"sp":"N","t":"More oftener snatched upon, and gulped by fangs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Afforded the beasts a food that roared alive,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Echoing through groves and hills and forest-trees,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as he viewed his living flesh entombed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within a living grave; whilst those whom flight"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had saved, with bone and body bitten, shrieked,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pressing their quivering palms to loathsome sores,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With horrible voices for eternal death-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Until, forlorn of help, and witless what"},{"sp":"N","t":"Might medicine their wounds, the writhing pangs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Took them from life. But not in those far times"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would one lone day give over unto doom"},{"sp":"N","t":"A soldiery in thousands marching on"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beneath the battle-banners, nor would then"},{"sp":"N","t":"The ramping breakers of the main seas dash"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whole argosies and crews upon the rocks."},{"sp":"N","t":"But ocean uprisen would often rave in vain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without all end or outcome, and give up"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its empty menacings as lightly too;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor soft seductions of a serene sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could lure by laughing billows any man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out to disaster: for the science bold"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of ship-sailing lay dark in those far times."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, 'twas then that lack of food gave o'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"Men's fainting limbs to dissolution: now"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis plenty overwhelms. Unwary, they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Oft for themselves themselves would then outpour"},{"sp":"N","t":"The poison; now, with nicer art, themselves"},{"sp":"N","t":"They give the drafts to others."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"BEGINNINGS OF CIVILIZATION"},{"sp":"N","t":"Afterwards,","st":"5.1011"},{"sp":"N","t":"When huts they had procured and pelts and fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And when the woman, joined unto the man,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Withdrew with him into one dwelling place,"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Were known; and when they saw an offspring born"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out themselves, then first the human race"},{"sp":"N","t":"Began to soften. For 'twas now that fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rendered their shivering frames less staunch to bear,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the canopy of the sky, the cold;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And Love reduced their shaggy hardiness;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And children, with the prattle and the kiss,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Soon broke the parents' haughty temper down."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, too, did neighbours 'gin to league as friends,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Eager to wrong no more or suffer wrong,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And urged for children and the womankind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mercy, of fathers, whilst with cries and gestures"},{"sp":"N","t":"They stammered hints how meet it was that all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should have compassion on the weak. And still,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though concord not in every wise could then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Begotten be, a good, a goodly part"},{"sp":"N","t":"Kept faith inviolate—or else mankind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Long since had been unutterably cut off,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And propagation never could have brought"},{"sp":"N","t":"The species down the ages."},{"sp":"N","t":"But nature 'twas","st":"5.1028"},{"sp":"N","t":"Urged men to utter various sounds of tongue"},{"sp":"N","t":"And need and use did mould the names of things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"About in same wise as the lack-speech years"},{"sp":"N","t":"Compel young children unto gesturings,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Making them point with finger here and there"},{"sp":"N","t":"At what's before them. For each creature feels"},{"sp":"N","t":"By instinct to what use to put his powers."},{"sp":"N","t":"Ere yet the bull-calf's scarce begotten horns"},{"sp":"N","t":"Project above his brows, with them he 'gins"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enraged to butt and savagely to thrust."},{"sp":"N","t":"But whelps of panthers and the lion's cubs"},{"sp":"N","t":"With claws and paws and bites are at the fray"},{"sp":"N","t":"Already, when their teeth and claws be scarce"},{"sp":"N","t":"As yet engendered. So again, we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"All breeds of winged creatures trust to wings"},{"sp":"N","t":"And from their fledgling pinions seek to get"},{"sp":"N","t":"A fluttering assistance. Thus, to think"},{"sp":"N","t":"That in those days some man apportioned round"},{"sp":"N","t":"To things their names, and that from him men learned"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their first nomenclature, is foolery."},{"sp":"N","t":"For why could he mark everything by words"},{"sp":"N","t":"And utter the various sounds of tongue, what time"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rest may be supposed powerless"},{"sp":"N","t":"To do the same? And, if the rest had not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Already one with other used words,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence was implanted in the teacher, then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fore-knowledge of their use, and whence was given"},{"sp":"N","t":"To him alone primordial faculty"},{"sp":"N","t":"To know and see in mind what 'twas he willed?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, one only man could scarce subdue"},{"sp":"N","t":"An overmastered multitude to choose"},{"sp":"N","t":"To get by heart his names of things. A task"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not easy 'tis in any wise to teach"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to persuade the deaf concerning what"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis needful for to do. For ne'er would they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Allow, nor ne'er in anywise endure"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perpetual vain dingdong in their ears"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of spoken sounds unheard before. And what,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At last, in this affair so wondrous is,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That human race (in whom a voice and tongue"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were now in vigour) should by divers words"},{"sp":"N","t":"Denote its objects, as each divers sense"},{"sp":"N","t":"Might prompt?- since even the speechless herds, aye, since"},{"sp":"N","t":"The very generations of wild beasts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are wont dissimilar and divers sounds"},{"sp":"N","t":"To rouse from in them, when there's fear or pain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And when they burst with joys. And this, forsooth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis thine to know from plainest facts: when first"},{"sp":"N","t":"Huge flabby jowls of mad Molossian hounds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Baring their hard white teeth, begin to snarl,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They threaten, with infuriate lips peeled back,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In sounds far other than with which they bark"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fill with voices all the regions round."},{"sp":"N","t":"And when with fondling tongue they start to lick"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their puppies, or do toss them round with paws,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Feigning with gentle bites to gape and snap,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They fawn with yelps of voice far other then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than when, alone within the house, they bay,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or whimpering slink with cringing sides from blows."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again the neighing of the horse, is that"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not seen to differ likewise, when the stud"},{"sp":"N","t":"In buoyant flower of his young years raves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Goaded by winged Love, amongst the mares,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And when with widening nostrils out he snorts"},{"sp":"N","t":"The call to battle, and when haply he"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whinnies at times with terror-quaking limbs?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lastly, the flying race, the dappled birds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hawks, ospreys, sea-gulls, searching food and life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Amid the ocean billows in the brine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Utter at other times far other cries"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than when they fight for food, or with their prey"},{"sp":"N","t":"Struggle and strain. And birds there are which change"},{"sp":"N","t":"With changing weather their own raucous songs-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As long-lived generations of the crows"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or flocks of rooks, when they be said to cry"},{"sp":"N","t":"For rain and water and to call at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"For winds and gales. Ergo, if divers moods"},{"sp":"N","t":"Compel the brutes, though speechless evermore,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To send forth divers sounds, O truly then"},{"sp":"N","t":"How much more likely 'twere that mortal men"},{"sp":"N","t":"In those days could with many a different sound"},{"sp":"N","t":"Denote each separate thing."},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest, perchance,","st":"5.1091"},{"sp":"N","t":"Concerning these affairs thou ponderest"},{"sp":"N","t":"In silent meditation, let me say"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twas lightning brought primevally to earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fire for mortals, and from thence hath spread"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'er all the lands the flames of heat. For thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even now we see so many objects, touched"},{"sp":"N","t":"By the celestial flames, to flash aglow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When thunderbolt has dowered them with heat."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet also when a many-branched tree,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beaten by winds, writhes swaying to and fro,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pressing 'gainst branches of a neighbour tree,"},{"sp":"N","t":"There by the power of mighty rub and rub"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is fire engendered; and at times out-flares"},{"sp":"N","t":"The scorching heat of flame, when boughs do chafe"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against the trunks. And of these causes, either"},{"sp":"N","t":"May well have given to mortal men the fire."},{"sp":"N","t":"Next, food to cook and soften in the flame"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sun instructed, since so oft they saw"},{"sp":"N","t":"How objects mellowed, when subdued by warmth"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by the raining blows of fiery beams,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through all the fields."},{"sp":"N","t":"And more and more each day","st":"5.1105"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would men more strong in sense, more wise in heart,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Teach them to change their earlier mode and life"},{"sp":"N","t":"By fire and new devices. Kings began"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cities to found and citadels to set,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As strongholds and asylums for themselves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And flocks and fields to portion for each man"},{"sp":"N","t":"After the beauty, strength, and sense of each-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For beauty then imported much, and strength"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had its own rights supreme. Thereafter, wealth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Discovered was, and gold was brought to light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which soon of honour stripped both strong and fair;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For men, however beautiful in form"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or valorous, will follow in the main"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rich man's party. Yet were man to steer"},{"sp":"N","t":"His life by sounder reasoning, he'd own"},{"sp":"N","t":"Abounding riches, if with mind content"},{"sp":"N","t":"He lived by thrift; for never, as I guess,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is there a lack of little in the world."},{"sp":"N","t":"But men wished glory for themselves and power"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even that their fortunes on foundations firm"},{"sp":"N","t":"Might rest forever, and that they themselves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The opulent, might pass a quiet life-"},{"sp":"N","t":"In vain, in vain; since, in the strife to climb"},{"sp":"N","t":"On to the heights of honour, men do make"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their pathway terrible; and even when once"},{"sp":"N","t":"They reach them, envy like the thunderbolt"},{"sp":"N","t":"At times will smite, O hurling headlong down"},{"sp":"N","t":"To murkiest Tartarus, in scorn; for, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All summits, all regions loftier than the rest,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Smoke, blasted as by envy's thunderbolts;"},{"sp":"N","t":"So better far in quiet to obey,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than to desire chief mastery of affairs"},{"sp":"N","t":"And ownership of empires. Be it so;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And let the weary sweat their life-blood out"},{"sp":"N","t":"All to no end, battling in hate along"},{"sp":"N","t":"The narrow path of man's ambition;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since all their wisdom is from others' lips,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all they seek is known from what they've heard"},{"sp":"N","t":"And less from what they've thought. Nor is this folly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Greater to-day, nor greater soon to be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than' twas of old."},{"sp":"N","t":"And therefore kings were slain,","st":"5.1136"},{"sp":"N","t":"And pristine majesty of golden thrones"},{"sp":"N","t":"And haughty sceptres lay o'erturned in dust;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And crowns, so splendid on the sovereign heads,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Soon bloody under the proletarian feet,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Groaned for their glories gone—for erst o'er-much"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dreaded, thereafter with more greedy zest"},{"sp":"N","t":"Trampled beneath the rabble heel. Thus things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down to the vilest lees of brawling mobs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Succumbed, whilst each man sought unto himself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dominion and supremacy. So next"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some wiser heads instructed men to found"},{"sp":"N","t":"The magisterial office, and did frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Codes that they might consent to follow laws."},{"sp":"N","t":"For humankind, o'er wearied with a life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fostered by force, was ailing from its feuds;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so the sooner of its own free will"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yielded to laws and strictest codes. For since"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each hand made ready in its wrath to take"},{"sp":"N","t":"A vengeance fiercer than by man's fair laws"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is now conceded, men on this account"},{"sp":"N","t":"Loathed the old life fostered by force. 'Tis thence"},{"sp":"N","t":"That fear of punishments defiles each prize"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of wicked days; for force and fraud ensnare"},{"sp":"N","t":"Each man around, and in the main recoil"},{"sp":"N","t":"On him from whence they sprung. Not easy 'tis"},{"sp":"N","t":"For one who violates by ugly deeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"The bonds of common peace to pass a life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Composed and tranquil. For albeit he 'scape"},{"sp":"N","t":"The race of gods and men, he yet must dread"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twill not be hid forever—since, indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So many, oft babbling on amid their dreams"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or raving in sickness, have betrayed themselves"},{"sp":"N","t":"(As stories tell) and published at last"},{"sp":"N","t":"Old secrets and the sins."},{"sp":"N","t":"And now what cause","st":"5.1161"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath spread divinities of gods abroad"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through mighty nations, and filled the cities full"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the high altars, and led to practices"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of solemn rites in season—rites which still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flourish in midst of great affairs of state"},{"sp":"N","t":"And midst great centres of man's civic life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rites whence still a poor mortality"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is grafted that quaking awe which rears aloft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still the new temples of gods from land to land"},{"sp":"N","t":"And drives mankind to visit them in throngs"},{"sp":"N","t":"On holy days- 'tis not so hard to give"},{"sp":"N","t":"Reason thereof in speech. Because, in sooth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even in those days would the race of man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be seeing excelling visages of gods"},{"sp":"N","t":"With mind awake; and in his sleeps, yet more-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bodies of wondrous growth. And, thus, to these"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would men attribute sense, because they seemed"},{"sp":"N","t":"To move their limbs and speak pronouncements high,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Befitting glorious visage and vast powers."},{"sp":"N","t":"And men would give them an eternal life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because their visages forevermore"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were there before them, and their shapes remained,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And chiefly, however, because men would not think"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beings augmented with such mighty powers"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could well by any force o'ermastered be."},{"sp":"N","t":"And men would think them in their happiness"},{"sp":"N","t":"Excelling far, because the fear of death"},{"sp":"N","t":"Vexed no one of them at all, and since"},{"sp":"N","t":"At same time in men's sleeps men saw them do"},{"sp":"N","t":"So many wonders, and yet feel therefrom"},{"sp":"N","t":"Themselves no weariness. Besides, men marked"},{"sp":"N","t":"How in a fixed order rolled around"},{"sp":"N","t":"The systems of the sky, and changed times"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of annual seasons, nor were able then"},{"sp":"N","t":"To know thereof the causes. Therefore 'twas"},{"sp":"N","t":"Men would take refuge in consigning all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto divinities, and in feigning all"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was guided by their nod. And in the sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"They set the seats and vaults of gods, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Across the sky night and the moon are seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"To roll along—moon, day, and night, and night's"},{"sp":"N","t":"Old awesome constellations evermore,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the night-wandering fireballs of the sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And flying flames, clouds, and the sun, the rains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Snow and the winds, the lightnings, and the hail,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the swift rumblings, and the hollow roar"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of mighty menacings forevermore."},{"sp":"N","t":"O humankind unhappy!- when it ascribed","st":"5.1194"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto divinities such awesome deeds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And coupled thereto rigours of fierce wrath!"},{"sp":"N","t":"What groans did men on that sad day beget"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even for themselves, and O what wounds for us,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What tears for our children's children! Nor, O man,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is thy true piety in this: with head"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the veil, still to be seen to turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fronting a stone, and ever to approach"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto all altars; nor so prone on earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forward to fall, to spread upturned palms"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before the shrines of gods, nor yet to dew"},{"sp":"N","t":"Altars with profuse blood of four-foot beasts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor vows with vows to link. But rather this:"},{"sp":"N","t":"To look on all things with a master eye"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mind at peace. For when we gaze aloft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the skiey vaults of yon great world"},{"sp":"N","t":"And ether, fixed high o'er twinkling stars,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And into our thought there come the journeyings"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of sun and moon, O then into our breasts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'erburdened already with their other ills,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Begins forthwith to rear its sudden head"},{"sp":"N","t":"One more misgiving: lest o'er us, percase,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It be the gods' immeasurable power"},{"sp":"N","t":"That rolls, with varied motion, round and round"},{"sp":"N","t":"The far white constellations. For the lack"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of aught of reasons tries the puzzled mind:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whether was ever a birth-time of the world,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And whether, likewise, any end shall be"},{"sp":"N","t":"How far the ramparts of the world can still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outstand this strain of ever-roused motion,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or whether, divinely with eternal weal"},{"sp":"N","t":"Endowed, they can through endless tracts of age"},{"sp":"N","t":"Glide on, defying the o'er-mighty powers"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the immeasurable ages. Lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What man is there whose mind with dread of gods"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cringes not close, whose limbs with terror-spell"},{"sp":"N","t":"Crouch not together, when the parched earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Quakes with the horrible thunderbolt amain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And across the mighty sky the rumblings run?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do not the peoples and the nations shake,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And haughty kings do they not hug their limbs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Strook through with fear of the divinities,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lest for aught foully done or madly said"},{"sp":"N","t":"The heavy time be now at hand to pay?"},{"sp":"N","t":"When, too, fierce force of fury-winds at sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sweepeth a navy's admiral down the main"},{"sp":"N","t":"With his stout legions and his elephants,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Doth he not seek the peace of gods with vows,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And beg in prayer, a-tremble, lulled winds"},{"sp":"N","t":"And friendly gales?- in vain, since, often up-caught"},{"sp":"N","t":"In fury-cyclones, is he borne along,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For all his mouthings, to the shoals of doom."},{"sp":"N","t":"Ah, so irrevocably some hidden power"},{"sp":"N","t":"Betramples forevermore affairs of men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And visibly grindeth with its heel in mire"},{"sp":"N","t":"The lictors' glorious rods and axes dire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Having them in derision! Again, when earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"From end to end is rocking under foot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And shaken cities ruin down, or threaten"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the verge, what wonder is it then"},{"sp":"N","t":"That mortal generations abase themselves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And unto gods in all affairs of earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Assign as last resort almighty powers"},{"sp":"N","t":"And wondrous energies to govern all?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now for the rest: copper and gold and iron","st":"5.1241"},{"sp":"N","t":"Discovered were, and with them silver's weight"},{"sp":"N","t":"And power of lead, when with prodigious heat"},{"sp":"N","t":"The conflagrations burned the forest trees"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the mighty mountains, by a bolt"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of lightning from the sky, or else because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Men, warring in the woodlands, on their foes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had hurled fire to frighten and dismay,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or yet because, by goodness of the soil"},{"sp":"N","t":"Invited, men desired to clear rich fields"},{"sp":"N","t":"And turn the countryside to pasture-lands,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or slay the wild and thrive upon the spoils."},{"sp":"N","t":"(For hunting by pit-fall and by fire arose"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before the art of hedging the covert round"},{"sp":"N","t":"With net or stirring it with dogs of chase.)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Howso the fact, and from what cause soever"},{"sp":"N","t":"The flamy heat with awful crack and roar"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had there devoured to their deepest roots"},{"sp":"N","t":"The forest trees and baked the earth with fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then from the boiling veins began to ooze"},{"sp":"N","t":"O rivulets of silver and of gold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of lead and copper too, collecting soon"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the hollow places of the ground."},{"sp":"N","t":"And when men saw the cooled lumps anon"},{"sp":"N","t":"To shine with splendour-sheen upon the ground,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much taken with that lustrous smooth delight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They 'gan to pry them out, and saw how each"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had got a shape like to its earthy mould."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then would it enter their heads how these same lumps,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If melted by heat, could into any form"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or figure of things be run, and how, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If hammered out, they could be nicely drawn"},{"sp":"N","t":"To sharpest points or finest edge, and thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yield to the forgers tools and give them power"},{"sp":"N","t":"To chop the forest down, to hew the logs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To shave the beams and planks, besides to bore"},{"sp":"N","t":"And punch and drill. And men began such work"},{"sp":"N","t":"At first as much with tools of silver and gold"},{"sp":"N","t":"As with the impetuous strength of the stout copper;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But vainly—since their over-mastered power"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would soon give way, unable to endure,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like copper, such hard labour. In those days"},{"sp":"N","t":"Copper it was that was the thing of price;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And gold lay useless, blunted with dull edge."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now lies the copper low, and gold hath come"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the loftiest honours. Thus it is"},{"sp":"N","t":"That rolling ages change the times of things:"},{"sp":"N","t":"What erst was of a price, becomes at last"},{"sp":"N","t":"A discard of no honour; whilst another"},{"sp":"N","t":"Succeeds to glory, issuing from contempt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And day by day is sought for more and more,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, when 'tis found, doth flower in men's praise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Objects of wondrous honour."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, Memmius,","st":"5.1281"},{"sp":"N","t":"How nature of iron discovered was, thou mayst"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of thine own self divine. Man's ancient arms"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were hands, and nails and teeth, stones too and boughs-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Breakage of forest trees—and flame and fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As soon as known. Thereafter force of iron"},{"sp":"N","t":"And copper discovered was; and copper's use"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was known ere iron's, since more tractable"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its nature is and its abundance more."},{"sp":"N","t":"With copper men to work the soil began,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With copper to rouse the hurly waves of war,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To straw the monstrous wounds, and seize away"},{"sp":"N","t":"Another's flocks and fields. For unto them,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus armed, all things naked of defence"},{"sp":"N","t":"Readily yielded. Then by slow degrees"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sword of iron succeeded, and the shape"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of brazen sickle into scorn was turned:"},{"sp":"N","t":"With iron to cleave the soil of earth they 'gan,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the contentions of uncertain war"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were rendered equal."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, lo, man was wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"Armed to mount upon the ribs of horse"},{"sp":"N","t":"And guide him with the rein, and play about"},{"sp":"N","t":"With right hand free, oft times before he tried"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perils of war in yoked chariot;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And yoked pairs abreast came earlier"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than yokes of four, or scythed chariots"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereinto clomb the men-at-arms. And next"},{"sp":"N","t":"The Punic folk did train the elephants-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those curst Lucanian oxen, hideous,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The serpent-handed, with turrets on their bulks-"},{"sp":"N","t":"To dure the wounds of war and panic-strike"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mighty troops of Mars. Thus Discord sad"},{"sp":"N","t":"Begat the one Thing after other, to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"The terror of the nations under arms,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And day by day to horrors of old war"},{"sp":"N","t":"She added an increase."},{"sp":"N","t":"Bulls, too, they tried","st":"5.1308"},{"sp":"N","t":"In war's grim business; and essayed to send"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outrageous boars against the foes. And some"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sent on before their ranks puissant lions"},{"sp":"N","t":"With armed trainers and with masters fierce"},{"sp":"N","t":"To guide and hold in chains—and yet in vain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since fleshed with pell-mell slaughter, fierce they flew,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And blindly through the squadrons havoc wrought,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shaking the frightful crests upon their heads,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now here, now there. Nor could the horsemen calm"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their horses, panic-breasted at the roar,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And rein them round to front the foe. With spring"},{"sp":"N","t":"The infuriate she-lions would up-leap"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now here, now there; and whoso came apace"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against them, these they'd rend across the face;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And others unwitting from behind they'd tear"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down from their mounts, and twining round them, bring"},{"sp":"N","t":"Tumbling to earth, o'ermastered by the wound,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And with those powerful fangs and hooked claws"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fasten upon them. Bulls would toss their friends,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And trample under foot, and from beneath"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rip flanks and bellies of horses with their horns,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And with a threat'ning forehead jam the sod;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And boars would gore with stout tusks their allies,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Splashing in fury their own blood on spears"},{"sp":"N","t":"Splintered in their own bodies, and would fell"},{"sp":"N","t":"In rout and ruin infantry and horse."},{"sp":"N","t":"For there the beasts-of-saddle tried to scape"},{"sp":"N","t":"The savage thrusts of tusk by shying off,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or rearing up with hoofs a-paw in air."},{"sp":"N","t":"In vain—since there thou mightest see them sink,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their sinews severed, and with heavy fall"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bestrew the ground. And such of these as men"},{"sp":"N","t":"Supposed well-trained long ago at home,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were in the thick of action seen to foam"},{"sp":"N","t":"In fury, from the wounds, the shrieks, the flight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The panic, and the tumult; nor could men"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aught of their numbers rally. For each breed"},{"sp":"N","t":"And various of the wild beasts fled apart"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hither or thither, as often in wars to-day"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flee those Lucanian oxen, by the steel"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grievously mangled, after they have wrought"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon their friends so many a dreadful doom."},{"sp":"N","t":"(If 'twas, indeed, that thus they did at all:"},{"sp":"N","t":"But scarcely I'll believe that men could not"},{"sp":"N","t":"With mind foreknow and see, as sure to come,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such foul and general disaster.- This"},{"sp":"N","t":"We, then, may hold as true in the great All,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In divers worlds on divers plan create,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Somewhere afar more likely than upon"},{"sp":"N","t":"One certain earth.) But men chose this to do"},{"sp":"N","t":"Less in the hope of conquering than to give"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their enemies a goodly cause of woe,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even though thereby they perished themselves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since weak in numbers and since wanting arms."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, clothes of roughly inter-plaited strands","st":"5.1350"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were earlier than loom-wove coverings;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The loom-wove later than man's iron is,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since iron is needful in the weaving art,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor by no other means can there be wrought"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such polished tools—the treadles, spindles, shuttles,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sounding yarn-beams. And nature forced the men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before the woman kind, to work the wool:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For all the male kind far excels in skill,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And cleverer is by much—until at last"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rugged farmer folk jeered at such tasks,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so were eager soon to give them o'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"To women's hands, and in more hardy toil"},{"sp":"N","t":"To harden arms and hands."},{"sp":"N","t":"But nature herself,","st":"5.1361"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mother of things, was the first seed-sower"},{"sp":"N","t":"And primal grafter; since the berries and acorns,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dropping from off the trees, would there beneath"},{"sp":"N","t":"Put forth in season swarms of little shoots;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence too men's fondness for ingrafting slips"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the boughs and setting out in holes"},{"sp":"N","t":"The young shrubs o'er the fields. Then would they try"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ever new modes of tilling their loved crofts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mark they would how earth improved the taste"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the wild fruits by fond and fostering care."},{"sp":"N","t":"And day by day they'd force the woods to move"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still higher up the mountain, and to yield"},{"sp":"N","t":"The place below for tilth, that there they might,"},{"sp":"N","t":"On plains and uplands, have their meadow-plats,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cisterns and runnels, crops of standing grain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And happy vineyards, and that all along"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'er hillocks, intervales, and plains might run"},{"sp":"N","t":"The silvery-green belt of olive-trees,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Marking the plotted landscape; even as now"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou seest so marked with varied loveliness"},{"sp":"N","t":"All the terrain which men adorn and plant"},{"sp":"N","t":"With rows of goodly fruit-trees and hedge round"},{"sp":"N","t":"With thriving shrubberies sown."},{"sp":"N","t":"But by the mouth","st":"5.1379"},{"sp":"N","t":"To imitate the liquid notes of birds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was earlier far 'mongst men than power to make,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By measured song, melodious verse and give"},{"sp":"N","t":"Delight to ears. And whistlings of the wind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Athrough the hollows of the reeds first taught"},{"sp":"N","t":"The peasantry to blow into the stalks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of hollow hemlock-herb. Then bit by bit"},{"sp":"N","t":"They learned sweet plainings, such as pipe out-pours,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beaten by finger-tips of singing men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When heard through unpathed groves and forest deeps"},{"sp":"N","t":"And woodsy meadows, through the untrod haunts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of shepherd folk and spots divinely still."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus time draws forward each and everything"},{"sp":"N","t":"Little by little unto the midst of men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And reason uplifts it to the shores of light."},{"sp":"N","t":"These tunes would soothe and glad the minds of mortals"},{"sp":"N","t":"When sated with food,—for songs are welcome then."},{"sp":"N","t":"And often, lounging with friends in the soft grass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beside a river of water, underneath"},{"sp":"N","t":"A big tree's branches, merrily they'd refresh"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their frames, with no vast outlay—most of all"},{"sp":"N","t":"If the weather were smiling and the times of the year"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were painting the green of the grass around with flowers."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then jokes, then talk, then peals of jollity"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would circle round; for then the rustic muse"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was in her glory; then would antic Mirth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Prompt them to garland head and shoulders about"},{"sp":"N","t":"With chaplets of intertwined flowers and leaves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to dance onward, out of tune, with limbs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Clownishly swaying, and with clownish foot"},{"sp":"N","t":"To beat our mother earth—from whence arose"},{"sp":"N","t":"Laughter and peals of jollity, for, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such frolic acts were in their glory then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Being more new and strange. And wakeful men"},{"sp":"N","t":"Found solaces for their unsleeping hours"},{"sp":"N","t":"In drawing forth variety of notes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In modulating melodies, in running"},{"sp":"N","t":"With puckered lips along the tuned reeds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence, even in our day do the watchmen guard"},{"sp":"N","t":"These old traditions, and have learned well"},{"sp":"N","t":"To keep true measure. And yet they no whit"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do get a larger fruit of gladsomeness"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than got the woodland aborigines"},{"sp":"N","t":"In olden times. For what we have at hand-"},{"sp":"N","t":"If theretofore naught sweeter we have known-"},{"sp":"N","t":"That chiefly pleases and seems best of all;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But then some later, likely better, find"},{"sp":"N","t":"Destroys its worth and changes our desires"},{"sp":"N","t":"Regarding good of yesterday."},{"sp":"N","t":"And thus","st":"5.1416"},{"sp":"N","t":"Began the loathing of the acorn; thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Abandoned were those beds with grasses strewn"},{"sp":"N","t":"And with the leaves beladen. Thus, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fell into new contempt the pelts of beasts-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Erstwhile a robe of honour, which, I guess,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aroused in those days envy so malign"},{"sp":"N","t":"That the first wearer went to woeful death"},{"sp":"N","t":"By ambuscades,—and yet that hairy prize,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rent into rags by greedy foemen there"},{"sp":"N","t":"And splashed by blood, was ruined utterly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beyond all use or vantage. Thus of old"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twas pelts, and of to-day 'tis purple and gold"},{"sp":"N","t":"That cark men's lives with cares and weary with war."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, methinks, resides the greater blame"},{"sp":"N","t":"With us vain men to-day: for cold would rack,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without their pelts, the naked sons of earth;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But us it nothing hurts to do without"},{"sp":"N","t":"The purple vestment, broidered with gold"},{"sp":"N","t":"And with imposing figures, if we still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Make shift with some mean garment of the Plebs."},{"sp":"N","t":"So man in vain futilities toils on"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forever and wastes in idle cares his years-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because, of very truth, he hath not learnt"},{"sp":"N","t":"What the true end of getting is, nor yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"At all how far true pleasure may increase."},{"sp":"N","t":"And 'tis desire for better and for more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath carried by degrees mortality"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out onward to the deep, and roused up"},{"sp":"N","t":"From the far bottom mighty waves of war."},{"sp":"N","t":"But sun and moon, those watchmen of the world,","st":"5.1436"},{"sp":"N","t":"With their own lanterns traversing around"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mighty, the revolving vault, have taught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto mankind that seasons of the years"},{"sp":"N","t":"Return again, and that the Thing takes place"},{"sp":"N","t":"After a fixed plan and order fixed."},{"sp":"N","t":"Already would they pass their life, hedged round"},{"sp":"N","t":"By the strong towers; and cultivate an earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"All portioned out and boundaried; already"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would the sea flower and sail-winged ships;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Already men had, under treaty pacts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Confederates and allies, when poets began"},{"sp":"N","t":"To hand heroic actions down in verse;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor long ere this had letters been devised-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence is our age unable to look back"},{"sp":"N","t":"On what has gone before, except where reason"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shows us a footprint."},{"sp":"N","t":"Sailings on the seas,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Tillings of fields, walls, laws, and arms, and roads,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dress and the like, all prizes, all delights"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of finer life, poems, pictures, chiselled shapes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of polished sculptures—all these arts were learned"},{"sp":"N","t":"By practice and the mind's experience,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As men walked forward step by eager step."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus time draws forward each and everything"},{"sp":"N","t":"Little by little into the midst of men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And reason uplifts it to the shores of light."},{"sp":"N","t":"For one thing after other did men see"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grow clear by intellect, till with their arts"},{"sp":"N","t":"They've now achieved the supreme pinnacle."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Book VI"},{"sp":"SEC","t":"PROEM"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twas Athens first, the glorious in name,","st":"6.1"},{"sp":"N","t":"That whilom gave to hapless sons of men"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sheaves of harvest, and re-ordered life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And decreed laws; and she the first that gave"},{"sp":"N","t":"Life its sweet solaces, when she begat"},{"sp":"N","t":"A man of heart so wise, who whilom poured"},{"sp":"N","t":"All wisdom forth from his truth-speaking mouth;"},{"sp":"N","t":"The glory of whom, though dead, is yet to-day,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because of those discoveries divine"},{"sp":"N","t":"Renowned of old, exalted to the sky."},{"sp":"N","t":"For when saw he that well-nigh everything"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which needs of man most urgently require"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was ready to hand for mortals, and that life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As far as might be, was established safe,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That men were lords in riches, honour, praise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And eminent in goodly fame of sons,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that they yet, O yet, within the home,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Still had the anxious heart which vexed life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unpausingly with torments of the mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And raved perforce with angry plaints, then he,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then he, the master, did perceive that 'twas"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vessel itself which worked the bane, and all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"However wholesome, which from here or there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was gathered into it, was by that bane"},{"sp":"N","t":"Spoilt from within,—in part, because he saw"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vessel so cracked and leaky that nowise"},{"sp":"N","t":"'T could ever be filled to brim; in part because"},{"sp":"N","t":"He marked how it polluted with foul taste"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whate'er it got within itself. So he,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The master, then by his truth-speaking words,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Purged the breasts of men, and set the bounds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of lust and terror, and exhibited"},{"sp":"N","t":"The supreme good whither we all endeavour,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And showed the path whereby we might arrive"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thereunto by a little cross-cut straight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what of ills in all affairs of mortals"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upsprang and flitted deviously about"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Whether by chance or force), since nature thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had destined; and from out what gates a man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Should sally to each combat. And he proved"},{"sp":"N","t":"That mostly vainly doth the human race"},{"sp":"N","t":"Roll in its bosom the grim waves of care."},{"sp":"N","t":"For just as children tremble and fear all"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the viewless dark, so even we at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dread in the light so many things that be"},{"sp":"N","t":"No whit more fearsome than what children feign,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shuddering, will be upon them in the dark."},{"sp":"N","t":"This terror then, this darkness of the mind,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not sunrise with its flaring spokes of light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor glittering arrows of morning can disperse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But only nature's aspect and her law."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore the more will I go on to weave"},{"sp":"N","t":"In verses this my undertaken task."},{"sp":"N","t":"And since I've taught thee that the world's great vaults","st":"6.43"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are mortal and that sky is fashioned"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of frame e'en born in time, and whatsoe'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"Therein go on and must perforce go on"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"The most I have unravelled; what remains"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do thou take in, besides; since once for all"},{"sp":"N","t":"To climb into that chariot' renowned"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Of winds arise; and they appeased are"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that all things again..."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Which were, are changed now, with fury stilled;"},{"sp":"N","t":"All other movements through the earth and sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which mortals gaze upon (O anxious oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"In quaking thoughts!), and which abase their minds"},{"sp":"N","t":"With dread of deities and press them crushed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down to the earth, because their ignorance"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of cosmic causes forces them to yield"},{"sp":"N","t":"All things unto the empery of gods"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to concede the kingly rule to them."},{"sp":"N","t":"For even those men who have learned full well"},{"sp":"N","t":"That godheads lead a long life free of care,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If yet meanwhile they wonder by what plan"},{"sp":"N","t":"Things can go on (and chiefly yon high things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Observed o'erhead on the ethereal coasts),"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again are hurried back unto the fears"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of old religion and adopt again"},{"sp":"N","t":"Harsh masters, deemed almighty,—wretched men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unwitting what can be and what cannot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by what law to each its scope prescribed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its boundary stone that clings so deep in Time."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore the more are they borne wandering on"},{"sp":"N","t":"By blindfold reason. And, Memmius, unless"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out thy mind thou spuest all of this"},{"sp":"N","t":"And casteth far from thee all thoughts which be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unworthy gods and alien to their peace,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then often will the holy majesties"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the high gods be harmful unto thee,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As by thy thought degraded,—not, indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That essence supreme of gods could be by this"},{"sp":"N","t":"So outraged as in wrath to thirst to seek"},{"sp":"N","t":"Revenges keen; but even because thyself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou plaguest with the notion that the gods,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even they, the Calm Ones in serene repose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do roll the mighty waves of wrath on wrath;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor wilt thou enter with a serene breast"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shrines of the gods; nor wilt thou able be"},{"sp":"N","t":"In tranquil peace of mind to take and know"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those images which from their holy bodies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are carried into intellects of men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As the announcers of their form divine."},{"sp":"N","t":"What sort of life will follow after this"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis thine to see. But that afar from us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Veriest reason may drive such life away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much yet remains to be embellished yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"In polished verses, albeit hath issued forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"So much from me already; lo, there is"},{"sp":"N","t":"The law and aspect of the sky to be"},{"sp":"N","t":"By reason grasped; there are the tempest times"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the bright lightnings to be hymned now-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even what they do and from what cause soe'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"They're borne along—that thou mayst tremble not,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Marking off regions of prophetic skies"},{"sp":"N","t":"For auguries, O foolishly distraught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as to whence the flying flame hath come,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or to which half of heaven it turns, or how"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through walled places it hath wound its way,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or, after proving its dominion there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How it hath speeded forth from thence amain-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereof nowise the causes do men know,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And think divinities are working there."},{"sp":"N","t":"Do thou, Calliope, ingenious Muse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Solace of mortals and delight of gods,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Point out the course before me, as I race"},{"sp":"N","t":"On to the white line of the utmost goal,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That I may get with signal praise the crown,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With thee my guide!"},{"sp":"SEC","t":"GREAT METEOROLOGICAL PHENOMENA, ETC."},{"sp":"N","t":"And so in first place, then,","st":"6.96"},{"sp":"N","t":"With thunder are shaken the blue deeps of heaven,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because the ethereal clouds, scudding aloft,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Together clash, what time 'gainst one another"},{"sp":"N","t":"The winds are battling. For never a sound there comes"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out the serene regions of the sky;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But wheresoever in a host more dense"},{"sp":"N","t":"The clouds foregather, thence more often comes"},{"sp":"N","t":"A crash with mighty rumbling. And, again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Clouds cannot be of so condensed a frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"As stones and timbers, nor again so fine"},{"sp":"N","t":"As mists and flying smoke; for then perforce"},{"sp":"N","t":"They'd either fall, borne down by their brute weight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like stones, or, like the smoke, they'd powerless be"},{"sp":"N","t":"To keep their mass, or to retain within"},{"sp":"N","t":"Frore snows and storms of hail. And they give forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'er skiey levels of the spreading world"},{"sp":"N","t":"A sound on high, as linen-awning, stretched"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'er mighty theatres, gives forth at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"A cracking roar, when much 'tis beaten about"},{"sp":"N","t":"Betwixt the poles and cross-beams. Sometimes, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Asunder rent by wanton gusts, it raves"},{"sp":"N","t":"And imitates the tearing sound of sheets"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of paper—even this kind of noise thou mayst"},{"sp":"N","t":"In thunder hear—or sound as when winds whirl"},{"sp":"N","t":"With lashings and do buffet about in air"},{"sp":"N","t":"A hanging cloth and flying paper-sheets."},{"sp":"N","t":"For sometimes, too, it chances that the clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cannot together crash head-on, but rather"},{"sp":"N","t":"Move side-wise and with motions contrary"},{"sp":"N","t":"Graze each the other's body without speed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From whence that dry sound grateth on our ears,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So long drawn-out, until the clouds have passed"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out their close positions."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, again,","st":"6.121"},{"sp":"N","t":"In following wise all things seem oft to quake"},{"sp":"N","t":"At shock of heavy thunder, and mightiest walls"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the wide reaches of the upper world"},{"sp":"N","t":"There on the instant to have sprung apart,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Riven asunder, what time a gathered blast"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the fierce hurricane hath all at once"},{"sp":"N","t":"Twisted its way into a mass of clouds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, there enclosed, ever more and more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Compelleth by its spinning whirl the cloud"},{"sp":"N","t":"To grow all hollow with a thickened crust"},{"sp":"N","t":"Surrounding; for thereafter, when the force"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the keen onset of the wind have weakened"},{"sp":"N","t":"That crust, lo, then the cloud, to-split in twain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gives forth a hideous crash with bang and boom."},{"sp":"N","t":"No marvel this; since oft a bladder small,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Filled up with air, will, when of sudden burst,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Give forth a like large sound."},{"sp":"N","t":"There's reason, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why clouds make sounds, as through them blow the winds:"},{"sp":"N","t":"We see, borne down the sky, oft shapes of clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rough-edged or branched many forky ways;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And 'tis the same, as when the sudden flaws"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of north-west wind through the dense forest blow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Making the leaves to sough and limbs to crash."},{"sp":"N","t":"It happens too at times that roused force"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the fierce hurricane to-rends the cloud,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Breaking right through it by a front assault;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For what a blast of wind may do up there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is manifest from facts when here on earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"A blast more gentle yet uptwists tall trees"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sucks them madly from their deepest roots."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, among the clouds are waves, and these"},{"sp":"N","t":"Give, as they roughly break, a rumbling roar;"},{"sp":"N","t":"As when along deep streams or the great sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"Breaks the loud surf. It happens, too, whenever"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out from one cloud into another falls"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fiery energy of thunderbolt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That straightaway the cloud, if full of wet,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Extinguishes the fire with mighty noise;"},{"sp":"N","t":"As iron, white from the hot furnaces,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sizzles, when speedily we've plunged its glow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down the cold water. Further, if a cloud"},{"sp":"N","t":"More dry receive the fire, 'twill suddenly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Kindle to flame and burn with monstrous sound,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As if a flame with whirl of winds should range"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the laurel-tressed mountains far,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upburning with its vast assault those trees;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor is there aught that in the crackling flame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Consumes with sound more terrible to man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than Delphic laurel of Apollo lord."},{"sp":"N","t":"Oft, too, the multitudinous crash of ice"},{"sp":"N","t":"And down-pour of swift hail gives forth a sound"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the mighty clouds on high; for when"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wind hath packed them close, each mountain mass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of rain-cloud, there congealed utterly"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mixed with hail-stones, breaks and booms..."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise, it lightens, when the clouds have struck,","st":"6.160"},{"sp":"N","t":"By their collision, forth the seeds of fire:"},{"sp":"N","t":"As if a stone should smite a stone or steel,"},{"sp":"N","t":"For light then too leaps forth and fire then scatters"},{"sp":"N","t":"The shining sparks. But with our ears we get"},{"sp":"N","t":"The thunder after eyes behold the flash,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because forever things arrive the ears"},{"sp":"N","t":"More tardily than the eyes—as thou mayst see"},{"sp":"N","t":"From this example too: when markest thou"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some man far yonder felling a great tree"},{"sp":"N","t":"With double-edged ax, it comes to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thine eye beholds the swinging stroke before"},{"sp":"N","t":"The blow gives forth a sound athrough thine ears:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus also we behold the flashing ere"},{"sp":"N","t":"We hear the thunder, which discharged is"},{"sp":"N","t":"At same time with the fire and by same cause,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Born of the same collision."},{"sp":"N","t":"In following wise","st":"6.173"},{"sp":"N","t":"The clouds suffuse with leaping light the lands,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the storm flashes with tremulous elan:"},{"sp":"N","t":"When the wind hath invaded a cloud, and, whirling there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath wrought (as I have shown above) the cloud"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into a hollow with a thickened crust,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It becomes hot of own velocity:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Just as thou seest how motion will o'erheat"},{"sp":"N","t":"And set ablaze all objects,—verily"},{"sp":"N","t":"A leaden ball, hurtling through length of space,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even melts. Therefore, when this same wind a-fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath split black cloud, it scatters the fire-seeds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which, so to say, have been pressed out by force"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of sudden from the cloud;—and these do make"},{"sp":"N","t":"The pulsing flashes of flame; thence followeth"},{"sp":"N","t":"The detonation which attacks our ears"},{"sp":"N","t":"More tardily than aught which comes along"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the sight of eyeballs. This takes place-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As know thou mayst—at times when clouds are dense"},{"sp":"N","t":"And one upon the other piled aloft"},{"sp":"N","t":"With wonderful upheavings—nor be thou"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deceived because we see how broad their base"},{"sp":"N","t":"From underneath, and not how high they tower."},{"sp":"N","t":"For make thine observations at a time"},{"sp":"N","t":"When winds shall bear athwart the horizon's blue"},{"sp":"N","t":"Clouds like to mountain-ranges moving on,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or when about the sides of mighty peaks"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou seest them one upon the other massed"},{"sp":"N","t":"And burdening downward, anchored in high repose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the winds sepulchred on all sides round:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then canst thou know their mighty masses, then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Canst view their caverns, as if builded there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of beetling crags; which, when the hurricanes"},{"sp":"N","t":"In gathered storm have filled utterly,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, prisoned in clouds, they rave around"},{"sp":"N","t":"With mighty roarings, and within those dens"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bluster like savage beasts, and now from here,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And now from there, send growlings through the clouds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And seeking an outlet, whirl themselves about,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And roll from 'mid the clouds the seeds of fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And heap them multitudinously there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in the hollow furnaces within"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wheel flame around, until from bursted cloud"},{"sp":"N","t":"In forky flashes they have gleamed forth."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, from following cause it comes to pass","st":"6.204"},{"sp":"N","t":"That yon swift golden hue of liquid fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Darts downward to the earth: because the clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Themselves must hold abundant seeds of fire;"},{"sp":"N","t":"For, when they be without all moisture, then"},{"sp":"N","t":"They be for most part of a flamy hue"},{"sp":"N","t":"And a resplendent. And, indeed, they must"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even from the light of sun unto themselves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take multitudinous seeds, and so perforce"},{"sp":"N","t":"Redden and pour their bright fires all abroad."},{"sp":"N","t":"And therefore, when the wind hath driven and thrust,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath forced and squeezed into one spot these clouds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They pour abroad the seeds of fire pressed out,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which make to flash these colours of the flame."},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise, it lightens also when the clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grow rare and thin along the sky; for, when"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wind with gentle touch unravels them"},{"sp":"N","t":"And breaketh asunder as they move, those seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which make the lightnings must by nature fall;"},{"sp":"N","t":"At such an hour the horizon lightens round"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without the hideous terror of dread noise"},{"sp":"N","t":"And skiey uproar."},{"sp":"N","t":"To proceed apace,","st":"6.219"},{"sp":"N","t":"What sort of nature thunderbolts possess"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is by their strokes made manifest and by"},{"sp":"N","t":"The brand-marks of their searing heat on things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And by the scorched scars exhaling round"},{"sp":"N","t":"The heavy fumes of sulphur. For all these"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are marks, O not of wind or rain, but fire."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, they often enkindle even the roofs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of houses and inside the very rooms"},{"sp":"N","t":"With swift flame hold a fierce dominion."},{"sp":"N","t":"Know thou that nature fashioned this fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Subtler than fires all other, with minute"},{"sp":"N","t":"And dartling bodies,—a fire 'gainst which there's naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can in the least hold out: the thunderbolt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mighty, passes through the hedging walls"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of houses, like to voices or a shout,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through stones, through bronze it passes, and it melts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the instant bronze and gold; and makes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise, the wines sudden to vanish forth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wine-jars intact,—because, ye see,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its heat arriving renders loose and porous"},{"sp":"N","t":"Readily all the wine—jar's earthen sides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And winding its way within, it scattereth"},{"sp":"N","t":"The elements primordial of the wine"},{"sp":"N","t":"With speedy dissolution—process which"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even in an age the fiery steam of sun"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could not accomplish, however puissant he"},{"sp":"N","t":"With his hot coruscations: so much more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Agile and overpowering is this force."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now in what manner engendered are these things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How fashioned of such impetuous strength"},{"sp":"N","t":"As to cleave towers asunder, and houses all"},{"sp":"N","t":"To overtopple, and to wrench apart"},{"sp":"N","t":"Timbers and beams, and heroes' monuments"},{"sp":"N","t":"To pile in ruins and upheave amain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to take breath forever out of men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to o'erthrow the cattle everywhere,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yes, by what force the lightnings do all this,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All this and more, I will unfold to thee,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor longer keep thee in mere promises."},{"sp":"N","t":"The bolts of thunder, then, must be conceived","st":"6.246"},{"sp":"N","t":"As all begotten in those crasser clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Up-piled aloft; for, from the sky serene"},{"sp":"N","t":"And from the clouds of lighter density,"},{"sp":"N","t":"None are sent forth forever. That 'tis so"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beyond a doubt, fact plain to sense declares:"},{"sp":"N","t":"To wit, at such a time the densed clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"So mass themselves through all the upper air"},{"sp":"N","t":"That we might think that round about all murk"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had parted forth from Acheron and filled"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mighty vaults of sky—so grievously,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As gathers thus the storm-clouds' gruesome might,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do faces of black horror hang on high-"},{"sp":"N","t":"When tempest begins its thunderbolts to forge."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, full often also out at sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"A blackest thunderhead, like cataract"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of pitch hurled down from heaven, and far away"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bulging with murkiness, down on the waves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Falls with vast uproar, and draws on amain"},{"sp":"N","t":"The darkling tempests big with thunderbolts"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hurricanes, itself the while so crammed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Tremendously with fires and winds, that even"},{"sp":"N","t":"Back on the lands the people shudder round"},{"sp":"N","t":"And seek for cover. Therefore, as I said,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The storm must be conceived as o'er our head"},{"sp":"N","t":"Towering most high; for never would the clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'erwhelm the lands with such a massy dark,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unless up-builded heap on lofty heap,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To shut the round sun off. Nor could the clouds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As on they come, engulf with rain so vast"},{"sp":"N","t":"As thus to make the rivers overflow"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fields to float, if ether were not thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Furnished with lofty-piled clouds. Lo, then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Here be all things fulfilled with winds and fires-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hence the long lightnings and the thunders loud."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, verily, I've taught thee even now"},{"sp":"N","t":"How cavernous clouds hold seeds innumerable"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of fiery exhalations, and they must"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off the sunbeams and the heat of these"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take many still. And so, when that same wind"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Which, haply, into one region of the sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"Collects those clouds) hath pressed from out the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"The many fiery seeds, and with that fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath at the same time inter-mixed itself,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O then and there that wind, a whirlwind now,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deep in the belly of the cloud spins round"},{"sp":"N","t":"In narrow confines, and sharpens there inside"},{"sp":"N","t":"In glowing furnaces the thunderbolt."},{"sp":"N","t":"For in a two-fold manner is that wind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enkindled all: it trembles into heat"},{"sp":"N","t":"Both by its own velocity and by"},{"sp":"N","t":"Repeated touch of fire. Thereafter, when"},{"sp":"N","t":"The energy of wind is heated through"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the fierce impulse of the fire hath sped"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deeply within, O then the thunderbolt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now ripened, so to say, doth suddenly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Splinter the cloud, and the aroused flash"},{"sp":"N","t":"Leaps onward, lumining with forky light"},{"sp":"N","t":"All places round. And followeth anon"},{"sp":"N","t":"A clap so heavy that the skiey vaults,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As if asunder burst, seem from on high"},{"sp":"N","t":"To engulf the earth. Then fearfully a quake"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pervades the lands, and 'long the lofty skies"},{"sp":"N","t":"Run the far rumblings. For at such a time"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nigh the whole tempest quakes, shook through and through,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And roused are the roarings,—from which shock"},{"sp":"N","t":"Comes such resounding and abounding rain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That all the murky ether seems to turn"},{"sp":"N","t":"Now into rain, and, as it tumbles down,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To summon the fields back to primeval floods:"},{"sp":"N","t":"So big the rains that be sent down on men"},{"sp":"N","t":"By burst of cloud and by the hurricane,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What time the thunder-clap, from burning bolt"},{"sp":"N","t":"That cracks the cloud, flies forth along. At times"},{"sp":"N","t":"The force of wind, excited from without,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Smiteth into a cloud already hot"},{"sp":"N","t":"With a ripe thunderbolt."},{"sp":"N","t":"And when that wind","st":"6.295"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath splintered that cloud, then down there cleaves forthwith"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yon fiery coil of flame which still we call,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even with our fathers' word, a thunderbolt."},{"sp":"N","t":"The same thing haps toward every other side"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whither that force hath swept. It happens, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That sometimes force of wind, though hurtled forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without all fire, yet in its voyage through space"},{"sp":"N","t":"Igniteth, whilst it comes along, along,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Losing some larger bodies which cannot"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pass, like the others, through the bulks of air,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, scraping together out of air itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some smaller bodies, carries them along,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And these, commingling, by their flight make fire:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much in the manner as oft a leaden ball"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grows hot upon its aery course, the while"},{"sp":"N","t":"It loseth many bodies of stark cold"},{"sp":"N","t":"And taketh into itself along the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"New particles of fire. It happens, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That force of blow itself arouses fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When force of wind, a-cold and hurtled forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without all fire, hath strook somewhere amain-"},{"sp":"N","t":"No marvel, because, when with terrific stroke"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Thas smitten, the elements of fiery-stuff"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can stream together from out the very wind"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, simultaneously, from out that thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which then and there receives the stroke: as flies"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fire when with the steel we hack the stone;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor yet, because the force of steel's a-cold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rush the less speedily together there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Under the stroke its seeds of radiance hot."},{"sp":"N","t":"And therefore, thuswise must an object too"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be kindled by a thunderbolt, if haply"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Thas been adapt and suited to the flames."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet force of wind must not be rashly deemed"},{"sp":"N","t":"As altogether and entirely cold-"},{"sp":"N","t":"That force which is discharged from on high"},{"sp":"N","t":"With such stupendous power; but if 'tis not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon its course already kindled with fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It yet arriveth warmed and mixed with heat."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, now, the speed and stroke of thunderbolt","st":"6.323"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is so tremendous, and with glide so swift"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those thunderbolts rush on and down, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their roused force itself collects itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"First always in the clouds, and then prepares"},{"sp":"N","t":"For the huge effort of their going-forth;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Next, when the cloud no longer can retain"},{"sp":"N","t":"The increment of their fierce impetus,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their force is pressed out, and therefore flies"},{"sp":"N","t":"With impetus so wondrous, like to shots"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hurled from the powerful Roman catapults."},{"sp":"N","t":"Note, too, this force consists of elements"},{"sp":"N","t":"Both small and smooth, nor is there aught that can"},{"sp":"N","t":"With ease resist such nature. For it darts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Between and enters through the pores of things;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And so it never falters in delay"},{"sp":"N","t":"Despite innumerable collisions, but"},{"sp":"N","t":"Flies shooting onward with a swift elan."},{"sp":"N","t":"Next, since by nature always every weight"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bears downward, doubled is the swiftness then"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that elan is still more wild and dread,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When, verily, to weight are added blows,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that more madly and more fiercely then"},{"sp":"N","t":"The thunderbolt shakes into shivers all"},{"sp":"N","t":"That blocks its path, following on its way."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, too, because it comes along, along"},{"sp":"N","t":"With one continuing elan, it must"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take on velocity anew, anew,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which still increases as it goes, and ever"},{"sp":"N","t":"Augments the bolt's vast powers and to the blow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gives larger vigour; for it forces all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All of the thunder's seeds of fire, to sweep"},{"sp":"N","t":"In a straight line unto one place, as 'twere,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Casting them one by other, as they roll,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into that onward course. Again, perchance,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In coming along, it pulls from out the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some certain bodies, which by their own blows"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enkindle its velocity. And, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It comes through objects leaving them unharmed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It goes through many things and leaves them whole,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because the liquid fire flieth along"},{"sp":"N","t":"Athrough their pores. And much it does transfix,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When these primordial atoms of the bolt"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have fallen upon the atoms of these things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Precisely where the intertwined atoms"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are held together. And, further, easily"},{"sp":"N","t":"Brass it unbinds and quickly fuseth gold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because its force is so minutely made"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of tiny parts and elements so smooth"},{"sp":"N","t":"That easily they wind their way within,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, when once in, quickly unbind all knots"},{"sp":"N","t":"And loosen all the bonds of union there."},{"sp":"N","t":"And most in autumn is shaken the house of heaven,","st":"6.357"},{"sp":"N","t":"The house so studded with the glittering stars,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the whole earth around—most too in spring"},{"sp":"N","t":"When flowery times unfold themselves: for, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the cold season is there lack of fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And winds are scanty in the hot, and clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have not so dense a bulk. But when, indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seasons of heaven are betwixt these twain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The divers causes of the thunderbolt"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then all concur; for then both cold and heat"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are mixed in the cross-seas of the year,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So that a discord rises among things"},{"sp":"N","t":"And air in vast tumultuosity"},{"sp":"N","t":"Billows, infuriate with the fires and winds-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of which the both are needed by the cloud"},{"sp":"N","t":"For fabrication of the thunderbolt."},{"sp":"N","t":"For the first part of heat and last of cold"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is the time of spring; wherefore must things unlike"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do battle one with other, and, when mixed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Tumultuously rage. And when rolls round"},{"sp":"N","t":"The latest heat mixed with the earliest chill-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The time which bears the name of autumn—then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise fierce cold-spells wrestle with fierce heats."},{"sp":"N","t":"On this account these seasons of the year"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are nominated \"cross-seas.\"- And no marvel"},{"sp":"N","t":"If in those times the thunderbolts prevail"},{"sp":"N","t":"And storms are roused turbulent in heaven,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since then both sides in dubious warfare rage"},{"sp":"N","t":"Tumultuously, the one with flames, the other"},{"sp":"N","t":"With winds and with waters mixed with winds."},{"sp":"N","t":"This, this it is, O Memmius, to see through","st":"6.379"},{"sp":"N","t":"The very nature of fire-fraught thunderbolt;"},{"sp":"N","t":"O this it is to mark by what blind force"},{"sp":"N","t":"It maketh each effect, and not, O not"},{"sp":"N","t":"To unwind Etrurian scrolls oracular,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Inquiring tokens of occult will of gods,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as to whence the flying flame hath come,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or to which half of heaven it turns, or how"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through walled places it hath wound its way,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or, after proving its dominion there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How it hath speeded forth from thence amain,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or what the thunderstroke portends of ill"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out high heaven. But if Jupiter"},{"sp":"N","t":"And other gods shake those refulgent vaults"},{"sp":"N","t":"With dread reverberations and hurl fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whither it pleases each, why smite they not"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mortals of reckless and revolting crimes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That such may pant from a transpierced breast"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forth flames of the red levin—unto men"},{"sp":"N","t":"A drastic lesson?- why is rather he-"},{"sp":"N","t":"O he self-conscious of no foul offence-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Involved in flames, though innocent, and clasped"},{"sp":"N","t":"Up-caught in skiey whirlwind and in fire?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nay, why, then, aim they at eternal wastes,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And spend themselves in vain?- perchance, even so"},{"sp":"N","t":"To exercise their arms and strengthen shoulders?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why suffer they the Father's javelin"},{"sp":"N","t":"To be so blunted on the earth? And why"},{"sp":"N","t":"Doth he himself allow it, nor spare the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even for his enemies? O why most oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aims he at lofty places? Why behold we"},{"sp":"N","t":"Marks of his lightnings most on mountain tops?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then for what reason shoots he at the sea?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"What sacrilege have waves and bulk of brine"},{"sp":"N","t":"And floating fields of foam been guilty of?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, if 'tis his will that we beware"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against the lightning-stroke, why feareth he"},{"sp":"N","t":"To grant us power for to behold the shot?"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, contrariwise, if wills he to o'erwhelm us,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Quite off our guard, with fire, why thunders he"},{"sp":"N","t":"Off in yon quarter, so that we may shun?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Why rouseth he beforehand darkling air"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the far din and rumblings? And O how"},{"sp":"N","t":"Canst thou believe he shoots at one same time"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into diverse directions? Or darest thou"},{"sp":"N","t":"Contend that never hath it come to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"That divers strokes have happened at one time?"},{"sp":"N","t":"But oft and often hath it come to pass,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And often still it must, that, even as showers"},{"sp":"N","t":"And rains o'er many regions fall, so too"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dart many thunderbolts at one same time."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, why never hurtles Jupiter"},{"sp":"N","t":"A bolt upon the lands nor pours abroad"},{"sp":"N","t":"Clap upon clap, when skies are cloudless all?"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or, say, doth he, so soon as ever the clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have come thereunder, then into the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"Descend in person, that from thence he may"},{"sp":"N","t":"Near-by decide upon the stroke of shaft?"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, lastly, why, with devastating bolt"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shakes he asunder holy shrines of gods"},{"sp":"N","t":"And his own thrones of splendour, and to-breaks"},{"sp":"N","t":"The well-wrought idols of divinities,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And robs of glory his own images"},{"sp":"N","t":"By wound of violence?"},{"sp":"N","t":"But to return apace,","st":"6.423"},{"sp":"N","t":"Easy it is from these same facts to know"},{"sp":"N","t":"In just what wise those things (which from their sort"},{"sp":"N","t":"The Greeks have named \"bellows\") do come down,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Discharged from on high, upon the seas."},{"sp":"N","t":"For it haps that sometimes from the sky descends"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the seas a column, as if pushed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Round which the surges seethe, tremendously"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aroused by puffing gusts; and whatso'er"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of ships are caught within that tumult then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Come into extreme peril, dashed along."},{"sp":"N","t":"This haps when sometimes wind's aroused force"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can't burst the cloud it tries to, but down-weighs"},{"sp":"N","t":"That cloud, until 'tis like a column from sky"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the seas pushed downward—gradually,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As if a Somewhat from on high were shoved"},{"sp":"N","t":"By fist and nether thrust of arm, and lengthened"},{"sp":"N","t":"Far to the waves. And when the force of wind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath rived this cloud, from out the cloud it rushes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down on the seas, and starts among the waves"},{"sp":"N","t":"A wondrous seething, for the eddying whirl"},{"sp":"N","t":"Descends and downward draws along with it"},{"sp":"N","t":"That cloud of ductile body. And soon as ever"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Thas shoved unto the levels of the main"},{"sp":"N","t":"That laden cloud, the whirl suddenly then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Plunges its whole self into the waters there"},{"sp":"N","t":"And rouses all the sea with monstrous roar,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Constraining it to seethe. It happens too"},{"sp":"N","t":"That very vortex of the wind involves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Itself in clouds, scraping from out the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds of cloud, and counterfeits, as 'twere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The \"bellows\" pushed from heaven. And when this shape"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath dropped upon the lands and burst apart,"},{"sp":"N","t":"It belches forth immeasurable might"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of whirlwind and of blast. Yet since 'tis formed"},{"sp":"N","t":"At most but rarely, and on land the hills"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must block its way, 'tis seen more oft out there"},{"sp":"N","t":"On the broad prospect of the level main"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the free horizons."},{"sp":"N","t":"Into being","st":"6.443"},{"sp":"N","t":"The clouds condense, when in this upper space"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the high heaven have gathered suddenly,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As round they flew, unnumbered particles-"},{"sp":"N","t":"World's rougher ones, which can, though interlinked"},{"sp":"N","t":"With scanty couplings, yet be fastened firm,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The one on other caught. These particles"},{"sp":"N","t":"First cause small clouds to form; and, thereupon,"},{"sp":"N","t":"These catch the one on other and swarm in a flock"},{"sp":"N","t":"And grow by their conjoining, and by winds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are borne along, along, until collects"},{"sp":"N","t":"The tempest fury. Happens, too, the nearer"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mountain summits neighbour to the sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The more unceasingly their far crags smoke"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the thick darkness of swart cloud, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"When first the mists do form, ere ever the eyes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can there behold them (tenuous as they be),"},{"sp":"N","t":"The carrier-winds will drive them up and on"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the topmost summits of the mountain;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then at last it happens, when they be"},{"sp":"N","t":"In vaster throng upgathered, that they can"},{"sp":"N","t":"By this very condensation lie revealed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And that at same time they are seen to surge"},{"sp":"N","t":"From very vertex of the mountain up"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into far ether. For very fact and feeling,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As we up-climb high mountains, proveth clear"},{"sp":"N","t":"That windy are those upward regions free."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, the clothes hung-out along the shore,","st":"6.470"},{"sp":"N","t":"When in they take the clinging moisture, prove"},{"sp":"N","t":"That nature lifts from over all the sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unnumbered particles. Whereby the more"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis manifest that many particles"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even from the salt upheavings of the main"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can rise together to augment the bulk"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of massed clouds. For moistures in these twain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are near akin. Besides, from out all rivers,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As well as from the land itself, we see"},{"sp":"N","t":"Up-rising mists and steam, which like a breath"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are forced out from them and borne aloft,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To curtain heaven with their murk, and make,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By slow foregathering, the skiey clouds."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, in addition, lo, the heat on high"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of constellated ether burdens down"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon them, and by sort of condensation"},{"sp":"N","t":"Weaveth beneath the azure firmament"},{"sp":"N","t":"The reek of darkling cloud. It happens, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That hither to the skies from the Beyond"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do come those particles which make the clouds"},{"sp":"N","t":"And flying thunderheads. For I have taught"},{"sp":"N","t":"That this their number is innumerable"},{"sp":"N","t":"And infinite the sum of the Abyss,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And I have shown with what stupendous speed"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those bodies fly and how they're wont to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Amain through incommunicable space."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore, 'tis not exceeding strange, if oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"In little time tempest and darkness cover"},{"sp":"N","t":"With bulking thunderheads hanging on high"},{"sp":"N","t":"The oceans and the lands, since everywhere"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through all the narrow tubes of yonder ether,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yea, so to speak, through all the breathing-holes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the great upper-world encompassing,"},{"sp":"N","t":"There be for the primordial elements"},{"sp":"N","t":"Exits and entrances."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now come, and how","st":"6.495"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rainy moisture thickens into being"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the lofty clouds, and how upon the lands"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis then discharged in down-pour of large showers,"},{"sp":"N","t":"I will unfold. And first triumphantly"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will I persuade thee that up-rise together,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With clouds themselves, full many seeds of water"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out all things, and that they both increase-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Both clouds and water which is in the clouds-"},{"sp":"N","t":"In like proportion, as our frames increase"},{"sp":"N","t":"In like proportion with our blood, as well"},{"sp":"N","t":"As sweat or any moisture in our members."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, the clouds take in from time to time"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much moisture risen from the broad marine,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilst the winds bear them o'er the mighty sea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like hanging fleeces of white wool. Thuswise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even from all rivers is there lifted up"},{"sp":"N","t":"Moisture into the clouds. And when therein"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds of water so many in many ways"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have come together, augmented from all sides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The close-jammed clouds then struggle to discharge"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their rain-storms for a two-fold reason: lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wind's force crowds them, and the very excess"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of storm-clouds (massed in a vaster throng)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Giveth an urge and pressure from above"},{"sp":"N","t":"And makes the rains out-pour. Besides when, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The clouds are winnowed by the winds, or scattered"},{"sp":"N","t":"Smitten on top by heat of sun, they send"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their rainy moisture, and distil their drops,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even as the wax, by fiery warmth on top,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wasteth and liquefies abundantly."},{"sp":"N","t":"But comes the violence of the bigger rains"},{"sp":"N","t":"When violently the clouds are weighted down"},{"sp":"N","t":"Both by their cumulated mass and by"},{"sp":"N","t":"The onset of the wind. And rains are wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"To endure awhile and to abide for long,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When many seeds of waters are aroused,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And clouds on clouds and racks on racks outstream"},{"sp":"N","t":"In piled layers and are borne along"},{"sp":"N","t":"From every quarter, and when all the earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Smoking exhales her moisture. At such a time"},{"sp":"N","t":"When sun with beams amid the tempest-murk"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath shone against the showers of black rains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then in the swart clouds there emerges bright"},{"sp":"N","t":"The radiance of the bow."},{"sp":"N","t":"And as to things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not mentioned here which of themselves do grow"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or of themselves are gendered, and all things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which in the clouds condense to being—all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Snow and the winds, hail and the hoar-frosts chill,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And freezing, mighty force—of lakes and pools"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mighty hardener, and mighty check"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which in the winter curbeth everywhere"},{"sp":"N","t":"The rivers as they go- 'tis easy still,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Soon to discover and with mind to see"},{"sp":"N","t":"How they all happen, whereby gendered,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When once thou well hast understood just what"},{"sp":"N","t":"Functions have been vouchsafed from of old"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the procreant atoms of the world."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now come, and what the law of earthquakes is","st":"6.535"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hearken, and first of all take care to know"},{"sp":"N","t":"That the under-earth, like to the earth around us,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is full of windy caverns all about;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And many a pool and many a grim abyss"},{"sp":"N","t":"She bears within her bosom, ay, and cliffs"},{"sp":"N","t":"And jagged scarps; and many a river, hid"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beneath her chine, rolls rapidly along"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its billows and plunging boulders. For clear fact"},{"sp":"N","t":"Requires that earth must be in every part"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alike in constitution. Therefore, earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With these things underneath affixed and set,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Trembleth above, jarred by big down-tumblings,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When time hath undermined the huge caves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The subterranean. Yea, whole mountains fall,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And instantly from spot of that big jar"},{"sp":"N","t":"There quiver the tremors far and wide abroad."},{"sp":"N","t":"And with good reason: since houses on the street"},{"sp":"N","t":"Begin to quake throughout, when jarred by a cart"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of no large weight; and, too, the furniture"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the house up-bounds, when a paving-block"},{"sp":"N","t":"Gives either iron rim of the wheels a jolt."},{"sp":"N","t":"It happens, too, when some prodigious bulk"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of age-worn soil is rolled from mountain slopes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into tremendous pools of water dark,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That the reeling land itself is rocked about"},{"sp":"N","t":"By the water's undulations; as a basin"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sometimes won't come to rest until the fluid"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within it ceases to be rocked about"},{"sp":"N","t":"In random undulations."},{"sp":"N","t":"And besides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When subterranean winds, up-gathered there"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the hollow deeps, bulk forward from one spot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And press with the big urge of mighty powers"},{"sp":"N","t":"Against the lofty grottos, then the earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bulks to that quarter whither push amain"},{"sp":"N","t":"The headlong winds. Then all the builded houses"},{"sp":"N","t":"Above ground—and the more, the higher up-reared"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the sky—lean ominously, careening"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the same direction; and the beams,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wrenched forward, over-hang, ready to go."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet dread men to believe that there awaits"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of the mighty world a time"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of doom and cataclysm, albeit they see"},{"sp":"N","t":"So great a bulk of lands to bulge and break!"},{"sp":"N","t":"And lest the winds blew back again, no force"},{"sp":"N","t":"Could rein things in nor hold from sure career"},{"sp":"N","t":"On to disaster. But now because those winds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Blow back and forth in alternation strong,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, so to say, rallying charge again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then repulsed retreat, on this account"},{"sp":"N","t":"Earth oftener threatens than she brings to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Collapses dire. For to one side she leans,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then back she sways; and after tottering"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forward, recovers then her seats of poise."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, this is why whole houses rock, the roofs"},{"sp":"N","t":"More than the middle stories, middle more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than lowest, and the lowest least of all."},{"sp":"N","t":"Arises, too, this same great earth-quaking,","st":"6.577"},{"sp":"N","t":"When wind and some prodigious force of air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Collected from without or down within"},{"sp":"N","t":"The old telluric deeps, have hurled themselves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Amain into those caverns sub-terrene,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And there at first tumultuously chafe"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the vasty grottos, borne about"},{"sp":"N","t":"In mad rotations, till their lashed force"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aroused out-bursts abroad, and then and there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Riving the deep earth, makes a mighty chasm-"},{"sp":"N","t":"What once in Syrian Sidon did befall,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And once in Peloponnesian Aegium,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Twain cities which such out-break of wild air"},{"sp":"N","t":"And earth's convulsion, following hard upon,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'erthrew of old. And many a walled town,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, hath fall'n by such omnipotent"},{"sp":"N","t":"Convulsions on the land, and in the sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"Engulfed hath sunken many a city down"},{"sp":"N","t":"With all its populace. But if, indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They burst not forth, yet is the very rush"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the wild air and fury-force of wind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then dissipated, like an ague-fit,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through the innumerable pores of earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To set her all a-shake—even as a chill,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When it hath gone into our marrow-bones,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sets us convulsively, despite ourselves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A-shivering and a-shaking. Therefore, men"},{"sp":"N","t":"With two-fold terror bustle in alarm"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through cities to and fro: they fear the roofs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Above the head; and underfoot they dread"},{"sp":"N","t":"The caverns, lest the nature of the earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Suddenly rend them open, and she gape,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Herself asunder, with tremendous maw,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, all confounded, seek to chock it full"},{"sp":"N","t":"With her own ruins. Let men, then, go on"},{"sp":"N","t":"Feigning at will that heaven and earth shall be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Inviolable, entrusted evermore"},{"sp":"N","t":"To an eternal weal: and yet at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"The very force of danger here at hand"},{"sp":"N","t":"Prods them on some side with this goad of fear-"},{"sp":"N","t":"This among others—that the earth, withdrawn"},{"sp":"N","t":"Abruptly from under their feet, be hurried down,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down into the abyss, and the Sum-of-Things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be following after, utterly fordone,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Till be but wrack and wreckage of a world."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"EXTRAORDINARY AND PARADOXICAL TELLURIC PHENOMENA"},{"sp":"N","t":"In chief, men marvel nature renders not","st":"6.608"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bigger and bigger the bulk of ocean, since"},{"sp":"N","t":"So vast the down-rush of the waters be,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And every river out of every realm"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cometh thereto; and add the random rains"},{"sp":"N","t":"And flying tempests, which spatter every sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"And every land bedew; add their own springs:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet all of these unto the ocean's sum"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shall be but as the increase of a drop."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore 'tis less a marvel that the sea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mighty ocean, increaseth not. Besides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sun with his heat draws off a mighty part:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yea, we behold that sun with burning beams"},{"sp":"N","t":"To dry our garments dripping all with wet;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And many a sea, and far out-spread beneath,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Do we behold. Therefore, however slight"},{"sp":"N","t":"The portion of wet that sun on any spot"},{"sp":"N","t":"Culls from the level main, he still will take"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off the waves in such a wide expanse"},{"sp":"N","t":"Abundantly. Then, further, also winds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sweeping the level waters, can bear off"},{"sp":"N","t":"A mighty part of wet, since we behold"},{"sp":"N","t":"Oft in a single night the highways dried"},{"sp":"N","t":"By winds, and soft mud crusted o'er at dawn."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, I've taught thee that the clouds bear off"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much moisture too, up-taken from the reaches"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the mighty main, and sprinkle it about"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'er all the zones, when rain is on the lands"},{"sp":"N","t":"And winds convey the aery racks of vapour."},{"sp":"N","t":"Lastly, since earth is porous through her frame,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And neighbours on the seas, girdling their shores,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The water's wet must seep into the lands"},{"sp":"N","t":"From briny ocean, as from lands it comes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the seas. For brine is filtered off,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then the liquid stuff seeps back again"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all re-poureth at the river-heads,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whence in fresh-water currents it returns"},{"sp":"N","t":"Over the lands, adown the channels which"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were cleft erstwhile and erstwhile bore along"},{"sp":"N","t":"The liquid-footed floods."},{"sp":"N","t":"And now the cause","st":"6.639"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereby athrough the throat of Aetna's Mount"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such vast tornado-fires out-breathe at times,"},{"sp":"N","t":"I will unfold: for with no middling might"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of devastation the flamy tempest rose"},{"sp":"N","t":"And held dominion in Sicilian fields:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Drawing upon itself the upturned faces"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of neighbouring clans, what time they saw afar"},{"sp":"N","t":"The skiey vaults a-fume and sparkling all,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And filled their bosoms with dread anxiety"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of what new thing nature were travailing at."},{"sp":"N","t":"In these affairs it much behooveth thee"},{"sp":"N","t":"To look both wide and deep, and far abroad"},{"sp":"N","t":"To peer to every quarter, that thou mayst"},{"sp":"N","t":"Remember how boundless is the Sum-of-Things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And mark how infinitely small a part"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the whole Sum is this one sky of ours-"},{"sp":"N","t":"O not so large a part as is one man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the whole earth. And plainly if thou viewest"},{"sp":"N","t":"This cosmic fact, placing it square in front,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And plainly understandest, thou wilt leave"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wondering at many things. For who of us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wondereth if some one gets into his joints"},{"sp":"N","t":"A fever, gathering head with fiery heat,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or any other dolorous disease"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along his members? For anon the foot"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grows blue and bulbous; often the sharp twinge"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seizes the teeth, attacks the very eyes;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out-breaks the sacred fire, and, crawling on"},{"sp":"N","t":"Over the body, burneth every part"},{"sp":"N","t":"It seizeth on, and works its hideous way"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the frame. No marvel this, since, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of things innumerable be seeds enough,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And this our earth and sky do bring to us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Enough of bane from whence can grow the strength"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of maladies uncounted. Thuswise, then,"},{"sp":"N","t":"We must suppose to all the sky and earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are ever supplied from out the infinite"},{"sp":"N","t":"All things, O all in stores enough whereby"},{"sp":"N","t":"The shaken earth can of a sudden move,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And fierce typhoons can over sea and lands"},{"sp":"N","t":"Go tearing on, and Aetna's fires o'erflow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And heaven become a flame-burst. For that, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Happens at times, and the celestial vaults"},{"sp":"N","t":"Glow into fire, and rainy tempests rise"},{"sp":"N","t":"In heavier congregation, when, percase,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds of water have foregathered thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out the infinite. \"Aye, but passing huge"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fiery turmoil of that conflagration!\""},{"sp":"N","t":"So sayst thou; well, huge many a river seems"},{"sp":"N","t":"To him that erstwhile ne'er a larger saw;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, huge seems tree or man; and everything"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which mortal sees the biggest of each class,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That he imagines to be \"huge\"; though yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"All these, with sky and land and sea to boot,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are all as nothing to the sum entire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the all-Sum."},{"sp":"N","t":"But now I will unfold","st":"6.680"},{"sp":"N","t":"At last how yonder suddenly angered flame"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out-blows abroad from vasty furnaces"},{"sp":"N","t":"Aetnaean. First, the mountain's nature is"},{"sp":"N","t":"All under-hollow, propped about, about"},{"sp":"N","t":"With caverns of basaltic piers. And, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In all its grottos be there wind and air-"},{"sp":"N","t":"For wind is made when air hath been uproused"},{"sp":"N","t":"By violent agitation. When this air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is heated through and through, and, raging round,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath made the earth and all the rocks it touches"},{"sp":"N","t":"Horribly hot, and hath struck off from them"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fierce fire of swiftest flame, it lifts itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hurtles thus straight upwards through its throat"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into high heav'n, and thus bears on afar"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its burning blasts and scattereth afar"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its ashes, and rolls a smoke of pitchy murk"},{"sp":"N","t":"And heaveth the while boulders of wondrous weight-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Leaving no doubt in thee that 'tis the air's"},{"sp":"N","t":"Tumultuous power. Besides, in mighty part,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sea there at the roots of that same mount"},{"sp":"N","t":"Breaks its old billows and sucks back its surf."},{"sp":"N","t":"And grottos from the sea pass in below"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even to the bottom of the mountain's throat."},{"sp":"N","t":"Herethrough thou must admit there go..."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"And the conditions force [the water and air]"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deeply to penetrate from the open sea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to out-blow abroad, and to up-bear"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thereby the flame, and to up-cast from deeps"},{"sp":"N","t":"The boulders, and to rear the clouds of sand."},{"sp":"N","t":"For at the top be \"bowls,\" as people there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are wont to name what we at Rome do call"},{"sp":"N","t":"The throats and mouths."},{"sp":"N","t":"There be, besides, some thing","st":"6.703"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of which 'tis not enough one only cause"},{"sp":"N","t":"To state—but rather several, whereof one"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will be the true: lo, if thou shouldst espy"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lying afar some fellow's lifeless corse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twere meet to name all causes of a death,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That cause of his death might thereby be named:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For prove thou mayst he perished not by steel,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By cold, nor even by poison nor disease,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet somewhat of this sort hath come to him"},{"sp":"N","t":"We know- And thus we have to say the same"},{"sp":"N","t":"In divers cases."},{"sp":"N","t":"Toward the summer, Nile"},{"sp":"N","t":"Waxeth and overfloweth the champaign,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unique in all the landscape, river sole"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the Aegyptians. In mid-season heats"},{"sp":"N","t":"Often and oft he waters Aegypt o'er,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Either because in summer against his mouths"},{"sp":"N","t":"Come those northwinds which at that time of year"},{"sp":"N","t":"Men name the Etesian blasts, and, blowing thus"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upstream, retard, and, forcing back his waves,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fill him o'erfull and force his flow to stop."},{"sp":"N","t":"For out of doubt these blasts which driven be"},{"sp":"N","t":"From icy constellations of the pole"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are borne straight up the river. Comes that river"},{"sp":"N","t":"From forth the sultry places down the south,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rising far up in midmost realm of day,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among black generations of strong men"},{"sp":"N","t":"With sun-baked skins. 'Tis possible, besides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That a big bulk of piled sand may bar"},{"sp":"N","t":"His mouths against his onward waves, when sea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wild in the winds, tumbles the sand to inland;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereby the river's outlet were less free,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise less headlong his descending floods."},{"sp":"N","t":"It may be, too, that in this season rains"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are more abundant at its fountain head,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because the Etesian blasts of those northwinds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then urge all clouds into those inland parts."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, soothly, when they're thus foregathered there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Urged yonder into midmost realm of day,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, crowded against the lofty mountain sides,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They're massed and powerfully pressed. Again,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perchance, his waters wax, O far away,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the Aethiopians' lofty mountains,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When the all-beholding sun with thawing beams"},{"sp":"N","t":"Drives the white snows to flow into the vales."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now come; and unto thee I will unfold,","st":"6.738"},{"sp":"N","t":"As to the Birdless spots and Birdless tarns,"},{"sp":"N","t":"What sort of nature they are furnished with."},{"sp":"N","t":"First, as to name of \"birdless,\"- that derives"},{"sp":"N","t":"From very fact, because they noxious be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto all birds. For when above those spots"},{"sp":"N","t":"In horizontal flight the birds have come,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forgetting to oar with wings, they furl their sails,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, with down-drooping of their delicate necks,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fall headlong into earth, if haply such"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nature of the spots, or into water,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If haply spreads thereunder Birdless tarn."},{"sp":"N","t":"Such spot's at Cumae, where the mountains smoke,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Charged with the pungent sulphur, and increased"},{"sp":"N","t":"With steaming springs. And such a spot there is"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the walls of Athens, even there"},{"sp":"N","t":"On summit of Acropolis, beside"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fane of Tritonian Pallas bountiful,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Where never cawing crows can wing their course,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Not even when smoke the altars with good gifts,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"But evermore they flee—yet not from wrath"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of Pallas, grieved at that espial old,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As poets of the Greeks have sung the tale;"},{"sp":"N","t":"But very nature of the place compels."},{"sp":"N","t":"In Syria also—as men say—a spot"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is to be seen, where also four-foot kinds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As soon as ever they've set their steps within,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Collapse, o'ercome by its essential power,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As if there slaughtered to the under-gods."},{"sp":"N","t":"Lo, all these wonders work by natural law,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And from what causes they are brought to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"The origin is manifest; so, haply,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Let none believe that in these regions stands"},{"sp":"N","t":"The gate of Orcus, nor us then suppose,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Haply, that thence the under-gods draw down"},{"sp":"N","t":"Souls to dark shores of Acheron—as stags,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wing-footed, are thought to draw to light,"},{"sp":"N","t":"By sniffing nostrils, from their dusky lairs"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wriggling generations of wild snakes."},{"sp":"N","t":"How far removed from true reason is this,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perceive thou straight; for now I'll try to say"},{"sp":"N","t":"Somewhat about the very fact."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, first,","st":"6.769"},{"sp":"N","t":"This do I say, as oft I've said before:"},{"sp":"N","t":"In earth are atoms of things of every sort;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And know, these all thus rise from out the earth-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Many life-giving which be good for food,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And many which can generate disease"},{"sp":"N","t":"And hasten death, O many primal seeds"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of many things in many modes—since earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Contains them mingled and gives forth discrete."},{"sp":"N","t":"And we have shown before that certain things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Be unto certain creatures suited more"},{"sp":"N","t":"For ends of life, by virtue of a nature,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A texture, and primordial shapes, unlike"},{"sp":"N","t":"For kinds alike. Then too 'tis thine to see"},{"sp":"N","t":"How many things oppressive be and foul"},{"sp":"N","t":"To man, and to sensation most malign:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Many meander miserably through ears;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Many in-wind athrough the nostrils too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Malign and harsh when mortal draws a breath;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of not a few must one avoid the touch;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of not a few must one escape the sight;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And some there be all loathsome to the taste;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And many, besides, relax the languid limbs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the frame, and undermine the soul"},{"sp":"N","t":"In its abodes within. To certain trees"},{"sp":"N","t":"There hath been given so dolorous a shade"},{"sp":"N","t":"That often they gender achings of the head,"},{"sp":"N","t":"If one but be beneath, outstretched on the sward."},{"sp":"N","t":"There is, again, on Helicon's high hills"},{"sp":"N","t":"A tree that's wont to kill a man outright"},{"sp":"N","t":"By fetid odour of its very flower."},{"sp":"N","t":"And when the pungent stench of the night-lamp,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Extinguished but a moment since, assails"},{"sp":"N","t":"The nostrils, then and there it puts to sleep"},{"sp":"N","t":"A man afflicted with the falling sickness"},{"sp":"N","t":"And foamings at the mouth. A woman, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At the heavy castor drowses back in chair,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And from her delicate fingers slips away"},{"sp":"N","t":"Her gaudy handiwork, if haply she"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath got the whiff at menstruation-time."},{"sp":"N","t":"Once more, if thou delayest in hot baths,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When thou art over-full, how readily"},{"sp":"N","t":"From stool in middle of the steaming water"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou tumblest in a fit! How readily"},{"sp":"N","t":"The heavy fumes of charcoal wind their way"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the brain, unless beforehand we"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of water 've drunk. But when a burning fever,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O'ermastering man, hath seized upon his limbs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then odour of wine is like a hammer-blow."},{"sp":"N","t":"And seest thou not how in the very earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sulphur is gendered and bitumen thickens"},{"sp":"N","t":"With noisome stench?- What direful stenches, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Scaptensula out-breathes from down below,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When men pursue the veins of silver and gold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"With pick-axe probing round the hidden realms"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deep in the earth?- Or what of deadly bane"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mines of gold exhale? O what a look,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And what a ghastly hue they give to men!"},{"sp":"N","t":"And seest thou not, or hearest, how they're wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"In little time to perish, and how fail"},{"sp":"N","t":"The life-stores in those folk whom mighty power"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of grim necessity confineth there"},{"sp":"N","t":"In such a task? Thus, this telluric earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out-streams with all these dread effluvia"},{"sp":"N","t":"And breathes them out into the open world"},{"sp":"N","t":"And into the visible regions under heaven."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, too, those Birdless places must up-send","st":"6.818"},{"sp":"N","t":"An essence bearing death to winged things,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which from the earth rises into the breezes"},{"sp":"N","t":"To poison part of skiey space, and when"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thither the winged is on pennons borne,"},{"sp":"N","t":"There, seized by the unseen poison, 'tis ensnared,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And from the horizontal of its flight"},{"sp":"N","t":"Drops to the spot whence sprang the effluvium."},{"sp":"N","t":"And when 'thas there collapsed, then the same power"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of that effluvium takes from all its limbs"},{"sp":"N","t":"The relics of its life. That power first strikes"},{"sp":"N","t":"The creatures with a wildering dizziness,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then thereafter, when they're once down-fallen"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the poison's very fountains, then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Life, too, they vomit out perforce, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"So thick the stores of bane around them fume."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, at times it happens that this power,"},{"sp":"N","t":"This exhalation of the Birdless places,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dispels the air betwixt the ground and birds,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Leaving well-nigh a void. And thither when"},{"sp":"N","t":"In horizontal flight the birds have come,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forthwith their buoyancy of pennons limps,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All useless, and each effort of both wings"},{"sp":"N","t":"Falls out in vain. Here, when without all power"},{"sp":"N","t":"To buoy themselves and on their wings to lean,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lo, nature constrains them by their weight to slip"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down to the earth, and lying prostrate there"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the well-nigh empty void, they spend"},{"sp":"N","t":"Their souls through all the openings of their frame."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"Further, the water of wells is colder then","st":"6.840"},{"sp":"N","t":"At summer time, because the earth by heat"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is rarefied, and sends abroad in air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whatever seeds it peradventure have"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of its own fiery exhalations."},{"sp":"N","t":"The more, then, the telluric ground is drained"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of heat, the colder grows the water hid"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the earth. Further, when all the earth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is by the cold compressed, and thus contracts"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, so to say, concretes, it happens, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That by contracting it expresses then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the wells what heat it bears itself."},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis said at Hammon's fane a fountain is,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In daylight cold and hot in time of night."},{"sp":"N","t":"This fountain men be-wonder over-much,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And think that suddenly it seethes in heat"},{"sp":"N","t":"By intense sun, the subterranean, when"},{"sp":"N","t":"Night with her terrible murk hath cloaked the lands-"},{"sp":"N","t":"What's not true reasoning by a long remove:"},{"sp":"N","t":"I' faith when sun o'erhead, touching with beams"},{"sp":"N","t":"An open body of water, had no power"},{"sp":"N","t":"To render it hot upon its upper side,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though his high light possess such burning glare,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How, then, can he, when under the gross earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Make water boil and glut with fiery heat?-"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, specially, since scarcely potent he"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through hedging walls of houses to inject"},{"sp":"N","t":"His exhalations hot, with ardent rays."},{"sp":"N","t":"What, then's, the principle? Why, this, indeed:"},{"sp":"N","t":"The earth about that spring is porous more"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than elsewhere the telluric ground, and be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Many the seeds of fire hard by the water;"},{"sp":"N","t":"On this account, when night with dew-fraught shades"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath whelmed the earth, anon the earth deep down"},{"sp":"N","t":"Grows chill, contracts; and thuswise squeezes out"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the spring what seeds she holds of fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"(As one might squeeze with fist), which render hot"},{"sp":"N","t":"The touch and steam of the fluid. Next, when sun,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Up-risen, with his rays has split the soil"},{"sp":"N","t":"And rarefied the earth with waxing heat,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Again into their ancient abodes return"},{"sp":"N","t":"The seeds of fire, and all the Hot of water"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the earth retires; and this is why"},{"sp":"N","t":"The fountain in the daylight gets so cold."},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides, the water's wet is beat upon"},{"sp":"N","t":"By rays of sun, and, with the dawn, becomes"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rarer in texture under his pulsing blaze;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And, therefore, whatso seeds it holds of fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"It renders up, even as it renders oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"The frost that it contains within itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"And thaws its ice and looseneth the knots."},{"sp":"N","t":"There is, moreover, a fountain cold in kind","st":"6.879"},{"sp":"N","t":"That makes a bit of tow (above it held)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Take fire forthwith and shoot a flame; so, too,"},{"sp":"N","t":"A pitch-pine torch will kindle and flare round"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along its waves, wherever 'tis impelled"},{"sp":"N","t":"Afloat before the breeze. No marvel, this:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because full many seeds of heat there be"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the water; and, from earth itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"Out of the deeps must particles of fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Athrough the entire fountain surge aloft,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And speed in exhalations into air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forth and abroad (yet not in numbers enow"},{"sp":"N","t":"As to make hot the fountain). And, moreo'er,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Some force constrains them, scattered through the water,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forthwith to burst abroad, and to combine"},{"sp":"N","t":"In flame above. Even as a fountain far"},{"sp":"N","t":"There is at Aradus amid the sea,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which bubbles out sweet water and disparts"},{"sp":"N","t":"From round itself the salt waves; and, behold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In many another region the broad main"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yields to the thirsty mariners timely help,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Belching sweet waters forth amid salt waves."},{"sp":"N","t":"Just so, then, can those seeds of fire burst forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Athrough that other fount, and bubble out"},{"sp":"N","t":"Abroad against the bit of tow; and when"},{"sp":"N","t":"They there collect or cleave unto the torch,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forthwith they readily flash aflame, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"The tow and torches, also, in themselves"},{"sp":"N","t":"Have many seeds of latent fire. Indeed,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And seest thou not, when near the nightly lamps"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thou bringest a flaxen wick, extinguished"},{"sp":"N","t":"A moment since, it catches fire before"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Thas touched the flame, and in same wise a torch?"},{"sp":"N","t":"And many another object flashes aflame"},{"sp":"N","t":"When at a distance, touched by heat alone,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Before 'tis steeped in veritable fire."},{"sp":"N","t":"This, then, we must suppose to come to pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"In that spring also."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now to other things!","st":"6.906"},{"sp":"N","t":"And I'll begin to treat by what decree"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of nature it came to pass that iron can be"},{"sp":"N","t":"By that stone drawn which Greeks the magnet call"},{"sp":"N","t":"After the country's name (its origin"},{"sp":"N","t":"Being in country of Magnesian folk)."},{"sp":"N","t":"This stone men marvel at; and sure it oft"},{"sp":"N","t":"Maketh a chain of rings, depending, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"From off itself! Nay, thou mayest see at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"Five or yet more in order dangling down"},{"sp":"N","t":"And swaying in the delicate winds, whilst one"},{"sp":"N","t":"Depends from other, cleaving to under-side,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And ilk one feels the stone's own power and bonds-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So over-masteringly its power flows down."},{"sp":"N","t":"In things of this sort, much must be made sure"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ere thou account of the thing itself canst give,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the approaches roundabout must be;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore the more do I exact of thee"},{"sp":"N","t":"A mind and ears attent."},{"sp":"N","t":"First, from all things"},{"sp":"N","t":"We see soever, evermore must flow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must be discharged and strewn about, about,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Bodies that strike the eyes, awaking sight."},{"sp":"N","t":"From certain things flow odours evermore,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As cold from rivers, heat from sun, and spray"},{"sp":"N","t":"From waves of ocean, eater-out of walls"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the coasts. Nor ever cease to seep"},{"sp":"N","t":"The varied echoings athrough the air."},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, too, there comes into the mouth at times"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wet of a salt taste, when by the sea"},{"sp":"N","t":"We roam about; and so, whene'er we watch"},{"sp":"N","t":"The wormwood being mixed, its bitter stings."},{"sp":"N","t":"To such degree from all things is each thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Borne streamingly along, and sent about"},{"sp":"N","t":"To every region round; and nature grants"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor rest nor respite of the onward flow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Since 'tis incessantly we feeling have,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And all the time are suffered to descry"},{"sp":"N","t":"And smell all things at hand, and hear them sound."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now will I seek again to bring to mind","st":"6.936"},{"sp":"N","t":"How porous a body all things have—a fact"},{"sp":"N","t":"Made manifest in my first canto, too."},{"sp":"N","t":"For, truly, though to know this doth import"},{"sp":"N","t":"For many things, yet for this very thing"},{"sp":"N","t":"On which straightway I'm going to discourse,"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Tis needful most of all to make it sure"},{"sp":"N","t":"That naught's at hand but body mixed with void."},{"sp":"N","t":"A first ensample: in grottos, rocks o'erhead"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sweat moisture and distil the oozy drops;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Likewise, from all our body seeps the sweat;"},{"sp":"N","t":"There grows the beard, and along our members all"},{"sp":"N","t":"And along our frame the hairs. Through all our veins"},{"sp":"N","t":"Disseminates the foods, and gives increase"},{"sp":"N","t":"And aliment down to the extreme parts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Even to the tiniest finger-nails. Likewise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through solid bronze the cold and fiery heat"},{"sp":"N","t":"We feel to pass; likewise, we feel them pass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through gold, through silver, when we clasp in hand"},{"sp":"N","t":"The brimming goblets. And, again, there flit"},{"sp":"N","t":"Voices through houses' hedging walls of stone;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Odour seeps through, and cold, and heat of fire"},{"sp":"N","t":"That's wont to penetrate even strength of iron."},{"sp":"N","t":"Again, where corselet of the sky girds round"},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"And at same time, some Influence of bane,"},{"sp":"N","t":"When from Beyond 'thas stolen into [our world]."},{"sp":"N","t":"And tempests, gathering from the earth and sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Back to the sky and earth absorbed retire-"},{"sp":"N","t":"With reason, since there's naught that's fashioned not"},{"sp":"N","t":"With body porous."},{"sp":"N","t":"Furthermore, not all","st":"6.959"},{"sp":"N","t":"The particles which be from things thrown off"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are furnished with same qualities for sense,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor be for all things equally adapt."},{"sp":"N","t":"A first ensample: the sun doth bake and parch"},{"sp":"N","t":"The earth; but ice he thaws, and with his beams"},{"sp":"N","t":"Compels the lofty snows, up-reared white"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the lofty hills, to waste away;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, wax, if set beneath the heat of him,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Melts to a liquid. And the fire, likewise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Will melt the copper and will fuse the gold,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But hides and flesh it shrivels up and shrinks."},{"sp":"N","t":"The water hardens the iron just off the fire,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But hides and flesh (made hard by heat) it softens."},{"sp":"N","t":"The oleaster-tree as much delights"},{"sp":"N","t":"The bearded she-goats, verily as though"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twere nectar-steeped and shed ambrosia;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than which is naught that burgeons into leaf"},{"sp":"N","t":"More bitter food for man. A hog draws back"},{"sp":"N","t":"For marjoram oil, and every unguent fears"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fierce poison these unto the bristled hogs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet unto us from time to time they seem,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As 'twere, to give new life. But, contrariwise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Though unto us the mire be filth most foul,"},{"sp":"N","t":"To hogs that mire doth so delightsome seem"},{"sp":"N","t":"That they with wallowing from belly to back"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are never cloyed."},{"sp":"N","t":"A point remains, besides,","st":"6.979"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which best it seems to tell of, ere I go"},{"sp":"N","t":"To telling of the fact at hand itself."},{"sp":"N","t":"Since to the varied things assigned be"},{"sp":"N","t":"The many pores, those pores must be diverse"},{"sp":"N","t":"In nature one from other, and each have"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its very shape, its own direction fixed."},{"sp":"N","t":"And so, indeed, in breathing creatures be"},{"sp":"N","t":"The several senses, of which each takes in"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto itself, in its own fashion ever,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Its own peculiar object. For we mark"},{"sp":"N","t":"How sounds do into one place penetrate,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into another flavours of all juice,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And savour of smell into a third. Moreover,"},{"sp":"N","t":"One sort through rocks we see to seep, and, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"One sort to pass through wood, another still"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through gold, and others to go out and off"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through silver and through glass. For we do see"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through some pores form-and-look of things to flow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through others heat to go, and some things still"},{"sp":"N","t":"To speedier pass than others through same pores."},{"sp":"N","t":"Of verity, the nature of these same paths,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Varying in many modes (as aforesaid)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because of unlike nature and warp and woof"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of cosmic things, constrains it so to be."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, since all these matters now have been"},{"sp":"N","t":"Established and settled well for us"},{"sp":"N","t":"As premises prepared, for what remains"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twill not be hard to render clear account"},{"sp":"N","t":"By means of these, and the whole cause reveal"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereby the magnet lures the strength of iron."},{"sp":"N","t":"First, stream there must from off the lode-stone seeds","st":"6.1002"},{"sp":"N","t":"Innumerable, a very tide, which smites"},{"sp":"N","t":"By blows that air asunder lying betwixt"},{"sp":"N","t":"The stone and iron. And when is emptied out"},{"sp":"N","t":"This space, and a large place between the two"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is made a void, forthwith the primal germs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of iron, headlong slipping, fall conjoined"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the vacuum, and the ring itself"},{"sp":"N","t":"By reason thereof doth follow after and go"},{"sp":"N","t":"Thuswise with all its body. And naught there is"},{"sp":"N","t":"That of its own primordial elements"},{"sp":"N","t":"More thoroughly knit or tighter linked coheres"},{"sp":"N","t":"Than nature and cold roughness of stout iron."},{"sp":"N","t":"Wherefore, 'tis less a marvel what I said,"},{"sp":"N","t":"That from such elements no bodies can"},{"sp":"N","t":"From out the iron collect in larger throng"},{"sp":"N","t":"And be into the vacuum borne along,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Without the ring itself do follow after."},{"sp":"N","t":"And this it does, and followeth on until"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Thath reached the stone itself and cleaved to it"},{"sp":"N","t":"By links invisible. Moreover, likewise,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The motion's assisted by a thing of aid"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Whereby the process easier becomes),-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Namely, by this: as soon as rarer grows"},{"sp":"N","t":"That air in front of the ring, and space between"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is emptied more and made a void, forthwith"},{"sp":"N","t":"It happens all the air that lies behind"},{"sp":"N","t":"Conveys it onward, pushing from the rear."},{"sp":"N","t":"For ever doth the circumambient air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Drub things unmoved, but here it pushes forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"The iron, because upon one side the space"},{"sp":"N","t":"Lies void and thus receives the iron in."},{"sp":"N","t":"This air, whereof I am reminding thee,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Winding athrough the iron's abundant pores"},{"sp":"N","t":"So subtly into the tiny parts thereof,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shoves it and pushes, as wind the ship and sails."},{"sp":"N","t":"The same doth happen in all directions forth:"},{"sp":"N","t":"From whatso side a space is made a void,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whether from crosswise or above, forthwith"},{"sp":"N","t":"The neighbour particles are borne along"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into the vacuum; for of verity,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They're set a-going by poundings from elsewhere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor by themselves of own accord can they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rise upwards into the air. Again, all things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Must in their framework hold some air, because"},{"sp":"N","t":"They are of framework porous, and the air"},{"sp":"N","t":"Encompasses and borders on all things."},{"sp":"N","t":"Thus, then, this air in iron so deeply stored"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is tossed evermore in vexed motion,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And therefore drubs upon the ring sans doubt"},{"sp":"N","t":"And shakes it up inside...."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"In sooth, that ring is thither borne along"},{"sp":"N","t":"To where 'thas once plunged headlong—thither, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto the void whereto it took its start."},{"sp":"N","t":"It happens, too, at times that nature of iron","st":"6.1042"},{"sp":"N","t":"Shrinks from this stone away, accustomed"},{"sp":"N","t":"By turns to flee and follow. Yea, I've seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"Those Samothracian iron rings leap up,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And iron filings in the brazen bowls"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seethe furiously, when underneath was set"},{"sp":"N","t":"The magnet stone. So strongly iron seems"},{"sp":"N","t":"To crave to flee that rock. Such discord great"},{"sp":"N","t":"Is gendered by the interposed brass,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because, forsooth, when first the tide of brass"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath seized upon and held possession of"},{"sp":"N","t":"The iron's open passage-ways, thereafter"},{"sp":"N","t":"Cometh the tide of the stone, and in that iron"},{"sp":"N","t":"Findeth all spaces full, nor now hath holes"},{"sp":"N","t":"To swim through, as before. 'Tis thus constrained"},{"sp":"N","t":"With its own current 'gainst the iron's fabric"},{"sp":"N","t":"To dash and beat; by means whereof it spues"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forth from itself—and through the brass stirs up-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The things which otherwise without the brass"},{"sp":"N","t":"It sucks into itself. In these affairs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Marvel thou not that from this stone the tide"},{"sp":"N","t":"Prevails not likewise other things to move"},{"sp":"N","t":"With its own blows: for some stand firm by weight,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As gold; and some cannot be moved forever,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Because so porous in their framework they"},{"sp":"N","t":"That there the tide streams through without a break,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of which sort stuff of wood is seen to be."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore, when iron (which lies between the two)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hath taken in some atoms of the brass,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then do the streams of that Magnesian rock"},{"sp":"N","t":"Move iron by their smitings."},{"sp":"N","t":"Yet these things","st":"6.1065"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are not so alien from others, that I"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of this same sort am ill prepared to name"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ensamples still of things exclusively"},{"sp":"N","t":"To one another adapt. Thou seest, first,"},{"sp":"N","t":"How lime alone cementeth stones: how wood"},{"sp":"N","t":"Only by glue-of-bull with wood is joined-"},{"sp":"N","t":"So firmly too that oftener the boards"},{"sp":"N","t":"Crack open along the weakness of the grain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ere ever those taurine bonds will lax their hold."},{"sp":"N","t":"The vine-born juices with the water-springs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are bold to mix, though not the heavy pitch"},{"sp":"N","t":"With the light oil-of-olive. And purple dye"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of shell-fish so uniteth with the wool's"},{"sp":"N","t":"Body alone that it cannot be ta'en"},{"sp":"N","t":"Away forever—nay, though thou gavest toil"},{"sp":"N","t":"To restore the same with the Neptunian flood,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nay, though all ocean willed to wash it out"},{"sp":"N","t":"With all its waves. Again, gold unto gold"},{"sp":"N","t":"Doth not one substance bind, and only one?"},{"sp":"N","t":"And is not brass by tin joined unto brass?"},{"sp":"N","t":"And other ensamples how many might one find!"},{"sp":"N","t":"What then? Nor is there unto thee a need"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of such long ways and roundabout, nor boots it"},{"sp":"N","t":"For me much toil on this to spend. More fit"},{"sp":"N","t":"It is in few words briefly to embrace"},{"sp":"N","t":"Things many: things whose textures fall together"},{"sp":"N","t":"So mutually adapt, that cavities"},{"sp":"N","t":"To solids correspond, these cavities"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of this thing to the solid parts of that,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And those of that to solid parts of this-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Such joinings are the best. Again, some things"},{"sp":"N","t":"Can be the one with other coupled and held,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Linked by hooks and eyes, as 'twere; and this"},{"sp":"N","t":"Seems more the fact with iron and this stone."},{"sp":"N","t":"Now, of diseases what the law, and whence","st":"6.1090"},{"sp":"N","t":"The Influence of bane upgathering can"},{"sp":"N","t":"Upon the race of man and herds of cattle"},{"sp":"N","t":"Kindle a devastation fraught with death,"},{"sp":"N","t":"I will unfold. And, first, I've taught above"},{"sp":"N","t":"That seeds there be of many things to us"},{"sp":"N","t":"Life-giving, and that, contrariwise, there must"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fly many round bringing disease and death."},{"sp":"N","t":"When these have, haply, chanced to collect"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to derange the atmosphere of earth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The air becometh baneful. And, lo, all"},{"sp":"N","t":"That Influence of bane, that pestilence,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or from Beyond down through our atmosphere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like clouds and mists, descends, or else collects"},{"sp":"N","t":"From earth herself and rises, when, a-soak"},{"sp":"N","t":"And beat by rains unseasonable and suns,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Our earth hath then contracted stench and rot."},{"sp":"N","t":"Seest thou not, also, that whoso arrive"},{"sp":"N","t":"In region far from fatherland and home"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are by the strangeness of the clime and waters"},{"sp":"N","t":"Distempered?- since conditions vary much."},{"sp":"N","t":"For in what else may we suppose the clime"},{"sp":"N","t":"Among the Britons to differ from Aegypt's own"},{"sp":"N","t":"(Where totters awry the axis of the world),"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or in what else to differ Pontic clime"},{"sp":"N","t":"From Gades' and from climes adown the south,"},{"sp":"N","t":"On to black generations of strong men"},{"sp":"N","t":"With sun-baked skins? Even as we thus do see"},{"sp":"N","t":"Four climes diverse under the four main-winds"},{"sp":"N","t":"And under the four main-regions of the sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"So, too, are seen the colour and face of men"},{"sp":"N","t":"Vastly to disagree, and fixed diseases"},{"sp":"N","t":"To seize the generations, kind by kind:"},{"sp":"N","t":"There is the elephant-disease which down"},{"sp":"N","t":"In midmost Aegypt, hard by streams of Nile,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Engendered is—and never otherwhere."},{"sp":"N","t":"In Attica the feet are oft attacked,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And in Achaean lands the eyes. And so"},{"sp":"N","t":"The divers spots to divers parts and limbs"},{"sp":"N","t":"Are noxious; 'tis a variable air"},{"sp":"N","t":"That causes this. Thus when an atmosphere,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alien by chance to us, begins to heave,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And noxious airs begin to crawl along,"},{"sp":"N","t":"They creep and wind like unto mist and cloud,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Slowly, and everything upon their way"},{"sp":"N","t":"They disarrange and force to change its state."},{"sp":"N","t":"It happens, too, that when they've come at last"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into this atmosphere of ours, they taint"},{"sp":"N","t":"And make it like themselves and alien."},{"sp":"N","t":"Therefore, asudden this devastation strange,"},{"sp":"N","t":"This pestilence, upon the waters falls,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or settles on the very crops of grain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or other meat of men and feed of flocks."},{"sp":"N","t":"Or it remains a subtle force, suspense"},{"sp":"N","t":"In the atmosphere itself; and when therefrom"},{"sp":"N","t":"We draw our inhalations of mixed air,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Into our body equally its bane"},{"sp":"N","t":"Also we must suck in. In manner like,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Oft comes the pestilence upon the kine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And sickness, too, upon the sluggish sheep."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor aught it matters whether journey we"},{"sp":"N","t":"To regions adverse to ourselves and change"},{"sp":"N","t":"The atmospheric cloak, or whether nature"},{"sp":"N","t":"Herself import a tainted atmosphere"},{"sp":"N","t":"To us or something strange to our own use"},{"sp":"N","t":"Which can attack us soon as ever it come."},{"sp":"SEC","t":"THE PLAGUE ATHENS"},{"sp":"N","t":"'Twas such a manner of disease, 'twas such","st":"6.1138"},{"sp":"N","t":"Mortal miasma in Cecropian lands"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whilom reduced the plains to dead men's bones,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unpeopled the highways, drained of citizens"},{"sp":"N","t":"The Athenian town. For coming from afar,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rising in lands of Aegypt, traversing"},{"sp":"N","t":"Reaches of air and floating fields of foam,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At last on all Pandion's folk it swooped;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whereat by troops unto disease and death"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were they o'er-given. At first, they'd bear about"},{"sp":"N","t":"A skull on fire with heat, and eyeballs twain"},{"sp":"N","t":"Red with suffusion of blank glare. Their throats,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Black on the inside, sweated oozy blood;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And the walled pathway of the voice of man"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was clogged with ulcers; and the very tongue,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The mind's interpreter, would trickle gore,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Weakened by torments, tardy, rough to touch."},{"sp":"N","t":"Next when that Influence of bane had chocked,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Down through the throat, the breast, and streamed had"},{"sp":"N","t":"E'en into sullen heart of those sick folk,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Then, verily, all the fences of man's life"},{"sp":"N","t":"Began to topple. From the mouth the breath"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would roll a noisome stink, as stink to heaven"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rotting cadavers flung unburied out."},{"sp":"N","t":"And, lo, thereafter, all the body's strength"},{"sp":"N","t":"And every power of mind would languish, now"},{"sp":"N","t":"In very doorway of destruction."},{"sp":"N","t":"And anxious anguish and ululation (mixed"},{"sp":"N","t":"With many a groan) companioned alway"},{"sp":"N","t":"The intolerable torments. Night and day,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Recurrent spasms of vomiting would rack"},{"sp":"N","t":"Alway their thews and members, breaking down"},{"sp":"N","t":"With sheer exhaustion men already spent."},{"sp":"N","t":"And yet on no one's body couldst thou mark"},{"sp":"N","t":"The skin with o'er-much heat to burn aglow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"But rather the body unto touch of hands"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would offer a warmish feeling, and thereby"},{"sp":"N","t":"Show red all over, with ulcers, so to say,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Inbranded, like the \"sacred fires\" o'erspread"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the members. The inward parts of men,"},{"sp":"N","t":"In truth, would blaze unto the very bones;"},{"sp":"N","t":"A flame, like flame in furnaces, would blaze"},{"sp":"N","t":"Within the stomach. Nor couldst aught apply"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unto their members light enough and thin"},{"sp":"N","t":"For shift of aid—but coolness and a breeze"},{"sp":"N","t":"Ever and ever. Some would plunge those limbs"},{"sp":"N","t":"On fire with bane into the icy streams,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hurling the body naked into the waves;"},{"sp":"N","t":"Many would headlong fling them deeply down","st":"6.1174"},{"sp":"N","t":"The water-pits, tumbling with eager mouth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Already agape. The insatiable thirst"},{"sp":"N","t":"That whelmed their parched bodies, lo, would make"},{"sp":"N","t":"A goodly shower seem like to scanty drops."},{"sp":"N","t":"Respite of torment was there none. Their frames"},{"sp":"N","t":"Forspent lay prone. With silent lips of fear"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would Medicine mumble low, the while she saw"},{"sp":"N","t":"So many a time men roll their eyeballs round,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Staring wide-open, unvisited of sleep,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The heralds of old death. And in those months"},{"sp":"N","t":"Was given many another sign of death:"},{"sp":"N","t":"The intellect of mind by sorrow and dread"},{"sp":"N","t":"Deranged, the sad brow, the countenance"},{"sp":"N","t":"Fierce and delirious, the tormented ears"},{"sp":"N","t":"Beset with ringings, the breath quick and short"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or huge and intermittent, soaking sweat"},{"sp":"N","t":"A-glisten on neck, the spittle in fine gouts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Tainted with colour of crocus and so salt,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The cough scarce wheezing through the rattling throat."},{"sp":"N","t":"Aye, and the sinews in the fingered hands"},{"sp":"N","t":"Were sure to contract, and sure the jointed frame"},{"sp":"N","t":"To shiver, and up from feet the cold to mount"},{"sp":"N","t":"Inch after inch: and toward the supreme hour"},{"sp":"N","t":"At last the pinched nostrils, nose's tip"},{"sp":"N","t":"A very point, eyes sunken, temples hollow,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Skin cold and hard, the shuddering grimace,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The pulled and puffy flesh above the brows!-"},{"sp":"N","t":"O not long after would their frames lie prone"},{"sp":"N","t":"In rigid death. And by about the eighth"},{"sp":"N","t":"Resplendent light of sun, or at the most"},{"sp":"N","t":"On the ninth flaming of his flambeau, they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would render up the life. If any then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had 'scaped the doom of that destruction, yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"Him there awaited in the after days"},{"sp":"N","t":"A wasting and a death from ulcers vile"},{"sp":"N","t":"And black discharges of the belly, or else"},{"sp":"N","t":"Through the clogged nostrils would there ooze along"},{"sp":"N","t":"Much fouled blood, oft with an aching head:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hither would stream a man's whole strength and flesh."},{"sp":"N","t":"And whoso had survived that virulent flow","st":"6.1205"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the vile blood, yet into thews of him"},{"sp":"N","t":"And into his joints and very genitals"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would pass the old disease. And some there were,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Dreading the doorways of destruction"},{"sp":"N","t":"So much, lived on, deprived by the knife"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of the male member; not a few, though lopped"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of hands and feet, would yet persist in life,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And some there were who lost their eyeballs: O"},{"sp":"N","t":"So fierce a fear of death had fallen on them!"},{"sp":"N","t":"And some, besides, were by oblivion"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of all things seized, that even themselves they knew"},{"sp":"N","t":"No longer. And though corpse on corpse lay piled"},{"sp":"N","t":"Unburied on ground, the race of birds and beasts"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would or spring back, scurrying to escape"},{"sp":"N","t":"The virulent stench, or, if they'd tasted there,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would languish in approaching death. But yet"},{"sp":"N","t":"Hardly at all during those many suns"},{"sp":"N","t":"Appeared a fowl, nor from the woods went forth"},{"sp":"N","t":"The sullen generations of wild beasts-"},{"sp":"N","t":"They languished with disease and died and died."},{"sp":"N","t":"In chief, the faithful dogs, in all the streets"},{"sp":"N","t":"Outstretched, would yield their breath distressfully"},{"sp":"N","t":"For so that Influence of bane would twist"},{"sp":"N","t":"Life from their members. Nor was found one sure"},{"sp":"N","t":"And universal principle of cure:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For what to one had given the power to take"},{"sp":"N","t":"The vital winds of air into his mouth,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And to gaze upward at the vaults of sky,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The same to others was their death and doom."},{"sp":"N","t":"In those affairs, O awfullest of all,","st":"6.1230"},{"sp":"N","t":"O pitiable most was this, was this:"},{"sp":"N","t":"Whoso once saw himself in that disease"},{"sp":"N","t":"Entangled, ay, as damned unto death,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would lie in wanhope, with a sullen heart,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would, in fore-vision of his funeral,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Give up the ghost, O then and there. For, lo,"},{"sp":"N","t":"At no time did they cease one from another"},{"sp":"N","t":"To catch contagion of the greedy plague,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"As though but woolly flocks and horned herds;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And this in chief would heap the dead on dead:"},{"sp":"N","t":"For who forbore to look to their own sick,"},{"sp":"N","t":"O these (too eager of life, of death afeard)"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would then, soon after, slaughtering Neglect"},{"sp":"N","t":"Visit with vengeance of evil death and base-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Themselves deserted and forlorn of help."},{"sp":"N","t":"But who had stayed at hand would perish there"},{"sp":"N","t":"By that contagion and the toil which then"},{"sp":"N","t":"A sense of honour and the pleading voice"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of weary watchers, mixed with voice of wail"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of dying folk, forced them to undergo."},{"sp":"N","t":"This kind of death each nobler soul would meet."},{"sp":"N","t":"The funerals, uncompanioned, forsaken,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Like rivals contended to be hurried through."},{"sp":"N","t":". . . . . ."},{"sp":"N","t":"And men contending to ensepulchre"},{"sp":"N","t":"Pile upon pile the throng of their own dead:"},{"sp":"N","t":"And weary with woe and weeping wandered home;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And then the most would take to bed from grief."},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor could be found not one, whom nor disease"},{"sp":"N","t":"Nor death, nor woe had not in those dread times"},{"sp":"N","t":"Attacked."},{"sp":"N","t":"By now the shepherds and neatherds all,","st":"6.1247"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yea, even the sturdy guiders of curved ploughs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Began to sicken, and their bodies would lie"},{"sp":"N","t":"Huddled within back-corners of their huts,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Delivered by squalor and disease to death."},{"sp":"N","t":"O often and often couldst thou then have seen"},{"sp":"N","t":"On lifeless children lifeless parents prone,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Or offspring on their fathers', mothers' corpse"},{"sp":"N","t":"Yielding the life. And into the city poured"},{"sp":"N","t":"O not in least part from the countryside"},{"sp":"N","t":"That tribulation, which the peasantry"},{"sp":"N","t":"Sick, sick, brought thither, thronging from every quarter,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Plague-stricken mob. All places would they crowd,"},{"sp":"N","t":"All buildings too; whereby the more would death"},{"sp":"N","t":"Up-pile a-heap the folk so crammed in town."},{"sp":"N","t":"Ah, many a body thirst had dragged and rolled"},{"sp":"N","t":"Along the highways there was lying strewn"},{"sp":"N","t":"Besides Silenus-headed water-fountains,-"},{"sp":"N","t":"The life-breath choked from that too dear desire"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of pleasant waters. Ah, everywhere along"},{"sp":"N","t":"The open places of the populace,"},{"sp":"N","t":"And along the highways, O thou mightest see"},{"sp":"N","t":"Of many a half-dead body the sagged limbs,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rough with squalor, wrapped around with rags,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Perish from very nastiness, with naught"},{"sp":"N","t":"But skin upon the bones, well-nigh already"},{"sp":"N","t":"Buried—in ulcers vile and obscene filth."},{"sp":"N","t":"All holy temples, too, of deities"},{"sp":"N","t":"Had Death becrammed with the carcasses;"},{"sp":"N","t":"And stood each fane of the Celestial Ones"},{"sp":"N","t":"Laden with stark cadavers everywhere-"},{"sp":"N","t":"Places which warders of the shrines had crowded"},{"sp":"N","t":"With many a guest. For now no longer men"},{"sp":"N","t":"Did mightily esteem the old Divine,"},{"sp":"N","t":"The worship of the gods: the woe at hand"},{"sp":"N","t":"Did over-master. Nor in the city then"},{"sp":"N","t":"Remained those rites of sepulture, with which"},{"sp":"N","t":"That pious folk had evermore been wont"},{"sp":"N","t":"To buried be. For it was wildered all"},{"sp":"N","t":"In wild alarms, and each and every one"},{"sp":"N","t":"With sullen sorrow would bury his own dead,"},{"sp":"N","t":"As present shift allowed. And sudden stress"},{"sp":"N","t":"And poverty to many an awful act"},{"sp":"N","t":"Impelled; and with a monstrous screaming they"},{"sp":"N","t":"Would, on the frames of alien funeral pyres,"},{"sp":"N","t":"Place their own kin, and thrust the torch beneath"},{"sp":"N","t":"Oft brawling with much bloodshed round about"},{"sp":"N","t":"Rather than quit dead bodies loved in life."}],[]);})();